ing purposes only, and are not recommended for general use.\tCore Updater Settings\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcore_updater_auto_backup\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tBackup Cores When Updating\tAutomatically create a backup of any installed cores when performing an online update. Enables easy rollback to a working core if an update introduces a regression.\tCore Updater Settings\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\talways_reload_core_on_run_content\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tbuiltin_mediaplayer_enable\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tUse Built-In Media Player\t\u0001\tMultimedia\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tbuiltin_imageviewer_enable\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tUse Built-In Image Viewer\t\u0001\tMultimedia\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tbundle_assets_extract_enable\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tfps_show\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tDisplay Framerate\tDisplay the current frames per second.\tOn-Screen Display\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tstatistics_show\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tDisplay Statistics\tDisplay on-screen technical statistics.\tOn-Screen Display\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tframecount_show\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tDisplay Frame Count\tDisplay the current frame count on-screen.\tOn-Screen Display\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmemory_show\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tDisplay Memory Usage\tDisplay the used and total amount of memory on the system.\tOn-Screen Display\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tui_menubar_enable\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow Menu Bar\tShow window menu bar.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tpause_nonactive\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tPause Content When Not Active\tPause content when RetroArch is not the active window.\tUser Interface\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tpause_on_disconnect\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tPause Content When Controller Disconnects\tPause content when any controller is disconnected. Resume with Start.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tauto_screenshot_filename\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tsuspend_screensaver_enable\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tSuspend Screensaver\tPrevent your system's screensaver from becoming active.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tapply_cheats_after_toggle\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tApply After Toggle\tApply cheat immediately after toggling.\tCheat Settings\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tapply_cheats_after_load\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tAuto-Apply Cheats During Game Load\tAuto-apply cheats when game loads.\tCheat Settings\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\trewind_enable\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tRewind Support\tReturn to a previous point in recent gameplay. This causes a severe performance hit when playing.\tRewind\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tfastforward_frameskip\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tFast-Forward Frameskip\tSkip frames according to fast-forward rate. This conserves power and allows the use of third party frame limiting.\tFrame Throttle\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvrr_runloop_enable\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tSync to Exact Content Framerate (G-Sync, FreeSync)\tNo deviation from core requested timing. Use for Variable Refresh Rate screens (G-Sync, FreeSync, HDMI 2.1 VRR).\tFrame Throttle\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_throttle_framerate\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tThrottle Menu Framerate\t\u0001\tFrame Throttle\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\trun_ahead_enabled\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\trun_ahead_secondary_instance\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\trun_ahead_hide_warnings\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tHide Run-Ahead Warnings\tHide the warning message that appears when using Run-Ahead and the core does not support save states.\tFrame Throttle\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tpreemptive_frames_enable\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tkiosk_mode_enable\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tKiosk Mode\tProtects the setup by hiding all configuration related settings.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tblock_sram_overwrite\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\treplay_auto_index\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tIncrement Replay Index Automatically\tBefore making a replay, the replay index is automatically increased. When loading content, the index will be set to the highest existing index.\tSaving\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tsavestate_auto_index\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tIncrement Save State Index Automatically\tBefore making a save state, the save state index is automatically increased. When loading content, the index will be set to the highest existing index.\tSaving\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tsavestate_auto_save\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tsavestate_auto_load\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tsavestate_thumbnail_enable\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tsave_file_compression\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tSaveRAM Compression\tWrite non-volatile SaveRAM files in an archived format. Dramatically reduces file size at the expense of (negligibly) increased saving/loading times. Only applies to cores that enable saving via the standard libretro SaveRAM interface.\tSaving\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tsavestate_file_compression\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tSave State Compression\tWrite save state files in an archived format. Dramatically reduces file size at the expense of increased saving/loading times.\tSaving\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tgame_specific_options\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tauto_overrides_enable\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tauto_remaps_enable\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinitial_disk_change_enable\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tglobal_core_options\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tauto_shaders_enable\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tscan_without_core_match\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tScan Without Core Match\tAllow content to be scanned and added to a playlist without a core installed that supports it.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tscan_serial_and_crc\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tScan Checks CRC on Possible Duplicates\tSometimes ISOs duplicate serials, particularly with PSP/PSN titles. Relying solely on the serial can sometimes cause the scanner to put content in the wrong system. This adds a CRC check, which slows down scanning considerably, but may be more accurate.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tsort_savefiles_enable\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tsort_savestates_enable\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tsort_savefiles_by_content_enable\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tsort_savestates_by_content_enable\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tsort_screenshots_by_content_enable\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tsavestates_in_content_dir\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tsavefiles_in_content_dir\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tsystemfiles_in_content_dir\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tscreenshots_in_content_dir\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tquit_press_twice\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tConfirm Quit/Close/Reset\tRequire the Quit/Close/Reset hotkey to be pressed twice.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tconfig_save_on_exit\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tremap_save_on_exit\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tshow_hidden_files\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tuse_last_start_directory\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tRemember Last Used Start Directory\tOpen File Browser at the last used location when loading content from the Start Directory. Note: Location will be reset to default upon restarting RetroArch.\tFile Browser\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcore_suggest_always\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0\tAlways Suggest Cores\tSuggest available cores even when a core is manually loaded.\tFile Browser\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcamera_allow\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tAllow Camera\tAllow cores to access the camera.\tPrivacy\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tlocation_allow\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tAllow Location\tAllow cores to access your location.\tPrivacy\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcloud_sync_enable\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tEnable Cloud Sync\tAttempt to sync configs, sram, and states to a cloud storage provider.\tCloud Sync\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcloud_sync_destructive\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tDestructive Cloud Sync\tWhen disabled, files are moved to a backup folder before being overwritten or deleted.\tCloud Sync\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcloud_sync_sync_saves\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tSync: Saves/States\tWhen enabled, saves/states will be synced to cloud.\tCloud Sync\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcloud_sync_sync_configs\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tSync: Configuration Files\tWhen enabled, configuration files will be synced to cloud.\tCloud Sync\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcloud_sync_sync_thumbs\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tSync: Thumbnail Images\tWhen enabled, thumbnail images will be synced to cloud. Not generally recommended except for large collections of custom thumbnail images; otherwise the thumbnail downloader is a better choice.\tCloud Sync\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcloud_sync_sync_system\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tSync: System Files\tWhen enabled, system files will be synced to cloud. This can significantly increase the time it takes to sync; use with caution.\tCloud Sync\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tdiscord_allow\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tDiscord Rich Presence\tAllow the Discord app to show data about the content played. Only available with the native desktop client.\tPrivacy\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tsteam_rich_presence_enable\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tEnable Rich Presence\tShare your current status within RetroArch on Steam.\tSteam\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tthreaded_data_runloop_enable\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tThreaded Tasks\tPerform tasks on a separate thread.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tlog_to_file\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tLog to File\tRedirect system event log messages to file. Requires 'Logging Verbosity' to be enabled.\tLogging\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tlog_to_file_timestamp\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tTimestamp Log Files\tWhen logging to file, redirect the output from each RetroArch session to a new timestamped file. If disabled, log is overwritten each time RetroArch is restarted.\tLogging\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tai_service_enable\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tAI Service Enabled\tEnable AI Service to run when the AI Service hotkey is pressed.\tAI Service\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tai_service_pause\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tPause During Translation\tPause core while screen is translated.\tAI Service\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\twifi_enabled\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tEnable Wi-Fi\t\u0001\tWi-Fi\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tgamemode_enable\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tGame Mode\t\u0001\tPower Management\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tswitch_oc\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tCPU Overclock\tEnable CPU Overclock frequencies\tNintendo Switch Options\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tswitch_cec\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tCEC Support\tEnable CEC Handshaking with TV when docking\tNintendo Switch Options\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tbluetooth_ertm_disable\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tBluetooth ERTM Disable\tDisable Bluetooth ERTM to fix pairing of some devices\tNintendo Switch Options\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\taudio_enable\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tAudio\tEnable audio output.\tAudio\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\taudio_sync\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tSynchronization\tSynchronize audio. Recommended.\tAudio\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\taudio_rate_control\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\taudio_enable_menu\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tMixer\tPlay simultaneous audio streams even in the menu.\tMenu Sounds\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\taudio_enable_menu_ok\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tEnable 'OK' Sound\t\u0001\tMenu Sounds\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\taudio_enable_menu_cancel\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tEnable 'Cancel' Sound\t\u0001\tMenu Sounds\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\taudio_enable_menu_notice\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tEnable 'Notice' Sound\t\u0001\tMenu Sounds\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\taudio_enable_menu_bgm\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tEnable 'BGM' Sound\t\u0001\tMenu Sounds\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\taudio_enable_menu_scroll\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tEnable 'Scroll' Sounds\t\u0001\tMenu Sounds\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\taudio_mute_enable\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tMute\tMute audio.\tAudio\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\taudio_mixer_mute_enable\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tMixer Mute\tMute mixer audio.\tAudio\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\taudio_respect_silent_mode\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tRespect Silent Mode\tMute all audio in Silent Mode.\tAudio\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\taudio_fastforward_mute\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tFast-Forward Audio Mute\tAutomatically mute audio when using fast-forward.\tAudio\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\taudio_fastforward_speedup\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tFast-Forward Audio Speedup\tSpeed up audio when fast-forwarding. Prevents crackling but shifts pitch.\tAudio\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\taudio_rewind_mute\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tRewind Audio Mute\tAutomatically mute audio when using rewind.\tAudio\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\taudio_wasapi_exclusive_mode\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tWASAPI Exclusive Mode\tAllow the WASAPI driver to take exclusive control of the audio device. If disabled, it will use shared mode instead.\tAudio\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\taudio_wasapi_float_format\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tWASAPI Float Format\tUse float format for the WASAPI driver, if supported by your audio device.\tAudio\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmicrophone_enable\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tMicrophone\tEnable audio input in supported cores. Has no overhead if the core isn't using a microphone.\tMicrophone\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmicrophone_wasapi_exclusive_mode\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tWASAPI Exclusive Mode\tAllow RetroArch to take exclusive control of the microphone device when using the WASAPI microphone driver. If disabled, RetroArch will use shared mode instead.\tMicrophone\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmicrophone_wasapi_float_format\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tWASAPI Float Format\tUse floating-point input for the WASAPI driver, if supported by your audio device.\tMicrophone\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcrt_switch_resolution_use_custom_refresh_rate\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tCustom Refresh Rate\tUse a custom refresh rate specified in the configuration file if needed.\tCRT SwitchRes\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcrt_switch_hires_menu\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tUse High Resolution Menu\tSwitch to high resolution modeline for use with high-resolution menus when no content is loaded.\tCRT SwitchRes\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_shader_enable\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tVideo Shaders\tEnable video shader pipeline.\tConfiguration\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_shader_watch_files\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tWatch Shader Files for Changes\tAutomatically apply changes made to shader files on disk.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_shader_remember_last_dir\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tRemember Last Used Shader Directory\tOpen File Browser at the last used directory when loading shader presets and passes.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_shader_preset_save_reference_enable\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tSimple Presets\tSave a shader preset which has a link to the original preset loaded and includes only the parameter changes you made.\tConfiguration\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_aspect_ratio_auto\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_scan_subframes\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tRolling scanline simulation\tWARNING: Rapid flickering may cause image persistence on some displays. Use at your own risk // Simulates a basic rolling scanline over multiple sub-frames by dividing the screen up vertically and rendering each part of the screen according to how many sub-frames there are.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_allow_rotate\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_windowed_fullscreen\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tWindowed Fullscreen Mode\tIf fullscreen, prefer using a fullscreen window to prevent display mode switching.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_crop_overscan\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tCrop Overscan (Restart required)\tCut off a few pixels around the edges of the image customarily left blank by developers which sometimes also contain garbage pixels.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_scale_integer\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tInteger Scale\tScale video in integer steps only. The base size depends on core-reported geometry and aspect ratio.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_smooth\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tBilinear Filtering\tAdd a slight blur to the image to soften hard pixel edges. This option has very little impact on performance. Should be disabled if using shaders.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_ctx_scaling\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tRGA Scaling\tHardware context scaling (if available).\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_force_aspect\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_frame_delay_auto\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tAutomatic Frame Delay\tAdjust effective 'Frame Delay' dynamically.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_dingux_ipu_keep_aspect\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tKeep Aspect Ratio\tMaintain 1:1 pixel aspect ratios when scaling content via the internal IPU. If disabled, images will be stretched to fill the entire display.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_threaded\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tThreaded Video\tImproves performance at the cost of latency and more video stuttering. Use only if full speed cannot be obtained otherwise.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_shared_context\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_vfilter\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tDeflicker\t\u0001\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_font_enable\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tOn-Screen Notifications\tShow on-screen messages.\tOn-Screen Display\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_force_srgb_disable\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tForce-Disable sRGB FBO\tForcibly disable sRGB FBO support. Some Intel OpenGL drivers on Windows have video problems with sRGB FBOs. Enabling this can work around it.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_fullscreen\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tFullscreen Display\tDisplay in fullscreen. Can be changed at runtime. Can be overridden by a command line switch.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_hdr_enable\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tEnable HDR\tEnable HDR if the display supports it.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_hdr_expand_gamut\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tExpand Gamut\tOnce the color space is converted to linear space, decide whether we should use an expanded colour gamut to get to HDR10.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_vsync\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tVertical Sync (VSync)\tSynchronize the output video of the graphics card to the refresh rate of the screen. Recommended.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_adaptive_vsync\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tAdaptive VSync\tVSync is enabled until performance falls below the target refresh rate. Can minimize stuttering when performance falls below real time, and be more energy efficient. Not compatible with 'Frame Delay'.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_hard_sync\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tHard GPU Sync\tHard-synchronize the CPU and GPU. Reduces latency at the cost of performance.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_waitable_swapchains\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tWaitable Swapchains\tHard-synchronize the CPU and GPU. Reduces latency at the cost of performance.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_disable_composition\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tDisable Desktop Composition\tWindow managers use composition to apply visual effects, detect unresponsive windows, among other things.\tUser Interface\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_gpu_screenshot\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tGPU Screenshot\tScreenshots capture GPU shaded material if available.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_post_filter_record\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tUse Post Filter Recording\tCapture the image after filters (but not shaders) are applied. The video will look as fancy as what you see on your screen.\tRecording\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_notch_write_over_enable\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tEnable fullscreen over notch in Android and iOS devices\t\u0001\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_use_metal_arg_buffers\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0\tUse Metal Argument Buffers (Restart required)\tTry to improve performance by using Metal argument buffers. Some cores may require this. This may break some shaders, particularly on old hardware or OS versions.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_msg_bgcolor_enable\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tNotification Background\tEnables a background color for the OSD.\tOn-Screen Display\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_window_show_decorations\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow Window Decorations\tShow window title bar and borders.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_window_save_positions\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tRemember Window Position and Size\tShow all content in a fixed size window of dimensions specified by 'Window Width' and 'Window Height', and save current window size and position upon closing RetroArch. When disabled, window size will be set dynamically based on 'Windowed Scale'.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_window_custom_size_enable\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tUse Custom Window Size\tShow all content in a fixed size window of dimensions specified by 'Window Width' and 'Window Height'. When disabled, window size will be set dynamically based on 'Windowed Scale'.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_enable_widgets\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tGraphics Widgets\tUse decorated animations, notifications, indicators and controls.\tOn-Screen Display\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_widget_scale_auto\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tScale Graphics Widgets Automatically\tAutomatically resize decorated notifications, indicators and controls based on current menu scale.\tOn-Screen Display\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_show_load_content_animation\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\"Load Content\" Startup Notification\tShow a brief launch feedback animation when loading content.\tOn-Screen Display\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnotification_show_autoconfig\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tInput (Autoconfig) Connection Notifications\tDisplay an on-screen message when connecting/disconnecting input devices.\tOn-Screen Display\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnotification_show_autoconfig_fails\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tInput (Autoconfig) Failure Notifications\tDisplay an on-screen message when input devices could not be configured.\tOn-Screen Display\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnotification_show_cheats_applied\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tCheat Code Notifications\tDisplay an on-screen message when cheat codes are applied.\tOn-Screen Display\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnotification_show_patch_applied\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tPatch Notifications\tDisplay an on-screen message when soft-patching ROMs.\tOn-Screen Display\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnotification_show_remap_load\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tInput Remap Loaded Notifications\tDisplay an on-screen message when loading input remap files.\tOn-Screen Display\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnotification_show_config_override_load\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tConfig Override Loaded Notifications\tDisplay an on-screen message when loading configuration override files.\tOn-Screen Display\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnotification_show_set_initial_disk\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tInitial Disc Restored Notifications\tDisplay an on-screen message when automatically restoring at launch the last used disc of multi-disc content loaded via M3U playlists.\tOn-Screen Display\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnotification_show_disk_control\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tDisc Control Notifications\tDisplay an on-screen message when inserting and ejecting discs.\tOn-Screen Display\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnotification_show_save_state\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tSave State Notifications\tDisplay an on-screen message when saving and loading save states.\tOn-Screen Display\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnotification_show_fast_forward\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tFast-Forward Notifications\tDisplay an on-screen indicator when fast-forwarding content.\tOn-Screen Display\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnotification_show_screenshot\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tScreenshot Notifications\tDisplay an on-screen message when taking a screenshot.\tOn-Screen Display\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnotification_show_refresh_rate\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tRefresh Rate Notifications\tDisplay an on-screen message when setting the refresh rate.\tOn-Screen Display\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnotification_show_netplay_extra\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tExtra Netplay Notifications\tDisplay non-essential netplay on-screen messages.\tOn-Screen Display\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnotification_show_when_menu_is_alive\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tMenu-only Notifications\tDisplay notifications only when menu is open.\tOn-Screen Display\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_unified_controls\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tUnified Menu Controls\tUse the same controls for both the menu and the game. Applies to the keyboard.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_disable_info_button\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tDisable Info Button\tPrevent menu info function.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_disable_search_button\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tDisable Search Button\tPrevent menu search function.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_disable_left_analog\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tDisable Left Analog in Menu\tPrevent menu left analog stick input.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_disable_right_analog\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tDisable Right Analog in Menu\tPrevent menu right analog stick input. Right analog stick cycles thumbnails in playlists.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_linear_filter\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tLinear Filter\tAdds a slight blur to the menu to soften hard pixel edges.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_horizontal_animation\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tHorizontal Animation\tEnable horizontal animation for the menu. This will have a performance hit.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_pause_libretro\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tPause Content When Menu Is Active\tPause the content if the menu is active.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_savestate_resume\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tResume Content After Using Save States\tAutomatically close the menu and resume content after saving or loading a state. Disabling this can improve save state performance on very slow devices.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_insert_disk_resume\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tResume Content After Changing Discs\tAutomatically close the menu and resume content after inserting or loading a new disc.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_mouse_enable\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tMouse Support\tAllow the menu to be controlled with a mouse.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_pointer_enable\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tTouch Support\tAllow the menu to be controlled with a touchscreen.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_timedate_enable\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow Date and Time\tShow current date and/or time inside the menu.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_battery_level_enable\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow Battery Level\tShow current battery level inside the menu.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_core_enable\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow Core Name\tShow current core name inside menu.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_show_sublabels\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow Menu Sub-Labels\tShow additional information for menu items.\tAppearance\n",
