OOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow 'Download Thumbnails'\tShow the 'Download Thumbnails' option when content is not running.\tUser Interface\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcontent_show_settings\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow 'Settings'\tShow the 'Settings' menu.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcontent_show_favorites\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow 'Favorites'\tShow the 'Favorites' menu.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcontent_show_favorites_first\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0\tShow Favorites First\tShow 'Favorites' before 'History'.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcontent_show_images\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow 'Images'\tShow the 'Images' menu.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcontent_show_music\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow 'Music'\tShow the 'Music' menu.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcontent_show_video\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow 'Videos'\tShow the 'Videos' menu.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcontent_show_netplay\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow 'Netplay'\tShow the 'Netplay' menu.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcontent_show_history\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow 'History'\tShow the recent history menu.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcontent_show_playlists\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow 'Playlists'\tShow the playlists in Main Menu. Ignored in GLUI if playlist tabs and navbar are enabled.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcontent_show_playlist_tabs\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow Playlist Tabs\tShow the playlist tabs. Does not affect RGUI. Navbar must be enabled in GLUI.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcontent_show_explore\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow 'Explore'\tShow the content explorer option.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_show_load_core\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow 'Load Core'\tShow the 'Load Core' option in the Main Menu.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_show_load_content\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow 'Load Content'\tShow the 'Load Content' option in the Main Menu.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_show_load_disc\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow 'Load Disc'\tShow the 'Load Disc' option in the Main Menu.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_show_dump_disc\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow 'Dump Disc'\tShow the 'Dump Disc' option in the Main Menu.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_show_eject_disc\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow 'Eject Disc'\tShow the 'Eject Disc' option in the Main Menu.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_show_information\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow 'Information'\tShow the 'Information' option in the Main Menu.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_show_configurations\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow 'Configuration File'\tShow the 'Configuration File' option in the Main Menu.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_show_latency\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow 'Latency'\tShow the 'Latency' option.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_show_rewind\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow 'Rewind'\tShow the 'Rewind' option.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_show_overlays\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow 'On-Screen Overlay'\tShow the 'On-Screen Overlay' option.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_show_help\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow 'Help'\tShow the 'Help' option in the Main Menu.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_show_quit_retroarch\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow 'Restart RetroArch'\tShow the 'Quit RetroArch' option in the Main Menu.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_show_restart_retroarch\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow 'Restart RetroArch'\tShow the 'Restart RetroArch' option in the Main Menu.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_show_reboot\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow 'Reboot'\tShow the 'Reboot' option.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_show_shutdown\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow 'Shutdown'\tShow the 'Shutdown' option.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_show_online_updater\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow 'Online Updater'\tShow the 'Online Updater' option in the Main Menu.\tUser Interface\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_show_core_updater\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow 'Core Downloader'\tShow the ability to update cores (and core info files) in the 'Online Updater' option.\tUser Interface\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_show_legacy_thumbnail_updater\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_show_core_manager_steam\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow 'Manage cores'\tShow the 'Manage cores' option in the Main Menu.\tUser Interface\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tfilter_by_current_core\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tFilter by Current Core\tFilter files being shown in File Browser by current core.\tFile Browser\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_use_preferred_system_color_theme\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tUse Preferred System Color Theme\tUse operating system's color theme (if any). Overrides theme settings.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_navigation_wraparound_enable\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tNavigation Wrap-Around\tWrap-around to beginning and/or end if boundary of list is reached horizontally or vertically.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_navigation_browser_filter_supported_extensions_enable\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tFilter Unknown Extensions\tFilter files being shown in File Browser by supported extensions.\tFile Browser\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_show_advanced_settings\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow Advanced Settings\tShow advanced settings for power users.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_thumbnail_background_enable\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0\tThumbnail Backgrounds\tEnables padding of unused space in thumbnail images with a solid background. This ensures a uniform display size for all images, improving menu appearance when viewing mixed content thumbnails with varying base dimensions.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmaterialui_icons_enable\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tIcons\tShow icons to the left of the menu entries.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmaterialui_switch_icons\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tSwitch Icons\tUse icons instead of ON/OFF text to represent 'toggle switch' menu settings entries.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmaterialui_playlist_icons_enable\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tPlaylist Icons (Restart required)\tShow system-specific icons in the playlists.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmaterialui_show_nav_bar\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow Navigation Bar\tDisplay permanent on-screen menu navigation shortcuts. Enables fast switching between menu categories. Recommended for touchscreen devices.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmaterialui_auto_rotate_nav_bar\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tAutomatically Rotate Navigation Bar\tAutomatically move the navigation bar to the right hand side of the screen when using landscape display orientations.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmaterialui_dual_thumbnail_list_view_enable\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow Secondary Thumbnail In List Views\tDisplays a secondary thumbnail when using 'List'-type playlist thumbnail view modes. This setting only applies when the screen has sufficient physical width to show two thumbnails.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmaterialui_thumbnail_background_enable\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tThumbnail Backgrounds\tEnables padding of unused space in thumbnail images with a solid background. This ensures a uniform display size for all images, improving menu appearance when viewing mixed content thumbnails with varying base dimensions.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\trgui_show_start_screen\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\trgui_background_filler_thickness_enable\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tBackground Filler Thickness\tIncrease coarseness of menu background checkerboard pattern.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\trgui_border_filler_thickness_enable\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tBorder Filler Thickness\tIncrease coarseness of menu border checkerboard.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\trgui_border_filler_enable\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tBorder Filler\tDisplay menu border.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_rgui_transparency\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tTransparency\tEnable background display of content while Quick Menu is active. Disabling transparency may alter theme colors.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_rgui_shadows\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShadow Effects\tEnable drop shadows for menu text, borders and thumbnails. Has a modest performance impact.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_rgui_full_width_layout\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tUse Full-Width Layout\tResize and position menu entries to make best use of available screen space. Disable this to use classic fixed-width two column layout.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\trgui_inline_thumbnails\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow Playlist Thumbnails\tEnable display of inline downscaled thumbnails while viewing playlists. Toggleable with RetroPad Select. When disabled, thumbnails can still be toggled fullscreen with RetroPad Start.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\trgui_swap_thumbnails\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tSwap Thumbnails\tSwaps the display positions of 'Top Thumbnail' and 'Bottom Thumbnail'.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\trgui_extended_ascii\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tExtended ASCII Support\tEnable display of non-standard ASCII characters. Required for compatibility with certain non-English Western languages. Has a moderate performance impact.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\trgui_switch_icons\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tSwitch Icons\tUse icons instead of ON/OFF text to represent 'toggle switch' menu settings entries.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\trgui_particle_effect_screensaver\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tScreensaver Background Animation\tDisplay background particle animation effect while menu screensaver is active.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\txmb_shadows_enable\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShadow Effects\tDraw drop shadows for icons, thumbnails and letters. This will have a minor performance hit.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\txmb_switch_icons\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tSwitch Icons\tUse icons instead of ON/OFF text to represent 'toggle switch' menu settings entries.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\txmb_vertical_thumbnails\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tThumbnail Vertical Disposition\tDisplay the left thumbnail under the right one, on the right side of the screen.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_xmb_show_title_header\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow Title Header\t\u0001\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tozone_collapse_sidebar\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tCollapse the Sidebar\tHave the left sidebar always collapsed.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tozone_scroll_content_metadata\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tUse Ticker Text for Content Metadata\tWhen enabled, each item of content metadata shown on the right sidebar of playlists (associated core, play time) will occupy a single line; strings exceeding the width of the sidebar will be displayed as scrolling ticker text. When disabled, each item of content metadata will be displayed statically, wrapped to occupy as many lines as required.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tozone_truncate_playlist_name\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tTruncate Playlist Names (Restart required)\tRemove the manufacturer names from the playlists. For example, 'Sony - PlayStation' becomes 'PlayStation'.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tozone_sort_after_truncate_playlist_name\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tSort Playlists After Name Truncation (Restart required)\tPlaylists will be re-sorted in alphabetical order after removing the manufacturer component of their names.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcheevos_enable\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tAchievements\tEarn achievements in classic games. For more information, visit 'https://retroachievements.org'.\tRetroAchievements\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcheevos_test_unofficial\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tTest Unofficial Achievements\tUse unofficial achievements and/or beta features for testing purposes.\tRetroAchievements\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcheevos_hardcore_mode_enable\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tHardcore Mode\tDisables cheats, rewind, slow-motion, and loading save states. Achievements earned in hardcore mode are uniquely marked so that you can show others what you've achieved without emulator assistance features. Toggling this setting at runtime will restart the game.\tRetroAchievements\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcheevos_challenge_indicators\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tActive Challenge Indicators\tShows on-screen indicators while certain achievements can be earned.\tVisibility\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcheevos_richpresence_enable\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tRich Presence\tPeriodically sends contextual game information to the RetroAchievements website. Has no effect if 'Hardcore Mode' is enabled.\tRetroAchievements\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcheevos_unlock_sound_enable\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tUnlock Sound\tPlay a sound when an achievement is unlocked.\tRetroAchievements\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcheevos_verbose_enable\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tVerbose Messages\tShows additional diagnostic and error messages.\tVisibility\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcheevos_auto_screenshot\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tAutomatic Screenshot\tAutomatically take a screenshot when an achievement is earned.\tRetroAchievements\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcheevos_badges_enable\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tAchievement Badges\tDisplay badges in the Achievement List.\tRetroAchievements\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcheevos_start_active\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\tStart the session with all achievements active (even the ones previously unlocked).\tRetroAchievements\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcheevos_appearance_padding_auto\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tAligned Padding\tSet whether achievement notifications should align with other types of on-screen notifications. Disable to set manual padding/position values.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcheevos_visibility_unlock\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tUnlock Notifications\tShows a notification when an achievement is unlocked.\tVisibility\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcheevos_visibility_mastery\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tMastery Notifications\tShows a notification when all achievements for a game are unlocked.\tVisibility\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcheevos_visibility_account\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tLogin Messages\tShows messages related to RetroAchievements account login.\tVisibility\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcheevos_visibility_lboard_start\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tLeaderboard Start Messages\tShows a description of a leaderboard when it becomes active.\tVisibility\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcheevos_visibility_lboard_submit\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tLeaderboard Submit Messages\tShows a message with the value being submitted when a leaderboard attempt is completed.\tVisibility\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcheevos_visibility_lboard_cancel\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tLeaderboard Failed Messages\tShows a message when a leaderboard attempt fails.\tVisibility\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcheevos_visibility_lboard_trackers\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tLeaderboard Trackers\tShows trackers on the screen with the current value of active leaderboards.\tVisibility\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcheevos_visibility_progress_tracker\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tProgress Indicator\tShows an on-screen indicator when progress is made towards certain achievements.\tVisibility\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_overlay_enable\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tDisplay Overlay\tOverlays are used for borders and on-screen controls.\tOn-Screen Overlay\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_overlay_enable_autopreferred\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tAutoload Preferred Overlay\tPrefer loading overlays based on system name before falling back to the default preset. Will be ignored if an override is set for the overlay preset.\tOn-Screen Overlay\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_overlay_behind_menu\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow Overlay Behind Menu\tShow the overlay behind instead of in front of the menu.\tOn-Screen Overlay\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_overlay_hide_in_menu\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tHide Overlay in Menu\tHide the overlay while inside the menu, and show it again when exiting the menu.\tOn-Screen Overlay\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_overlay_hide_when_gamepad_connected\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tHide Overlay When Controller Is Connected\tHide the overlay when a physical controller is connected in port 1, and show it again when the controller is disconnected.\tOn-Screen Overlay\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_overlay_show_mouse_cursor\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow Mouse Cursor With Overlay\tShow the mouse cursor when using an on-screen overlay.\tOn-Screen Overlay\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_overlay_auto_rotate\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tAuto-Rotate Overlay\tIf supported by current overlay, automatically rotate layout to match screen orientation/aspect ratio.\tOn-Screen Overlay\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_overlay_auto_scale\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tAuto-Scale Overlay\tAutomatically adjust overlay scale and UI element spacing to match screen aspect ratio. Produces best results with controller overlays.\tOn-Screen Overlay\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_osk_overlay_auto_scale\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tAuto-Scale Keyboard Overlay\tAdjust keyboard overlay to its original aspect ratio. Disable to stretch to screen.\tKeyboard Overlay\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_overlay_pointer_enable\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tEnable Overlay Lightgun, Mouse, and Pointer\tUse any touch inputs not pressing overlay controls to create pointing device input for the core.\tOn-Screen Overlay\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_overlay_lightgun_trigger_on_touch\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tTrigger on Touch\tSend trigger input with pointer input.\tOverlay Lightgun\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_overlay_lightgun_allow_offscreen\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tAllow Off-Screen\tAllow out-of-bounds aiming. Disable to clamp off-screen aim to the in-bounds edge.\tOverlay Lightgun\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_overlay_mouse_hold_to_drag\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tLong Press to Drag\tLong press the screen to begin holding a button.\tOverlay Mouse\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_overlay_mouse_dtap_to_drag\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tDouble Tap to Drag\tDouble tap the screen to begin holding a button on the second tap. Adds latency to mouse clicks.\tOverlay Mouse\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_touch_vmouse_pointer\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tTouch VMouse as Pointer\tEnable to pass touch events from the input touchscreen.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_touch_vmouse_mouse\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tTouch VMouse as Mouse\tEnable virtual mouse emulation using input touch events.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_touch_vmouse_touchpad\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tTouch VMouse Touchpad Mode\tEnable along with Mouse to utilize use the touch screen as a touchpad.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_touch_vmouse_trackball\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tTouch VMouse Trackball Mode\tEnable along with Mouse to utilize use the touch screen as a trackball, adding inertia to the pointer.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_touch_vmouse_gesture\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tTouch VMouse Gestures\tEnable touchscreen gestures, including tapping, tap-dragging, and finger swiping.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_backtouch_enable\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tTouch\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_backtouch_toggle\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tPrefer Front Touch\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tsmall_keyboard_enable\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tSmall Keyboard\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tkeyboard_gamepad_enable\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tKeyboard Controller Mapping\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_autodetect_enable\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tAutoconfig\tAutomatically configures controllers that have a profile, Plug-and-Play style.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_turbo_enable\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tTurbo Fire\tDisabled stops all turbo fire operations.\tTurbo Fire\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_turbo_allow_dpad\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tTurbo Allow D-Pad Directions\tIf enabled, digital directional inputs (also known as d-pad or 'hatswitch') can be turbo.\tTurbo Fire\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_auto_mouse_grab\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tAutomatic Mouse Grab\tEnable mouse grab on application focus.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_remap_binds_enable\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tRemap Controls for This Core\tOverride the input binds with the remapped binds set for the current core.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_remap_sort_by_controller_enable\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tSort Remaps By Gamepad\tRemaps will only apply to the active gamepad in which they were saved.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_hotkey_device_merge\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tHotkey Device Type Merge\tBlock all hotkeys from both keyboard and controller device types if either type has 'Hotkey Enable' set.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_hotkey_follows_player1\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0\tHotkeys Follow Player 1\tHotkeys are bound to core port 1, even if core port 1 is remapped to a different user. Note: keyboard hotkeys will not work if core port 1 is remapped to any user > 1 (keyboard input is from user 1).\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tall_users_control_menu\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tAll Users Control Menu\tAllow any user to control the menu. If disabled, only User 1 can control the menu.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_swap_ok_cancel_buttons\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tMenu Swap OK and Cancel Buttons\tSwap buttons for OK/Cancel. Disabled is the Japanese button orientation, enabled is the western orientation.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_swap_scroll_buttons\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tMenu Swap Scroll Buttons\tSwap buttons for scrolling. Disabled scrolls 10 items with L/R and alphabetically with L2/R2.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_singleclick_playlists\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0\tSingle-Click Playlists\tSkip 'Run' menu when launching playlist entries. Press D-Pad while holding OK to access 'Run' menu.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_allow_tabs_back\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0\tAllow Back From Tabs\tReturn to Main Menu from tabs/sidebar when pressing Back.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_nowinkey_enable\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tDisable Windows Hotkeys (Restart required)\tKeep Win-key combinations inside the application.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_sensors_enable\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tAuxiliary Sensor Input\tEnable input from accelerometer, gyroscope and illuminance sensors, if supported by the current hardware. May have a performance impact and/or increase power drain on some platforms.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvibrate_on_keypress\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tVibrate on Key Press\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tenable_device_vibration\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tEnable Device Vibration (For Supported Cores)\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tsustained_performance_mode\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tSustained Performance Mode\t\u0001\tPower Management\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcontent_runtime_log\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tSave Runtime Log (Per Core)\tKeep track of how long each item of content has run for, with records separated by core.\tSaving\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcontent_runtime_log_aggregate\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tSave Runtime Log (Aggregate)\tKeep track of how long each item of content has run for, recorded as the aggregate total across all cores.\tSaving\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\thistory_list_enable\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tHistory\tMaintain a playlist of recently used games, images, music, and videos.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tplaylist_entry_rename\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tAllow to Rename Entries\tAllow playlist entries to be renamed.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tplaylist_use_old_format\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tSave Playlists Using Old Format\tWrite playlists using depreciated plain-text format. When disabled, playlists are formatted using JSON.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tplaylist_compression\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tCompress Playlists\tArchive playlist data when writing to disk. Reduces file size and loading times at the expense of (negligibly) increased CPU usage. May be used with either old or new format playlists.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tplaylist_show_sublabels\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow Playlist Sub-Labels\tShow additional information for each playlist entry, such as current core association and runtime (if available). Has a variable performance impact.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tplaylist_show_entry_idx\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow Playlist Entry Index\tShow entry numbers when viewing playlists. Display format is dependent upon the currently selected menu driver.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tplaylist_sort_alphabetical\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tSort Playlists Alphabetically\tSort content playlists in alphabetical order, excluding the 'History', 'Images', 'Music' and 'Videos' playlists.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tplaylist_fuzzy_archive_match\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tFuzzy Archive Matching\tWhen searching playlists for entries associated with compressed files, match only the archive file name instead of [file name]+[content]. Enable this to avoid duplicate content history entries when loading compressed files.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tplaylist_portable_paths\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tPortable Playlists\tWhen enabled, and 'File Browser' directory is also selected, the current value of parameter 'File Browser' is saved in the playlist. When the playlist is loaded on another system where the same option is enabled, the value of parameter 'File Browser' is compared with the playlist value; if different, the playlist entries' paths are automatically fixed.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tplaylist_use_filename\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tUse Filenames for Thumbnail Matching\tWhen enabled, will find thumbnails by the entry's filename, rather than its label.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tplaylist_allow_non_png\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tAllow All Supported Image Types for Thumbnails\tWhen enabled, local thumbnails can be added in all image types supported by RetroArch (such as jpeg). May have a minor performance impact.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tframe_time_counter_reset_after_fastforwarding\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tReset After Fast-Forward\tReset the frame time counter after fast-forwarding.\tFrame Time Counter\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tframe_time_counter_reset_after_load_state\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tReset After Load State\tReset the frame time counter after loading a state.\tFrame Time Counter\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tframe_time_counter_reset_after_save_state\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tReset After Save State\tReset the frame time counter after saving a state.\tFrame Time Counter\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnetwork_cmd_enable\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tNetwork Commands\t\u0001\tNetwork\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tstdin_cmd_enable\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tstdin Commands\tstdin command interface.\tNetwork\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnetplay_show_only_connectable\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tOnly Connectable Rooms\t\u0001\tNetwork\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnetplay_show_only_installed_cores\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tOnly Installed Cores\t\u0001\tNetwork\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnetplay_show_passworded\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tPassworded Rooms\t\u0001\tNetwork\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnetplay_public_announce\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tPublicly Announce Netplay\tWhether to announce netplay games publicly. If unset, clients must manually connect rather than using the public lobby.\tNetwork\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnetplay_start_as_spectator\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tNetplay Spectator Mode\tStart netplay in spectator mode.\tNetwork\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnetplay_nat_traversal\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tNetplay NAT Traversal\tWhen hosting, attempt to listen for connections from the public Internet, using UPnP or similar technologies to escape LANs.\tNetwork\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnetplay_fade_chat\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tFade Chat\tFade chat messages over time.\tNetwork\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnetplay_allow_pausing\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tAllow Pausing\tAllow players to pause during netplay.\tNetwork\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnetplay_allow_slaves\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tAllow Slave-Mode Clients\tAllow connections in slave mode. Slave-mode clients require very little processing power on either side, but will suffer significantly from network latency.\tNetwork\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnetplay_require_slaves\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tDisallow Non-Slave-Mode Clients\tDisallow connections not in slave mode. Not recommended except for very fast networks with very weak machines.\tNetwork\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnetplay_use_mitm_server\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tUse Relay Server\tForward netplay connections through a man-in-the-middle server. Useful if the host is behind a firewall or has NAT/UPnP problems.\tNetwork\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnetplay_request_device_p1\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnetplay_request_device_p2\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnetplay_request_device_p3\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnetplay_request_device_p4\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnetplay_request_device_p5\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnetplay_request_device_p6\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnetplay_request_device_p7\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnetplay_request_device_p8\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnetplay_request_device_p9\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnetplay_request_device_p10\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnetplay_request_device_p11\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnetplay_request_device_p12\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnetplay_request_device_p13\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\n",
    "retroarch\t\u0001\t\tnetplay_request_device_p14\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnetplay_request_device_p15\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnetplay_request_device_p16\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnetplay_ping_show\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tDisplay Netplay Ping\tDisplay the ping for the current netplay room.\tOn-Screen Display\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnetwork_on_demand_thumbnails\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tOn-Demand Thumbnail Downloads\tAutomatically download missing thumbnails while browsing playlists. Has a severe performance impact.\tNetwork\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnetwork_remote_enable\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tNetwork RetroPad\t\u0001\tNetwork\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\treplay_checkpoint_deserialize\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0\tReplay Checkpoint Deserialize\tWhether to deserialize checkpoints stored in replays during regular playback.\tSaving\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tandroid_input_disconnect_workaround\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tAndroid disconnect workaround\tWorkaround for controllers disconnecting and reconnecting. Impedes 2 players with the identical controllers.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnew3ds_speedup_enable\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tEnable New3DS Clock / L2 Cache\tEnable New3DS clock speed (804MHz) and L2 cache.\tUser Interface\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_3ds_lcd_bottom\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t3DS Bottom Screen\tEnable display of status information on bottom screen. Disable to increase battery life and improve performance.\tUser Interface\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tbottom_font_enable\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tFont Enable\tDisplay bottom menu font. Enable to display button descriptions on the bottom screen. This excludes the save state date.\tUser Interface\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_wiiu_prefer_drc\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tOptimize for Wii U GamePad (Restart required)\tUse an exact 2x scale of the GamePad as the viewport. Disable to display at the native TV resolution.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tgcdwebserver_alert\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tquick_menu_show_game_ai\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow 'Game AI'\tShow the 'Game AI' option.\tUser\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_scale_factor\tFLOAT\t\u0001\t\u0001\t5\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tScale Factor\tScale the size of user interface elements in the menu.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_widget_scale_factor\tFLOAT\t1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tGraphics Widgets Scale Override\tApply a manual scaling factor override when drawing display widgets. Only applies when 'Scale Graphics Widgets Automatically' is disabled. Can be used to increase or decrease the size of decorated notifications, indicators and controls independently from the menu itself.\tOn-Screen Display\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_widget_scale_factor_windowed\tFLOAT\t1.0\t\u0001\t5\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tGraphics Widgets Scale Override (Windowed)\tApply a manual scaling factor override when drawing display widgets in windowed mode. Only applies when 'Scale Graphics Widgets Automatically' is disabled. Can be used to increase or decrease the size of decorated notifications, indicators and controls independently from the menu itself.\tOn-Screen Display\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_wallpaper_opacity\tFLOAT\t0.900\t0\t1\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tBackground Opacity\tModify the opacity of the background image.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_framebuffer_opacity\tFLOAT\t0.900\t0\t1\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tOpacity\tModify the opacity of the default menu background.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_footer_opacity\tFLOAT\t1.000\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_header_opacity\tFLOAT\t1.000\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_ticker_speed\tFLOAT\t2.0\t\u0001\t10\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tTicker Text Speed\tThe animation speed when scrolling long menu text.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\trgui_particle_effect_speed\tFLOAT\t1.0\t\u0001\t10\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tBackground Animation Speed\tAdjust speed of background particle animation effects.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_screensaver_animation_speed\tFLOAT\t1.0\t\u0001\t10\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tMenu Screensaver Animation Speed\tAdjust speed of menu screensaver animation effect.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tozone_thumbnail_scale_factor\tFLOAT\t1.0\t1\t2\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tThumbnail Scale Factor\tScale the size of the thumbnail bar.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tozone_padding_factor\tFLOAT\t1.0\t0\t2\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0\tPadding Factor\tScale the horizontal padding size.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tozone_font_scale_factor_global\tFLOAT\t1.0\t0\t3\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0\tFont Scale Factor\tScale the font size linearly across the menu.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tozone_font_scale_factor_title\tFLOAT\t1.0\t0\t3\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0\tTitle Font Scale Factor\tScale the font size for the title text in the menu header.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tozone_font_scale_factor_sidebar\tFLOAT\t1.0\t0\t3\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0\tLeft Sidebar Font Scale Factor\tScale the font size for the text in the left sidebar.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tozone_font_scale_factor_label\tFLOAT\t1.0\t0\t3\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0\tLabels Font Scale Factor\tScale the font size for the labels of menu options and playlist entries. Also affects text size in the help boxes.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tozone_font_scale_factor_sublabel\tFLOAT\t1.0\t0\t3\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0\tSublabels Font Scale Factor\tScale the font size for the sublabels of menu options and playlist entries.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tozone_font_scale_factor_time\tFLOAT\t1.0\t0\t3\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0\tTimedate Font Scale Factor\tScale the font size of the time and date indicator in the top-right corner of the menu.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tozone_font_scale_factor_footer\tFLOAT\t1.0\t0\t3\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0\tFooter Font Scale Factor\tScale the font size of the text in the menu footer. Also affects text size in the right thumbnail sidebar.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcheevos_appearance_padding_h\tFLOAT\t0.0\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tManual Horizontal Padding\tDistance from left/right screen edge, which can compensate for display overscan.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcheevos_appearance_padding_v\tFLOAT\t0.0\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tManual Vertical Padding\tDistance from top/bottom screen edge, which can compensate for display overscan.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tfastforward_ratio\tFLOAT\t0.0\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tFast-Forward Rate\tThe maximum rate at which content will be run when using fast-forward (e.g., 5.0x for 60 fps content = 300 fps cap). If set to 0.0x, fast-forward ratio is unlimited (no FPS cap).\tFrame Throttle\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tslowmotion_ratio\tFLOAT\t3.0\t1\t10\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tSlow-Motion Rate\tThe rate that content will play when using slow-motion.\tFrame Throttle\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\taudio_rate_control_delta\tFLOAT\t0.005\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tDynamic Audio Rate Control\tHelps smooth out imperfections in timing when synchronizing audio and video. Be aware that if disabled, proper synchronization is nearly impossible to obtain.\tAudio\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\taudio_max_timing_skew\tFLOAT\t0.05\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tMaximum Timing Skew\tThe maximum change in audio input rate. Increasing this enables very large changes in timing at the cost of an inaccurate audio pitch (e.g. running PAL cores on NTSC displays).\tAudio\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\taudio_volume\tFLOAT\t0.0\t-80\t12\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tVolume Gain (dB)\tAudio volume (in dB). 0 dB is normal volume, and no gain is applied.\tAudio\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\taudio_mixer_volume\tFLOAT\t0.0\t-80\t12\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tMixer Volume Gain (dB)\tGlobal audio mixer volume (in dB). 0 dB is normal volume, and no gain is applied.\tAudio\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_aspect_ratio\tFLOAT\t\u0001\t\u0001\t16\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tConfig Aspect Ratio\tFloating point value for video aspect ratio (width / height).\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_viewport_bias_x\tFLOAT\t0.5\t0\t1\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tViewport Anchor Bias X\tHorizontal position of content when viewport is wider than content width. 0.0 is far left, 0.5 is center, 1.0 is far right.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_viewport_bias_y\tFLOAT\t0.5\t0\t1\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tViewport Anchor Bias Y\tVertical position of content when viewport is taller than content height. 0.0 is top, 0.5 is center, 1.0 is bottom.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_viewport_bias_portrait_x\tFLOAT\t0.5\t0\t1\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tViewport Anchor Bias X (Portrait Orientation)\tHorizontal position of content when viewport is wider than content width. 0.0 is far left, 0.5 is center, 1.0 is far right. (Portrait Orientation)\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_viewport_bias_portrait_y\tFLOAT\t0.0\t0\t1\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tViewport Anchor Bias Y (Portrait Orientation)\tVertical position of content when viewport is taller than content height. 0.0 is top, 0.5 is center, 1.0 is bottom. (Portrait Orientation)\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_refresh_rate\tFLOAT\t\u0001\t0\t0\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tVertical Refresh Rate\tVertical refresh rate of your screen. Used to calculate a suitable audio input rate. This will be ignored if 'Threaded Video' is enabled.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_autoswitch_pal_threshold\tFLOAT\t54.50\t50\t56\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tAutomatic Refresh Rate PAL Threshold\tMaximum refresh rate to be considered PAL.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcrt_video_refresh_rate\tFLOAT\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_message_pos_x\tFLOAT\t0.05\t0\t1\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tNotification Position (Horizontal)\tSpecify custom X axis position for on-screen text. 0 is left edge.\tOn-Screen Display\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_message_pos_y\tFLOAT\t0.05\t0\t1\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tNotification Position (Vertical)\tSpecify custom Y axis position for on-screen text. 0 is bottom edge.\tOn-Screen Display\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_font_size\tFLOAT\t\u0001\t1\t100\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tNotification Size\tSpecify the font size in points. When widgets are used, this size has effect only to on-screen statistics display.\tOn-Screen Display\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_msg_bgcolor_opacity\tFLOAT\t1.0\t0\t1\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tNotification Background Opacity\tSets the opacity of the OSD background color. Valid values are between 0.0 and 1.0.\tOn-Screen Display\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_hdr_max_nits\tFLOAT\t1000.0\t0\t10000\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tPeak Luminance\tSet the peak luminance (in cd/m2) your display can reproduce. See RTings for your display's peak luminance.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_hdr_paper_white_nits\tFLOAT\t200.0\t0\t10000\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tPaper White Luminance\tSet the luminance at which paper white should be i.e. readable text or luminance at the top of the SDR (Standard Dynamic Range) range. Useful for adjusting to different lighting conditions in your environment.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_hdr_display_contrast\tFLOAT\t5.0\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tContrast\tGamma/contrast control for HDR. Takes the colors and increases the overall range between the brightest parts and the darkest parts of the image. The higher HDR Contrast is, the larger this difference becomes, while the lower the contrast is, the more washed out the image becomes. Helps users tune the image to their liking and what they feel looks best on their display.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_axis_threshold\tFLOAT\t0.5\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tInput Button Axis Threshold\tHow far an axis must be tilted to result in a button press when using 'Analog to Digital'.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_analog_deadzone\tFLOAT\t0.0\t0\t1\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tAnalog Deadzone\tIgnore analog stick movements below deadzone value.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_analog_sensitivity\tFLOAT\t1.0\t-5\t5\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tAnalog Sensitivity\tAdjust the sensitivity of analog sticks.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_sensor_accelerometer_sensitivity\tFLOAT\t1.0\t-5\t5\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0\tAccelerometer Sensitivity\tAdjust the sensitivity of the Accelerometer.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_sensor_gyroscope_sensitivity\tFLOAT\t1.0\t-5\t5\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0\tGyroscope Sensitivity\tAdjust the sensitivity of the Gyroscope.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_overlay_opacity\tFLOAT\t\u0001\t0\t1\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tOverlay Opacity\tOpacity of all UI elements of the overlay.\tOn-Screen Overlay\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_osk_overlay_opacity\tFLOAT\t\u0001\t0\t1\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tKeyboard Overlay Opacity\tOpacity of all UI elements of the keyboard overlay.\tKeyboard Overlay\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_overlay_scale_landscape\tFLOAT\t1.0\t0\t2\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t(Landscape) Overlay Scale\tScale of all UI elements of the overlay when using landscape display orientations.\tOn-Screen Overlay\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_overlay_aspect_adjust_landscape\tFLOAT\t0.0\t-2\t2\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t(Landscape) Overlay Aspect Adjustment\tApply an aspect ratio correction factor to the overlay when using landscape display orientations. Positive values increase (while negative values decrease) effective overlay width.\tOn-Screen Overlay\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_overlay_x_separation_landscape\tFLOAT\t0.0\t-2\t2\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t(Landscape) Overlay Horizontal Separation\tIf supported by current preset, adjust the spacing between UI elements in the left and right halves of an overlay when using landscape display orientations. Positive values increase (while negative values decrease) the separation of the two halves.\tOn-Screen Overlay\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_overlay_y_separation_landscape\tFLOAT\t0.0\t-2\t2\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t(Landscape) Overlay Vertical Separation\tIf supported by current preset, adjust the spacing between UI elements in the top and bottom halves of an overlay when using landscape display orientations. Positive values increase (while negative values decrease) the separation of the two halves.\tOn-Screen Overlay\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_overlay_x_offset_landscape\tFLOAT\t0.0\t-1\t1\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t(Landscape) Overlay X Offset\tHorizontal overlay offset when using landscape display orientations. Positive values shift overlay to the right; negative values to the left.\tOn-Screen Overlay\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_overlay_y_offset_landscape\tFLOAT\t0.0\t-1\t1\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t(Landscape) Overlay Y Offset\tVertical overlay offset when using landscape display orientations. Positive values shift overlay upwards; negative values downwards.\tOn-Screen Overlay\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_overlay_scale_portrait\tFLOAT\t1.0\t0\t2\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t(Portrait) Overlay Scale\tScale of all UI elements of the overlay when using portrait display orientations.\tOn-Screen Overlay\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_overlay_aspect_adjust_portrait\tFLOAT\t0.0\t-2\t2\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t(Portrait) Overlay Aspect Adjustment\tApply an aspect ratio correction factor to the overlay when using portrait display orientations. Positive values increase (while negative values decrease) effective overlay height.\tOn-Screen Overlay\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_overlay_x_separation_portrait\tFLOAT\t0.0\t-2\t2\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t(Portrait) Overlay Horizontal Separation\tIf supported by current preset, adjust the spacing between UI elements in the left and right halves of an overlay when using portrait display orientations. Positive values increase (while negative values decrease) the separation of the two halves.\tOn-Screen Overlay\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_overlay_y_separation_portrait\tFLOAT\t0.0\t-2\t2\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t(Portrait) Overlay Vertical Separation\tIf supported by current preset, adjust the spacing between UI elements in the top and bottom halves of an overlay when using portrait display orientations. Positive values increase (while negative values decrease) the separation of the two halves.\tOn-Screen Overlay\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_overlay_x_offset_portrait\tFLOAT\t0.0\t-1\t1\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t(Portrait) Overlay X Offset\tHorizontal overlay offset when using portrait display orientations. Positive values shift overlay to the right; negative values to the left.\tOn-Screen Overlay\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_overlay_y_offset_portrait\tFLOAT\t0.0\t-1\t1\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t(Portrait) Overlay Y Offset\tVertical overlay offset when using portrait display orientations. Positive values shift overlay upwards; negative values downwards.\tOn-Screen Overlay\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_overlay_mouse_speed\tFLOAT\t1.0\t\u0001\t5\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tMouse Speed\tAdjust cursor movement speed.\tOverlay Mouse\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_overlay_mouse_swipe_threshold\tFLOAT\t1.0\t0\t10\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tSwipe Threshold\tAdjust the allowable drift range when detecting a long press or tap. Expressed as a percentage of the smaller screen dimension.\tOverlay Mouse\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tbottom_font_scale\tFLOAT\t1.48\t1\t2\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tFont Scale\tAdjust bottom screen font scale.\tUser Interface\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tfrontend_log_level\tINT\t1\t0\t3\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tFrontend Logging Level\tSet log level for the frontend. If a log level issued by the frontend is below this value, it is ignored.\tLogging\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tlibretro_log_level\tINT\t1\t0\t3\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tCore Logging Level\tSet log level for cores. If a log level issued by a core is below this value, it is ignored.\tLogging\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tfps_update_interval\tINT\t256\t1\t512\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tFramerate Update Interval (In Frames)\tFramerate display will be updated at the set interval in frames.\tOn-Screen Display\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmemory_update_interval\tINT\t256\t1\t512\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tMemory Usage Update Interval (In Frames)\tMemory usage display will be updated at the set interval in frames.\tOn-Screen Display\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcore_updater_auto_backup_history_size\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t500\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tCore Backup History Size\tSpecify how many automatically generated backups to keep for each installed core. When this limit is reached, creating a new backup via an online update will delete the oldest backup. Manual core backups are unaffected by this setting.\tCore Updater Settings\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tautosave_interval\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t0\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tSaveRAM Autosave Interval\tAutomatically save the non-volatile SaveRAM at a regular interval (in seconds).\tSaving\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\trewind_granularity\tINT\t\u0001\t1\t32768\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tRewind Frames\tThe number of frames to rewind per step. Higher values increase the rewind speed.\tRewind\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\trewind_buffer_size_step\tINT\t\u0001\t1\t100\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tRewind Buffer Size Step (MB)\tEach time the rewind buffer size value is increased or decreased, it will change by this amount.\tRewind\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\trun_ahead_frames\tINT\t1\t1\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tNumber of Frames to Run-Ahead\tThe number of frames to run ahead. Causes gameplay issues such as jitter if the number of lag frames internal to the game is exceeded.\tFrame Throttle\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\treplay_max_keep\tINT\t0\t0\t999\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tMaximum Auto-Increment Replays to Keep\tLimit the number of replays that will be created when 'Increment Replay Index Automatically' is enabled. If limit is exceeded when recording a new replay, the existing replay with the lowest index will be deleted. A value of '0' means unlimited replays will be recorded.\tSaving\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\treplay_checkpoint_interval\tINT\t0\t0\t0\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tReplay Checkpoint Interval\tAutomatically bookmark the game state during replay recording at a regular interval (in seconds).\tSaving\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tsavestate_max_keep\tINT\t0\t0\t999\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tMaximum Auto-Increment Save States to Keep\tLimit the number of save states that will be created when 'Increment Save State Index Automatically' is enabled. If limit is exceeded when saving a new state, the existing state with the lowest index will be deleted. A value of '0' means unlimited states will be recorded.\tSaving\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcontent_show_add_entry\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow 'Import Content'\tShow the 'Import Content' entry inside the Main Menu or Playlists.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcontent_show_contentless_cores\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow 'Contentless Cores'\tSpecify the type of core (if any) to show in the 'Contentless Cores' menu. When set to 'Custom', individual core visibility may be toggled via the 'Manage Cores' menu.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcontent_history_size\tINT\t200\t1\t9999\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tHistory Size\tLimit the number of entries in recent playlist for games, images, music, and videos.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tplaylist_entry_remove_enable\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tAllow to Remove Entries\tAllow playlist entries to be removed.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tplaylist_show_inline_core_name\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow Associated Cores in Playlists\tSpecify when to tag playlist entries with the currently associated core (if any). This setting is ignored when playlist sublabels are enabled.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tplaylist_show_history_icons\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow Content Specific Icons in History and Favorites\tShow specific icons for each history and favorites playlist entry. Has a variable performance impact.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tplaylist_sublabel_runtime_type\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tPlaylist Sub-Label Runtime\tSelect which type of runtime log record to display on playlist sublabels. The corresponding runtime log must be enabled via the 'Saving' options menu.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tplaylist_sublabel_last_played_style\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t'Last Played' Date and Time Style\tSet the style of the date and time displayed for 'Last Played' timestamp information. '(AM/PM)' options will have a small performance impact on some platforms.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tquit_on_close_content\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tQuit on Close Content\tAutomatically quit RetroArch when closing content. 'CLI' quits only when content is launched via command line.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_thumbnails\tINT\t3\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\tType of thumbnail to display.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_left_thumbnails\tINT\t0\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\tType of thumbnail to display at the left.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_icon_thumbnails\tINT\t0\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tIcon Thumbnail\tType of playlist icon thumbnail to display.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_thumbnail_upscale_threshold\tINT\t0\t0\t1024\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tThumbnail Upscaling Threshold\tAutomatically upscale thumbnail images with a width/height smaller than the specified value. Improves picture quality. Has a moderate performance impact.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_timedate_style\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tStyle of Date and Time\tChange the style current date and/or time is shown inside the menu.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_timedate_date_separator\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tDate Separator\tSpecify character to use as a separator between year/month/day components when current date is shown inside the menu.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_ticker_type\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tTicker Text Animation\tSelect horizontal scrolling method used to display long menu text.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_scroll_delay\tINT\t256\t1\t999\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tMenu Scroll Delay\tInitial delay in milliseconds when holding a direction to scroll.\tUser Interface\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_screensaver_timeout\tINT\t0\t0\t1800\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tMenu Screensaver Timeout\tWhile menu is active, a screensaver will be displayed after the specified period of inactivity.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_screensaver_animation\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tMenu Screensaver Animation\tEnable an animation effect while the menu screensaver is active. Has a modest performance impact.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_remember_selection\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tRemember Selection When Changing Tabs\tRemember previous cursor position in tabs. RGUI does not have tabs, but Playlists and Settings behave as such.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_startup_page\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0\tStartup Page\tInitial menu page on startup.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\trgui_menu_color_theme\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tColor Theme\tSelect a different color theme. Choosing 'Custom' enables the use of menu theme preset files.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\trgui_thumbnail_downscaler\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tThumbnail Downscaling Method\tResampling method used when shrinking large thumbnails to fit the display.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\trgui_thumbnail_delay\tINT\t0\t0\t1024\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tThumbnail Delay (ms)\tApplies a time delay between selecting a playlist entry and loading its associated thumbnails. Setting this to a value of at least 256 ms enables fast lag-free scrolling on even the slowest devices.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\trgui_internal_upscale_level\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tInternal Upscaling\tUpscale menu interface before drawing to screen. When used with 'Menu Linear Filter' enabled, removes scaling artifacts (uneven pixels) while maintaining a sharp image. Has a significant performance impact that increases with upscaling level.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\trgui_aspect_ratio\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tAspect Ratio\tSelect menu aspect ratio. Widescreen ratios increase the horizontal resolution of the menu interface. (May require a restart if 'Lock Menu Aspect Ratio' is disabled)\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\trgui_aspect_ratio_lock\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tLock Aspect Ratio\tEnsures that the menu is always displayed with the correct aspect ratio. If disabled, the quick menu will be stretched to match the currently loaded content.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\trgui_particle_effect\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tBackground Animation\tEnable background particle animation effect. Has a significant performance impact.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_xmb_animation_opening_main_menu\tINT\t0\t0\t3\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tAnimation Main Menu Opens/Closes\tThe animation that triggers when opening a submenu.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_xmb_animation_horizontal_highlight\tINT\t0\t0\t2\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tAnimation Horizontal Icon Highlight\tThe animation that triggers when scrolling between tabs.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_xmb_animation_move_up_down\tINT\t0\t0\t2\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tAnimation Move Up/Down\tThe animation that triggers when moving up or down.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_xmb_thumbnail_scale_factor\tINT\t100\t\u0001\t100\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tThumbnail Scale Factor\tReduce thumbnail display size by scaling maximum allowed width.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_xmb_vertical_fade_factor\tINT\t100\t0\t500\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tVertical Fade Factor\t\u0001\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\txmb_alpha_factor\tINT\t90\t0\t100\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tColor Theme Alpha Factor\t\u0001\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\txmb_layout\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t2\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tLayout\tSelect a different layout for the XMB interface.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\txmb_theme\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tIcon Theme\tSelect a different icon theme for RetroArch.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\txmb_menu_color_theme\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tColor Theme\tSelect a different background color theme.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_shader_pipeline\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShader Pipeline\tSelect an animated background effect. Can be GPU-intensive depending on the effect. If performance is unsatisfactory, either turn this off or revert to a simpler effect.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_font_color_red\tINT\t255\t0\t255\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tFont Color (Red)\t\u0001\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_font_color_green\tINT\t255\t0\t255\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tFont Color (Green)\t\u0001\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_font_color_blue\tINT\t255\t0\t255\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tFont Color (Blue)\t\u0001\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmaterialui_menu_color_theme\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tColor Theme\tSelect a different background color theme.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmaterialui_menu_transition_animation\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tTransition Animation\tEnable smooth animation effects when navigating between different levels of the menu.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmaterialui_thumbnail_view_portrait\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tPortrait Thumbnail View\tSpecify playlist thumbnail view mode when using portrait display orientations.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmaterialui_thumbnail_view_landscape\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tLandscape Thumbnail View\tSpecify playlist thumbnail view mode when using landscape display orientations.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmaterialui_landscape_layout_optimization\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tOptimize Landscape Layout\tAutomatically adjust menu layout to better fit the screen when using landscape display orientations.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tozone_menu_color_theme\tINT\t1\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tColor Theme\tSelect a different color theme.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tozone_header_separator\tINT\t1\t0\t2\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0\tHeader Separator\tAlternative width for header and footer separators.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tozone_font_scale\tINT\t0\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0\tFont Scale\tDefine whether the font size in the menu should have its own scaling, and if it should be scaled globally or with separate values for each part of the menu.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\taudio_out_rate\tINT\t\u0001\t1000\t192000\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tOutput Rate (Hz)\tAudio output sample rate.\tAudio\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\taudio_latency\tINT\t0\t0\t512\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tAudio Latency (ms)\tMaximum audio latency in milliseconds. The driver aims to keep actual latency at 50% of this value. Might not be honored if the audio driver can't provide given latency.\tAudio\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\taudio_resampler_quality\tINT\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tResampler Quality\tLower this value to favor performance/lower latency over audio quality, increase for better audio quality at the expense of performance/lower latency.\tAudio\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\taudio_block_frames\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tBlock Frames\t\u0001\tAudio\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmidi_volume\tINT\t100\t0\t100\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tVolume\tSet output volume (%).\tMIDI\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\taudio_wasapi_sh_buffer_length\tINT\t0\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tWASAPI Shared Buffer Length\tThe intermediate buffer length (in frames) when using the WASAPI driver in shared mode.\tAudio\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmicrophone_latency\tINT\t0\t0\t512\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tAudio Input Latency (ms)\tDesired audio input latency in milliseconds. Might not be honored if the microphone driver can't provide given latency.\tAudio\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmicrophone_resampler_quality\tINT\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tResampler Quality\tLower this value to favor performance/lower latency over audio quality, increase for better audio quality at the expense of performance/lower latency.\tMicrophone\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmicrophone_block_frames\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tMicrophone Block Frames\t\u0001\tAudio\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmicrophone_rate\tINT\t\u0001\t1000\t192000\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tDefault Input Rate (Hz)\tAudio input sample rate, used if a core doesn't request a specific number.\tAudio\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmicrophone_wasapi_sh_buffer_length\tINT\t0\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tWASAPI Shared Buffer Length\tThe intermediate buffer length (in frames) when using the WASAPI driver in shared mode.\tMicrophone\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcrt_switch_resolution\tINT\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tCRT SwitchRes\tFor CRT displays only. Attempts to use exact core/game resolution and refresh rate.\tCRT SwitchRes\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcrt_switch_resolution_super\tINT\t2560\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tCRT Super Resolution\tSwitch among native and ultrawide super resolutions.\tCRT SwitchRes\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcustom_viewport_width\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcustom_viewport_height\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcustom_viewport_x\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcustom_viewport_y\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\taspect_ratio_index\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tAspect Ratio\tSet display aspect ratio.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_autoswitch_refresh_rate\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tAutomatic Refresh Rate Switch\tSwitch screen refresh rate automatically based on current content.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_monitor_index\tINT\t0\t0\t1\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tMonitor Index\tSelect which display screen to use.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_windowed_position_x\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_windowed_position_y\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_windowed_position_width\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t7680\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tWindow Width\tSet the custom width for the display window.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_windowed_position_height\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t4320\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tWindow Height\tSet the custom height for the display window.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_window_auto_width_max\tINT\t1920\t0\t7680\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tMaximum Window Width\tSet the maximum width of the display window when automatically resizing based on 'Windowed Scale'.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_window_auto_height_max\tINT\t1080\t0\t4320\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tMaximum Window Height\tSet the maximum height of the display window when automatically resizing based on 'Windowed Scale'.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_fullscreen_x\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t7680\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tFullscreen Width\tSet the custom width size for the non-windowed fullscreen mode. Leaving it unset will use the desktop resolution.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_fullscreen_y\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t4320\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tFullscreen Height\tSet the custom height size for the non-windowed fullscreen mode. Leaving it unset will use the desktop resolution.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_scale\tINT\t3\t1\t10\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tWindowed Scale\t\u0001\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_scale_integer_axis\tINT\t0\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tInteger Scale Axis\tScale either height or width, or both height and width. Half steps apply only to high resolution sources.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_scale_integer_scaling\tINT\t0\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tInteger Scale Scaling\tRound down or up to the next integer. 'Smart' drops to underscale when image is cropped too much, and finally falls back to non-integer scaling if the underscale margins are too large.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_window_opacity\tINT\t100\t1\t100\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tWindow Opacity\tSet the window transparency.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_shader_delay\tINT\t0\t0\t0\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tAuto-Shader Delay\tDelay auto-loading shaders (in ms). Can work around graphical glitches when using 'screen grabbing' software.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_viwidth\tINT\t640\t640\t720\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tSet VI Screen Width\t\u0001\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_overscan_correction_top\tINT\t0\t0\t24\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tOverscan Correction (Top)\tAdjust display overscan cropping by reducing image size by specified number of scan lines (taken from top of screen). May introduce scaling artifacts.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_overscan_correction_bottom\tINT\t0\t0\t24\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tOverscan Correction (Bottom)\tAdjust display overscan cropping by reducing image size by specified number of scan lines (taken from bottom of screen). May introduce scaling artifacts.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_hard_sync_frames\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tHard GPU Sync Frames\tSet how many frames the CPU can run ahead of the GPU when using 'Hard GPU Sync'.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_frame_delay\tINT\t0\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tFrame Delay\tReduces latency at the cost of a higher risk of video stuttering.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_max_swapchain_images\tINT\t3\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tMax Swapchain Images\tTells the video driver to explicitly use a specified buffering mode.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_black_frame_insertion\tINT\t0\t0\t15\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tBlack Frame Insertion\tWARNING: Rapid flickering may cause image persistence on some displays. Use at your own risk // Insert black frame(s) between frames. Can greatly reduce motion blur by emulating CRT scan out, but at cost of brightness.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_bfi_dark_frames\tINT\t1\t1\t15\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tBlack Frame Insertion - Dark Frames\tAdjust number of black frames in total BFI scan out sequence. More equals higher motion clarity, less equals higher brightness. Not applicable at 120hz as there is only 1 BFI frame to work with total. Settings higher than possible will limit you to the maximum possible for your chosen refresh rate.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_shader_subframes\tINT\t1\t1\t16\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShader Sub-frames\tWARNING: Rapid flickering may cause image persistence on some displays. Use at your own risk // Simulates a basic rolling scanline over multiple sub-frames by dividing the screen up vertically and rendering each part of the screen according to how many sub-frames there are.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_swap_interval\tINT\t1\t0\t4\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tVSync Swap Interval\tUse a custom swap interval for VSync. Effectively reduces monitor refresh rate by the specified factor. 'Auto' sets factor based on core-reported frame rate, providing improved frame pacing when running e.g. 30 fps content on a 60 Hz display or 60 fps content on a 120 Hz display.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_rotation\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t3\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tVideo Rotation\tForces a certain rotation of the video. The rotation is added to rotations which the core sets.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tscreen_orientation\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t3\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tScreen Orientation\tForces a certain orientation of the screen from the operating system.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_msg_bgcolor_red\tINT\t0\t0\t255\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tNotification Background Color (Red)\tSets the red value of the OSD background color. Valid values are between 0 and 255.\tOn-Screen Display\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_msg_bgcolor_green\tINT\t0\t0\t255\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tNotification Background Color (Green)\tSets the green value of the OSD background color. Valid values are between 0 and 255.\tOn-Screen Display\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_msg_bgcolor_blue\tINT\t0\t0\t255\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tNotification Background Color (Blue)\tSets the blue value of the OSD background color. Valid values are between 0 and 255.\tOn-Screen Display\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_stream_port\tINT\t56400\t1\t65536\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tUDP Stream Port\t\u0001\tRecording\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_record_threads\tINT\t2\t1\t8\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tRecording Threads\t\u0001\tRecording\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_record_quality\tINT\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tRecording Quality\t\u0001\tRecording\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_stream_quality\tINT\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tStreaming Quality\t\u0001\tRecording\n",
    "retroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_record_scale_factor\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_stream_scale_factor\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tstreaming_mode\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tStreaming Mode\t\u0001\tRecording\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tscreen_brightness\tINT\t100\t5\t100\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tScreen Brightness\tIncrease or decrease the screen brightness.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_bind_timeout\tINT\t3\t1\t5\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tBind Timeout\tAmount of seconds to wait until proceeding to the next bind.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_bind_hold\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t5\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tBind Hold\tAmount of seconds to hold an input to bind it.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_turbo_period\tINT\t6\t2\t100\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tTurbo Period\tThe period in frames when turbo-enabled buttons are pressed.\tTurbo Fire\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_turbo_duty_cycle\tINT\t0\t0\t100\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tTurbo Duty Cycle\tThe number of frames from the Turbo Period the buttons are held down for. If this number is equal to or greater than the Turbo Period, the buttons will never release.\tTurbo Fire\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_turbo_mode\tINT\t0\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tTurbo Mode\tSelect the general behavior of turbo mode.\tTurbo Fire\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_turbo_button\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tTurbo Button\tTarget turbo button in 'Single Button' mode.\tTurbo Fire\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_max_users\tINT\t\u0001\t1\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tMaximum Users\tMaximum amount of users supported by RetroArch.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_menu_toggle_gamepad_combo\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tMenu Toggle (Controller Combo)\tController button combination to toggle menu.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_poll_type_behavior\tINT\t2\t0\t2\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tPolling Behavior (Restart required)\tInfluences how input polling is done in RetroArch. Setting it to 'Early' or 'Late' can result in less latency, depending on your configuration.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_quit_gamepad_combo\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tQuit (Controller Combo)\tController button combination to quit RetroArch.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_hotkey_block_delay\tINT\t5\t0\t600\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tHotkey Enable Delay (Frames)\tAdd a delay in frames before normal input is blocked after pressing the assigned 'Hotkey Enable' key. Allows normal input from the 'Hotkey Enable' key to be captured when it is mapped to another action (e.g. RetroPad 'Select').\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_mouse_scale\tINT\t1\t1\t4\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tMouse Scale\tAdjust x/y scale for Wiimote light gun speed.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_touch_scale\tINT\t1\t1\t4\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tTouch Scale\tAdjust x/y scale of touchscreen coordinates to accommodate OS-level display scaling.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_rumble_gain\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t100\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tVibration Strength\tSpecify the magnitude of haptic feedback effects.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_auto_game_focus\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tAuto Enable 'Game Focus' Mode\tAlways enable 'Game Focus' mode when launching and resuming content. When set to 'Detect', option will be enabled if current core implements frontend keyboard callback functionality.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_block_timeout\tINT\t0\t0\t4\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tInput Block Timeout\tThe number of milliseconds to wait to get a complete input sample. Use it if you have issues with simultaneous button presses (Android only).\tFrame Throttle\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tkeyboard_gamepad_mapping_type\tINT\t1\t0\t3\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tKeyboard Controller Mapping Type\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_overlay_show_inputs\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow Inputs on Overlay\tShow registered inputs on the on-screen overlay. 'Touched' highlights overlay elements that are pressed/clicked. 'Physical (Controller)' highlights actual input passed to cores, typically from a connected controller/keyboard.\tOn-Screen Overlay\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_overlay_show_inputs_port\tINT\t0\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tShow Inputs From Port\tSelect the port of the input device to monitor when 'Show Inputs on Overlay' is set to 'Physical (Controller)'.\tOn-Screen Overlay\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_overlay_dpad_diagonal_sensitivity\tINT\t80\t0\t100\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tD-Pad Diagonal Sensitivity\tAdjust the size of diagonal zones. Set to 100% for 8-way symmetry.\tOn-Screen Overlay\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_overlay_abxy_diagonal_sensitivity\tINT\t50\t0\t100\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tABXY Overlap Sensitivity\tAdjust the size of overlap zones in the face button diamond. Set to 100% for 8-way symmetry.\tOn-Screen Overlay\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_overlay_analog_recenter_zone\tINT\t0\t0\t100\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tAnalog Recentering Zone\tAnalog stick input will be relative to first touch if pressed within this zone.\tOn-Screen Overlay\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tsplit_joycon_p1\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tsplit_joycon_p2\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tsplit_joycon_p3\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tsplit_joycon_p4\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tsplit_joycon_p5\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tsplit_joycon_p6\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tsplit_joycon_p7\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tsplit_joycon_p8\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnotification_show_screenshot_duration\tINT\t0\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tScreenshot Notification Persistence\tDefine the duration of the on-screen screenshot message.\tOn-Screen Display\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnotification_show_screenshot_flash\tINT\t0\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tScreenshot Flash Effect\tDisplay a white flashing effect on-screen with the desired duration when taking a screenshot.\tOn-Screen Display\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnetplay_ip_port\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t65535\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tNetplay TCP Port\tThe port of the host IP address. Can be either a TCP or UDP port.\tNetwork\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnetplay_max_connections\tINT\t3\t1\t31\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tMax Simultaneous Connections\tThe maximum number of active connections that the host will accept before refusing new ones.\tNetwork\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnetplay_max_ping\tINT\t0\t0\t500\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tPing Limiter\tThe maximum connection latency (ping) that the host will accept. Set it to 0 for no limit.\tNetwork\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnetplay_chat_color_name\tINT\t32768\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tChat Color (Nickname)\tFormat: #RRGGBB or RRGGBB\tNetwork\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnetplay_chat_color_msg\tINT\t16777215\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tChat Color (Message)\tFormat: #RRGGBB or RRGGBB\tNetwork\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnetplay_input_latency_frames_min\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnetplay_input_latency_frames_range\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnetplay_share_digital\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tDigital Input Sharing\t\u0001\tNetwork\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnetplay_share_analog\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tAnalog Input Sharing\t\u0001\tNetwork\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnetwork_cmd_port\tINT\t55355\t0\t65535\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tNetwork Command Port\t\u0001\tNetwork\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnetwork_remote_base_port\tINT\t55400\t0\t65535\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tNetwork RetroPad Base Port\t\u0001\tNetwork\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcloud_sync_sync_mode\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2\tSync Mode\tAutomatic: Sync on RetroArch startup and when cores are unloaded. Manual: Only sync when 'Sync Now' button is manually triggered.\tCloud Sync\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tuser_language\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tLanguage\tSet the language of the user interface.\tUser\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tbundle_assets_extract_version_current\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tbundle_assets_extract_last_version\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcheevos_appearance_anchor\tINT\t0\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tPosition\tSet the corner/edge of the screen which achievement notifications will appear from.\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcheevos_visibility_summary\tINT\t1\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tStartup Summary\tShows information about the game being loaded and the user's current progress. 'All Identified Games' will show summary for games with no published achievements.\tVisibility\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\taccessibility_narrator_speech_speed\tINT\t5\t1\t10\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tText-to-Speech Speed\tThe speed for the Text-to-Speech voice.\tAccessibility\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tai_service_mode\tINT\t1\t0\t2\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tAI Service Output\tShow translation as a text overlay (Image Mode), play as Text-To-Speech (Speech), or use a system narrator like NVDA (Narrator).\tAI Service\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tai_service_target_lang\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tTarget Language\tThe language the service will translate to. 'Default' is English.\tAI Service\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tai_service_source_lang\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tSource Language\tThe language the service will translate from. If set to 'Default', it will attempt to auto-detect the language. Setting it to a specific language will make the translation more accurate.\tAI Service\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tlibnx_overclock\tINT\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_3ds_display_mode\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t3DS Display Mode\tSelects between 3D and 2D display modes. In '3D' mode, pixels are square and a depth effect is applied when viewing the Quick Menu. '2D' mode provides the best performance.\tUser Interface\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_dingux_ipu_filter_type\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tImage Interpolation\tSpecify image interpolation method when scaling content via the internal IPU. 'Bicubic' or 'Bilinear' is recommended when using CPU-powered video filters. This option has no performance impact.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_dingux_refresh_rate\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tVertical Refresh Rate\tSet vertical refresh rate of the display. '50 Hz' will enable smooth video when running PAL content.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_dingux_rs90_softfilter_type\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tImage Interpolation\tSpecify image interpolation method when 'Integer Scale' is disabled. 'Nearest Neighbor' has the least performance impact.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcpu_scaling_mode\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcpu_min_freq\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcpu_max_freq\tINT\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tsteam_rich_presence_format\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tRich Presence Content Format\tDecide what information related to the content will be shared.\tSteam\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_overlay_lightgun_trigger_delay\tINT\t1\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tTrigger Delay (frames)\tDelay trigger input to allow the cursor time to move. This delay is also used to wait for the correct multi-touch count.\tOverlay Lightgun\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_overlay_lightgun_two_touch_input\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t2-Touch Input\tSelect input to send when two pointers are on screen. Trigger Delay should be nonzero to distinguish from other input.\tOverlay Lightgun\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_overlay_lightgun_three_touch_input\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t3-Touch Input\tSelect input to send when three pointers are on screen. Trigger Delay should be nonzero to distinguish from other input.\tOverlay Lightgun\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_overlay_lightgun_four_touch_input\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\t4-Touch Input\tSelect input to send when four pointers are on screen. Trigger Delay should be nonzero to distinguish from other input.\tOverlay Lightgun\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_overlay_mouse_hold_msec\tINT\t200\t0\t1000\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tLong Press Threshold (ms)\tAdjust the hold time required for a long press.\tOverlay Mouse\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_overlay_mouse_dtap_msec\tINT\t200\t0\t500\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tDouble Tap Threshold (ms)\tAdjust the allowable time between taps when detecting a double tap.\tOverlay Mouse\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\trewind_buffer_size\tINT\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tRewind Buffer Size (MB)\tThe amount of memory (in MB) to reserve for the rewind buffer. Increasing this will increase the amount of rewind history.\tRewind\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcontent_favorites_size\tINT\t200\t-1\t9999\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tFavorites Size\tLimit the number of entries in the 'Favorites' playlist. Once the limit is reached, new additions will be prevented until old entries are removed. Setting a value of -1 allows 'unlimited' entries. WARNING: Reducing the value will delete existing entries!\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tstate_slot\tINT\t0\t-1\t999\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tState Slot\tChange the currently selected state slot.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\treplay_slot\tINT\t0\t-1\t999\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tReplay Slot\tChange the currently selected state slot.\t\u0001\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_xmb_title_margin\tINT\t5\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tTitle Margin\t\u0001\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tmenu_xmb_title_margin_horizontal_offset\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tTitle Margin Horizontal Offset\t\u0001\tAppearance\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcrt_switch_center_adjust\tINT\t0\t-50\t50\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tHorizontal Centering\tCycle through these options if the image is not centered properly on the display.\tCRT SwitchRes\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcrt_switch_porch_adjust\tINT\t0\t-50\t100\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tHorizontal Size\tCycle through these options to adjust the horizontal settings to change the image size.\tCRT SwitchRes\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tcrt_switch_vertical_adjust\tINT\t0\t-20\t20\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0\tVertical Centring\t\u0001\tCRT SwitchRes\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_window_offset_x\tINT\t0\t-50\t50\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tScreen Horizontal Offset\tForces a certain offset horizontally to the video. The offset is applied globally.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_window_offset_y\tINT\t0\t-50\t50\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tScreen Vertical Offset\tForces a certain offset vertically to the video. The offset is applied globally.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvideo_max_frame_latency\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tMax Frame Latency\tTells the video driver to explicitly use a specified buffering mode.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\td3d10_gpu_index\tINT\t0\t0\t15\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tGPU Index\tSelect which graphics card to use.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\td3d11_gpu_index\tINT\t0\t0\t15\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tGPU Index\tSelect which graphics card to use.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\td3d12_gpu_index\tINT\t0\t0\t15\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tGPU Index\tSelect which graphics card to use.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tvulkan_gpu_index\tINT\t0\t0\t15\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tGPU Index\tSelect which graphics card to use.\tVideo\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tnetplay_check_frames\tINT\t600\t0\t5184000\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tNetplay Check Frames\tThe frequency (in frames) that netplay will verify that the host and client are in sync.\tNetwork\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tbottom_font_color_red\tINT\t255\t0\t255\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tFont Color Red\tAdjust bottom screen font red color.\tUser Interface\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tbottom_font_color_green\tINT\t255\t0\t255\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tFont Color Green\tAdjust bottom screen font green color.\tUser Interface\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tbottom_font_color_blue\tINT\t255\t0\t255\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tFont Color Blue\tAdjust bottom screen font blue color.\tUser Interface\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tbottom_font_color_opacity\tINT\t255\t0\t255\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tFont Color Opacity\tAdjust bottom screen font opacity.\tUser Interface\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_overlay_lightgun_port\tINT\t-1\t-1\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tLightgun Port\tSet the core port to receive input from the overlay lightgun.\tOverlay Lightgun\nretroarch\t\u0001\t\tinput_turbo_bind\tINT\t-1\t-1\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv1.22.2,v1.22.1,v1.22.0,v1.21.0\tTurbo Bind\tTurbo activating RetroPad bind. Empty uses the port-specific bind.\tTurbo Fire\neden\t\u0001\tLibraryApplet\tcabinet_applet_mode\tENUM\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ECustom frontend\u001F1\u001EReal applet\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tAmiibo editor\t\u0001\tLibrary Applet\neden\t\u0001\tLibraryApplet\tcontroller_applet_mode\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ECustom frontend\u001F1\u001EReal applet\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tController configuration\t\u0001\tLibrary Applet\neden\t\u0001\tLibraryApplet\tdata_erase_applet_mode\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ECustom frontend\u001F1\u001EReal applet\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tData erase\t\u0001\tLibrary Applet\neden\t\u0001\tLibraryApplet\terror_applet_mode\tENUM\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ECustom frontend\u001F1\u001EReal applet\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tError\t\u0001\tLibrary Applet\neden\t\u0001\tLibraryApplet\tnet_connect_applet_mode\tENUM\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ECustom frontend\u001F1\u001EReal applet\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tNet connect\t\u0001\tLibrary Applet\neden\t\u0001\tLibraryApplet\tplayer_select_applet_mode\tENUM\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ECustom frontend\u001F1\u001EReal applet\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tPlayer select\t\u0001\tLibrary Applet\neden\t\u0001\tLibraryApplet\tswkbd_applet_mode\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ECustom frontend\u001F1\u001EReal applet\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tSoftware keyboard\t\u0001\tLibrary Applet\neden\t\u0001\tLibraryApplet\tmii_edit_applet_mode\tENUM\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ECustom frontend\u001F1\u001EReal applet\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tMii Edit\t\u0001\tLibrary Applet\neden\t\u0001\tLibraryApplet\tweb_applet_mode\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ECustom frontend\u001F1\u001EReal applet\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tOnline web\t\u0001\tLibrary Applet\neden\t\u0001\tLibraryApplet\tshop_applet_mode\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ECustom frontend\u001F1\u001EReal applet\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tShop\t\u0001\tLibrary Applet\neden\t\u0001\tLibraryApplet\tphoto_viewer_applet_mode\tENUM\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ECustom frontend\u001F1\u001EReal applet\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tPhoto viewer\t\u0001\tLibrary Applet\neden\t\u0001\tLibraryApplet\toffline_web_applet_mode\tENUM\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ECustom frontend\u001F1\u001EReal applet\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tOffline web\t\u0001\tLibrary Applet\neden\t\u0001\tLibraryApplet\tlogin_share_applet_mode\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ECustom frontend\u001F1\u001EReal applet\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tLogin share\t\u0001\tLibrary Applet\neden\t\u0001\tLibraryApplet\twifi_web_auth_applet_mode\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ECustom frontend\u001F1\u001EReal applet\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tWifi web auth\t\u0001\tLibrary Applet\neden\t\u0001\tLibraryApplet\tmy_page_applet_mode\tENUM\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ECustom frontend\u001F1\u001EReal applet\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tMy page\t\u0001\tLibrary Applet\neden\t\u0001\tLibraryApplet\tenable_overlay\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0\tEnable Overlay Applet\tEnables Horizon\\'s built-in overlay applet. Press and hold the home button for 1 second to show it.\tLibrary Applet\neden\t\u0001\tAudio\toutput_engine\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EAuto\u001F1\u001ECubeb\u001F2\u001ESdl2\u001F3\u001ENull\u001F4\u001EOboe\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tOutput Engine\t\u0001\tAudio\neden\t\u0001\tSystem\tsound_index\tENUM\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EMono\u001F1\u001EStereo\u001F2\u001ESurround\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tSound Output Mode\t\u0001\tSystem Audio\neden\t\u0001\tAudio\tvolume\tINT\t100\t0\t200\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tVolume\t\u0001\tAudio\neden\t\u0001\tAudio\taudio_muted\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tMute audio\t\u0001\tAudio\neden\t\u0001\tCore\tuse_multi_core\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tMulticore CPU Emulation\tThis option increases CPU emulation thread use from 1 to the maximum of 4. This is mainly a debug option and shouldn't be disabled.\tCore\neden\t\u0001\tCore\tuse_speed_limit\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tCore\neden\t\u0001\tCore\tspeed_limit\tINT\t100\t0\t9999\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tLimit Speed Percent\tControls the game's maximum rendering speed, but it's up to each game if it runs faster or not. 200% for a 30 FPS game is 60 FPS, and for a 60 FPS game it will be 120 FPS. Disabling it means unlocking the framerate to the maximum your PC can reach.\tCore\neden\t\u0001\tCore\tslow_speed_limit\tINT\t50\t0\t9999\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0\tSlow Speed\tWhen the Slow Speed hotkey is pressed, the speed will be limited to this percentage.\tCore\neden\t\u0001\tCore\tturbo_speed_limit\tINT\t200\t0\t9999\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0\tTurbo Speed\tWhen the Turbo Speed hotkey is pressed, the speed will be limited to this percentage.\tCore\neden\t\u0001\tCore\tsync_core_speed\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tSynchronize Core Speed\tSynchronizes CPU core speed with the game's maximum rendering speed to boost FPS without affecting game speed (animations, physics, etc.). Can help reduce stuttering at lower framerates.\tCore\neden\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpu_accuracy\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EAuto\u001F1\u001EAccurate\u001F2\u001EUnsafe\u001F3\u001EParanoid (disables most optimizations)\u001F4\u001EDebugging\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tAccuracy\tChange the accuracy of the emulated CPU (for debugging only).\tCpu\neden\t\u0001\tCpu\tfast_cpu_time\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EOff\u001F1\u001EBoost (1700MHz)\u001F2\u001EFast) ENUM(MemoryLayout\u001F3\u001EMemory_4Gb\u001F4\u001EMemory_6Gb\u001F5\u001EMemory_8Gb\u001F6\u001EMemory_10Gb\u001F7\u001EMemory_12Gb\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tCPU Overclock\tOverclocks the emulated CPU to remove some FPS limiters. Weaker CPUs may see reduced performance, and certain games may behave improperly. Use Boost (1700MHz) to run at the Switch's highest native clock, or Fast (2000MHz) to run at 2x clock.\tCpu\neden\t\u0001\tCpu\tuse_custom_cpu_ticks\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tCpu\neden\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpu_ticks\tINT\t16000\t77\t65535\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tCustom CPU Ticks\tSet a custom value of CPU ticks. Higher values can increase performance, but may cause deadlocks. A range of 77-21000 is recommended.\tCpu\neden\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_page_tables\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tCpu Debug\neden\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_block_linking\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tCpu Debug\neden\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_return_stack_buffer\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tCpu Debug\neden\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_fast_dispatcher\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tCpu Debug\neden\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_context_elimination\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tCpu Debug\neden\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_const_prop\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tCpu Debug\neden\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_misc_ir\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tCpu Debug\neden\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_reduce_misalign_checks\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tCpu Debug\neden\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_fastmem\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tCpu Debug\neden\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_fastmem_exclusives\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tCpu Debug\neden\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_recompile_exclusives\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tCpu Debug\neden\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_ignore_memory_aborts\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tCpu Debug\neden\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_unsafe_unfuse_fma\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tUnfuse FMA (improve performance on CPUs without FMA)\tThis option improves speed by reducing accuracy of fused-multiply-add instructions on CPUs without native FMA support.\tCpu Unsafe\neden\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_unsafe_reduce_fp_error\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tFaster FRSQRTE and FRECPE\tThis option improves the speed of some approximate floating-point functions by using less accurate native approximations.\tCpu Unsafe\neden\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_unsafe_ignore_standard_fpcr\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tFaster ASIMD instructions (32 bits only)\tThis option improves the speed of 32 bits ASIMD floating-point functions by running with incorrect rounding modes.\tCpu Unsafe\neden\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_unsafe_inaccurate_nan\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tInaccurate NaN handling\tThis option improves speed by removing NaN checking. Please note this also reduces accuracy of certain floating-point instructions.\tCpu Unsafe\neden\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_unsafe_fastmem_check\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tDisable address space checks\tThis option improves speed by eliminating a safety check before every memory operation. Disabling it may allow arbitrary code execution.\tCpu Unsafe\neden\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_unsafe_ignore_global_monitor\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tIgnore global monitor\tThis option improves speed by relying only on the semantics of cmpxchg to ensure safety of exclusive access instructions. Please note this may result in deadlocks and other race conditions.\tCpu Unsafe\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tvulkan_device\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tDevice\tThis setting selects the GPU to use (Vulkan only).\tRenderer\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tresolution_setup\tENUM\t3\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001E0.25X (180p/270p) [EXPERIMENTAL]\u001F1\u001E0.5X (360p/540p) [EXPERIMENTAL]\u001F2\u001E0.75X (540p/810p) [EXPERIMENTAL]\u001F3\u001E1X (720p/1080p)\u001F4\u001E1.25X (900p/1350p) [EXPERIMENTAL]\u001F5\u001E1.5X (1080p/1620p) [EXPERIMENTAL]\u001F6\u001E2X (1440p/2160p)\u001F7\u001E3X (2160p/3240p)\u001F8\u001E4X (2880p/4320p)\u001F9\u001E5X (3600p/5400p)\u001F10\u001E6X (4320p/6480p)\u001F11\u001E7X (5040p/7560p)\u001F12\u001E8X (5760p/8640p)\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tResolution\tForces to render at a different resolution. Higher resolutions require more VRAM and bandwidth. Options lower than 1X can cause artifacts.\tRenderer\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tuse_vsync\tENUM\t2\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EImmediate\u001F1\u001EMailbox\u001F2\u001EFifo\u001F3\u001EFifoRelaxed\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tVSync Mode\tFIFO (VSync) does not drop frames or exhibit tearing but is limited by the screen refresh rate. FIFO Relaxed allows tearing as it recovers from a slow down. Mailbox can have lower latency than FIFO and does not tear but may drop frames. Immediate (no synchronization) presents whatever is available and can exhibit tearing.\tRenderer\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tscaling_filter\tENUM\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ENearest Neighbor\u001F1\u001EBilinear\u001F2\u001EBicubic\u001F3\u001EGaussian\u001F4\u001ELanczos\u001F5\u001EScaleForce\u001F6\u001EAMD FidelityFX Super Resolution\u001F7\u001EArea\u001F8\u001EZero-Tangent\u001F9\u001EB-Spline\u001F10\u001EMitchell\u001F11\u001ESpline-1\u001F12\u001EMMPX\u001F13\u001EMaxEnum\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tWindow Adapting Filter\t\u0001\tRenderer\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tfsr_sharpening_slider\tINT\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tFSR Sharpness\tDetermines how sharpened the image will look using FSR's dynamic contrast.\tRenderer\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\taspect_ratio\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EDefault (16:9)\u001F1\u001EForce 4:3\u001F2\u001EForce 21:9\u001F3\u001EForce 16:10\u001F4\u001EStretch to Window\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tAspect Ratio\tStretches the renderer to fit the specified aspect ratio. Most games only support 16:9, so modifications are required to get other ratios. Also controls the aspect ratio of captured screenshots.\tRenderer\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tanti_aliasing\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ENone\u001F1\u001EFXAA\u001F2\u001ESMAA\u001F3\u001EMaxEnum\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tAnti-Aliasing Method\tThe anti-aliasing method to use. SMAA offers the best quality. FXAA can produce a more stable picture in lower resolutions.\tRenderer\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tbg_red\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tbg_green\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tbg_blue\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tdma_accuracy\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EDefault\u001F1\u001EUnsafe (fast)\u001F2\u001ESafe (stable)\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tDMA Accuracy\tControls the DMA precision accuracy. Safe precision fixes issues in some games but may degrade performance.\tRenderer Advanced\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tvram_usage_mode\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EConservative\u001F1\u001EAggressive\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tVRAM Usage Mode\tSelects whether the emulator should prefer to conserve memory or make maximum usage of available video memory for performance. Aggressive mode may impact performance of other applications such as recording software.\tRenderer Advanced\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tnvdec_emulation\tENUM\t2\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ENo Video Output\u001F1\u001ECPU Video Decoding\u001F2\u001EGPU Video Decoding (Default)\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tNVDEC emulation\tSpecifies how videos should be decoded. It can either use the CPU or the GPU for decoding, or perform no decoding at all (black screen on videos). In most cases, GPU decoding provides the best performance.\tRenderer Advanced\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\taccelerate_astc\tENUM\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ECPU\u001F1\u001EGPU\u001F2\u001ECPU Asynchronous\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0\tASTC Decoding Method\tThis option controls how ASTC textures should be decoded. CPU: Use the CPU for decoding. GPU: Use the GPU's compute shaders to decode ASTC textures (recommended). CPU Asynchronously: Use the CPU to decode ASTC textures on demand. EliminatesASTC decoding stuttering but may present artifacts.\tRenderer Advanced\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tframe_pacing_mode\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EAuto\u001F1\u001E30 FPS\u001F2\u001E60 FPS\u001F3\u001E90 FPS\u001F4\u001E120 FPS\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0\tFrame Pacing Mode (Vulkan only)\tControls how the emulator manages frame pacing to reduce stuttering and make the frame rate smoother and more consistent.\tRenderer Advanced\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tastc_recompression\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EUncompressed (Best quality)\u001F1\u001EBC1 (Low quality)\u001F2\u001EBC3 (Medium quality)\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tASTC Recompression Method\tMost GPUs lack support for ASTC textures and must decompress to anintermediate format: RGBA8. BC1/BC3: The intermediate format will be recompressed to BC1 or BC3 format,  saving VRAM but degrading image quality.\tRenderer Advanced\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tsync_memory_operations\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tSync Memory Operations\tEnsures data consistency between compute and memory operations. This option fixes issues in games, but may degrade performance. Unreal Engine 4 games often see the most significant changes thereof.\tRenderer Advanced\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tforce_max_clock\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tForce maximum clocks (Vulkan only)\tRuns work in the background while waiting for graphics commands to keep the GPU from lowering its clock speed.\tRenderer Advanced\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tuse_disk_shader_cache\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tUse persistent pipeline cache\tAllows saving shaders to storage for faster loading on following game boots. Disabling it is only intended for debugging.\tRenderer Advanced\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tuse_vulkan_driver_pipeline_cache\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tUse Vulkan pipeline cache\tEnables GPU vendor-specific pipeline cache. This option can improve shader loading time significantly in cases where the Vulkan driver does not store pipeline cache files internally.\tRenderer Advanced\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tenable_compute_pipelines\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tEnable Compute Pipelines (Intel Vulkan Only)\tRequired by some games. This setting only exists for Intel proprietary drivers and may crash if enabled. Compute pipelines are always enabled on all other drivers.\tRenderer Advanced\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tuse_video_framerate\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tSync to framerate of video playback\tRun the game at normal speed during video playback, even when the framerate is unlocked.\tRenderer Advanced\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tbarrier_feedback_loops\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tBarrier feedback loops\tImproves rendering of transparency effects in specific games.\tRenderer Advanced\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tenable_buffer_history\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0\tEnable buffer history\tEnables access to previous buffer states. This option may improve rendering quality and performance consistency in some games.\tRenderer Advanced\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tuse_optimized_vertex_buffers\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer Advanced\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tfast_gpu_time\tENUM\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EOff\u001F1\u001EMedium (256)\u001F2\u001EHigh) ENUM(GpuUnswizzleSize\u001F3\u001EVerySmall\u001F4\u001ESmall\u001F5\u001EOff\u001F6\u001ELarge\u001F7\u001EVeryLarge) ENUM(GpuUnswizzle\u001F8\u001EVeryLow\u001F9\u001ELow\u001F10\u001EOff\u001F11\u001EMedium (256)\u001F12\u001EHigh) ENUM(GpuUnswizzleChunk\u001F13\u001EVeryLow\u001F14\u001ELow\u001F15\u001EOff\u001F16\u001EMedium (256)\u001F17\u001EHigh) ENUM(TemperatureUnits\u001F18\u001ECelsius\u001F19\u001EFahrenheit) ENUM(ExtendedDynamicState\u001F20\u001EDisabled\u001F21\u001EEDS1\u001F22\u001EEDS2\u001F23\u001EEDS3\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tFast GPU Time\tOverclocks the emulated GPU to increase dynamic resolution and render distance. Use 256 for maximal performance and 512 for maximal graphics fidelity.\tRenderer Hacks\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tskip_cpu_inner_invalidation\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tSkip CPU Inner Invalidation\tSkips certain cache invalidations during memory updates, reducing CPU usage and improving latency. This may cause soft-crashes.\tRenderer Hacks\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tfix_bloom_effects\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tFix bloom effects\tRemoves bloom in Burnout.\tRenderer Hacks\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\temulate_bgr565\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer Hacks\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tuse_asynchronous_shaders\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tEnable asynchronous shader compilation\tMay reduce shader stutter.\tRenderer Hacks\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tgpu_unswizzle_enabled\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0\tGPU Unswizzle\tAccelerates BCn 3D texture decoding using GPU compute. Disable if experiencing crashes or graphical glitches.\tRenderer Hacks\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tsample_shading_fraction\tINT\t0\t0\t100\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tSample Shading\tAllows the fragment shader to execute per sample in a multi-sampled fragment instead of once per fragment. Improves graphics quality at the cost of performance. Higher values improve quality but degrade performance.\tRenderer Extensions\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tdebug\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer Debug\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tshader_feedback\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer Debug\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tnsight_aftermath\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer Debug\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tdisable_shader_loop_safety_checks\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer Debug\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\trenderdoc_hotkey\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer Debug\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tpatch_old_qcom_drivers\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer Debug\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tdisable_buffer_reorder\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer Debug\neden\t\u0001\tSystem\tlanguage_index\tENUM\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EJapanese (日本語)\u001F1\u001EAmerican English\u001F2\u001EFrench (français)\u001F3\u001EGerman (Deutsch)\u001F4\u001EItalian (italiano)\u001F5\u001ESpanish (español)\u001F6\u001EChinese\u001F7\u001EKorean (한국어)\u001F8\u001EDutch (Nederlands)\u001F9\u001EPortuguese (português)\u001F10\u001ERussian (Русский)\u001F11\u001ETaiwanese\u001F12\u001EBritish English\u001F13\u001ECanadian French\u001F14\u001ELatin American Spanish\u001F15\u001ESimplified Chinese\u001F16\u001ETraditional Chinese (正體中文)\u001F17\u001EBrazilian Portuguese (português do Brasil)\u001F18\u0