\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tcontinuous\t\u0001\t\u0001\tEmulator\nvita3k\t\u0001\t\tback-camera-id\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tcontinuous\t\u0001\t\u0001\tEmulator\nvita3k\t\u0001\t\tback-camera-image\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tcontinuous\t\u0001\t\u0001\tEmulator\nvita3k\t\u0001\t\tback-camera-color\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tcontinuous\t\u0001\t\u0001\tEmulator\nvita3k\t\u0001\t\ttracy-primitive-impl\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tcontinuous\t\u0001\t\u0001\tEmulator\nxenia\t\u0001\tDisplay\tfullscreen\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tWhether to launch the emulator in fullscreen.\tDisplay\nxenia\t\u0001\tGeneral\tcontroller_hotkeys\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tHotkeys for Xbox and PS controllers.\tGeneral\nxenia\t\u0001\tDisplay\tpostprocess_antialiasing\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tPost-processing anti-aliasing effect to apply to the image output of the game. Using post-process anti-aliasing is heavily recommended when AMD FidelityFX Contrast Adaptive Sharpening or Super Resolution 1.0 is active. Use: [none, fxaa, fxaa_extreme]  none (or any value not listed here):   Don't alter the original image.  fxaa:   NVIDIA Fast Approximate Anti-Aliasing 3.11, normal quality preset (12).  fxaa_extreme:   NVIDIA Fast Approximate Anti-Aliasing 3.11, extreme quality preset (39).\tDisplay\nxenia\t\u0001\tDisplay\tpostprocess_scaling_and_sharpening\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tPost-processing effect to use for resampling and/or sharpening of the final display output. Use: [bilinear, cas, fsr]  bilinear (or any value not listed here):   Original image at 1:1, simple bilinear stretching for resampling.  cas:   Use AMD FidelityFX Contrast Adaptive Sharpening (CAS) for sharpening at scaling factors of up to 2x2, with additional bilinear stretching for larger factors.  fsr:   Use AMD FidelityFX Super Resolution 1.0 (FSR) for highest-quality upscaling, or AMD FidelityFX Contrast Adaptive Sharpening for sharpening while not scaling or downsampling.   For scaling by factors of more than 2x2, multiple FSR passes are done.\tDisplay\nxenia\t\u0001\tDisplay\tpostprocess_ffx_cas_additional_sharpness\tFLOAT\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tAdditional sharpness for AMD FidelityFX Contrast Adaptive Sharpening (CAS), from 0 to 1. Higher is sharper.\tDisplay\nxenia\t\u0001\tDisplay\tpostprocess_ffx_fsr_max_upsampling_passes\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tMaximum number of upsampling passes performed in AMD FidelityFX Super Resolution 1.0 (FSR) before falling back to bilinear stretching after the final pass. Each pass upscales only to up to 2x2 the previous size. If the game outputs a 1280x720 image, 1 pass will upscale it to up to 2560x1440 (below 4K), after 2 passes it will be upscaled to a maximum of 5120x2880 (including 3840x2160 for 4K), and so on. This variable has no effect if the display resolution isn't very high, but may be reduced on resolutions like 4K or 8K in case the performance impact of multiple FSR upsampling passes is too high, or if softer edges are desired. The default value is the maximum internally supported by Xenia.\tDisplay\nxenia\t\u0001\tDisplay\tpostprocess_ffx_fsr_sharpness_reduction\tFLOAT\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tSharpness reduction for AMD FidelityFX Super Resolution 1.0 (FSR), in stops. Lower is sharper.\tDisplay\nxenia\t\u0001\tDisplay\tpostprocess_dither\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tDither the final image output from the internal precision to 8 bits per channel so gradients are smoother. On a 10bpc display, the lower 2 bits will still be kept, but noise will be added to them - disabling may be recommended for 10bpc, but it depends on the 10bpc displaying capabilities of the actual display used.\tDisplay\nxenia\t\u0001\tGeneral\trecent_titles_entry_amount\tINT\t10\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tAllows user to define how many titles is saved in list of recently played titles.\tGeneral\nxenia\t\u0001\tGeneral\tdisable_doubleclick_fullscreen\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tAllows the user to disable the behavior where a fast double-click causes Xenia to enter fullscreen mode.\tGeneral\nxenia\t\u0001\tAPU\tapu\tSTRING\tany\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\t\u0001\tAPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU\tgpu\tSTRING\tany\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\t\u0001\tGPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tHID\thid\tSTRING\tany\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\t\u0001\tHID\nxenia\t\u0001\tStorage\tmount_scratch\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tEnable scratch mount\tStorage\nxenia\t\u0001\tStorage\tmount_cache\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tEnable cache mount\tStorage\nxenia\t\u0001\tStorage\tmount_memory_unit\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tEnable memory unit (MU) mount\tStorage\nxenia\t\u0001\tGeneral\tdiscord\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tEnable Discord rich presence\tGeneral\nxenia\t\u0001\tAPU\tmute\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tMutes all audio output.\tAPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tAPU\tenable_xmp\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tEnables Music Player playback.\tAPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tAPU\tffmpeg_verbose\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tVerbose FFmpeg output (debug and above)\tAPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tAPU\tuse_dedicated_xma_thread\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tEnables XMA decoding on separate thread. Disabled should produce better results, but decrease performance a bit.\tAPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tAPU\txma_decoder\tSTRING\tnew\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tDecoder version used to process XMA audio. Use: [fake, master, old, new]  fake:    No audio will be decoded.  master:    Version of decoder exactly like on base version of Xenia.  old:    Decoder based on master version of decoder with few improvements.  new:    New version of decoder. Provides highest stability, but isn't yet finished. \tAPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tCPU\tclock_no_scaling\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tDisable scaling code. Time management and locking is bypassed. Guest system time is directly pulled from host.\tCPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tCPU\tclock_source_raw\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tOn x64, Use the RDTSC instruction as the time source. Requires invariant TSC. On a64, Use the CNTVCT_EL0 register as the time source\tCPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tLogging\tlog_to_logcat\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tWrite log output to Android Logcat.\tLogging\nxenia\t\u0001\tLogging\tlog_to_stdout\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tWrite log output to stdout\tLogging\nxenia\t\u0001\tLogging\tlog_to_debugprint\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tDump the log to DebugPrint.\tLogging\nxenia\t\u0001\tLogging\tflush_log\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tFlush log file after each log line batch.\tLogging\nxenia\t\u0001\tLogging\tlog_mask\tINT\t0\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tDisables specific categorizes for more granular debug logging. Kernel = 1, Apu = 2, Cpu = 4, Gpu = 8.\tLogging\nxenia\t\u0001\tLogging\tlog_level\tINT\t2\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tMaximum level to be logged. (0=error, 1=warning, 2=info, 3=debug)\tLogging\nxenia\t\u0001\tWin32\twin32_high_resolution_timer\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tRequests high-resolution timer from the NT kernel\tWin32\nxenia\t\u0001\tWin32\twin32_mmcss\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tOpt in the Multimedia Class Scheduler Service (MMCSS) scheduling for prioritized access to CPU resources\tWin32\nxenia\t\u0001\tMemory\twritable_executable_memory\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tAllow mapping memory with both write and execute access, for simulating behavior on platforms where that's not supported\tMemory\nxenia\t\u0001\tLinux\tuse_shm_open\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tBack guest memory and the code cache with a /dev/shm file instead of memfd. Exposes both as named files that other processes can open to inspect guest memory or JIT output while a title runs.\tLinux\nxenia\t\u0001\tx64\tx64_extension_mask\tINT\t-1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tAllow the detection and utilization of specific instruction set features.     0 = x86_64 + AVX1     1 = AVX2     2 = FMA     4 = LZCNT     8 = BMI1    16 = BMI2    32 = F16C    64 = Movbe   128 = GFNI   256 = AVX512F   512 = AVX512VL  1024 = AVX512BW  2048 = AVX512DQ  4096 = AVX512VBMI    -1 = Detect and utilize all possible processor features \tx64\nxenia\t\u0001\ta64\ta64_extension_mask\tINT\t-1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tAllow the detection and utilization of specific instruction set features.     0 = armv8.0     1 = Large System Extensions(LSE) atomic operations     2 = FPCR.FZ flushes denormal inputs (skip software flush)    -1 = Detect and utilize all possible processor features \ta64\nxenia\t\u0001\tUI\tprofiler_dpi_scaling\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tApply window DPI scaling to the profiler.\tUI\nxenia\t\u0001\tUI\tshow_profiler\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tShow profiling UI by default.\tUI\nxenia\t\u0001\tConfig\tdefaults_date\tINT\t0\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tDo not modify - internal version of the default values in the config, for seamless updates if default value of any option is changed.\tConfig\nxenia\t\u0001\ta64\ta64_max_stackpoints\tINT\t65536\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tMax number of host->guest stack mappings we can record.\ta64\nxenia\t\u0001\ta64\ta64_enable_host_guest_stack_synchronization\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tRecords entries for guest/host stack mappings at function starts and checks for reentry at return sites. Has slight performance impact, but fixes crashes in games that use setjmp/longjmp.\ta64\nxenia\t\u0001\tx64\tmax_stackpoints\tINT\t65536\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tMax number of host->guest stack mappings we can record.\tx64\nxenia\t\u0001\tx64\tenable_host_guest_stack_synchronization\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tRecords entries for guest/host stack mappings at function starts and checks for reentry at return sites. Has slight performance impact, but fixes crashes in games that use setjmp/longjmp.\tx64\nxenia\t\u0001\tCPU\tdebugprint_trap_log\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tLog debugprint traps to the active debugger\tCPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tCPU\tignore_undefined_externs\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tDon't exit when an undefined extern is called.\tCPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tCPU\temit_source_annotations\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tAdd extra movs and nops to make disassembly easier to read.\tCPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tx64\tenable_incorrect_roundingmode_behavior\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tDisables the FPU/VMX MXCSR sharing workaround, potentially causing incorrect rounding behavior and denormal handling in VMX code. The workaround may cause reduced CPU performance but is a more accurate emulation\tx64\nxenia\t\u0001\tx64\talign_all_basic_blocks\tINT\t0\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tAligns the start of all basic blocks to N bytes. Only specify a power of 2, 16 is the recommended value. Results in larger icache usage, but potentially faster loops\tx64\nxenia\t\u0001\tx64\tinstrument_call_times\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tCompute time taken for functions, for profiling guest code\tx64\nxenia\t\u0001\tCPU\telide_e0_check\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tEliminate e0 check on some memory accesses, like to r13(tls) or r1(sp)\tCPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tx64\tenable_rmw_context_merging\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tPermit merging read-modify-write HIR instr sequences together into x86 instructions that use a memory operand.\tx64\nxenia\t\u0001\tx64\txop_rotates\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\trotate via xop\tx64\nxenia\t\u0001\tx64\txop_left_shifts\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tshl via xop\tx64\nxenia\t\u0001\tx64\txop_right_shifts\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tshr via xop\tx64\nxenia\t\u0001\tx64\txop_arithmetic_right_shifts\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tsar via xop\tx64\nxenia\t\u0001\tx64\txop_compares\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tcompare via xop\tx64\nxenia\t\u0001\tCPU\tuse_fast_dot_product\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tUse less accurate dot-product exception handling that converts all infinite results to QNaN.\tCPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tCPU\tno_round_to_single\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tNot for users, breaks games. Skip rounding double values to single precision and back\tCPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tCPU\tinline_loadclock\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tDirectly read cached guest clock without calling the LoadClock method (it gets repeatedly updated by calls from other threads)\tCPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tx64\tdelay_via_maybeyield\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\timplement the db16cyc instruction via MaybeYield, may improve scheduling of guest threads\tx64\nxenia\t\u0001\tCPU\tinline_mmio_access\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tInline constant MMIO loads and stores.\tCPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tCPU\tpermit_float_constant_evaluation\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tAllow float constant evaluation, may produce incorrect results and break games math\tCPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tCPU\tstore_all_context_values\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tDon't strip dead context stores to aid in debugging.\tCPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tCPU\tfull_optimization_even_with_debug\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tFor developer use to analyze the quality of the generated code, not intended for actual debugging of the code\tCPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tCPU\tcpu\tSTRING\tany\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tDoes nothing. CPU backend [any, x64].\tCPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tCPU\tload_module_map\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tLoads a .map for symbol names and to diff with the generated symbol database.\tCPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tCPU\tdisassemble_functions\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tDisassemble functions during generation.\tCPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tCPU\ttrace_functions\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tGenerate tracing for function statistics.\tCPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tCPU\ttrace_function_coverage\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tGenerate tracing for function instruction coverage statistics.\tCPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tCPU\ttrace_function_references\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tGenerate tracing for function address references.\tCPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tCPU\ttrace_function_data\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tGenerate tracing for function result data.\tCPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tCPU\tvalidate_hir\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tPerform validation checks on the HIR during compilation.\tCPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tCPU\tpvr\tINT\t7407360\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tKnown PVR's.  0x710200 = Used by Zephyr   0x710300 = Used by Zephyr  0x710500 = Used by Jasper  0x710700 = Default  0x710800 = Used by Corona V1 & V2 Processor version and revision number. Bits 0 to 15 are the version number. Bits 16 to 31 are the revision number. Note: Some XEXs (such as mfgbootlauncher.xex) may check for a value that's less than 0x710700.\tCPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tCPU\tbreak_on_instruction\tINT\t0\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tint3 before the given guest address is executed.\tCPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tCPU\tbreak_condition_gpr\tINT\t-1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tGPR compared to\tCPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tCPU\tbreak_condition_value\tINT\t0\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tvalue compared against\tCPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tCPU\tbreak_condition_op\tSTRING\teq\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tcomparison operator\tCPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tCPU\tbreak_condition_truncate\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\ttruncate value to 32-bits\tCPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tCPU\tbreak_on_debugbreak\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tint3 on JITed __debugbreak requests.\tCPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tCPU\tignore_trap_instructions\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tGenerate no code for powerpc trap instructions, can result in better performance in games that aggressively check with trap.\tCPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tCPU\tdisable_prefetch_and_cachecontrol\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tDisables translating ppc prefetch/cache flush instructions to host prefetch/cacheflush instructions. This may improve performance as these instructions were written with the Xbox 360's cache in mind, and modern processors do their own automatic prefetching.\tCPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tCPU\tno_reserved_ops\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tFor testing whether a game may have races with a broken reserved load/store impl\tCPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tCPU\tbreak_on_unimplemented_instructions\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tBreak to the host debugger (or crash if no debugger attached) if an unimplemented PowerPC instruction is encountered.\tCPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tCPU\tdump_translated_hir_functions\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tdumps translated hir\tCPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tCPU\tdisable_context_promotion\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tDisables Context Promotion optimizations, this may be needed for some sports games, but will reduce performance.\tCPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tGeneral\tdebug\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tAllow debugging and retain debug information.\tGeneral\nxenia\t\u0001\tCPU\tbreak_on_start\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tBreak into the debugger on startup.\tCPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tCPU\tdebug_symbol_loader\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tEnable dbghelp debug logging and validation.\tCPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tCPU\tdisable_instruction_infocache\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tDisables caching records of called instructions/mmio accesses.\tCPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tCPU\twritable_code_segments\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tEnables a program to write to its own code segments in memory.\tCPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tCPU\tenable_early_precompilation\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tEnable pre-compiling guest functions that we know we've called/that we've recognized as being functions via simple heuristics, good for error finding/stress testing with the JIT\tCPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tUI\timgui_debug\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tShow ImGui debugging tools.\tUI\nxenia\t\u0001\tGeneral\ttime_scalar\tFLOAT\t1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tScalar used to speed or slow time (1x, 2x, 1/2x, etc).\tGeneral\nxenia\t\u0001\tGeneral\tlaunch_module\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tExecutable to launch from the .iso or the package instead of default.xex or the module specified by the game. Leave blank to launch the default module.\tGeneral\nxenia\t\u0001\tGeneral\tallow_game_relative_writes\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tNot useful to non-developers. Allows code to write to paths relative to game://. Used for generating test data to compare with original hardware. \tGeneral\nxenia\t\u0001\tGeneral\tpriority_class\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tForces Xenia to use different process priority than default one. It might affect performance and cause unexpected bugs. Possible values: 0 - Normal, 1 - Above normal, 2 - High\tGeneral\nxenia\t\u0001\tLogging\tlog_guest_driven_gpu_register_written_values\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tOnly does anything in debug builds, if set will log every write to a gpu register done by a guest. Does not log writes that are done by the CP on its own, just ones the guest makes or instructs it to make.\tLogging\nxenia\t\u0001\tLogging\tdisassemble_pm4\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tOnly does anything in debug builds, if set will disassemble and log all PM4 packets sent to the CP.\tLogging\nxenia\t\u0001\tLogging\tlog_ringbuffer_kickoff_initiator_bts\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tOnly does anything in debug builds, if set will log the pseudo-stacktrace of the guest thread that wrote the new read position.\tLogging\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU\tclear_memory_page_state\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tRefresh state of memory pages to enable gpu written data. (Use for 'Team Ninja' Games to fix missing character models)\tGPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU\tocclusion_query\tSTRING\tfast\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tControls hardware occlusion query behavior for EVENT_WRITE_ZPD. Used for effects like lens flares, object culling, and auto-exposure.  fake: Write a fake result without asking the GPU. Safe for most games,        though some effects may look slightly wrong.  fast: Ask the GPU but don't wait for the answer. Writes a cached        result immediately and updates it when the GPU catches up.        Cached results bias toward visible when guessing. (default)  fast-alt: Variant of fast mode that keeps cached zero results for            unresolved reports. May improve effects relying on precise            visibility, but may be less stable for occlusion culling.  strict: Ask the GPU and wait for the real result before continuing.          Most accurate, but may be somewhat less performant.\tGPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU\tocclusion_query_full_counters\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tControls in-shader emulation of the ZFail, StencilFail and Total ZPD counters to supplement both native and counter-based ZPass testing. Most titles only use the ZPass counter, so this is off by default since it's typically slow and rife with readback sync. RTV/FBO approximates Total and ZFail, whereas ROV/FSI uses depth/stencil tests in-shader to count everything like Xenos does.\tGPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU\tocclusion_query_viz\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tEnables VIZ_QUERY (VIZ) visibility tests for draws with a VIZ token. VIZ is the 360's version of conditional rendering / predication queries. Titles mostly use it to combat overdraw, but it can also be used for post-process effects like lens flares. When enabled, coarse occlusion queries feed predicates which, when available, can skip draws that aren't visible. Since VIZ is primarily a GPU mechanism, most readback sync is avoided. With that said, VIZ and standard occlusion queries can both cause a noticeable penalty with ROV and FSI, especially when combined.\tGPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU\treadback_resolve\tSTRING\tnone\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tControls CPU readback of render-to-texture resolve results.  fast: Read from previous frame (1 frame delay, no GPU stall, slight performance hit)  full: Wait for GPU to finish (accurate but slow, GPU-CPU sync stall)  none: Disable readback completely (some games render better without it)\tGPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU\treadback_resolve_half_pixel_offset\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tWhen resolution scaling and readback resolve are enabled, resolve downscaling keeps one supersample out of each scaled pixel block. This selects the center of the block instead of the top-left corner, which can be closer to where the GPU would have sampled the original pixel, and can help with thin features and edge coverage. Both choices give a real rendered value, but they can disagree where geometry edges fall inside a pixel block. This matters when the CPU reads the resolve as data instead of an image, such as for gamma correction readbacks, occlusion checks, and GPU buffers reused later in the frame.\tGPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU\treadback_memexport\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tRead data written by memory export in shaders on the CPU. This may be needed in some games (but many only access exported data on the GPU, and this flag isn't needed to handle such behavior), but causes mid-frame synchronization, so it has a huge performance impact.\tGPU\n",
    "xenia\t\u0001\tD3D12\td3d12_bindless\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tUse bindless resources where available - may improve performance, but may make debugging more complicated.\tD3D12\nxenia\t\u0001\tD3D12\td3d12_submit_on_primary_buffer_end\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tSubmit the command list when a PM4 primary buffer ends if it's possible to submit immediately to try to reduce frame latency.\tD3D12\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU.Debug\tnative_stencil_value_output_d3d12_intel\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tAllow stencil reference output usage on Direct3D 12 on Intel GPUs - not working on UHD Graphics 630 as of March 2021 (driver 27.20.0100.8336).\tGPU.Debug\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU\trender_target_path_d3d12\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tRender target emulation path to use on Direct3D 12. Use: [any, rtv, rov]  rtv:   Host render targets and fixed-function blending and depth / stencil testing, copying between render targets when needed.   Lower accuracy (limited pixel format support).   Performance limited primarily by render target layout changes requiring copying, but generally higher.  rov:   Manual pixel packing, blending and depth / stencil testing, with free render target layout changes.   Requires a GPU supporting rasterizer-ordered views.   Highest accuracy (all pixel formats handled in software).   Performance limited primarily by overdraw.   On AMD drivers, currently causes shader compiler crashes in many cases.  Any other value:   Choose what is considered the most optimal for the system (currently always RTV because the ROV path is much slower now, except for Intel GPUs, which have a bug in stencil testing that causes Xbox 360 Direct3D 9 clears not to work).\tGPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tD3D12\td3d12_dxbc_disasm\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tDisassemble DXBC shaders after generation.\tD3D12\nxenia\t\u0001\tD3D12\td3d12_dxbc_disasm_dxilconv\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tDisassemble DXBC shaders after conversion to DXIL, if DXIL shaders are supported by the OS, and DirectX Shader Compiler DLLs available at https://github.com/microsoft/DirectXShaderCompiler/releases are present.\tD3D12\nxenia\t\u0001\tD3D12\td3d12_pipeline_creation_threads\tINT\t-1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tNumber of threads used for graphics pipeline creation. -1 to calculate automatically (75% of logical CPU cores), a positive number to specify the number of threads explicitly (up to the number of logical CPU cores), 0 to disable multithreaded pipeline creation.\tD3D12\nxenia\t\u0001\tD3D12\td3d12_tessellation_wireframe\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tDisplay tessellated surfaces as wireframe for debugging.\tD3D12\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU.Debug\texecute_unclipped_draw_vs_on_cpu\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tExecute the vertex shader for draws with clipping disabled, primarily screen-space draws (such as clears), on the CPU when possible to estimate the extent of the EDRAM involved in the draw. Enabling this may significantly improve GPU performance as otherwise up to the entire EDRAM may be considered used in draws without clipping, potentially resulting in spurious EDRAM range ownership transfer round trips between host render targets. Also, on hosts where certain render target formats have to be emulated in a lossy way (for instance, 16-bit fixed-point via 16-bit floating-point), this prevents corruption of other render targets located after the current ones in the EDRAM by lossy range ownership transfers done for those draws.\tGPU.Debug\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU.Debug\texecute_unclipped_draw_vs_on_cpu_with_scissor\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tDon't restrict the usage of execute_unclipped_draw_vs_on_cpu to only non-scissored draws (with the right and the bottom sides of the scissor rectangle at 8192 or beyond) even though if the scissor rectangle is present, it's usually sufficient for esimating the height of the render target. Enabling this may cause excessive processing of vertices on the CPU, as some games draw rectangles (for their UI, for instance) without clipping, but with a proper scissor rectangle.\tGPU.Debug\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU\tresolve_resolution_scale_fill_half_pixel_offset\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tWhen using resolution scaling, apply the hack that stretches the first surely covered host pixel in the left and top sides of render target resolve areas to eliminate the gap caused by the half-pixel offset (this is necessary for certain games to display the scene graphics).\tGPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU\tdepth_bias_shader_offset\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tRoute decal host render target draws with polygon offset through shader depth. This avoids Z-fighting in games that rely on tiny depth bias values that host fixed function depth bias cannot reproduce reliably.This likely causes some minor performance penalty, but the cost should be minimal if only a small portion of the scene is affected.\tGPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU\twindow_offset_in_edram\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tRenders every tile of a predicated tiling frame at the same position as the depth prepass by applying the window offset in EDRAM rather than the viewport. Fixes depth artifacts in the bottom tile of the screen. Disable this if tiles start shifting or banding. Works on every render target path. ROV and FSI apply it to every tile since their pixel shaders directly address EDRAM and can offset sideways or past the end of EDRAM, RTV and FBO keep sideways offsets, and tiles that would run past the target, in the viewport.\tGPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU.Debug\tdxbc_switch\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tUse switch rather than if for flow control. Turning this off or on may improve stability, though this heavily depends on the driver - on AMD, it's recommended to have this set to true, as some titles appear to crash when if is used for flow control (possibly the shader compiler tries to flatten them). On Intel HD Graphics, this is ignored because of a crash with the switch instruction.\tGPU.Debug\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU.Debug\tdxbc_source_map\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tDisassemble Xenos instructions as comments in the resulting DXBC for debugging.\tGPU.Debug\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU\tuse_fuzzy_alpha_epsilon\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tUse approximate compare for alpha values to prevent flickering on NVIDIA graphics cards\tGPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU.Debug\ttrace_gpu_stream\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tTrace all GPU packets.\tGPU.Debug\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU.Debug\ttrace_gpu_frames\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tComma-separated frame numbers to capture as single frame GPU traces, the same way as a manual frame trace request, for example \"300,1200\". Frames are counted by the swaps before them, and each trace is named after its frame number.\tGPU.Debug\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU\tvsync\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tEnable VSYNC.\tGPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU\tframerate_limit\tINT\t0\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tMaximum frames per second. 0 = Unlimited frames. Defaults to 60, when set to 0, and VSYNC is enabled.\tGPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU\tgpu_allow_invalid_fetch_constants\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tAllow texture and vertex fetch constants with invalid type - generally unsafe because the constant may contain completely invalid values, but may be used to bypass fetch constant type errors in certain games until the real reason why they're invalid is found.\tGPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU\tgpu_allow_invalid_upload_range\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tAllows games to read data from pages that are marked as no access.\tGPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU.Debug\tnon_seamless_cube_map\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tDisable filtering between cube map faces near edges where possible (Vulkan with VK_EXT_non_seamless_cube_map) to reproduce the Direct3D 9 behavior.\tGPU.Debug\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU.Debug\thalf_pixel_offset\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tEnable support of vertex half-pixel offset (D3D9 PA_SU_VTX_CNTL PIX_CENTER). Generally games are aware of the half-pixel offset, and having this enabled is the correct behavior (disabling this may significantly break post-processing in some games), but in certain games it might have been ignored, resulting in slight blurriness of UI textures, for instance, when they are read between texels rather than at texel centers, or the leftmost/topmost pixels may not be fully covered when MSAA is used with fullscreen passes.\tGPU.Debug\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU\tocclusion_query_fake_lower_threshold\tINT\t80\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tLower end of the fake sample count value written on EVENT_WRITE_ZPD when real occlusion queries are disabled. -1 writes nothing, resulting in some games that sit and hang. 0 means the fake result stays fully occluded.\tGPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU\tocclusion_query_fake_upper_threshold\tINT\t100\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tUpper end of the fake sample count value written on EVENT_WRITE_ZPD when real occlusion queries are disabled. Keep this higher than occlusion_query_fake_lower_threshold. Ignored if occlusion_query_fake_lower_threshold is -1.\tGPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU\tanisotropic_override\tINT\t-1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tForces anisotropic filtering (AF) for eligible textures. Higher values keep textures sharper at oblique angles at the cost of GPU bandwidth, though most GPUs handle up to 16x fine. In rare cases, forcing AF can introduce visual artifacts.  -1 = No override   0 = Disable anisotropic filtering   1 = Force 1x anisotropic filtering   2 = Force 2x anisotropic filtering   3 = Force 4x anisotropic filtering   4 = Force 8x anisotropic filtering   5 = Force 16x anisotropic filtering\tGPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU.Debug\tno_discard_stencil_in_transfer_pipelines\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tSkip stencil bit discard in render target transfer pipelines. May improve performance on some GPUs.\tGPU.Debug\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU\tgpu_3d_to_2d_texture\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tHandle shaders that sample 3D textures as 2D by creating a 2D texture from slice 0 of the guest memory.\tGPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU\tasync_shader_compilation\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tCompile shaders and create pipelines asynchronously in background threads. Eliminates shader compilation stutter but may cause brief rendering artifacts while pipelines are being created. When disabled, pipelines are created synchronously which causes stutter but no visual artifacts.\tGPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU\tforce_depth_clamp\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tUse host depth clamping instead of near and far plane clipping when guest clipping is enabled. X/Y/W clipping is unaffected. On Vulkan, this requires depthClamp support.\tGPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU\tmulsc_round_toward_zero\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tRound mulsc products toward zero instead of to nearest even. This fixes bad geometry in several Volition Engine titles and possibly others. This rounding behavior hasn't been confirmed on real hardware, so it's disabled by default.\tGPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU\txenos_sample_positions\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tRasterize 2x and 4x MSAA render targets at the Xenos sample positions, like real hardware, if the GPU and driver support it. Only applies to RTV/FBO - ROV/FSI render targets always use Xenos positions since they safely map coverage and calculate depth in-shader.\tGPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU\ttexture_point_snap\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tSnap normalized point sampled 2D texture coordinates to texel centers. Fixes texture seams in titles that use virtual textures, e.g. idTech 5, but may cause rendering issues in other titles.\tGPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tVideo\tcustom_internal_display_resolution_x\tINT\t0\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tCustom width. See internal_display_resolution. Range 1-1920.\tVideo\nxenia\t\u0001\tVideo\tcustom_internal_display_resolution_y\tINT\t0\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tCustom height. See internal_display_resolution. Range 1-1080. \tVideo\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU.Debug\tstore_shaders\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tStore shaders persistently and load them when loading games to avoid runtime spikes and freezes when playing the game not for the first time.\tGPU.Debug\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU.Debug\tforce_convert_triangle_fans_to_lists\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tFor host graphics API downlevel support testing only, force CPU conversion of triangle fans to triangle lists even if the host supports triangle fan primitives natively.\tGPU.Debug\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU.Debug\tforce_convert_line_loops_to_strips\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tFor host graphics API downlevel support testing only, force CPU conversion of line loops to line strips even if the host supports line loop primitives natively.\tGPU.Debug\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU.Debug\tforce_convert_quad_lists_to_triangle_lists\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tFor host graphics API downlevel support testing only, force CPU conversion of quad lists to quad strips even if the host supports quad list primitives natively or via geometry shader emulation. May also be useful for graphics debugging when the debugger doesn't display the geometry generated by geometry shaders properly.\tGPU.Debug\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU.Debug\tignore_32bit_vertex_index_support\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tFor host graphics API downlevel testing only (useful only for Qualcomm Adreno 4xx-level host GPU testing), force indirection or pre-masking and pre-swapping of 32-bit vertex indices as if the host only supports 24-bit indices.\tGPU.Debug\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU.Debug\tprimitive_processor_cache_min_indices\tINT\t4096\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tSmallest number of guest indices to store in the cache to try reusing later in the same frame if processing (such as primitive type conversion or reset index replacement) is performed. Setting this to a very high value may result in excessive CPU processing, while a very low value may result in excessive locking and lookups. Negative values disable caching.\tGPU.Debug\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU.Debug\tdebug_msaa_2x_as_4x\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tUse 4x MSAA with 2 samples instead of native 2x MSAA when available. For scalability testing on host GPU APIs where 2x is not mandatory. MSAA will be of a similar or worse quality and use more memory.\tGPU.Debug\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU.Debug\tdepth_transfer_not_equal_test\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tWhen transferring data between depth render targets, use the \"not equal\" test to avoid writing rewriting depth via shader depth output if it's the same as the one currently in the depth buffer in case of round trips of the data. Settings this to true may make transfer round trips more friendly to depth compression depending on how the GPU implements it (as arbitrary depth output may result in it being disabled completely), which is beneficial to subsequent rendering, while setting this to false may reduce bandwidth usage during transfers as the previous depth won't need to be read.\tGPU.Debug\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU\tdepth_float24_round\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tWhether to round to the nearest even, rather than truncating (rounding towards zero), the depth when converting it to 24-bit floating-point (20e4) from the host precision (32-bit floating point) when using a host depth buffer. false:  Recommended.  The conversion may move the depth values farther away from the camera.  Without depth_float24_convert_in_pixel_shader:   The \"greater or equal\" depth test function continues to work fine if the full host precision depth data is lost, it's still possible to draw another pass of the same geometry with it.   (See the description of depth_float24_convert_in_pixel_shader for more information about full precision depth data loss.)  With depth_float24_convert_in_pixel_shader:   Faster - the pixel shader for hidden surfaces may still be skipped (using conservative depth output). true:  Only for special cases of issues caused by minor 32-bit floating-point rounding errors, for instance, when the game tries to draw something at the camera plane by setting Z of the vertex position to W.  The conversion may move the depth values closer or farther.  Using the same rounding mode as in the Direct3D 9 reference rasterizer.  Without depth_float24_convert_in_pixel_shader:   Not possible to recover from a full host precision depth data loss - in subsequent passes of rendering the same geometry, half of the samples will be failing the depth test with the \"greater or equal\" depth test function.  With depth_float24_convert_in_pixel_shader:   Slower - depth rejection before the pixel shader is not possible. When the depth buffer is emulated in software (via the fragment shader interlock / rasterizer-ordered view), this is ignored, and rounding to the nearest even is always done.\tGPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU\tdepth_float24_convert_in_pixel_shader\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tWhether to convert the depth values to 24-bit floating-point (20e4) from the host precision (32-bit floating point) directly in the pixel shaders of guest draws when using a host depth buffer. This prevents visual artifacts (interleaved stripes of parts of surfaces rendered and parts not rendered, having either the same width in case of the \"greater or equal\" depth test function, or the former being much thinner than the latter with the \"equal\" function) if the full host precision depth data is lost. This issue may happen if the game reloads the depth data previously evicted from the EDRAM to the RAM back to the EDRAM, but the EDRAM region that previously contained that depth buffer was overwritten by another depth buffer, or the game loads it to a different location in the EDRAM than it was previously placed at, thus Xenia is unable to restore the depth data with the original precision, and instead falls back to converting the lower-precision values, so in subsequent rendering passes for the same geometry, the actual depth values of the surfaces don't match those stored in the depth buffer anymore. This is a costly option because it makes the GPU unable to use depth buffer compression, and also with MSAA, forces the pixel shader to run for every subpixel sample rather than for the entire pixel, making pixel shading 2 or 4 times heavier depending on the MSAA sample count. The rounding direction is controlled by the depth_float24_round configuration variable. Note that with depth_float24_round = true, this becomes even more costly because pixel shaders must be executed regardless of whether the surface is behind the previously drawn surfaces. With depth_float24_round = false, conservative depth output is used, however, so depth rejection before the pixel shader may still work. If sample-rate shading is not supported by the host GPU, the conversion in the pixel shader is done only when MSAA is not used. When the depth buffer is emulated in software (via the fragment shader interlock / rasterizer-ordered view), this is ignored because 24-bit depth is always used directly.\tGPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU\tdraw_resolution_scaled_texture_offsets\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tApply offsets from texture fetch instructions taking resolution scale into account for render-to-texture, for more correct shadow filtering, bloom, etc., in some cases.\tGPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU\tdraw_resolution_scale_threshold\tINT\t0\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tSurface pitch in pixels at or below render targets skip being upscaled by draw_resolution_scale_x/y. 0 disables it. Small offscreen surfaces like bloom or depth of field buffers often break when upscaled and keeping them native avoids that. The pitch is compared after alignment to 80 pixel EDRAM tiles, so prefer conservative values, only as high as the broken effects need. Host render targets only.\tGPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU.Debug\tgamma_render_target_as_unorm16\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tWhen the host can't write 8 bits per component pixels with piecewise linear gamma encoding directly with correct blending, use the 16-bit unsigned normalized format, if supported, for conceptually correct 8_8_8_8_GAMMA render target format blending in linear color space. Greatly increases accuracy for this format, but may result in render target copying costs if the game switches between 8_8_8_8_GAMMA and 8_8_8_8 views for the same EDRAM render target.\tGPU.Debug\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU.Debug\tmrt_edram_used_range_clamp_to_min\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tWith host render targets, if multiple render targets are bound, estimate the EDRAM range modified in any of them to be not bigger than the distance between any two render targets in the EDRAM, rather than allowing the last one claim the rest of the EDRAM. Has effect primarily on draws without viewport clipping. Setting this to false results in higher accuracy in rare cases, but may increase the amount of copying that needs to be done sometimes.\tGPU.Debug\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU\tnative_stencil_value_output\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tUse pixel shader stencil reference output where available for purposes like copying between render targets. Can be disabled for scalability testing, in this case, much more expensive drawing of 8 quads will be done.\tGPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU.Debug\tsnorm16_render_target_full_range\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tWhen the host can only support 16_16 and 16_16_16_16 render targets as -1...1, remap -32...32 to -1...1 to use the full possible range of values, at the expense of multiplicative blending correctness.\tGPU.Debug\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU.Debug\texecute_unclipped_draw_vs_on_cpu_for_psi_render_backend\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tIf execute_unclipped_draw_vs_on_cpu is enabled, execute the vertex shader for unclipped draws on the CPU even when using the pixel shader interlock (rasterizer-ordered view) implementation of the render backend on the host, for which no expensive copying between host render targets is needed when the ownership of a EDRAM range is changed. If this is enabled, excessive barriers may be eliminated when switching between different render targets in separate EDRAM locations.\tGPU.Debug\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU.Debug\taliased_depth_read_only\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tMatches interlock behavior by handling disjoint color and depth aliases for host render targets, keeping read-only depth bound when color writes only the unused stencil bits. May slightly increase overhead from keeping both host targets live and bound.\tGPU.Debug\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU\tshader_input_type\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\t'vs', 'ps', or unspecified to infer from the given filename.\tGPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU\tshader_input_little_endian\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tWhether the input shader binary is little-endian (from an Arm device with the Qualcomm Adreno 200, for instance).\tGPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU\tshader_output_type\tSTRING\tucode\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tTranslator to use: [ucode, spirv, spirvtext, dxbc, dxbctext].\tGPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU\tvertex_shader_output_type\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tType of the host interface to produce the vertex or domain shader for: [vertex or unspecified, linedomaincp, linedomainpatch, triangledomaincp, triangledomainpatch, quaddomaincp, quaddomainpatch].\tGPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU\tshader_output_bindless_resources\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tOutput host shader with bindless resources used.\tGPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU\tshader_output_pixel_shader_interlock\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tOutput host shader with a render backend implementation based on pixel shader interlock.\tGPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU\tspirv_disable_rounding_mode_rte\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tDisable RoundingModeRTE capability in SPIR-V shaders. Enable this to allow shader debugging in RenderDoc, which doesn't support this capability.\tGPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU\tdraw_resolution_scale_x\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tInteger pixel width scale used for scaling the rendering resolution opaquely to the game. Values from 1 to 7 may be supported, depending on device capabilities. Requires sparse binding (Vulkan) or tiled resources (D3D12) for scales above 1x1. The emulator will automatically clamp to the maximum supported scale if the requested value exceeds device limits. Various effects and parts of game rendering pipelines may work incorrectly as pixels become ambiguous from the game's perspective and because half-pixel offset (which normally doesn't affect coverage when MSAA isn't used) becomes full-pixel.\tGPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU\tdraw_resolution_scale_y\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tInteger pixel width scale used for scaling the rendering resolution opaquely to the game. See draw_resolution_scale_x for more information.\tGPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU.Debug\ttexture_cache_memory_limit_soft\tINT\t384\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tMaximum host texture memory usage (in megabytes) above which old textures will be destroyed.\tGPU.Debug\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU.Debug\ttexture_cache_memory_limit_soft_lifetime\tINT\t30\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tSeconds a texture should be unused to be considered old enough to be deleted if texture memory usage exceeds texture_cache_memory_limit_soft.\tGPU.Debug\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU.Debug\ttexture_cache_memory_limit_hard\tINT\t768\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tMaximum host texture memory usage (in megabytes) above which textures will be destroyed as soon as possible.\tGPU.Debug\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU.Debug\ttexture_cache_memory_limit_render_to_texture\tINT\t24\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tPart of the host texture memory budget (in megabytes) that will be scaled by the current drawing resolution scale. If texture_cache_memory_limit_soft, for instance, is 384, and this is 24, it will be assumed that the game will be using roughly 24 MB of render-to-texture (resolve) targets and 384 - 24 = 360 MB of regular textures - so with 2x2 resolution scaling, the soft limit will be 360 + 96 MB, and with 3x3, it will be 360 + 216 MB.\tGPU.Debug\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU.Debug\ttiled_shared_memory\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tEnable tiled/sparse resources for efficient large address space support. Disable for graphics debugger compatibility.\tGPU.Debug\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU\ttexture_dump\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tDump textures to DDS\tGPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tVulkan\tvulkan_depth_bias_force_unorm\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tApply the depth bias in constant units on float depth buffers where VK_EXT_depth_bias_control supports it, so the bias keeps its absolute size at every depth. Otherwise, the bias unit of a float depth buffer shrinks with the depth, and decals may Z-fight, especially with reversed depth.\tVulkan\nxenia\t\u0001\tVulkan\tvulkan_pipeline_creation_threads\tINT\t-1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tNumber of threads used for graphics pipeline creation. -1 to calculate automatically (75% of logical CPU cores), a positive number to specify the number of threads explicitly (up to the number of logical CPU cores), 0 to disable multithreaded pipeline creation.\tVulkan\nxenia\t\u0001\tGPU\trender_target_path_vulkan\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tRender target emulation path to use on Vulkan. Use: [any, fbo, fsi]  fbo:   Host framebuffers and fixed-function blending and depth / stencil testing, copying between render targets when needed.   Lower accuracy (limited pixel format support).   Performance limited primarily by render target layout changes requiring copying, but generally higher.  fsi:   Manual pixel packing, blending and depth / stencil testing, with free render target layout changes.   Requires a GPU supporting fragment shader interlock.   Highest accuracy (all pixel formats handled in software).   Performance limited primarily by overdraw.  Any other value:   Choose what is considered the most optimal for the system (currently always FB because the FSI path is much slower now).\tGPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tVulkan\tvulkan_sparse_shared_memory\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tEnable sparse binding for shared memory emulation. Disabling it increases video memory usage - a 512 MB buffer is created - but allows graphics debuggers that don't support sparse binding to work.\tVulkan\nxenia\t\u0001\tGeneral\thid\tSTRING\tany\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tInput system. Use: [any, nop, sdl, winkey, xinput]\tGeneral\nxenia\t\u0001\tHID\tguide_button\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tForward guide button presses to guest.\tHID\nxenia\t\u0001\tHID\tvibration\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tToggle controller vibration.\tHID\nxenia\t\u0001\tHID\tleft_stick_deadzone_percentage\tFLOAT\t0.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tDefines deadzone level for left stick. Allowed range [0.0-1.0].\tHID\nxenia\t\u0001\tHID\tright_stick_deadzone_percentage\tFLOAT\t0.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tDefines deadzone level for right stick. Allowed range [0.0-1.0].\tHID\nxenia\t\u0001\tHID\tkeyboard_mode\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tAllows user do specify keyboard working mode. Possible values: 0 - Disabled, 1 - Enabled, 2 - Passthrough. Passthrough requires controller being connected!\tHID\nxenia\t\u0001\tHID\tkeyboard_user_index\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tController port that keyboard emulates. [0, 3] - Keyboard is assigned to selected slot. Passthrough does not require assigning slot.\tHID\nxenia\t\u0001\tHID\tcontroller_subtypes\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tWhat kind of controller each slot is reported as, when the kind SDL reports is not what the title expects: a comma separated list of slot:kind, e.g. \"0:guitar\". Kinds: gamepad, guitar, guitar_bass, guitar_alternate, drums, wheel, arcade_stick, flight_stick, dance_pad, arcade_pad. Guitar Hero and Rock Band read this to decide whether they are being played on an instrument or on a pad. Empty, the default, leaves every slot as SDL reports it.\tHID\nxenia\t\u0001\tHID\tguitar_whammy_on_stick\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tSlots whose guitar sends its whammy bar as the left trigger, e.g. \"0\" or \"0,2\". The trigger is sent to the right stick's X instead, where titles read the whammy, and that axis's own input (a tilt sensor on some guitars) is dropped. Only for a slot reported as a guitar. Empty, the default, changes nothing.\tHID\nxenia\t\u0001\tUI\theadless\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tDon't display any UI, using defaults for prompts as needed.\tUI\nxenia\t\u0001\tLogging\tlog_high_frequency_kernel_calls\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tLog kernel calls with the kHighFrequency tag.\tLogging\nxenia\t\u0001\tKernel\tapply_title_update\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tApply title updates.\tKernel\nxenia\t\u0001\tKernel\tallow_incompatible_title_update\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tAllow title updates with mismatched signatures to be applied.\tKernel\nxenia\t\u0001\tKernel\tkernel_build_version\tINT\t1888\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tDefine current kernel version\tKernel\nxenia\t\u0001\tUI\tshow_achievement_notification\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tShow achievement notification on screen.\tUI\nxenia\t\u0001\tKernel\tdefault_achievements_backend\tSTRING\tGPD\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tDefines which achievements backend should be used as an default. Possible options: GPD.\tKernel\nxenia\t\u0001\tProfiles\tlogged_profile_slot_0_xuid\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tXUID of the profile to load on boot in slot 0\tProfiles\nxenia\t\u0001\tProfiles\tlogged_profile_slot_1_xuid\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tXUID of the profile to load on boot in slot 1\tProfiles\nxenia\t\u0001\tProfiles\tlogged_profile_slot_2_xuid\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tXUID of the profile to load on boot in slot 2\tProfiles\nxenia\t\u0001\tProfiles\tlogged_profile_slot_3_xuid\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tXUID of the profile to load on boot in slot 3\tProfiles\nxenia\t\u0001\tKernel\tallow_avatar_initialization\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tEnable Avatar Initialization Only set true when testing Avatar games. Certain games may crash due to requirement of full avatar implementation.\tKernel\nxenia\t\u0001\tContent\tlicense_mask\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tSet license mask for activated content.  0 = No licenses enabled.  1 = First license enabled. Generally the full version license in      Xbox Live Arcade titles.  -1 or 0xFFFFFFFF = All possible licenses enabled. Generally a                     bad idea, could lead to undefined behavior.\tContent\nxenia\t\u0001\tVideo\tavpack\tINT\t8\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tVideo modes  0 = PAL-60 Component (SD)  1 = Unused  2 = PAL-60 SCART  3 = 480p Component (HD)  4 = HDMI+A  5 = PAL-60 Composite/S-Video  6 = VGA  7 = TV PAL-60  8 = HDMI (default)\tVideo\nxenia\t\u0001\tKernel\tstaging_mode\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tEnables preview mode in dashboards to render debug information.\tKernel\nxenia\t\u0001\tUI\tstorage_selection_dialog\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tShow storage device selection dialog when the game requests it.\tUI\nxenia\t\u0001\tVideo\tenable_3d_mode\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tEnables usage of stereoscopic mode in titles.\tVideo\nxenia\t\u0001\tStorage\tforce_mount_devkit\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tForce devkit mount\tStorage\nxenia\t\u0001\tKernel\tconsole_type\tINT\t-1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tConsole Type Identifier: -1 - Retail, 0 - Development Kit, 1 - Test Kit\tKernel\nxenia\t\u0001\tMemory\tignore_offset_for_ranged_allocations\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tAllows to ignore 4k offset for physical allocations with provided range. Certain titles check if result matches provided lower range.\tMemory\nxenia\t\u0001\tKernel\tallow_mic_initialization\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tEnable Mic Initialization  Only set true when testing mic related functions\tKernel\nxenia\t\u0001\tKernel\tcl\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tSpecify additional command-line provided to guest.\tKernel\nxenia\t\u0001\tKernel\tkernel_debug_monitor\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tEnable debug monitor.\tKernel\nxenia\t\u0001\tKernel\tkernel_cert_monitor\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tEnable cert monitor.\tKernel\nxenia\t\u0001\tKernel\tkernel_pix\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tEnable PIX.\tKernel\nxenia\t\u0001\tLogging\tlog_string_format_kernel_calls\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tLog usage of print formatters like sprintf.\tLogging\nxenia\t\u0001\tVideo\tinterlaced\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tToggles interlaced mode.\tVideo\nxenia\t\u0001\tKernel\tkernel_display_gamma_type\tINT\t2\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tDisplay gamma type: 0 - linear, 1 - sRGB (CRT), 2 - BT.709 (HDTV), 3 - power specified via kernel_display_gamma_power.\tKernel\nxenia\t\u0001\tKernel\tkernel_display_gamma_power\tFLOAT\t2.22222233\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tDisplay gamma to use with kernel_display_gamma_type 3.\tKernel\nxenia\t\u0001\tKernel\tignore_thread_priorities\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tIgnores game-specified thread priorities.\tKernel\nxenia\t\u0001\tKernel\tignore_thread_affinities\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tIgnores game-specified thread affinities.\tKernel\nxenia\t\u0001\tKernel\tstack_size_multiplier_hack\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tA hack for games with setjmp/longjmp issues.\tKernel\nxenia\t\u0001\tKernel\tmain_xthread_stack_size_multiplier_hack\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tA hack for games with setjmp/longjmp issues.\tKernel\nxenia\t\u0001\tMemory\tprotect_zero\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tProtect the zero page from reads and writes.\tMemory\nxenia\t\u0001\tCPU\temit_inline_mmio_checks\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tEmit inline MMIO range checks for all I32 loads/stores instead of relying on exception-based MMIO detection.\tCPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tCPU\temit_mmio_aware_stores_for_recorded_exception_addresses\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tUses info gathered via record_mmio_access_exceptions to emit special stores that are faster than trapping the exception\tCPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tCPU\trecord_mmio_access_exceptions\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tFor guest addresses records whether we caught any mmio accesses for them. This info can then be used on a subsequent run to instruct the recompiler to emit checks\tCPU\nxenia\t\u0001\tMemory\tprotect_on_release\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tProtect released memory to prevent accesses.\tMemory\nxenia\t\u0001\tMemory\tscribble_heap\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tScribble specific or random value into all allocated heap memory.\tMemory\nxenia\t\u0001\tMemory\tscribble_heap_value\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tValue used to fill all allocated heap memory. 0 - Random value. Valid range: [1-255]\tMemory\nxenia\t\u0001\tGeneral\tapply_patches\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tEnables custom patching functionality\tGeneral\nxenia\t\u0001\tGeneral\tallow_plugins\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tAllows loading of plugins/trainers from plugins\\title_id\\plugin.xex. Plugin are homebrew xex modules which can be used for making mods. This feature is experimental.\tGeneral\nxenia\t\u0001\tD3D12\td3d12_allow_variable_refresh_rate_and_tearing\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tIn fullscreen, allow using variable refresh rate on displays supporting it. On displays not supporting VRR, screen tearing may occur in certain cases.\tD3D12\nxenia\t\u0001\tD3D12\td3d12_debug\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tEnable Direct3D 12 and DXGI debug layer.\tD3D12\nxenia\t\u0001\tD3D12\td3d12_break_on_error\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tBreak on Direct3D 12 validation errors.\tD3D12\nxenia\t\u0001\tD3D12\td3d12_break_on_warning\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tBreak on Direct3D 12 validation warnings.\tD3D12\nxenia\t\u0001\tD3D12\td3d12_adapter\tINT\t-1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tIndex of the DXGI adapter to use. -1 for any physical adapter, -2 for WARP software rendering.\tD3D12\nxenia\t\u0001\tD3D12\td3d12_queue_priority\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tGraphics (direct) command queue scheduling priority, 0 - normal, 1 - high, 2 - global realtime (requires administrator privileges, may impact system responsibility)\tD3D12\nxenia\t\u0001\tUI\tfont_size\tINT\t14\t0\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tAllows user to set custom font size.\tUI\nxenia\t\u0001\tGeneral\tnotification_sound_path\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tPath (including filename) to selected notification sound. Sound MUST be in wav format!\tGeneral\nxenia\t\u0001\tDisplay\thost_present_from_non_ui_thread\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tAllow the GPU emulation thread to present the guest output to the host surface directly instead of requesting the UI thread to do so through the host window system.\tDisplay\nxenia\t\u0001\tDisplay\tpresent_render_pass_clear\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tOn graphics backends where this is supported, use the clear render pass load operation in presentation instead of clear commands clearing only the letterbox area.\tDisplay\nxenia\t\u0001\tDisplay\tpresent_letterbox\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tMaintain aspect ratio when stretching by displaying bars around the image when there's no more overscan area to crop out.\tDisplay\nxenia\t\u0001\tDisplay\tpresent_safe_area_x\tINT\t100\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tPercentage of the image width that can be kept when presenting to maintain aspect ratio without letterboxing or stretching.\tDisplay\nxenia\t\u0001\tDisplay\tpresent_safe_area_y\tINT\t100\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tPercentage of the image height that can be kept when presenting to maintain aspect ratio without letterboxing or stretching.\tDisplay\nxenia\t\u0001\tVulkan\tvulkan_log_debug_messages\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tWrite Vulkan VK_EXT_debug_utils messages to the Xenia log, as opposed to the OS debug output.\tVulkan\nxenia\t\u0001\tVulkan\tvulkan_allow_present_mode_immediate\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tWhen available, allow the immediate presentation mode (1st priority), offering the lowest latency with the possibility of tearing in certain cases, and, depending on the configuration, variable refresh rate.\tVulkan\nxenia\t\u0001\tVulkan\tvulkan_allow_present_mode_mailbox\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tWhen available, allow the mailbox presentation mode (2nd priority), offering low latency without the possibility of tearing.\tVulkan\nxenia\t\u0001\tVulkan\tvulkan_allow_present_mode_fifo_relaxed\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tWhen available, allow the relaxed first-in-first-out presentation mode (3rd priority), which causes waiting for host display vertical sync, but may present with tearing if frames don't meet the host display refresh rate.\tVulkan\nxenia\t\u0001\tVulkan\tvulkan_semaphore_reuse_workaround\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tWait for presentation queue idle before each frame to prevent semaphore reuse. May fix rendering issues but causes significant performance loss.\tVulkan\nxenia\t\u0001\tVulkan\tvulkan_validation\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tEnable the Vulkan validation layer (VK_LAYER_KHRONOS_validation). Messages will be written to the Xenia log if 'vulkan_log_debug_messages' is enabled, or to the OS debug output otherwise.\tVulkan\nxenia\t\u0001\tVulkan\tvulkan_device\tINT\t-1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tIndex of the preferred Vulkan physical device, or -1 to use any compatible device.\tVulkan\nxenia\t\u0001\tUI\twindow_size_x\tINT\t1280\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tXenia window width\tUI\nxenia\t\u0001\tUI\twindow_size_y\tINT\t720\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tXenia window height\tUI\nxenia\t\u0001\tLogging\tenable_console\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tc28af1125d\t\u0001\tOpen a console window with the main window\tLogging\ncitron\t\u0001\tLibraryApplet\tcabinet_applet_mode\tENUM\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ECustom frontend\u001F1\u001EReal applet\t0\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tAmiibo editor\t\u0001\tLibrary Applet\ncitron\t\u0001\tLibraryApplet\tcontroller_applet_mode\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ECustom frontend\u001F1\u001EReal applet\t0\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tController configuration\t\u0001\tLibrary Applet\ncitron\t\u0001\tLibraryApplet\tdata_erase_applet_mode\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ECustom frontend\u001F1\u001EReal applet\t0\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tData erase\t\u0001\tLibrary Applet\ncitron\t\u0001\tLibraryApplet\terror_applet_mode\tENUM\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ECustom frontend\u001F1\u001EReal applet\t0\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tError\t\u0001\tLibrary Applet\n",
    "citron\t\u0001\tLibraryApplet\tnet_connect_applet_mode\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ECustom frontend\u001F1\u001EReal applet\t0\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tNet connect\t\u0001\tLibrary Applet\ncitron\t\u0001\tLibraryApplet\tplayer_select_applet_mode\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ECustom frontend\u001F1\u001EReal applet\t0\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tPlayer select\t\u0001\tLibrary Applet\ncitron\t\u0001\tLibraryApplet\tswkbd_applet_mode\tENUM\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ECustom frontend\u001F1\u001EReal applet\t0\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tSoftware keyboard\t\u0001\tLibrary Applet\ncitron\t\u0001\tLibraryApplet\tmii_edit_applet_mode\tENUM\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ECustom frontend\u001F1\u001EReal applet\t0\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tMii Edit\t\u0001\tLibrary Applet\ncitron\t\u0001\tLibraryApplet\tweb_applet_mode\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ECustom frontend\u001F1\u001EReal applet\t0\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tOnline web\t\u0001\tLibrary Applet\ncitron\t\u0001\tLibraryApplet\tshop_applet_mode\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ECustom frontend\u001F1\u001EReal applet\t0\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tShop\t\u0001\tLibrary Applet\ncitron\t\u0001\tLibraryApplet\tphoto_viewer_applet_mode\tENUM\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ECustom frontend\u001F1\u001EReal applet\t0\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tPhoto viewer\t\u0001\tLibrary Applet\ncitron\t\u0001\tLibraryApplet\toffline_web_applet_mode\tENUM\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ECustom frontend\u001F1\u001EReal applet\t0\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tOffline web\t\u0001\tLibrary Applet\ncitron\t\u0001\tLibraryApplet\tlogin_share_applet_mode\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ECustom frontend\u001F1\u001EReal applet\t0\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tLogin share\t\u0001\tLibrary Applet\ncitron\t\u0001\tLibraryApplet\twifi_web_auth_applet_mode\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ECustom frontend\u001F1\u001EReal applet\t0\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tWifi web auth\t\u0001\tLibrary Applet\ncitron\t\u0001\tLibraryApplet\tmy_page_applet_mode\tENUM\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ECustom frontend\u001F1\u001EReal applet\t0\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tMy page\t\u0001\tLibrary Applet\ncitron\t\u0001\tSystem\tqlaunch_enabled\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tEnable Home Menu (QLaunch)\tWhen enabled, pressing the Home button will launch the firmware's Home Menu. Requires firmware to be installed.\tSystem\ncitron\t\u0001\tAudio\toutput_engine\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EAuto\u001F1\u001ECubeb\u001F2\u001ESdl2\u001F3\u001EOpenAL\u001F4\u001ENull\u001F5\u001EOboe\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tOutput Engine\t\u0001\tAudio\ncitron\t\u0001\tSystem\tsound_index\tENUM\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EMono\u001F1\u001EStereo\u001F2\u001ESurround\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tSound Output Mode\t\u0001\tSystem Audio\ncitron\t\u0001\tAudio\tvolume\tINT\t100\t0\t200\t\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tVolume\t\u0001\tAudio\ncitron\t\u0001\tAudio\taudio_muted\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tMute audio\t\u0001\tAudio\ncitron\t\u0001\tCore\tuse_multi_core\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tMulticore CPU Emulation\tThis option increases CPU emulation thread use from 1 to the Switch's maximum of 4. This is mainly a debug option and shouldn't be disabled.\tCore\ncitron\t\u0001\tCore\tmemory_layout_mode\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001E4GB DRAM (Default)\u001F1\u001E6GB DRAM (Unsafe)\u001F2\u001E8GB DRAM (Unsafe)\u001F3\u001E10GB DRAM (Unsafe)\u001F4\u001E12GB DRAM (Unsafe)\u001F5\u001E14GB DRAM (Unsafe)\u001F6\u001E16GB DRAM (Unsafe)\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tMemory Layout\tIncreases the amount of emulated RAM from the stock 4GB of the retail Switch to the developer kit's 8/6GB. It's doesn't improve stability or performance and is intended to let big texture mods fit in emulated RAM. Enabling it will increase memory use. It is not recommended to enable unless a specific game with a texture mod needs it.\tCore\ncitron\t\u0001\tCore\tspeed_limit\tINT\t100\t0\t9999\t\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tLimit Speed Percent\tControls the game's maximum rendering speed, but it's up to each game if it runs faster or not. 200% for a 30 FPS game is 60 FPS, and for a 60 FPS game it will be 120 FPS. Disabling it means unlocking the framerate to the maximum your PC can reach.\tCore\ncitron\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpu_accuracy\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EAuto\u001F1\u001EAccurate\u001F2\u001EUnsafe\u001F3\u001EParanoid (disables most optimizations)\u001F4\u001EUltra Low (aggressive, may break some games)\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tAccuracy\tThis setting controls the accuracy of the emulated CPU. Don't change this unless you know what you are doing.\tCpu\ncitron\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpu_debug_mode\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\t\u0001\t\u0001\tCpu Debug\ncitron\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_page_tables\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\t\u0001\t\u0001\tCpu Debug\ncitron\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_block_linking\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\t\u0001\t\u0001\tCpu Debug\ncitron\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_return_stack_buffer\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\t\u0001\t\u0001\tCpu Debug\ncitron\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_fast_dispatcher\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\t\u0001\t\u0001\tCpu Debug\ncitron\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_context_elimination\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\t\u0001\t\u0001\tCpu Debug\ncitron\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_const_prop\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\t\u0001\t\u0001\tCpu Debug\ncitron\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_misc_ir\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\t\u0001\t\u0001\tCpu Debug\ncitron\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_reduce_misalign_checks\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\t\u0001\t\u0001\tCpu Debug\ncitron\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_fastmem\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\t\u0001\t\u0001\tCpu Debug\ncitron\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_fastmem_exclusives\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\t\u0001\t\u0001\tCpu Debug\ncitron\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_recompile_exclusives\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\t\u0001\t\u0001\tCpu Debug\ncitron\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_ignore_memory_aborts\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\t\u0001\t\u0001\tCpu Debug\ncitron\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_unsafe_unfuse_fma\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tUnfuse FMA (improve performance on CPUs without FMA)\tThis option improves speed by reducing accuracy of fused-multiply-add instructions on CPUs without native FMA support.\tCpu Unsafe\ncitron\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_unsafe_reduce_fp_error\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tFaster FRSQRTE and FRECPE\tThis option improves the speed of some approximate floating-point functions by using less accurate native approximations.\tCpu Unsafe\ncitron\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_unsafe_ignore_standard_fpcr\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tFaster ASIMD instructions (32 bits only)\tThis option improves the speed of 32 bits ASIMD floating-point functions by running with incorrect rounding modes.\tCpu Unsafe\ncitron\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_unsafe_inaccurate_nan\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tInaccurate NaN handling\tThis option improves speed by removing NaN checking. Please note this also reduces accuracy of certain floating-point instructions.\tCpu Unsafe\ncitron\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_unsafe_fastmem_check\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tDisable address space checks\tThis option improves speed by eliminating a safety check before every memory read/write in guest. Disabling it may allow a game to read/write the emulator's memory.\tCpu Unsafe\ncitron\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_unsafe_ignore_global_monitor\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tIgnore global monitor\tThis option improves speed by relying only on the semantics of cmpxchg to ensure safety of exclusive access instructions. Please note this may result in deadlocks and other race conditions.\tCpu Unsafe\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tbackend\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EVulkan\u001F1\u001ENull\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tAPI\tSwitches between the available graphics APIs. Vulkan is recommended in most cases.\tRenderer\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tvulkan_device\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tDevice\tThis setting selects the GPU to use with the Vulkan backend.\tRenderer\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tuse_disk_shader_cache\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tUse disk pipeline cache\tAllows saving shaders to storage for faster loading on following game boots. Disabling it is only intended for debugging.\tRenderer\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tuse_asynchronous_gpu_emulation\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tUse asynchronous GPU emulation\tUses an extra CPU thread for rendering. This option should always remain enabled.\tRenderer\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\taccelerate_astc\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ECPU\u001F1\u001EGPU\u001F2\u001ECPU Asynchronous\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tASTC Decoding Method\tThis option controls how ASTC textures should be decoded. CPU: Use the CPU for decoding, slowest but safest method. GPU: Use the GPU's compute shaders to decode ASTC textures, recommended for most games and users. CPU Asynchronously: Use the CPU to decode ASTC textures as they arrive. Completely eliminates ASTC decoding stuttering at the cost of rendering issues while the texture is being decoded.\tRenderer\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tuse_vsync\tENUM\t2\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EImmediate\u001F1\u001EMailbox\u001F2\u001EFifo\u001F3\u001EFifoRelaxed\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tVSync Mode\tFIFO (VSync) does not drop frames or exhibit tearing but is limited by the screen refresh rate. FIFO Relaxed is similar to FIFO but allows tearing as it recovers from a slow down. Mailbox can have lower latency than FIFO and does not tear but may drop frames. Immediate (no synchronization) just presents whatever is available and can exhibit tearing.\tRenderer\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tnvdec_emulation\tENUM\t2\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ENo Video Output\u001F1\u001ECPU Video Decoding\u001F2\u001EGPU Video Decoding (Default)\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tNVDEC emulation\tSpecifies how videos should be decoded. It can either use the CPU or the GPU for decoding, or perform no decoding at all (black screen on videos). In most cases, GPU decoding provides the best performance.\tRenderer\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tfullscreen_mode\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EBorderless Windowed\u001F1\u001EExclusive Fullscreen\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tFullscreen Mode\tThe method used to render the window in fullscreen. Borderless offers the best compatibility with the on-screen keyboard that some games request for input. Exclusive fullscreen may offer better performance and better Freesync/Gsync support.\tRenderer\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\taspect_ratio\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EDefault (16:9)\u001F1\u001EForce 4:3\u001F2\u001EForce 21:9\u001F3\u001EForce 16:10\u001F4\u001EForce 32:9\u001F5\u001EStretch to Window\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tAspect Ratio\tStretches the game to fit the specified aspect ratio. Switch games only support 16:9, so custom game mods are required to get other ratios. Also controls the aspect ratio of captured screenshots.\tRenderer\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tresolution_setup\tENUM\t3\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001E0.25X (180p/270p) [EXPERIMENTAL]\u001F1\u001E0.5X (360p/540p) [EXPERIMENTAL]\u001F2\u001E0.75X (540p/810p) [EXPERIMENTAL]\u001F3\u001E1X (720p/1080p)\u001F4\u001E1.5X (1080p/1620p) [EXPERIMENTAL]\u001F5\u001E2X (1440p/2160p)\u001F6\u001E3X (2160p/3240p)\u001F7\u001E4X (2880p/4320p)\u001F8\u001E5X (3600p/5400p)\u001F9\u001E6X (4320p/6480p)\u001F10\u001E7X (5040p/7560p)\u001F11\u001E8X (5760p/8640p)\u001F12\u001E1.25X (900p/1350p) [EXPERIMENTAL]\u001F13\u001E1.75X (1260p/1890p) [EXPERIMENTAL]\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tResolution\tForces the game to render at a different resolution. Higher resolutions require much more VRAM and bandwidth. Options lower than 1X can cause rendering issues.\tRenderer\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tscaling_filter\tENUM\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ENearest Neighbor\u001F1\u001EBilinear\u001F2\u001EBicubic\u001F3\u001EGaussian\u001F4\u001EScaleForce\u001F5\u001EScaleFX\u001F6\u001ELanczos\u001F7\u001EAMD FidelityFX™️ Super Resolution\u001F8\u001EAMD FidelityFX™️ Super Resolution 2.0\u001F9\u001ECRT EasyMode\u001F10\u001ECRT Royale\u001F11\u001ECAS (Contrast Adaptive Sharpening)\u001F12\u001EMaxEnum\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tWindow Adapting Filter\t\u0001\tRenderer\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tanti_aliasing\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ENone\u001F1\u001EFXAA\u001F2\u001ESMAA\u001F3\u001ETAA\u001F4\u001EMaxEnum\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tAnti-Aliasing Method\tThe anti-aliasing method to use. SMAA offers the best quality. FXAA has a lower performance impact and can produce a better and more stable picture under very low resolutions.\tRenderer\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tfsr_sharpening_slider\tINT\t25\t0\t200\t\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tFSR Sharpness\tDetermines how sharpened the image will look while using FSR's dynamic contrast.\tRenderer\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tcas_sharpening_slider\tINT\t50\t0\t100\t\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tCAS Sharpness\tDetermines the level of sharpening applied by the Contrast Adaptive Sharpening (CAS) filter.\tRenderer\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tcrt_scanline_strength\tFLOAT\t1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tCRT Scanline Strength\tControls the intensity of scanlines. Higher values create more pronounced horizontal lines.\tRenderer\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tcrt_curvature\tFLOAT\t0.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tCRT Curvature\tApplies barrel distortion to simulate the curved screen of a CRT monitor.\tRenderer\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tcrt_gamma\tFLOAT\t1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tCRT Gamma\tAdjusts the gamma correction curve. Higher values brighten the image, lower values darken it.\tRenderer\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tcrt_bloom\tFLOAT\t0.33\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tCRT Bloom\tControls the glow effect around bright areas, simulating phosphor persistence.\tRenderer\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tcrt_mask_type\tINT\t1\t0\t2\t\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tCRT Mask Type\tSelects the phosphor mask pattern: None, Aperture Grille (vertical stripes), or Shadow Mask (triangular pattern).\tRenderer\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tcrt_brightness\tFLOAT\t1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tCRT Brightness\tAdjusts overall brightness of the CRT effect. Use to compensate for darkening from other effects.\tRenderer\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tcrt_alpha\tFLOAT\t1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tCRT Alpha\tControls transparency of the CRT effect. Lower values make the effect more transparent.\tRenderer\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tlanczos_quality\tINT\t3\t2\t4\t\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tLanczos Quality\tThe quality of the Lanczos filter. Higher is sharper but more expensive.\tRenderer\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tfsr2_quality_mode\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EQuality\u001F1\u001EBalanced\u001F2\u001EPerformance\u001F3\u001EUltra Performance\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tFSR 2.0 Quality Mode\tSelects the quality mode for FSR 2.0 upscaling. Quality provides better image quality, Performance provides better performance.\tRenderer\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tframe_skipping\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EDisabled\u001F1\u001EEnabled\u001F2\u001EMaxEnum\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tFrame Skipping\tSkips frames to maintain performance when the system cannot keep up with the target frame rate.\tRenderer\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tframe_skipping_mode\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EAdaptive\u001F1\u001EFixed\u001F2\u001EMaxEnum\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tFrame Skipping Mode\tAdaptive mode skips frames based on performance, while Fixed mode skips a specific number of frames.\tRenderer\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tbg_red\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tbg_green\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tbg_blue\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tgpu_accuracy\tENUM\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ELow\u001F1\u001ENormal\u001F2\u001EHigh\u001F3\u001EExtreme\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tAccuracy Level\tGPU emulation accuracy. Most games render fine with Normal, but High is still required for some. Particles tend to only render correctly with High accuracy. Extreme should only be used for debugging. This option can be changed while playing. Some games may require booting on high to render properly.\tRenderer Advanced\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tmax_anisotropy\tENUM\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EAutomatic\u001F1\u001EDefault\u001F2\u001E2x\u001F3\u001E4x\u001F4\u001E8x\u001F5\u001E16x\u001F6\u001E32x\u001F7\u001E64x\u001F8\u001E128x\u001F9\u001E256x\u001F10\u001E512x\u001F11\u001E1024x\u001F12\u001E2048x\u001F13\u001E4096x\u001F14\u001E8192x\u001F15\u001E16384x\u001F16\u001E32768x\u001F17\u001E65536x\u001F18\u001E131072x\u001F19\u001E262144x\u001F20\u001E524288x\u001F21\u001E1048576x\u001F22\u001E2097152x\u001F23\u001E4194304x\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tAnisotropic Filtering\tControls the quality of texture rendering at oblique angles. It's a light setting and safe to set at 16x on most GPUs.\tRenderer Advanced\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tastc_recompression\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EUncompressed (Best quality)\u001F1\u001EBC1 (Low quality)\u001F2\u001EBC3 (Medium quality)\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tASTC Recompression Method\tAlmost all desktop and laptop dedicated GPUs lack support for ASTC textures, forcing the emulator to decompress to an intermediate format any card supports, RGBA8. This option recompresses RGBA8 to either the BC1 or BC3 format, saving VRAM but negatively affecting image quality.\tRenderer Advanced\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tvram_usage_mode\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EConservative\u001F1\u001EAggressive\u001F2\u001EHighEnd\u001F3\u001EInsane\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tVRAM Usage Mode\tSelects whether the emulator should prefer to conserve memory or make maximum usage of available video memory for performance. Has no effect on integrated graphics. Aggressive mode may severely impact the performance of other applications such as recording software.\tRenderer Advanced\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tvram_limit_mb\tINT\t0\t0\t32768\t\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tVRAM Limit (MB)\tSets the maximum VRAM usage limit in megabytes. Set to 0 for auto-detection (80% of available VRAM). Recommended: 6144 for 8GB GPUs, 4096 for 6GB GPUs.\tRenderer Advanced\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tgc_aggressiveness\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EOff (Not Recommended)\u001F1\u001ELight (Recommended)\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tGC Aggressiveness\tControls how aggressively the emulator evicts unused textures and buffers from VRAM. Off: Disable automatic cleanup (default). Light: Gentle cleanup, keeps more textures cached.\tRenderer Advanced\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\ttexture_eviction_frames\tINT\t0\t0\t60\t\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tTexture Eviction Frames\tNumber of frames a texture must be unused before it can be evicted. Set to 0 for auto-tuning based on VRAM pressure (recommended). Lower values free VRAM faster but may cause more texture reloading.\tRenderer Advanced\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tbuffer_eviction_frames\tINT\t0\t0\t120\t\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tBuffer Eviction Frames\tNumber of frames a buffer must be unused before it can be evicted. Set to 0 for auto-tuning based on VRAM pressure (recommended). Lower values free VRAM faster but may cause more buffer reloading.\tRenderer Advanced\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tsparse_texture_priority_eviction\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tSparse Texture Priority Eviction\tPrioritize evicting large sparse textures when VRAM pressure is high. This helps prevent VRAM exhaustion in games with large texture atlases.\tRenderer Advanced\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tlog_vram_usage\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tLog VRAM Usage\tEnable logging of VRAM usage statistics for debugging purposes. Check the log for 'VRAM GC' and 'VRAM Status' messages.\tRenderer Advanced\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tandroid_astc_mode\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EAuto\u001F1\u001ENative\u001F2\u001EDecompress\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer Advanced\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tforce_max_clock\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tForce maximum clocks (Vulkan only)\tRuns work in the background while waiting for graphics commands to keep the GPU from lowering its clock speed.\tRenderer Advanced\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tuse_asynchronous_shaders\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tUse asynchronous shader building (Hack)\tEnables asynchronous shader compilation, which may reduce shader stutter. This feature is experimental.\tRenderer Advanced\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tuse_fast_gpu_time\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tUse Fast GPU Time (Hack)\tEnables Fast GPU Time. This option will force most games to run at their highest native resolution.\tRenderer Advanced\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tuse_vulkan_driver_pipeline_cache\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tUse Vulkan pipeline cache\tEnables GPU vendor-specific pipeline cache. This option can improve shader loading time significantly in cases where the Vulkan driver does not store pipeline cache files internally.\tRenderer Advanced\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tenable_compute_pipelines\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tEnable Compute Pipelines (Intel Vulkan Only)\tEnable compute pipelines, required by some games. This setting only exists for Intel proprietary drivers, and may crash if enabled. Compute pipelines are always enabled on all other drivers.\tRenderer Advanced\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tuse_video_framerate\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tSync to framerate of video playback\tRun the game at normal speed during video playback, even when the framerate is unlocked.\tRenderer Advanced\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tbarrier_feedback_loops\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tBarrier feedback loops\tImproves rendering of transparency effects in specific games.\tRenderer Advanced\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tenable_buffer_history\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27\tEnable buffer history\tEnables access to previous buffer states. This option may improve rendering quality and performance consistency in some games.\tRenderer Advanced\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\twider_reciprocals\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tWider reciprocals\tWidens Recip32 to use F64 in intermediate stages.\tRenderer Advanced\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\textended_dynamic_state\tENUM\t3\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EDisabled\u001F1\u001EEDS1\u001F2\u001EEDS2\u001F3\u001EEDS3\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tExtended Dynamic State\tSelects the level of Vulkan Extended Dynamic State support. EDS3: Enables all Extended Dynamic State features (recommended). EDS2: Enables EDS1 and EDS2 features only. EDS1: Enables basic Extended Dynamic State features only. Disabled: Disables all Extended Dynamic State features (may reduce compatibility).\tRenderer Advanced\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tuse_conditional_rendering\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tUse conditional rendering\tEnables conditional rendering based on query results. Disabling this can fix flickering objects in some games but may impact performance. Try disabling if you see objects appearing and disappearing rapidly.\tRenderer Advanced\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tdebug\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer Debug\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tshader_feedback\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer Debug\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tnsight_aftermath\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer Debug\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tdisable_shader_loop_safety_checks\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer Debug\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\trenderdoc_hotkey\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer Debug\ncitron\t\u0001\tRenderer\tdisable_buffer_reorder\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer Debug\ncitron\t\u0001\tSystem\tlanguage_index\tENUM\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EJapanese (日本語)\u001F1\u001EAmerican English\u001F2\u001EFrench (français)\u001F3\u001EGerman (Deutsch)\u001F4\u001EItalian (italiano)\u001F5\u001ESpanish (español)\u001F6\u001EChinese\u001F7\u001EKorean (한국어)\u001F8\u001EDutch (Nederlands)\u001F9\u001EPortuguese (português)\u001F10\u001ERussian (Русский)\u001F11\u001ETaiwanese\u001F12\u001EBritish English\u001F13\u001ECanadian French\u001F14\u001ELatin American Spanish\u001F15\u001ESimplified Chinese\u001F16\u001ETraditional Chinese (正體中文)\u001F17\u001EBrazilian Portuguese (português do Brasil)\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tLanguage\tNote: this can be overridden when region setting is auto-select\tSystem\ncitron\t\u0001\tSystem\tregion_index\tENUM\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EJapan\u001F1\u001EUSA\u001F2\u001EEurope\u001F3\u001EAustralia\u001F4\u001EChina\u001F5\u001EKorea\u001F6\u001ETaiwan\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tRegion\tThe region of the emulated Switch.\tSystem\ncitron\t\u0001\tSystem\ttime_zone_index\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EAuto\u001F1\u001EDefault\u001F2\u001ECET\u001F3\u001ECST6CDT\u001F4\u001ECuba\u001F5\u001EEET\u001F6\u001EEgypt\u001F7\u001EEire\u001F8\u001EEST\u001F9\u001EEST5EDT\u001F10\u001EGB\u001F11\u001EGB-Eire\u001F12\u001EGMT\u001F13\u001EGMT+0\u001F14\u001EGMT-0\u001F15\u001EGMT0\u001F16\u001EGreenwich\u001F17\u001EHongkong\u001F18\u001EHST\u001F19\u001EIceland\u001F20\u001EIran\u001F21\u001EIsrael\u001F22\u001EJamaica\u001F23\u001EJapan\u001F24\u001EKwajalein\u001F25\u001ELibya\u001F26\u001EMET\u001F27\u001EMST\u001F28\u001EMST7MDT\u001F29\u001ENavajo\u001F30\u001ENZ\u001F31\u001ENZ-CHAT\u001F32\u001EPoland\u001F33\u001EPortugal\u001F34\u001EPRC\u001F35\u001EPST8PDT\u001F36\u001EROC\u001F37\u001EROK\u001F38\u001ESingapore\u001F39\u001ETurkey\u001F40\u001EUCT\u001F41\u001EUniversal\u001F42\u001EUTC\u001F43\u001EW-SU\u001F44\u001EWET\u001F45\u001EZulu\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\tTime Zone\tThe time zone of the emulated Switch.\tSystem\ncitron\t\u0001\tSystem\tcustom_rtc_enabled\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\t\u0001\t\u0001\tSystem\ncitron\t\u0001\tSystem\tcustom_rtc_offset\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\t2026-04-27,2026-04-17,2026-03-27,2026-03-20\t\u0001