tch by running the full boot ROMs, instead of starting with the second-stage loader. Requires a full BIOS/bootROM dump.\tDSi-mode\nmelonds\t\u0001\tInstance0.Firmware\tOverrideSettings\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\tOverride settings from external firmware\t\u0001\tFirmware\nmelonds\t\u0001\tInstance0.Firmware\tUsername\tSTRING\tmelonDS\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tFirmware\nmelonds\t\u0001\tInstance0.Firmware\tLanguage\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tFirmware\nmelonds\t\u0001\tInstance0.Firmware\tFavouriteColour\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tFirmware\nmelonds\t\u0001\tInstance0.Firmware\tBirthdayMonth\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tFirmware\nmelonds\t\u0001\tInstance0.Firmware\tBirthdayDay\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tFirmware\nmelonds\t\u0001\tInstance0.Firmware\tMessage\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tFirmware\nmelonds\t\u0001\tInstance0.DSi.Battery\tLevel\tINT\t15\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tDSi\nmelonds\t\u0001\tInstance0.DSi.Battery\tCharging\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tDSi\nmelonds\t\u0001\tInstance0.DS.Battery\tLevelOkay\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tDS\nmelonds\t\u0001\tJIT\tMaxBlockSize\tINT\t32\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\tMaximum JIT block size\t\u0001\tCPU emulation\nmelonds\t\u0001\tJIT\tLiteralOptimisations\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\tLiteral optimisations\t\u0001\tCPU emulation\nmelonds\t\u0001\tJIT\tBranchOptimisations\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\tBranch optimisations\t\u0001\tCPU emulation\nmelonds\t\u0001\tJIT\tFastMemory\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\tFast memory\t\u0001\tCPU emulation\nmelonds\t\u0001\tJIT\tEnable\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\tEnable JIT recompiler\t\u0001\tCPU emulation\nmelonds\t\u0001\tInstance0.Gdb.ARM7\tPort\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tDevtools\nmelonds\t\u0001\tInstance0.Gdb.ARM9\tPort\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tDevtools\nmelonds\t\u0001\tInstance0.Gdb.ARM7\tBreakOnStartup\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\tBreak on startup\t\u0001\tDevtools\nmelonds\t\u0001\tInstance0.Gdb.ARM9\tBreakOnStartup\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\tBreak on startup\t\u0001\tDevtools\nmelonds\t\u0001\tDSi.DSP\tHLE\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1\tDSP HLE\t\u0001\tDSi-mode\nmelonds\t\u0001\tEmu\tDirectBoot\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\tBoot game directly\tWhen loading a ROM, completely skip the regular boot process (&quot;Nintendo DS&quot; screen) to boot the ROM directly. Note: if your firmware dump isn't bootable, the ROM will be booted directly regardless of this setting.\tGeneral\nmelonds\t\u0001\tInstance0.Firmware\tMAC\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\tMAC address\t\u0001\tFirmware\nmelonds\t\u0001\tDLDI\tEnable\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\tEnable DLDI (for homebrew)\tEnable the built-in DLDI driver, to let homebrew access files from an emulated SD card.\tDLDI\nmelonds\t\u0001\tDLDI\tImageSize\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\tImage size\tSize of the SD image. If set to Auto: * if an image file exists, the volume size will be that of the image file * if no image file exists and folder sync is enabled, the volume size will be determined from the synced folder's contents * otherwise, the volume size will default to 512 MB\tDLDI\nmelonds\t\u0001\tDLDI\tReadOnly\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\tRead-only SD\tMake the emulated SD card read-only.\tDLDI\nmelonds\t\u0001\tDLDI\tFolderSync\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\tSync SD to folder:\tSync the emulated SD card to the given folder. The folder's contents will be copied to the SD image, and any change made to the SD image will be reflected to the folder.\tDLDI\nmelonds\t\u0001\tDSi.SD\tEnable\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\tEnable DSi SD card\tSimulate a SD card being inserted in the DSi's SD slot.\tDSi-mode\nmelonds\t\u0001\tDSi.SD\tImageSize\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\t\u0001\tSize of the SD image. If set to Auto: * if an image file exists, the volume size will be that of the image file * if no image file exists and folder sync is enabled, the volume size will be determined from the synced folder's contents * otherwise, the volume size will default to 512 MB\tDSi-mode\nmelonds\t\u0001\tDSi.SD\tReadOnly\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\tRead-only SD\tMake the emulated SD card read-only.\tDSi-mode\nmelonds\t\u0001\tDSi.SD\tFolderSync\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\tSync SD to folder:\tSync the emulated SD card to the given folder. The folder's contents will be copied to the SD image, and any change made to the SD image will be reflected to the folder.\tDSi-mode\nmelonds\t\u0001\t3D.Soft\tThreaded\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\tUse separate thread\tRun the software renderer on a separate thread. Yields better performance on multi-core CPUs.\t3D\nmelonds\t\u0001\t3D.GL\tBetterPolygons\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\tImproved polygon splitting\tEnabling this may help reduce distortion on quads and more complex polygons, but may also reduce performance.\t3D\nmelonds\t\u0001\t3D.GL\tScaleFactor\tINT\t1\t1\t16\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\t\u0001\tThe resolution at which the 3D graphics will be rendered. Higher resolutions improve graphics quality when the main window is enlarged, but may also cause glitches.\t3D\nmelonds\t\u0001\t3D.GL\tHiresCoordinates\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\tUse high resolution coordinates\t\u0001\t3D\nmelonds\t\u0001\tMouse\tHide\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\tHide mouse after inactivity\t\u0001\tMouse\nmelonds\t\u0001\tMouse\tHideSeconds\tINT\t5\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tMouse\nmelonds\t\u0001\t\tPauseLostFocus\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\tPause emulation when window is not in focus\t\u0001\tGeneral\nmelonds\t\u0001\t\tUITheme\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tGeneral\nmelonds\t\u0001\tLAN\tPlayerName\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tLAN\nmelonds\t\u0001\tLAN\tHostNumPlayers\tINT\t16\t2\t16\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tLAN\nmelonds\t\u0001\tMP\tRecvTimeout\tINT\t25\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tMP\nmelonds\t\u0001\tLAN\tDirectMode\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\tDirect mode [TEXT PLACEHOLDER]\tDirect mode directly routes network traffic to the host network. It is the most reliable, but requires an ethernet connection. Non-direct mode uses a layer of emulation to get around this, but is more prone to problems.\tLAN\nmelonds\t\u0001\tInstance0.Window0\tShowOSD\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tWindow0\nmelonds\t\u0001\tInstance0.Window0\tScreenRotation\tINT\t0\t0\t3\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tWindow0\nmelonds\t\u0001\tInstance0.Window0\tScreenGap\tINT\t0\t0\t500\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tWindow0\nmelonds\t\u0001\tInstance0.Window0\tScreenLayout\tINT\t0\t0\t3\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tWindow0\nmelonds\t\u0001\tInstance0.Window0\tScreenSizing\tINT\t0\t0\t5\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tWindow0\nmelonds\t\u0001\tInstance0.Window0\tIntegerScaling\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tWindow0\nmelonds\t\u0001\tInstance0.Window0\tScreenSwap\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tWindow0\nmelonds\t\u0001\tInstance0.Window0\tScreenAspectTop\tINT\t0\t0\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tWindow0\nmelonds\t\u0001\tInstance0.Window0\tScreenAspectBot\tINT\t0\t0\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tWindow0\nmelonds\t\u0001\tInstance0.Window0\tScreenFilter\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tWindow0\nmelonds\t\u0001\tScreen\tFilter\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.1,1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tScreen\nbanjorecomp\tsound.json\t\tmain_volume\tINT\t100\t0\t100\t\t0\t\u0001\tv1.0.2\tMain Volume\tControls the main volume of the game.\tSound\nbanjorecomp\tgraphics.json\t\tres_option\tENUM\tAuto\t\u0001\t\u0001\tOriginal\u001FOriginal2x\u001EOriginal 2x\u001FAuto\t0\t\u0001\tv1.0.2\tResolution\tSets the output resolution of the game. Original matches the game's original 240p resolution. Original 2x will render at 480p. Auto will scale based on the game window's resolution.\tGraphics\nbanjorecomp\tgraphics.json\t\tds_option\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EOff\u001F2\u001E2x\u001F4\u001E4x\t0\t\u0001\tv1.0.2\tDownsampling Quality\tRenders at a higher resolution and scales it down to the output resolution for increased quality. Only available in Original and Original 2x resolution. Note: 4x downsampling quality at Original 2x resolution may cause performance issues on low end devices, as it will cause the game to render at almost 4k internal resolution.\tGraphics\nbanjorecomp\tgraphics.json\t\tar_option\tENUM\tExpand\t\u0001\t\u0001\tOriginal\u001FExpand\t0\t\u0001\tv1.0.2\tAspect Ratio\tSets the horizontal aspect ratio. Original uses the game's original 4:3 aspect ratio. Expand will adjust to match the game window's aspect ratio.\tGraphics\nbanjorecomp\tgraphics.json\t\twm_option\tENUM\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\tWindowed\u001FFullscreen\t0\t\u0001\tv1.0.2\tWindow Mode\tSets whether the game should display Windowed or Fullscreen. You can also use F11 or Alt + Enter to toggle this option.\tGraphics\nbanjorecomp\tgraphics.json\t\trr_option\tENUM\tDisplay\t\u0001\t\u0001\tOriginal\u001FDisplay\u001FManual\t0\t\u0001\tv1.0.2\tFramerate\t\u0001\tGraphics\nbanjorecomp\tgraphics.json\t\trr_manual_value\tINT\t60\t20\t240\t\t0\t\u0001\tv1.0.2\t\u0001\t\u0001\tGraphics\nbanjorecomp\tgraphics.json\t\tmsaa_option\tENUM\tMSAA2X\t\u0001\t\u0001\tNone\u001FMSAA2X\u001E2X\u001FMSAA4X\u001E4X\t0\t\u0001\tv1.0.2\tMS Anti-Aliasing\tSets the multisample anti-aliasing (MSAA) quality level. This reduces jagged edges in the final image at the expense of rendering performance. Note: This option won't be available if your GPU does not support programmable MSAA sample positions, as it is currently required to avoid rendering glitches.\tGraphics\nbanjorecomp\tgraphics.json\t\thr_option\tENUM\tClamp16x9\t\u0001\t\u0001\tOriginal\u001FClamp16x9\u001E16:9\u001FExpand\t0\t\u0001\tv1.0.2\tHUD Placement\tAdjusts the placement of HUD elements to fit the selected aspect ratio. Expand will use the aspect ratio of the game's output window.\tGraphics\nbanjorecomp\tgeneral.json\t\trumble_strength\tINT\t25\t0\t100\t\t0\t\u0001\tv1.0.2\tRumble Strength\tControls the strength of rumble when using a controller that supports it. Setting this to zero will disable rumble.\tGeneral\n",
    "banjorecomp\tgeneral.json\t\tjoystick_deadzone\tINT\t5\t0\t100\t\t0\t\u0001\tv1.0.2\tJoystick Deadzone\tApplies a deadzone to joystick inputs.\tGeneral\nbanjorecomp\tgeneral.json\t\tbackground_input_mode\tENUM\tOn\t\u0001\t\u0001\tOff\u001FOn\t0\t\u0001\tv1.0.2\tBackground Input Mode\tAllows the game to read controller input when out of focus. This setting does not affect keyboard input.\tGeneral\nbanjorecomp\tgeneral.json\t\tnote_saving_mode\tENUM\tOn\t\u0001\t\u0001\tOff\u001FNotes\u001EOnly Notes\u001FJinjos\u001EOnly Jinjos\u001FOn\u001EBoth\t0\t\u0001\tv1.0.2\tNote & Jinjo Saving\tSaves collected notes and jinjos so that you don't need to collect them again when revisiting a level. Both is the default, while off matches the original game. Changing this setting will only take effect when entering/exiting a level, or restarting the game.\tGeneral\nbanjorecomp\tgeneral.json\t\tanalog_cam_mode\tENUM\tOff\t\u0001\t\u0001\tOff\u001FOn\t0\t\u0001\tv1.0.2\tAnalog Camera\tEnables the analog camera.\tGeneral\nbanjorecomp\tgeneral.json\t\tanalog_camera_sensitivity\tINT\t3\t1\t10\t\t0\t\u0001\tv1.0.2\tAnalog Camera Sensitivity\tSets the sensitivity of the right stick analog camera, if enabled.\tGeneral\nbanjorecomp\tgeneral.json\t\tthird_person_camera_invert_mode\tENUM\tInvertX\t\u0001\t\u0001\tInvertNone\u001ENone\u001FInvertX\u001EInvert X\u001FInvertY\u001EInvert Y\u001FInvertBoth\u001EInvert Both\t0\t\u0001\tv1.0.2\tInvert Camera\tInverts the camera controls for the third person camera if it's enabled. Invert X is the default and matches the original game. If analog camera is off, only the Invert X setting will take effect.\tGeneral\nbanjorecomp\tgeneral.json\t\tfirst_person_invert_mode\tENUM\tInvertY\t\u0001\t\u0001\tInvertNone\u001ENone\u001FInvertX\u001EInvert X\u001FInvertY\u001EInvert Y\u001FInvertBoth\u001EInvert Both\t0\t\u0001\tv1.0.2\tInvert First Person View\tInverts the camera controls in first person view. Invert Y is the default and matches the original game.\tGeneral\nbanjorecomp\tgeneral.json\t\tflying_and_swimming_invert_mode\tENUM\tInvertY\t\u0001\t\u0001\tInvertNone\u001ENone\u001FInvertX\u001EInvert X\u001FInvertY\u001EInvert Y\u001FInvertBoth\u001EInvert Both\t0\t\u0001\tv1.0.2\tInvert Flying & Swimming\tInverts the controls for swimming and flying. Invert Y is the default and matches the original game.\tGeneral\nbanjorecomp\tsound.json\t\tbgm_volume\tINT\t100\t0\t100\t\t0\t\u0001\tv1.0.2\tBackground Music Volume\tControls the overall volume of background music.\tSound\nbanjorecomp\tgraphics.json\t\tcutscene_aspect_ratio_mode\tENUM\tClamp16x9\t\u0001\t\u0001\tOriginal\u001FClamp16x9\u001E16:9\u001FExpand\t0\t\u0001\tv1.0.2\tCutscene Aspect Ratio\tSets the aspect ratio limit for cutscenes. Cutscenes have been adjusted to work in 16:9, which is the default option. Wider aspect ratios may show details that weren't meant to be on-screen.\tGraphics\nsssv-recomp\tsound.json\t\tmain_volume\tINT\t100\t0\t100\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.0\tMain Volume\tControls the main volume of the game.\tSound\nsssv-recomp\tgraphics.json\t\tres_option\tENUM\tAuto\t\u0001\t\u0001\tOriginal\u001FOriginal2x\u001EOriginal 2x\u001FAuto\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.0\tResolution\tSets the output resolution of the game. Original matches the game's original 240p resolution. Original 2x will render at 480p. Auto will scale based on the game window's resolution.\tGraphics\nsssv-recomp\tgraphics.json\t\tds_option\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EOff\u001F2\u001E2x\u001F4\u001E4x\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.0\tDownsampling Quality\tRenders at a higher resolution and scales it down to the output resolution for increased quality. Only available in Original and Original 2x resolution. Note: 4x downsampling quality at Original 2x resolution may cause performance issues on low end devices, as it will cause the game to render at almost 4k internal resolution.\tGraphics\nsssv-recomp\tgraphics.json\t\tar_option\tENUM\tExpand\t\u0001\t\u0001\tOriginal\u001FExpand\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.0\tAspect Ratio\tSets the horizontal aspect ratio. Original uses the game's original 4:3 aspect ratio. Expand will adjust to match the game window's aspect ratio.\tGraphics\nsssv-recomp\tgraphics.json\t\twm_option\tENUM\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\tWindowed\u001FFullscreen\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.0\tWindow Mode\tSets whether the game should display Windowed or Fullscreen. You can also use F11 or Alt + Enter to toggle this option.\tGraphics\nsssv-recomp\tgraphics.json\t\trr_option\tENUM\tDisplay\t\u0001\t\u0001\tOriginal\u001FDisplay\u001FManual\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.0\tFramerate\t\u0001\tGraphics\nsssv-recomp\tgraphics.json\t\trr_manual_value\tINT\t60\t20\t240\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tGraphics\nsssv-recomp\tgraphics.json\t\tmsaa_option\tENUM\tMSAA2X\t\u0001\t\u0001\tNone\u001FMSAA2X\u001E2X\u001FMSAA4X\u001E4X\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.0\tMS Anti-Aliasing\tSets the multisample anti-aliasing (MSAA) quality level. This reduces jagged edges in the final image at the expense of rendering performance. Note: This option won't be available if your GPU does not support programmable MSAA sample positions, as it is currently required to avoid rendering glitches.\tGraphics\nsssv-recomp\tgraphics.json\t\thr_option\tENUM\tClamp16x9\t\u0001\t\u0001\tOriginal\u001FClamp16x9\u001E16:9\u001FExpand\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.0\tHUD Placement\tAdjusts the placement of HUD elements to fit the selected aspect ratio. Expand will use the aspect ratio of the game's output window.\tGraphics\nsssv-recomp\tgeneral.json\t\trumble_strength\tINT\t25\t0\t100\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.0\tRumble Strength\tControls the strength of rumble when using a controller that supports it. Setting this to zero will disable rumble.\tGeneral\nsssv-recomp\tgeneral.json\t\tjoystick_deadzone\tINT\t5\t0\t100\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.0\tJoystick Deadzone\tApplies a deadzone to joystick inputs.\tGeneral\nsssv-recomp\tgeneral.json\t\tbackground_input_mode\tENUM\tOn\t\u0001\t\u0001\tOff\u001FOn\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.0\tBackground Input Mode\tAllows the game to read controller input when out of focus. This setting does not affect keyboard input.\tGeneral\nharvestmoon64-recomp\tsound.json\t\tmain_volume\tINT\t100\t0\t100\t\t0\t\u0001\tv1.2.2\tMain Volume\tControls the main volume of the game.\tSound\nharvestmoon64-recomp\tgraphics.json\t\tres_option\tENUM\tAuto\t\u0001\t\u0001\tOriginal\u001FOriginal2x\u001EOriginal 2x\u001FAuto\t0\t\u0001\tv1.2.2\tResolution\tSets the output resolution of the game. Original matches the game's original 240p resolution. Original 2x will render at 480p. Auto will scale based on the game window's resolution.\tGraphics\nharvestmoon64-recomp\tgraphics.json\t\tds_option\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EOff\u001F2\u001E2x\u001F4\u001E4x\t0\t\u0001\tv1.2.2\tDownsampling Quality\tRenders at a higher resolution and scales it down to the output resolution for increased quality. Only available in Original and Original 2x resolution. Note: 4x downsampling quality at Original 2x resolution may cause performance issues on low end devices, as it will cause the game to render at almost 4k internal resolution.\tGraphics\nharvestmoon64-recomp\tgraphics.json\t\tar_option\tENUM\tExpand\t\u0001\t\u0001\tOriginal\u001FExpand\t0\t\u0001\tv1.2.2\tAspect Ratio\tSets the horizontal aspect ratio. Original uses the game's original 4:3 aspect ratio. Expand will adjust to match the game window's aspect ratio.\tGraphics\nharvestmoon64-recomp\tgraphics.json\t\twm_option\tENUM\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\tWindowed\u001FFullscreen\t0\t\u0001\tv1.2.2\tWindow Mode\tSets whether the game should display Windowed or Fullscreen. You can also use F11 or Alt + Enter to toggle this option.\tGraphics\nharvestmoon64-recomp\tgraphics.json\t\trr_option\tENUM\tDisplay\t\u0001\t\u0001\tOriginal\u001FDisplay\u001FManual\t0\t\u0001\tv1.2.2\tFramerate\t\u0001\tGraphics\nharvestmoon64-recomp\tgraphics.json\t\trr_manual_value\tINT\t60\t20\t240\t\t0\t\u0001\tv1.2.2\t\u0001\t\u0001\tGraphics\nharvestmoon64-recomp\tgraphics.json\t\tmsaa_option\tENUM\tMSAA2X\t\u0001\t\u0001\tNone\u001FMSAA2X\u001E2X\u001FMSAA4X\u001E4X\t0\t\u0001\tv1.2.2\tMS Anti-Aliasing\tSets the multisample anti-aliasing (MSAA) quality level. This reduces jagged edges in the final image at the expense of rendering performance. Note: This option won't be available if your GPU does not support programmable MSAA sample positions, as it is currently required to avoid rendering glitches.\tGraphics\nharvestmoon64-recomp\tgraphics.json\t\thr_option\tENUM\tClamp16x9\t\u0001\t\u0001\tOriginal\u001FClamp16x9\u001E16:9\u001FExpand\t0\t\u0001\tv1.2.2\tHUD Placement\tAdjusts the placement of HUD elements to fit the selected aspect ratio. Expand will use the aspect ratio of the game's output window.\tGraphics\nharvestmoon64-recomp\tgeneral.json\t\trumble_strength\tINT\t25\t0\t100\t\t0\t\u0001\tv1.2.2\tRumble Strength\tControls the strength of rumble when using a controller that supports it. Setting this to zero will disable rumble.\tGeneral\nharvestmoon64-recomp\tgeneral.json\t\tjoystick_deadzone\tINT\t5\t0\t100\t\t0\t\u0001\tv1.2.2\tJoystick Deadzone\tApplies a deadzone to joystick inputs.\tGeneral\nharvestmoon64-recomp\tgeneral.json\t\tbackground_input_mode\tENUM\tOn\t\u0001\t\u0001\tOff\u001FOn\t0\t\u0001\tv1.2.2\tBackground Input Mode\tAllows the game to read controller input when out of focus. This setting does not affect keyboard input.\tGeneral\nharvestmoon64-recomp\tsound.json\t\tmusic_volume\tINT\t100\t0\t100\t\t0\t\u0001\tv1.2.2\tMusic Volume\tControls background music volume.\tSound\nharvestmoon64-recomp\tsound.json\t\tambience_volume\tINT\t100\t0\t100\t\t0\t\u0001\tv1.2.2\tAmbience Volume\tControls ambient/environmental sound volume.\tSound\ndk64-recomp\tsound.json\t\tmain_volume\tINT\t100\t0\t100\t\t0\t\u0001\tv1.0.3\tMain Volume\tControls the main volume of the game.\tSound\ndk64-recomp\tgraphics.json\t\tres_option\tENUM\tAuto\t\u0001\t\u0001\tOriginal\u001FOriginal2x\u001EOriginal 2x\u001FAuto\t0\t\u0001\tv1.0.3\tResolution\tSets the output resolution of the game. Original matches the game's original 240p resolution. Original 2x will render at 480p. Auto will scale based on the game window's resolution.\tGraphics\ndk64-recomp\tgraphics.json\t\tds_option\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EOff\u001F2\u001E2x\u001F4\u001E4x\t0\t\u0001\tv1.0.3\tDownsampling Quality\tRenders at a higher resolution and scales it down to the output resolution for increased quality. Only available in Original and Original 2x resolution. Note: 4x downsampling quality at Original 2x resolution may cause performance issues on low end devices, as it will cause the game to render at almost 4k internal resolution.\tGraphics\ndk64-recomp\tgraphics.json\t\tar_option\tENUM\tExpand\t\u0001\t\u0001\tOriginal\u001FExpand\t0\t\u0001\tv1.0.3\tAspect Ratio\tSets the horizontal aspect ratio. Original uses the game's original 4:3 aspect ratio. Expand will adjust to match the game window's aspect ratio.\tGraphics\ndk64-recomp\tgraphics.json\t\twm_option\tENUM\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\tWindowed\u001FFullscreen\t0\t\u0001\tv1.0.3\tWindow Mode\tSets whether the game should display Windowed or Fullscreen. You can also use F11 or Alt + Enter to toggle this option.\tGraphics\ndk64-recomp\tgraphics.json\t\trr_option\tENUM\tDisplay\t\u0001\t\u0001\tOriginal\u001FDisplay\u001FManual\t0\t\u0001\tv1.0.3\tFramerate\t\u0001\tGraphics\ndk64-recomp\tgraphics.json\t\trr_manual_value\tINT\t60\t20\t240\t\t0\t\u0001\tv1.0.3\t\u0001\t\u0001\tGraphics\ndk64-recomp\tgraphics.json\t\tmsaa_option\tENUM\tMSAA2X\t\u0001\t\u0001\tNone\u001FMSAA2X\u001E2X\u001FMSAA4X\u001E4X\t0\t\u0001\tv1.0.3\tMS Anti-Aliasing\tSets the multisample anti-aliasing (MSAA) quality level. This reduces jagged edges in the final image at the expense of rendering performance. Note: This option won't be available if your GPU does not support programmable MSAA sample positions, as it is currently required to avoid rendering glitches.\tGraphics\ndk64-recomp\tgraphics.json\t\thr_option\tENUM\tClamp16x9\t\u0001\t\u0001\tOriginal\u001FClamp16x9\u001E16:9\u001FExpand\t0\t\u0001\tv1.0.3\tHUD Placement\tAdjusts the placement of HUD elements to fit the selected aspect ratio. Expand will use the aspect ratio of the game's output window.\tGraphics\ndk64-recomp\tgeneral.json\t\trumble_strength\tINT\t25\t0\t100\t\t0\t\u0001\tv1.0.3\tRumble Strength\tControls the strength of rumble when using a controller that supports it. Setting this to zero will disable rumble.\tGeneral\ndk64-recomp\tgeneral.json\t\tgyro_sensitivity\tINT\t25\t0\t100\t\t0\t\u0001\tv1.0.3\tGyro Sensitivity\tControls the sensitivity of gyro aiming when using items in first person for controllers that support it.Setting this to zero will disable gyro. Note: To recalibrate controller gyro, set the controller down on a still, flat surface for 5 seconds.\tGeneral\ndk64-recomp\tgeneral.json\t\tmouse_sensitivity\tINT\t\u0001\t0\t100\t\t0\t\u0001\tv1.0.3\tMouse Sensitivity\tControls the sensitivity of mouse aiming when using items in first person. Setting this to zero will disable mouse aiming. Note: This option does not allow mouse buttons to activate items. Mouse aiming is intended to be used with inputs that are mapped to mouse movement, such as gyro on Steam Deck.\tGeneral\ndk64-recomp\tgeneral.json\t\tjoystick_deadzone\tINT\t5\t0\t100\t\t0\t\u0001\tv1.0.3\tJoystick Deadzone\tApplies a deadzone to joystick inputs.\tGeneral\ndk64-recomp\tgeneral.json\t\tbackground_input_mode\tENUM\tOn\t\u0001\t\u0001\tOff\u001FOn\t0\t\u0001\tv1.0.3\tBackground Input Mode\tAllows the game to read controller input when out of focus. This setting does not affect keyboard input.\tGeneral\ndk64-recomp\tgeneral.json\t\tthird_person_camera_invert_mode\tENUM\tInvertNone\t\u0001\t\u0001\tInvertNone\u001ENone\u001FInvertX\u001EInvert X\t0\t\u0001\tv1.0.3\tInvert Camera\tInverts the camera controls for the third person camera if it's enabled.\tGeneral\ndk64-recomp\tgeneral.json\t\tfirst_person_invert_mode\tENUM\tInvertY\t\u0001\t\u0001\tInvertNone\u001ENone\u001FInvertX\u001EInvert X\u001FInvertY\u001EInvert Y\u001FInvertBoth\u001EInvert Both\t0\t\u0001\tv1.0.3\tInvert First Person View\tInverts the camera controls in first person view. Invert Y is the default and matches the original game.\tGeneral\ndk64-recomp\tgeneral.json\t\tgyro_invert_mode\tENUM\tInvertY\t\u0001\t\u0001\tInvertNone\u001ENone\u001FInvertX\u001EInvert X\u001FInvertY\u001EInvert Y\u001FInvertBoth\u001EInvert Both\t0\t\u0001\tv1.0.3\tInvert Gyro\tInverts gyro controls.\tGeneral\ndk64-recomp\tgeneral.json\t\tmouse_invert_mode\tENUM\tInvertY\t\u0001\t\u0001\tInvertNone\u001ENone\u001FInvertX\u001EInvert X\u001FInvertY\u001EInvert Y\u001FInvertBoth\u001EInvert Both\t0\t\u0001\tv1.0.3\tInvert Mouse\tInverts Mouse controls.\tGeneral\ndk64-recomp\tgeneral.json\t\tswimming_invert_mode\tENUM\tInvertY\t\u0001\t\u0001\tInvertNone\u001ENone\u001FInvertX\u001EInvert X\u001FInvertY\u001EInvert Y\u001FInvertBoth\u001EInvert Both\t0\t\u0001\tv1.0.3\tInvert Swimming\tInverts the controls for swimming. Invert Y is the default and matches the original game.\tGeneral\ndk64-recomp\tgeneral.json\t\tstory_skip\tENUM\tOff\t\u0001\t\u0001\tOff\u001ENone\u001FIntroStory\u001EIntro Story Only\u001FVanillaOn\u001EOn\t0\t\u0001\tv1.0.3\tStory Skip\tSkips some story cutscenes. Off: No story cutscenes are skipped. Intro Story Only: Only the 5-minute introductory story is skipped. The K. Rool level intros will still play. On: Both the introductory story and all K. Rool level intros are skipped.\tGeneral\ndk64-recomp\tgeneral.json\t\tcamera_type\tENUM\tFree\t\u0001\t\u0001\tFree\u001EFree Cam\u001FFollow\u001EFollow Cam\u001FBetterFree\u001EBetter Free Cam\u001FAnalog\u001EAnalog Camera\t0\t\u0001\tv1.0.3\tCamera Type\tChanges the camera behavior. Free Cam: Camera can be controlled via pressing C-Left and C-Right. The camera does not try to push itself behind the player. Follow Cam: Similar to Free Cam, but the camera tries to push itself behind the player. Better Free Cam: Similar to Free Cam, but instead of a button press turning the camera 45 degrees, holding the button moves the camera at 5 degrees per frame. Analog Camera: Control of the camera is controlled by your right analogue stick. It is advised that C-Up is remapped to something outside your right analogue stick in order to have a good time with this.\tGeneral\ndk64-recomp\tgeneral.json\t\tanalog_camera_sensitivity\tINT\t3\t1\t10\t\t0\t\u0001\tv1.0.3\tAnalog Camera Sensitivity\tSets the sensitivity of the right stick analog camera, if enabled.\tGeneral\ndk64-recomp\tgeneral.json\t\tlightning_flashes\tENUM\tReduced\t\u0001\t\u0001\tOff\u001FReduced\u001FVanilla\t0\t\u0001\tv1.0.3\tLightning Flash Frequency\tChanges the frequency of lightning flashes within the game. Vanilla: Lightning flashes at vanilla frequency Reduced: Lightning flashes at 10x as less Off: Lightning flashes are completely disabled\tGeneral\ndk64-recomp\tsound.json\t\tbgm_volume\tINT\t100\t0\t100\t\t0\t\u0001\tv1.0.3\tBackground Music Volume\tControls the overall volume of background music.\tSound\ndk64-recomp\tsound.json\t\tsfx_volume\tINT\t100\t0\t100\t\t0\t\u0001\tv1.0.3\tSFX Volume\tControls the overall volume of sound effects.\tSound\ndk64-recomp\tgraphics.json\t\tcutscene_borders\tENUM\tOn\t\u0001\t\u0001\tOff\u001FOn\t0\t\u0001\tv1.0.3\tCutscene Borders\tIf turned on, cutscenes will show borders on the top and the bottom of the screen as in the vanilla game.\tGraphics\ndk64-recomp\tgraphics.json\t\tdraw_distance\tINT\t0\t0\t100\t\t0\t\u0001\tv1.0.3\tDraw Distance\tControls the draw distance within the game from 0% (vanilla) to 100% (10x vanilla). Some objects do not get a draw distance increase for technical reasons.\tGraphics\nlamborghini-recomp\tsound.json\t\tmain_volume\tINT\t100\t0\t100\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.9.0\tMain Volume\tControls the main volume of the game.\tSound\nlamborghini-recomp\tgraphics.json\t\tres_option\tENUM\tAuto\t\u0001\t\u0001\tOriginal\u001FOriginal2x\u001EOriginal 2x\u001FAuto\t0\t\u0001\tv0.9.0\tResolution\tSets the output resolution of the game. Original matches the game's original 240p resolution. Original 2x will render at 480p. Auto will scale based on the game window's resolution.\tGraphics\nlamborghini-recomp\tgraphics.json\t\tds_option\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EOff\u001F2\u001E2x\u001F4\u001E4x\t0\t\u0001\tv0.9.0\tDownsampling Quality\tRenders at a higher resolution and scales it down to the output resolution for increased quality. Only available in Original and Original 2x resolution. Note: 4x downsampling quality at Original 2x resolution may cause performance issues on low end devices, as it will cause the game to render at almost 4k internal resolution.\tGraphics\nlamborghini-recomp\tgraphics.json\t\tar_option\tENUM\tExpand\t\u0001\t\u0001\tOriginal\u001FExpand\t0\t\u0001\tv0.9.0\tAspect Ratio\tSets the horizontal aspect ratio. Original uses the game's original 4:3 aspect ratio. Expand will adjust to match the game window's aspect ratio.\tGraphics\nlamborghini-recomp\tgraphics.json\t\twm_option\tENUM\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\tWindowed\u001FFullscreen\t0\t\u0001\tv0.9.0\tWindow Mode\tSets whether the game should display Windowed or Fullscreen. You can also use F11 or Alt + Enter to toggle this option.\tGraphics\nlamborghini-recomp\tgraphics.json\t\trr_option\tENUM\tDisplay\t\u0001\t\u0001\tOriginal\u001FDisplay\u001FManual\t0\t\u0001\tv0.9.0\tFramerate\t\u0001\tGraphics\nlamborghini-recomp\tgraphics.json\t\trr_manual_value\tINT\t60\t20\t240\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.9.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tGraphics\nlamborghini-recomp\tgraphics.json\t\tmsaa_option\tENUM\tMSAA2X\t\u0001\t\u0001\tNone\u001FMSAA2X\u001E2X\u001FMSAA4X\u001E4X\t0\t\u0001\tv0.9.0\tMS Anti-Aliasing\tSets the multisample anti-aliasing (MSAA) quality level. This reduces jagged edges in the final image at the expense of rendering performance. Note: This option won't be available if your GPU does not support programmable MSAA sample positions, as it is currently required to avoid rendering glitches.\tGraphics\nlamborghini-recomp\tgraphics.json\t\thr_option\tENUM\tClamp16x9\t\u0001\t\u0001\tOriginal\u001FClamp16x9\u001E16:9\u001FExpand\t0\t\u0001\tv0.9.0\tHUD Placement\tAdjusts the placement of HUD elements to fit the selected aspect ratio. Expand will use the aspect ratio of the game's output window.\tGraphics\nlamborghini-recomp\tgeneral.json\t\trumble_strength\tINT\t25\t0\t100\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.9.0\tRumble Strength\tControls the strength of rumble when using a controller that supports it. Setting this to zero will disable rumble.\tGeneral\nlamborghini-recomp\tgeneral.json\t\tjoystick_deadzone\tINT\t5\t0\t100\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.9.0\tJoystick Deadzone\tApplies a deadzone to joystick inputs.\tGeneral\nlamborghini-recomp\tgeneral.json\t\tbackground_input_mode\tENUM\tOn\t\u0001\t\u0001\tOff\u001FOn\t0\t\u0001\tv0.9.0\tBackground Input Mode\tAllows the game to read controller input when out of focus. This setting does not affect keyboard input.\tGeneral\naerogauge-recomp\tsound.json\t\tmain_volume\tINT\t100\t0\t100\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.6.2\tMain Volume\tControls the main volume of the game.\tSound\naerogauge-recomp\tgraphics.json\t\tres_option\tENUM\tAuto\t\u0001\t\u0001\tOriginal\u001FOriginal2x\u001EOriginal 2x\u001FAuto\t0\t\u0001\tv0.6.2\tResolution\tSets the output resolution of the game. Original matches the game's original 240p resolution. Original 2x will render at 480p. Auto will scale based on the game window's resolution.\tGraphics\naerogauge-recomp\tgraphics.json\t\tds_option\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EOff\u001F2\u001E2x\u001F4\u001E4x\t0\t\u0001\tv0.6.2\tDownsampling Quality\tRenders at a higher resolution and scales it down to the output resolution for increased quality. Only available in Original and Original 2x resolution. Note: 4x downsampling quality at Original 2x resolution may cause performance issues on low end devices, as it will cause the game to render at almost 4k internal resolution.\tGraphics\naerogauge