based on the game window's resolution.\tGraphics\nbattlezone-recomp\tgraphics.json\t\tds_option\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EOff\u001F2\u001E2x\u001F4\u001E4x\t0\t\u0001\tv0.1.0-beta\tDownsampling Quality\tRenders at a higher resolution and scales it down to the output resolution for increased quality. Only available in Original and Original 2x resolution. Note: 4x downsampling quality at Original 2x resolution may cause performance issues on low end devices, as it will cause the game to render at almost 4k internal resolution.\tGraphics\nbattlezone-recomp\tgraphics.json\t\tar_option\tENUM\tExpand\t\u0001\t\u0001\tOriginal\u001FExpand\t0\t\u0001\tv0.1.0-beta\tAspect Ratio\tSets the horizontal aspect ratio. Original uses the game's original 4:3 aspect ratio. Expand will adjust to match the game window's aspect ratio.\tGraphics\nbattlezone-recomp\tgraphics.json\t\twm_option\tENUM\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\tWindowed\u001FFullscreen\t0\t\u0001\tv0.1.0-beta\tWindow Mode\tSets whether the game should display Windowed or Fullscreen. You can also use F11 or Alt + Enter to toggle this option.\tGraphics\nbattlezone-recomp\tgraphics.json\t\trr_option\tENUM\tDisplay\t\u0001\t\u0001\tOriginal\u001FDisplay\u001FManual\t0\t\u0001\tv0.1.0-beta\tFramerate\t\u0001\tGraphics\nbattlezone-recomp\tgraphics.json\t\trr_manual_value\tINT\t60\t20\t240\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.1.0-beta\t\u0001\t\u0001\tGraphics\nbattlezone-recomp\tgraphics.json\t\tmsaa_option\tENUM\tMSAA2X\t\u0001\t\u0001\tNone\u001FMSAA2X\u001E2X\u001FMSAA4X\u001E4X\t0\t\u0001\tv0.1.0-beta\tMS Anti-Aliasing\tSets the multisample anti-aliasing (MSAA) quality level. This reduces jagged edges in the final image at the expense of rendering performance. Note: This option won't be available if your GPU does not support programmable MSAA sample positions, as it is currently required to avoid rendering glitches.\tGraphics\nbattlezone-recomp\tgraphics.json\t\thr_option\tENUM\tClamp16x9\t\u0001\t\u0001\tOriginal\u001FClamp16x9\u001E16:9\u00