0001\t9.3.1\tN64 Logo Spin Speed\t\u0001\tCosmetics / N64 Logo\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCosmetics\u001FMoon\tSize\tFLOAT\t1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tMoon Size\t\u0001\tCosmetics / Moon\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCosmetics\u001FKak\u001FWindmill_Speed\tValue\tFLOAT\t100.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tKak Windmill Speed\t\u0001\tCosmetics / Kak / Windmill_Speed\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCosmetics\tDefaultColorScheme\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EN64\u001F1\u001EGamecube\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tColor Scheme\t\u0001\tCosmetics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCosmetics\tRainbowSync\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tSync Rainbow colors\t\u0001\tCosmetics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCosmetics\tRainbowSpeed\tFLOAT\t0.6\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tRainbow Speed\t\u0001\tCosmetics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCosmetics\tRandomizeCosmeticsGenModes\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EManual\u001F1\u001EOn New Scene\u001F2\u001EOn Rando Gen Only\u001F3\u001EOn File Load\u001F4\u001EOn File Load (Seeded)\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tAutomatically Randomize All Cosmetics\tSet when the cosmetics is automaticly randomized:\\n- Manual: Manually randomize cosmetics by pressing the 'Randomize all' button\\n- On New Scene : Randomizes when you enter a new scene.\\n- On Rando Gen Only: Randomizes only when you generate a new randomizer.\\n- On File Load: Randomizes on File Load.\\n- On File Load (Seeded): Randomizes on file load based on the current randomizer seed/file.\tCosmetics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCosmetics\tAdvancedMode\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tAdvanced Mode\tSome cosmetic options may not apply if you have any mods that provide custom models for the cosmetic option.\\n\\nFor example, if you have custom Link model, then the Link's Hair color option will most likely not apply.\tCosmetics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCosmetics\u001FTrails\u001FDuration\tValue\tINT\t4\t2\t20\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tTrails Duration\t\u0001\tCosmetics / Trails / Duration\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tRandomizedEnemies\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EDisabled\u001F1\u001ERandom\u001F2\u001ERandom (Seeded)\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tEnemy Randomizer\tReplaces fixed enemies throughout the game with a random enemy. Bosses, Mini-Bosses and a few specific regular enemies are excluded.\\nEnemies that need more than Deku Nuts & either Deku Sticks or a sword to kill are excluded from spawning in \"clear enemy\" rooms.\\n\\n- Random: Enemies are randomized every time you load a room.\\n- Random (Seeded): Enemies are randomized based on the current randomizer seed/file.\\n\tEnhancements / Extra Modes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tRandomizedEnemySizes\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tRandomized Enemy Sizes\tEnemies and Bosses spawn with random sizes.\tEnhancements / Extra Modes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tEnemySizeScalesHealth\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tScale Health with Size\tScales normal enemies Health with their randomized size.\\n*This will NOT affect Bosses!*\tEnhancements / Extra Modes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tEnemyRandomizerAirWalkVoidouts\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tEnemies Walk over Voidout Pits\tGround enemies will air walk over pits/floors that void out Link\\nto prevent softlocks. Can be toggled to make enemies fall down\\nor fly back up from a void pit.\tEnhancements / Extra Modes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FRandomizedEnemyList\tAll\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tSelect all Enemies\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Extra Modes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FTimeSplits\tEnable\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tEnable Time Splits\t\u0001\tSettings / Time Splits\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FTimeSplits\tShowHeaders\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tShow Headers\t\u0001\tSettings / Time Splits\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FTimeSplits\tOpacity\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tHide Background\t\u0001\tSettings / Time Splits\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FTimeSplits\tHighlight\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tHighlight Active Split\t\u0001\tSettings / Time Splits\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FTimeSplits\tFollow\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFollow Active Split\t\u0001\tSettings / Time Splits\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FTimeSplits\tCompare\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tCompare Splits\t\u0001\tSettings / Time Splits\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgRemote\u001FAnchor\tShowOtherPlayersOnMinimap\tBOOL\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tShow Other Players on Minimap\t\u0001\tRemote / Anchor\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgRemote\u001FAnchor\u001FRoomSettings\tPvpMode\tENUM\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EOff\u001F1\u001EOn\u001F2\u001EOn + Friendly Fire\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tPvP Mode\t\u0001\tRemote / Anchor / Room Settings\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgRemote\u001FAnchor\u001FRoomSettings\tShowLocationsMode\tENUM\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ENone\u001F1\u001ETeam Only\u001F2\u001EAll\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tShow Locations For\t\u0001\tRemote / Anchor / Room Settings\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgRemote\u001FAnchor\u001FRoomSettings\tTeleportMode\tENUM\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ENone\u001F1\u001ETeam Only\u001F2\u001EAll\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tAllow Teleporting To\t\u0001\tRemote / Anchor / Room Settings\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgRemote\u001FAnchor\u001FRoomSettings\tSyncItemsAndFlags\tBOOL\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tSync Items & Flags\t\u0001\tRemote / Anchor / Room Settings\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FMenu\tTheme\tENUM\t5\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ERed\u001F1\u001EDark Red\u001F2\u001EOrange\u001F3\u001EGreen\u001F4\u001EDark Green\u001F5\u001ELight Blue\u001F6\u001EBlue\u001F7\u001EDark Blue\u001F8\u001EIndigo\u001F9\u001EViolet\u001F10\u001EPurple\u001F11\u001EBrown\u001F12\u001EGray\u001F13\u001EDark Gray\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tMenu Theme\tChanges the Theme of the Menu Widgets.\tSettings / General\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\tControlNav\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tMenu Controller Navigation\tAllows controller navigation of the port menu (Settings, Enhancements,...)\\nCAUTION: This will disable game inputs while the menu is visible.\\n\\nD-pad to move between items, A to select, B to move up in scope.\tSettings / General\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FMenu\tBackgroundOpacity\tFLOAT\t0.85\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tMenu Background Opacity\tSets the opacity of the background of the port menu.\tSettings / General\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\tCursorVisibility\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tCursor Always Visible\tMakes the cursor always visible, even in full screen.\tSettings / General\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FMenu\tSidebarSearch\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tSearch In Sidebar\tDisplays the Search menu as a sidebar entry in Settings instead of in the header.\tSettings / General\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FMenu\tSearchAutofocus\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tSearch Input Autofocus\tSearch input box gets autofocus when visible. Does not affect using other widgets.\tSettings / General\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\tBootSequence\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EDefault\u001F1\u001EAuthentic\u001F2\u001EFile Select\u001F3\u001EDebug Warp Screen\u001F4\u001EWarp Point\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tBoot Sequence\tConfigure what happens when starting or resetting the game.\\n\\nDefault: LUS logo -> N64 logo\\nAuthentic: N64 logo only\\nFile Select: Skip to file select menu\\nDebug Warp Screen: Skip to the debug warp screen\\nWarp Point: Skip to active warp point (if set), see Dev Tools -> General\tSettings / General\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\tTitleScreenTranslation\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tTranslate Title Screen\t\u0001\tSettings / General\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\tA11yTTS\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tText to Speech\tEnables text to speech for in-game dialogue\tSettings / General\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\tA11yDisableIdleCam\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tDisable Idle Camera Re-Centering\tDisables the automatic re-centering of the camera when idle.\tSettings / General\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\tA11yNoScreenFlashForFinishingBlow\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tDisable Screen Flash for Finishing Blow\tDisables the white screen flash on enemy kill.\tSettings / General\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\tA11yNoJabuWobble\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tDisable Jabu Wobble\tDisable the geometry wobble and camera distortion inside Jabu.\tSettings / General\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\tA11yNoHeatHaze\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tDisable Heat Haze\tDisable the heat haze distortion effect in Death Mountain / Fire Temple.\tSettings / General\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\tImGuiScale\tENUM\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ESmall\u001F1\u001ENormal\u001F2\u001ELarge\u001F3\u001EX-Large\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tImGui Menu Scaling\tChanges the scaling of the ImGui menu elements.\tSettings / General\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FVolume\tMaster\tINT\t40\t0\t100\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tMaster Volume\t\u0001\tSettings / Audio\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FVolume\tMainMusic\tINT\t100\t0\t100\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tMain Music Volume\t\u0001\tSettings / Audio\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FVolume\tSubMusic\tINT\t100\t0\t100\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tSub Music Volume\t\u0001\tSettings / Audio\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FVolume\tFanfare\tINT\t100\t0\t100\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFanfare Volume\t\u0001\tSettings / Audio\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FVolume\tSFX\tINT\t100\t0\t100\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tSound Effects Volume\t\u0001\tSettings / Audio\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\tInternalResolution\tFLOAT\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tInternal Resolution\tMultiplies your output resolution by the value inputted, as a more intensive but effective form of anti-aliasing.\tSettings / Graphics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\tMSAAValue\tINT\t1\t1\t8\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tAnti-aliasing (MSAA)\tActivates MSAA (multi-sample anti-aliasing) from 2x up to 8x, to smooth the edges of rendered geometry.\\nHigher sample count will result in smoother edges on models, but may reduce performance.\tSettings / Graphics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\tInterpolationFPS\tINT\t20\t20\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tCurrent FPS\t\u0001\tSettings / Graphics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\tMatchRefreshRate\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tMatch Refresh Rate\tMatches interpolation value to the refresh rate of your display.\tSettings / Graphics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\tVsyncEnabled\tBOOL\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tEnable Vsync\tRemoves tearing, but clamps your max FPS to your display's refresh rate.\tSettings / Graphics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\tSdlWindowedFullscreen\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tWindowed Fullscreen\tEnables Windowed Fullscreen Mode.\tSettings / Graphics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\tEnableMultiViewports\tBOOL\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tAllow multi-windows\tAllows multiple windows to be opened at once. Requires a reload to take effect.\tSettings / Graphics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FNotifications\tPosition\tENUM\t3\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ETop Left\u001F1\u001ETop Right\u001F2\u001EBottom Left\u001F3\u001EBottom Right\u001F4\u001EHidden\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tPosition\tWhich corner of the screen notifications appear in.\tSettings / Notifications\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FNotifications\tDuration\tFLOAT\t10.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tDuration (seconds)\tHow long notifications are displayed for.\tSettings / Notifications\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FNotifications\tBgOpacity\tFLOAT\t0.5\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tBackground Opacity\tHow opaque the background of notifications is.\tSettings / Notifications\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FNotifications\tSize\tFLOAT\t1.8\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tSize\tHow large notifications are.\tSettings / Notifications\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FNotifications\tMute\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tMute Notification Sound\tPrevent notifications from playing a sound.\tSettings / Notifications\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tAutosave\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tAutosave\tSave the game automatically on a 3 minute interval and when soft-resetting the game. The interval autosave will wait if the game is paused in any way (dialogue, pause screen up, cutscenes, etc.).\\n\\nThe soft-reset save will *not* trigger in cutscene maps like the Chamber of Sages!\tEnhancements / Quality of Life\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tAutosaveNotification\tBOOL\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tNotification on Autosave\tShow a notification when the game is autosaved.\tEnhancements / Quality of Life\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tRememberSaveLocation\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tRemember Save Location\tWhen loading a save, places Link at the last entrance he went through.\\nThis doesn't work if the save was made in grottos, fairy fountains, or dungeons.\tEnhancements / Quality of Life\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tBetterSaveMenu\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tBetter Save Menu\tReplaces the authentic save menu with a textbox that asks Yes or No for saving,\\nthen asks if you want to Continue, Reset, or Reset to Spawn.\tEnhancements / Quality of Life\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tChestSizeAndTextureMatchContents\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tContainers Match Contents\tToggle to change container textures to match their contents in randomizer games.\\nCategories: Major items, Lesser items, Junk items, Small keys, Boss keys, Skulltula Tokens.\tEnhancements / Quality of Life\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tChestSizeDependsStoneOfAgony\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tContainers of Agony\tOnly change the texture of containers if you have the Stone of Agony.\tEnhancements / Quality of Life\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tNightGSAlwaysSpawn\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tNighttime GS Always Spawn\tNighttime Skulltulas will spawn during both day and night.\tEnhancements / Quality of Life\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tDayGravePull\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tPull Grave During the Day\tAllows graves to be pulled when child during the day.\tEnhancements / Quality of Life\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tDampeAllNight\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tDampe Appears All Night\tMakes Dampe appear anytime during the night, not just his usual working hours.\tEnhancements / Quality of Life\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tMarketSneak\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tExit Market at Night\tAllows exiting Hyrule Castle Market Town to Hyrule Field at night by speaking to the guard next to the gate.\tEnhancements / Quality of Life\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tOpenAllHours\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tShops and Games Always Open\tShops and Minigames are open both day and night. Requires a scene reload to take effect.\tEnhancements / Quality of Life\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tPauseWarp\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tPause Warp\tSelection of warp song in pause menu initiates a warp. Disables song playback.\tEnhancements / Quality of Life\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tNaviOnL\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tAnswer Navi Prompt with L Button\tSpeak to Navi with L but enter First-Person Camera with C-Up.\tEnhancements / Quality of Life\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tNoInputForCredits\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tDon't Require Input for Credits Sequence\tRemoves the Input Requirement on Text boxes after defeating Ganon, allowing the Credits Sequence to continue to progress.\tEnhancements / Quality of Life\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tIncludeHeldInputsBufferWindow\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tInclude Held Inputs at the Start of Pause Buffer Input Window\tTypically, inputs that are held prior to the buffer window are not included in the buffer. This setting changes that behavior to include them. This may cause some inputs to be re-triggered undesireably, for instance Z-Targeting something you might not want to.\tEnhancements / Quality of Life\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tPauseBufferWindow\tINT\t0\t0\t40\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tPause Buffer Input Windowframes\tAdds back in a delay after unpausing before the game resumes playing again, where inputs can be held prematurely to be input immediately after the game resumes. This essentially brings back behaviour from console releases which are lost on default because SoH isn't limited to N64 hardware.\tEnhancements / Quality of Life\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\tSimulatedInputLag\tINT\t0\t0\t6\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tSimulated Input Lagframes\tBuffers your inputs to be executed a specified amount of frames later.\tEnhancements / Quality of Life\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FReworkedTargeting\tEnabled\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tReworked Targeting\tReworks targeting functionality\\n- Press Z while locked always untargets (in Toggle mode)\\n- Use the configured button combo to switch between targets\tEnhancements / Quality of Life\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FInjectItemCounts\tGoldSkulltula\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tGold Skulltula Tokens\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Quality of Life\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FInjectItemCounts\tHeartPiece\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tPieces of Heart\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Quality of Life\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FInjectItemCounts\tHeartContainer\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tHeart Containers\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Quality of Life\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tDisableCritWiggle\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tDisable Crit Wiggle\tDisable Random Camera Wiggle at Low Health.\tEnhancements / Quality of Life\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tBetterOwl\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tBetter Owl\tThe default response to Kaepora Gaebora is always that you understood what he said.\tEnhancements / Quality of Life\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tEasyButterflyFairies\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tEasy Butterfly Fairies\tButterflies will transform into a fairy as soon as you approach them with a Deku Stick, skipping the need to stand still and let the butterfly land on your stick.\tEnhancements / Quality of Life\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tDropThrowOnlyObjects\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tAllow Dropping Throw-Only Objects\tAllows normally throw-only objects (such as Cuccos, pots, grass, and small rocks) to be dropped by pressing A while standing still. Can be toggled while holding an object.\tEnhancements / Quality of Life\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tQuitFishingAtDoor\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tQuit Fishing at Door\tFisherman asks if you want to quit at the door if you try to leave the Fishing Pond while still holding the Fishing Rod.\tEnhancements / Quality of Life\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tInstantPutaway\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tInstant Putaway\tAllow Link to put items away without having to wait around.\tEnhancements / Quality of Life\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tResetNaviTimer\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tNavi Timer Resets on Scene Change\tResets the Navi timer on scene change. If you have already talked to her, she will try and talk to you again, instead of needing a save warp or death.\tEnhancements / Quality of Life\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tCowOfTime\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tLink's Cow in Both Time Periods\tAllows the Lon Lon Ranch Obstacle Course reward to be shared across time periods.\tEnhancements / Quality of Life\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FTimeSavers\tSleepingWaterfall\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EAlways\u001F1\u001EOnce\u001F2\u001ENever\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tPlay Zelda's Lullaby to Open Sleeping Waterfall\tAlways: Link must always play Zelda's Lullaby to open the waterfall entrance to Zora's Domain.\\nOnce: Link only needs to play Zelda's Lullaby once to open the waterfall; after that, it stays open permanently.\\nNever: Link never needs to play Zelda's Lullaby to open the waterfall. He only needs to have learned it and have an Ocarina.\tEnhancements / Quality of Life\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FTimeSavers\tSkipJabuJabuFish\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tSkip Feeding Jabu-Jabu\tAllow Link to enter Jabu-Jabu without feeding him a fish.\tEnhancements / Quality of Life\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FTimeSavers\u001FSkipCutscene\tIntro\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tSkip Intro\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Skips & Speed-ups\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FTimeSavers\u001FSkipCutscene\tEntrances\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tSkip Entrance Cutscenes\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Skips & Speed-ups\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FTimeSavers\u001FSkipCutscene\tStory\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tSkip Story Cutscenes\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Skips & Speed-ups\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FTimeSavers\u001FSkipCutscene\tLearnSong\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tSkip Song Cutscenes\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Skips & Speed-ups\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tWarpSongSkipAnimation\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tSkip Warp Cutscenes\tWarp songs skip the departure and arrival cutscenes, fading immediately to the destination.\tEnhancements / Skips & Speed-ups\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FTimeSavers\u001FSkipCutscene\tBossIntro\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tSkip Boss Introductions\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Skips & Speed-ups\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FTimeSavers\u001FSkipCutscene\tQuickBossDeaths\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tQuick Boss Deaths\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Skips & Speed-ups\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FTimeSavers\u001FSkipCutscene\tOnePoint\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tSkip One Point Cutscenes (Chests, Door Unlocks, etc.)\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Skips & Speed-ups\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FTimeSavers\tSkipOwlInteractions\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tSkip Owl Interactions\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Skips & Speed-ups\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FTimeSavers\tSkipMiscInteractions\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tSkip Misc Interactions\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Skips & Speed-ups\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FTimeSavers\tDisableTitleCard\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tDisable Title Card\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Skips & Speed-ups\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FTimeSavers\u001FSkipCutscene\tGlitchAiding\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tExclude Glitch-Aiding Cutscenes\tDon't skip cutscenes that are associated with useful glitches. Currently, it is only the Fire Temple Darunia CS, Forest Temple Poe Sisters CS, Dodongo Boss Door Switch CS, Water Temple Dragon Switch CS, the Box Skip One Point in Jabu, Early Hammer Switch CS in MQ Spirit, and Cow Switch Chest CS in MQ Jabu.\tEnhancements / Skips & Speed-ups\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tFastBottles\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tSkip Bottle Pickup Messages\tSkip Pickup Messages for Bottle Swipes.\tEnhancements / Skips & Speed-ups\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tFastDrops\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tSkip Consumable Item Pickup Messages\tSkip Pickup Messages for new Consumable Items.\tEnhancements / Skips & Speed-ups\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FTimeSavers\tSkipForcedDialog\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ENone\u001F1\u001ENavi\u001F2\u001ENPCs\u001F3\u001EAll\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tSkip Forced Dialog\tPrevent forced conversations with Navi and/or other NPCs.\tEnhancements / Skips & Speed-ups\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tSkipText\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tSkip Text\tHolding down B skips text.\tEnhancements / Skips & Speed-ups\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tTextSpeed\tINT\t1\t1\t6\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tText Speed\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Skips & Speed-ups\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tSlowTextSpeed\tINT\t1\t1\t5\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tSlow Text Speed\tChanges the speed of sections of text that normally are paced slower than the text surrounding it.\tEnhancements / Skips & Speed-ups\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tFasterHeavyBlockLift\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFaster Heavy Block Lift\tSpeeds up lifting Silver Rocks and Obelisks.\tEnhancements / Skips & Speed-ups\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tFasterShadowShip\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFaster Shadow Ship\tSpeeds up ship in Shadow Temple.\tEnhancements / Skips & Speed-ups\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tFastChests\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFast Chests\tMakes Link always kick the chest to open it, instead of doing the longer chest opening animation for major items.\tEnhancements / Skips & Speed-ups\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tImprovedRoll\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tImproved Roll\tAllows Link to chain a new roll by pressing A during a roll, maintaining maximum roll speed.\tEnhancements / Skips & Speed-ups\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tImprovedRollSteering\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tImproved Roll Steering\tAllows slight directional steering with the control stick while rolling. Steering is automatically disabled while Z is held, preserving Z-target roll glitch setups.\tEnhancements / Skips & Speed-ups\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tSkipSwimDeepEndAnim\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tSkip Water Take Breath Animation\tSkips Link's taking breath animation after coming up from water. This setting does not interfere with getting items from underwater.\tEnhancements / Skips & Speed-ups\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tFasterBottleEmpty\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tEmpty Bottles Faster\tSpeeds up emptying animation when dumping out the contents of a bottle.\tEnhancements / Skips & Speed-ups\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tClimbSpeed\tINT\t0\t0\t12\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tVine/Ladder Climb Speed +\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Skips & Speed-ups\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tFasterBlockPush\tINT\t0\t0\t5\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tBlock Pushing Speed +\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Skips & Speed-ups\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tCrawlSpeed\tINT\t1\t1\t5\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tCrawl Speed\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Skips & Speed-ups\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tGlitchAidingCrawlspaces\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tExclude Glitch-Aiding Crawlspaces\tDon't increase crawl speed when exiting glitch-useful crawlspaces.\\nCurrently it is only the BOTW crawlspace to a locked door.\tEnhancements / Skips & Speed-ups\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tMweepSpeed\tFLOAT\t1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tKing Zora Speed\tIncrease the speed of King Zora's move animation (\"mweep\")\tEnhancements / Skips & Speed-ups\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tFasterPauseMenu\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFaster Pause Menu\tSpeeds up animation of the pause menu, similar to Majora's Mask\tEnhancements / Skips & Speed-ups\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FTimeSavers\tSkipChildStealth\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tSkip Child Stealth\tThe crawlspace into Hyrule Castle goes straight to Zelda, skipping the guards.\tEnhancements / Skips & Speed-ups\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FTimeSavers\tSkipTowerEscape\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tSkip Tower Escape\tSkip the tower escape sequence between Ganondorf and Ganon.\tEnhancements / Skips & Speed-ups\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tInstantScarecrow\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tSkip Playing Scarecrow's Song\tPierre appears when an Ocarina is pulled out. Requires learning the Scarecrow's Song first.\\nWithout the randomizer option \"Start with Scarecrow's Song\" enabled for a seed, this still requires you to teach the scarecrow the song as both ages before summoning.\tEnhancements / Skips & Speed-ups\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tFasterRupeeAccumulator\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFaster Rupee Accumulator\tCauses your Wallet to fill and empty faster when you gain or lose money.\tEnhancements / Skips & Speed-ups\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tSkulltulaFreeze\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tNo Skulltula Freeze\tStops the game from freezing the player when picking up Gold Skulltula Tokens. Does not apply in randomizer savefiles.\tEnhancements / Skips & Speed-ups\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tSkipSaveConfirmation\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tSkip Save Confirmation\tSkip the \"Game Saved\" confirmation screen.\tEnhancements / Skips & Speed-ups\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tLinkDefaultName\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tLink as Default File Name\tAllows you to have \"Link\" as a premade file name.\tEnhancements / Skips & Speed-ups\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tFasterBeanSkull\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tSpawn Bean Skulltula Faster\tMakes Gold Skulltulas come out of bean patches faster after bugs dig into the center.\tEnhancements / Skips & Speed-ups\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tForgeTime\tINT\t3\t0\t3\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tBiggoron Forge Timedays\tAllows you to change the number of days it takes for Biggoron to forge the Biggoron's Sword.\tEnhancements / Skips & Speed-ups\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tDisableBombBillboarding\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tDisable Bomb Billboarding\tDisables bombs always rotating to face the camera. To be used in conjunction with mods that want to replace bombs with 3D objects.\tEnhancements / Graphics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tDisableGrottoRotation\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tDisable Grotto Fixed Rotation\tDisables Grottos rotating with the Camera. To be used in conjunction with mods that want to replace grottos with 3D objects.\tEnhancements / Graphics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tDisableLinkSwordTrail\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tDisable Link's Sword Trail\tDisables the sword trail effect when swinging Link's sword. Useful when using mods that replace Link's sword model.\tEnhancements / Graphics\n",
    "shipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tDisableFixedCamera\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tDisable Fixed Camera\tDisables the fixed camera in maps that use 2D pre-rendered backgrounds. Enable this when using a mod that implements 3D backdrops for these areas.\\nRequires Scene Change to alter.\tEnhancements / Graphics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tTextSpacing\tINT\t6\t4\t6\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tIngame Text Spacing\tSpace between text characters (useful for HD font textures).\tEnhancements / Graphics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tDisableLOD\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tDisable LOD\tTurns off the Level of Detail setting, making models use their Higher-Poly variants at any distance.\tEnhancements / Graphics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tEnemyHealthBar\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tEnemy Health Bars\tRenders a health bar for Enemies when Z-Targeted.\tEnhancements / Graphics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tNewDrops\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tEnable 3D Dropped Items/Projectiles\tReplaces most 2D items and projectiles on the overworld with their equivalent 3D models.\tEnhancements / Graphics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tPauseMenuAnimatedLink\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tAnimated Link in Pause Menu\tTurns the Static Image of Link in the Pause Menu's Equipment Subscreen into a model cycling through his idle animations.\tEnhancements / Graphics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tEquipmentAlwaysVisible\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tShow Age-Dependent Equipment\tMakes all equipment visible, regardless of age.\tEnhancements / Graphics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tScaleAdultEquipmentAsChild\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tScale Adult Equipment as Child\tScales all of the Adult Equipment, as well as moving some a bit, to fit on Child Link better. May not work properly with some mods.\tEnhancements / Graphics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tFirstPersonGauntlets\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tShow Gauntlets in First-Person\tRenders Gauntlets when using the Bow and Hookshot like in OoT3D.\tEnhancements / Graphics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tShowDoorLocksOnBothSides\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tShow Chains on Both Sides of Locked Doors\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Graphics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tToTMedallionsColors\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tColor Temple of Time's Medallions\tWhen Medallions are collected, the Medallion imprints around the Master Sword Pedestal in the Temple of Time will become colored-in.\tEnhancements / Graphics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tMinimalUI\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tMinimal UI\tHides most of the UI when not needed.\\nNOTE: Doesn't activate until scene transition.\tEnhancements / Graphics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tDisableTunicWarningText\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tDisable Hot/Underwater Warning Text\tDisables warning text when you don't have the Goron/Zora Tunic on in Hot/Underwater conditions.\tEnhancements / Graphics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tRememberMapToggleState\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tRemember Minimap State Between Areas\tPreserve the minimap visibility state when going between areas rather than default it to \"on\" when going through loading zones.\tEnhancements / Graphics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tVisualAgony\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tVisual Stone of Agony\tDisplays an icon and plays a sound when Stone of Agony should be activated, for those without rumble.\tEnhancements / Graphics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tNoHUDHeartAnimation\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tDisable HUD Heart Animations\tDisables the Beating Animation of the Hearts on the HUD.\tEnhancements / Graphics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tDrawLineupTick\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tGlitch Line-up Tick\tDisplays a tick in the top center of the screen to help with glitch line-ups in SoH, since traditional UI based line-ups do not work outside of 4:3\tEnhancements / Graphics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tDisableBlackBars\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tDisable Black Bar Letterboxes\tDisables Black Bar Letterboxes during cutscenes and Z-Targeting. NOTE: There may be minor visual glitches that were covered up by the black bars. Please disable this setting before reporting a bug.\tEnhancements / Graphics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tDynamicWalletIcon\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tDynamic Wallet Icon\tChanges the Rupee in the Wallet icon to match the wallet size you currently have.\tEnhancements / Graphics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tAlwaysShowDungeonMinimapIcon\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tAlways Show Dungeon Entrances\tAlways shows dungeon entrance icons on the Minimap.\tEnhancements / Graphics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tBetterAmmoRendering\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tBetter Ammo Rendering in Pause Menu\tAmmo counts in the pause menu will work correctly regardless of the position of items in the Inventory.\tEnhancements / Graphics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FFileSelect\tMoreInfo\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tMore Info\tShows what items you have collected in the File Select screen, like in N64 Randomizer.\tEnhancements / Graphics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FFileSelect\tTimeFlow\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tEnable Passage of Time\tThe skybox in the background of the File Select screen will go through the day and night cycle over time.\tEnhancements / Graphics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FFileSelect\tHideNormalQuest\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tHide Original\tHides the original game when selecting a quest type on the File Select screen.\tEnhancements / Graphics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FFileSelect\tHideMasterQuest\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tHide Master Quest\tHides the Master Quest option when selecting a quest type on the File Select screen.\tEnhancements / Graphics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FFileSelect\tHideRandomizerQuest\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tHide Randomizer\tHides the Randomizer option when selecting a quest type on the File Select screen.\tEnhancements / Graphics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FFileSelect\tHideBossRushQuest\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tHide Boss Rush\tHides the Boss Rush option when selecting a quest type on the File Select screen.\tEnhancements / Graphics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FFileSelect\tHideSpeedrunQuest\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tHide Speedrun\tHides the Speedrun option when selecting a quest type on the File Select screen.\tEnhancements / Graphics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FFileSelect\tHideSpeedrunMasterQuest\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tHide Speedrun Master Quest\tHides the Speedrun Master Quest option when selecting a quest type on the File Select screen.\tEnhancements / Graphics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\tLowResMode\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tN64 Mode\tSets the aspect ratio to 4:3 and lowers resolution to 240p, the N64's native resolution.\tEnhancements / Graphics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tRemoveSpinAttackDarkness\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tRemove Spin Attack Darkness\tRemove the Darkness that appears when charging a Spin Attack.\tEnhancements / Graphics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tDisableLinkSpinWithGoronPot\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tDisable Link Spinning With Goron Pot\tLink will not spin when the Goron Pot starts to spin.\tEnhancements / Graphics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tDisableDrawDistance\tINT\t1\t1\t5\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tIncrease Actor Draw Distance\tIncreases the range in which Actors/Objects are drawn.\tEnhancements / Graphics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tDisableKokiriDrawDistance\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tDisable Kokiri Fade\tThe Kokiri are mystical beings that fade into view when approached. Enabling this will remove their draw distance.\tEnhancements / Graphics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tWidescreenActorCulling\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tWidescreen Actor Culling\tAdjusts the Horizontal Culling Plane to account for Widescreen Resolutions.\tEnhancements / Graphics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tExtendedCullingExcludeGlitchActors\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tCull Glitch Useful Actors\tExclude Actors that are useful for Glitches from the extended culling ranges. Some actors may still draw in the extended ranges, but will not \"update\" so that certain glitches that leverage the original culling requirements will still work.\\n\\nThe following actors are excluded:\\n - White Clothed Gerudos\\n - King Zora\\n - Gossip Stones\\n - Boulders\\n - Blue Warps\\n - Darunia\\n - Gold Skulltulas\tEnhancements / Graphics\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tDpadEquips\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tEquip Items on Dpad\tEquip items and equipment on the D-pad. If used with \"D-pad on Pause Screen\", you must hold C-Up to equip instead of navigate.\tEnhancements / Items\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tItemUnequip\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tAllow unequipping Items\tAllows unequipping items from C-Buttons/D-pad by hovering over an equipped item and pressing the button it's equipped to.\tEnhancements / Items\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tAssignableTunicsAndBoots\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tAssignable Shields, Tunics and Boots\tAllows equipping Shields, Tunics and Boots to C-Buttons/D-pad.\tEnhancements / Items\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tEquipmentCanBeRemoved\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tEquipment Toggle\tAllows equipment to be removed by toggling it on/off in the equipment subscreen.\tEnhancements / Items\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tToggleStrength\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tAllow Strength Equipment to be Toggled\tAllows Strength to be toggled on and off by pressing A on the Strength Upgrade in the Equipment Subscreen of the Pause Menu. This allows performing some glitches that require the player to not have Strength.\tEnhancements / Items\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tUnsheatheWithoutSlashing\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tUnsheathe Sword Without Slashing\tAllows Link to unsheathe the sword without slashing automatically.\tEnhancements / Items\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tSwordToggle\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ENone\u001F1\u001EChild Toggle\u001F2\u001EBoth Ages\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tSword Toggle Options\tIntroduces Options for unequipping Link's sword\\n\\nNone: Only Biggoron's Sword/Giant's Knife can be toggled. Doing so will equip the Master Sword.\\n\\nChild Toggle: This will allow for completely unequipping any sword as Child link.\\n\\nBoth Ages: Any sword can be unequipped as either age. This may lead to swordless glitches as adult.\tEnhancements / Items\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tAskToEquip\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tAsk to Equip New Items\tAdds a prompt to equip newly-obtained Swords, Shields, and Tunics.\tEnhancements / Items\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tDpadNoDropOcarinaInput\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tPrevent Dropped Ocarina Inputs\tPrevent dropping inputs when playing the Ocarina too quickly.\tEnhancements / Items\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tFastOcarinaPlayback\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFast Ocarina Playback\tSkip the part where the Ocarina Playback is called when you play a song.\tEnhancements / Items\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tTimeTravel\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EDisabled\u001F1\u001EOcarina of Time\u001F2\u001EOcarina of Time + Master Sword\u001F3\u001EAny Ocarina\u001F4\u001EAny Ocarina + Master Sword\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tTime Travel with Song of Time\tAllows Link to freely change age by playing the Song of Time.\\nTime Blocks can still be used properly.\\n\\nRequirements:\\n - Obtained the Song of Time\\n - Obtained the Ocarina of Time (depends on selection)\\n - Obtained the Master Sword (depends on selection)\\n - Not within range of a Time Block\\n - Not within range of Ocarina Playing spots\tEnhancements / Items\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tMMBunnyHood\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EVanilla\u001F1\u001EFaster Run\u001F2\u001EFaster + Longer Jump\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tBunny Hood Effect\tWearing the Bunny Hood grants a speed and jump boost like in Majora's Mask.\\nCan also be limited to only the speed boost.\\nRandomizer logic only accounts for this when the seed's own \"Bunny Hood Effect\" setting is on.\\nAlso disables NPC's reactions to wearing the Bunny Hood.\tEnhancements / Items\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tAdultMasks\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tMasks Equippable as Adult\tAllows masks to be equipped normally from the pause menu as adult.\\nRandomizer logic only accounts for this when the seed's own \"Masks as Adult\" setting is on.\tEnhancements / Items\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tPersistentMasks\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tPersistent Masks\tStops masks from automatically unequipping in certain situations:\\n- When entering a new scene\\n- When not in any C-Button or the D-pad\\n- When saving and quitting\\n- When dying\\n- When traveling through time (if \"Masks Equippable as Adult\" is activated)\tEnhancements / Items\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tHideBunnyHood\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tInvisible Bunny Hood\tTurns Bunny Hood Invisible while still maintaining its effects.\tEnhancements / Items\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tMaskSelect\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tMask Select in Inventory\tAfter completing the mask trading sub-quest, press A and any direction on the mask slot to change masks.\tEnhancements / Items\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tRemoteBombchu\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tRemote Bombchu\tAllows you to control a Bombchu after dropping it.\\nControl Stick: Steer\\nB: Detonate\\nA: Quit Control\tEnhancements / Items\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tNutsExplodeBombs\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tDeku Nuts Explode Bombs\tMake Deku Nuts explode Bombs, similar to how they interact with Bombchus. This does not affect Bomb Flowers.\tEnhancements / Items\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tRemoveExplosiveLimit\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tRemove Explosive Limit\tRemoves the cap of 3 active explosives being deployed at once.\tEnhancements / Items\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tStaticExplosionRadius\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tStatic Explosion Radius\tExplosions are now a static size, like in Majora's Mask and OoT3D. Makes Bombchu hovering much easier.\tEnhancements / Items\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tDisableFirstPersonChus\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tPrevent Bombchus Forcing First-Person\tPrevent Bombchus from forcing the camera into first-person mode when released.\tEnhancements / Items\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tBetterBombchuShopping\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tBetter Bombchu Shopping\tBombchus do not sell out when bought, and a 10 pack of Bombchus costs 99 rupees instead of 100.\tEnhancements / Items\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tSeparateArrows\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tEquip Multiple Arrows at Once\tAllow the Bow and Magic Arrows to be equipped at the same time on different slots. NOTE: This will disable the behavior of the 'Equip Dupe' glitch.\tEnhancements / Items\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tSkipArrowAnimation\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tSkip Magic Arrow Equip Animation\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Items\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tBlueFireArrows\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tBlue Fire Arrows\tAllows Ice Arrows to melt Red Ice. May require a room reload if toggled during gameplay.\tEnhancements / Items\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tSunlightArrows\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tSunlight Arrows\tAllows Light Arrows to activate Sun Switches. May require a room reload if toggled during gameplay.\tEnhancements / Items\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tBowSlingshotAmmoFix\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tBow as Child/Slingshot as Adult\tAllows Child Link to use a Bow with Arrows.\\nAllows Adult Link to use a Slingshot with Seeds.\\n\\nRequires glitches or the 'Timeless Equipment' cheat to equip.\tEnhancements / Items\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tBowReticle\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tAiming Reticle for the Bow/Slingshot\tAiming with a Bow or Slingshot will display a reticle as with the Hookshot when the projectile is ready to fire.\tEnhancements / Items\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tBowArrowCycle\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tArrow Cycle\tAllows cycling between different arrow types (Normal, Fire, Ice, Light) while aiming the bow. Press the R button to cycle to the next available arrow type. Only works when aiming and only cycles to arrow types you own with sufficient magic.\tEnhancements / Items\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tHookshotableReticle\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tTargetable Hookshot Reticle\tMakes the Hookshot Reticle use a different color when aiming at hookshotable collision.\tEnhancements / Items\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tFastBoomerang\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tInstant Boomerang Recall\tInstantly return the Boomerang to Link by pressing its item button while it's in the air.\tEnhancements / Items\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tBoomerangFirstPerson\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tAim Boomerang in First-Person Mode\tChange aiming for the Boomerang from Third-Person to First-Person to see past Link's head.\tEnhancements / Items\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tBoomerangReticle\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tAiming Reticle for Boomerang\tAiming with the Boomerang will display a reticle as with the Hookshot.\tEnhancements / Items\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tBetterFarore\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tBetter Farore's Wind\tHelps FW persist between ages, gives Child and Adult separate FW points, and can be used in more places.\tEnhancements / Items\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tFastFarores\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFaster Farore's Wind\tGreatly decreases cast time of Farore's Wind magic spell.\tEnhancements / Items\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tRebottleBlueFire\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tRebottle Blue Fire\tBlue Fire dropped from a bottle can be bottled.\tEnhancements / Items\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tGravediggingTourFix\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFix the Gravedigging Tour Glitch\tFixes a bug where the Gravedigging Tour Heart Piece disappears if the area reloads.\tEnhancements / Fixes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tFixDampeGoingBackwards\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFix Dampé Going Backwards\tFixes Dampé going backwards in certain circumstances when the player is going backwards.\tEnhancements / Fixes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tFixKokiriForestQuestState\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFix Kokiri Forest Quest State\tFixes Kokiri animation state to match their text state when getting Zelda's Letter before Kokiri Emerald.\tEnhancements / Fixes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tFixFloorSwitches\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFix Raised Floor Switches\tFixes the two raised floor switches, the one in the Forest Temple basement and the one at the top of the Fire Temple. This will lower them, making activating them easier.\tEnhancements / Fixes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tFixZoraHintDialogue\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFix Zora Hint Dialogue\tFixes one Zora's dialogue giving a hint about bringing Ruto's Letter to King Zora to properly occur before moving King Zora rather than after.\tEnhancements / Fixes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tFixVineFall\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFix Falling from Vine Edges\tPrevents immediately falling off climbable surfaces if climbing on the edges.\tEnhancements / Fixes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tBushDropFix\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFix Bush Item Drops\tFixes the bushes to drop items correctly rather than spawning undefined items.\tEnhancements / Fixes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tFixFlexDrops\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFix Flex Drops\tThe flex drop gives whichever ammo you are lowest on, but doesn't check that you own the item to hold it, so the drop is lost. This makes it skip ammo you can't carry.\tEnhancements / Fixes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tEnemySpawnsOverWaterboxes\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFix Enemies not Spawning Near Water\tCauses respawning enemies, like Stalchildren, to appear on land near bodies of water. Fixes an incorrect calculation that acted like water underneath ground was above it.\tEnhancements / Fixes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tFixSawSoftlock\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFix Poacher's Saw Softlock\tPrevents the Poacher's Saw softlock from mashing through the text, or with Skip Text enabled.\tEnhancements / Fixes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tAnubisFix\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFix Anubis Fireballs\tMake Anubis Fireballs do Fire damage when reflected back at them with the Mirror Shield.\tEnhancements / Fixes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tGCDoorsAfterFireFix\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFix Goron City Doors After Fire Temple\tForces Goron City doors open if you somehow complete Fire Temple without talking to Goron Link and receiving the Goron Tunic.\tEnhancements / Fixes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tMQWaterLockFix\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFix MQ Water 1F Lock\tThe second small key lock in MQ Water Temple is removed before the player can reach it by a shared flag with some Stalfos on the way to Dark Link.\\nEnabling this will cause that lock to use a different flag, working as intended.\tEnhancements / Fixes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tDekuNutUpgradeFix\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFix Deku Nut Upgrade\tPrevents the Forest Stage Deku Nut upgrade from becoming unobtainable after receiving the Poacher's Saw.\tEnhancements / Fixes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tCrouchStabHammerFix\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFix Megaton Hammer Crouch Stab\tMake the Megaton Hammer's crouch stab able to destroy rocks without first swinging it normally.\tEnhancements / Fixes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tCrouchStabFix\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tRemove Power Crouch Stab\tMake crouch stabbing always do the same damage as a regular slash.\tEnhancements / Fixes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tFixBrokenGiantsKnife\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFix Broken Giant's Knife Bug\tFixes the Broken Giant's Knife flag not being reset when Medigoron fixes it.\tEnhancements / Fixes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tFixCameraDrift\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFix Camera Drift\tFixes camera slightly drifting to the left when standing still due to a math error. May impact certain glitches.\tEnhancements / Fixes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tFixCameraSwing\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFix Camera Swing\tFixes camera getting stuck on collision when standing still. Also fixes slight shift back in camera when Link stops moving. May impact certain glitches.\tEnhancements / Fixes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tFixHangingLedgeSwingRate\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFix Hanging Ledge Swing Rate\tFixes camera swing rate when the player falls off a ledge and the camera swings around. May impact certain glitches.\tEnhancements / Fixes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tFixMenuLR\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFix L&R Pause Menu\tMakes the L and R buttons in the pause menu the same color.\tEnhancements / Fixes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tFixDungeonMinimapIcon\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFix Dungeon Entrances\tRemoves the Dungeon Entrance icon on the top-left corner of the screen when no dungeon is present on the current map.\tEnhancements / Fixes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tTwoHandedIdle\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFix Two-Handed Idle Animations\tRe-Enables the two-handed idle animation, a seemingly finished animation that was disabled on accident in the original game.\tEnhancements / Fixes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tNaviTextFix\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFix Navi Text HUD Position\tCorrectly centers the Navi text prompt on the HUD's C-Up button.\tEnhancements / Fixes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tGerudoWarriorClothingFix\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFix Gerudo Warrior's Clothing Colors\tPrevent the Gerudo Warrior's clothes changing color when changing Link's tunic or using bombs in front of her.\tEnhancements / Fixes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tFixTexturesOOB\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFix Out of Bounds Textures\tFixes authentic out of bounds texture reads, instead loading textures with the correct size.\tEnhancements / Fixes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tFixEyesOpenWhileSleeping\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFix Link's Eyes Open while Sleeping\tFixes Link's eyes being open in the opening cutscene when he is supposed to be sleeping.\tEnhancements / Fixes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tFixHammerHand\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFix Hand Holding Hammer\tFixes Adult Link having a backwards left hand when holding the Megaton Hammer.\tEnhancements / Fixes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tSceneSpecificDirtPathFix\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EDisabled\u001F1\u001EConsistent Vanish\u001F2\u001ENo Vanish\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFix Vanishing Paths\tDisabled: Paths vanish more the higher the resolution (Z-Fighting is based on resolution).\\nConsistent: Certain paths vanish the same way in all resolutions.\\nNo Vanish: Paths do not vanish, Link seems to sink in to some paths.\\nThis might affect other decal effects.\tEnhancements / Fixes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tSilverRupeeJingleExtend\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFix Missing Jingle after 5 Silver Rupees\tAdds 5 higher pitches for the Silver Rupee Jingle for the rooms with more than 5 Silver Rupees. Only relevant for playthroughs involving Master Quest Dungeons.\tEnhancements / Fixes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tFixDaruniaDanceSpeed\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFix Darunia Dancing too Fast\tFixes Darunia's dancing speed so he dances to the beat of Saria's Song, like in the Original Game.\tEnhancements / Fixes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tCreditsFix\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFix Credits Timing (PAL)\tExtend certain credits scenes so the music lines up properly with the visuals. (PAL only)\tEnhancements / Fixes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tRedGanonBlood\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tRed Ganon Blood\tRestore the original red blood from NTSC 1.0/1.1. Disable for Green blood.\tEnhancements / Fixes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tGSCutscene\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tRestore Old Gold Skulltula Cutscene\tRestore pre-release behavior where defeating a Gold Skulltula will play a cutscene showing it die.\tEnhancements / Fixes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tPulsateBossIcon\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tPulsate Boss Icon\tRestores an unfinished feature to pulsate the boss room icon when you are in the boss room.\tEnhancements / Fixes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tSariaGestureFriendsForever\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tSaria's Friends Forever Gesture\tRestores an unused animation of Saria when she says, \"Saria and Link will be friends forever.\"\tEnhancements / Fixes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tHoverFishing\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFish while Hovering\tRestore a bug from NTSC 1.0 that allows casting the Fishing Rod while using the Hover Boots.\tEnhancements / Fixes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tN64WeirdFrames\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tN64 Weird Frames\tRestores N64 Weird Frames allowing weirdshots and weirdslides to behave the same as N64.\tEnhancements / Fixes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tBombchusOOB\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tBombchus Out of Bounds\tAllows Bombchus to explode out of bounds. Similar to GameCube and Wii VC.\tEnhancements / Fixes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tQuickPutaway\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tQuick Putaway\tRestore a bug from NTSC 1.0 that allows putting away an item without an animation and performing Putaway Ocarina Items.\tEnhancements / Fixes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tQuickBongoKill\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tQuick Bongo Kill\tRestore a bug from NTSC 1.0 that allows bypassing Bongo Bongo's intro cutscene to quickly kill him.\tEnhancements / Fixes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tEarlyEyeballFrog\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tEarly Eyeball Frog\tRestores a bug from NTSC 1.0/1.1 that allows you to obtain the eyeball frog from King Zora instead of the Zora Tunic by Holding Shield.\tEnhancements / Fixes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tChildHookshotSoftlock\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tChild Hookshot Softlock\tUsing the Hookshot as child softlocks.\tEnhancements / Fixes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tNGCKaleidoSwitcher\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFix L&Z Page Switch in Pause Menu\tMakes L and R switch pages like on the GameCube. Z opens the Debug Menu instead.\tEnhancements / Fixes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tWideShutterDoorRange\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tWide Door Ranges\tRestores the wider range of certain shutter doors from NTSC 1.0.\\nNotably affects Jabu-Jabu and boss doors.\tEnhancements / Fixes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tGraveHoles\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tGrave Hole Jumps\tRestores NTSC 1.0 behavior where Link jumps over grave holes and grabs the ledges.\tEnhancements / Fixes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tPermanentHeartLoss\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tPermanent Heart Loss\tWhen you lose 4 quarters of a heart you will permanently lose that Heart Container.\\n\\nDisabling this after the fact will restore your Heart Containers.\tEnhancements / Difficulty\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tDamageMult\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EVanilla (1x)\u001F1\u001EDouble (2x)\u001F2\u001EQuadruple (4x)\u001F3\u001EOctuple (8x)\u001F4\u001EFoolish (16x)\u001F5\u001ERidiculous (32x)\u001F6\u001EMerciless (64x)\u001F7\u001EPure Torture (128x)\u001F8\u001EOHKO (256x)\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tDamage Multiplier\tModifies all sources of damage not affected by other sliders:\\n2x: Can survive all common attacks from the start of the game.\\n4x: Dies in 1 hit to any substantial attack from the start of the game.\\n8x: Can only survive trivial damage from the start of the game.\\n16x: Can survive all common attacks with max health without double defense.\\n32x: Can survive all common attacks with max health and double defense.\\n64x: Can survive trivial damage with max health without double defense.\\n128x: Can survive trivial damage with max health and double defense.\\n256x: Cannot survive damage.\tEnhancements / Difficulty\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tFallDamageMult\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EVanilla (1x)\u001F1\u001EDouble (2x)\u001F2\u001EQuadruple (4x)\u001F3\u001EOctuple (8x)\u001F4\u001EFoolish (16x)\u001F5\u001ERidiculous (32x)\u001F6\u001EMerciless (64x)\u001F7\u001EPure Torture (128x)\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFall Damage Multiplier\tModifies all fall damage:\\n2x: Can survive all fall damage from the start of the game.\\n4x: Can only survive short fall damage from the start of the game.\\n8x: Cannot survive any fall damage from the start of the game.\\n16x: Can survive all fall damage with max health without double defense.\\n32x: Can survive all fall damage with max health and double defense.\\n64x: Can survive short fall damage with double defense.\\n128x: Cannot survive fall damage.\tEnhancements / Difficulty\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tVoidDamageMult\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EVanilla (1x)\u001F1\u001EDouble (2x)\u001F2\u001EQuadruple (4x)\u001F3\u001EOctuple (8x)\u001F4\u001EFoolish (16x)\u001F5\u001ERidiculous (32x)\u001F6\u001EMerciless (64x)\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tVoid Damage Multiplier\tModifies damage taken after falling into a void:\\n2x: Can survive void damage from the start of the game.\\n4x: Cannot survive void damage from the start of the game.\\n8x: Can survive void damage twice with max health without double defense.\\n16x: Can survive void damage with max health without double defense.\\n32x: Can survive void damage with max health and double defense.\\n64x: Cannot survive void damage.\tEnhancements / Difficulty\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tBonkDamageMult\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ENo Damage\u001F1\u001E0.25 Hearts\u001F2\u001E0.5 Hearts\u001F3\u001E1 Heart\u001F4\u001E2 Hearts\u001F5\u001E4 Hearts\u001F6\u001E8 Hearts\u001F7\u001EOHKO\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tBonk Damage Multiplier\tModifies Damage taken after Bonking.\tEnhancements / Difficulty\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tFullHealthSpawn\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tSpawn with Full Health\tRespawn with Full Health instead of 3 hearts.\tEnhancements / Difficulty\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tNoHeartDrops\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tNo Heart Drops\tDisables Heart Drops, but not Heart Placements, like from a Deku Scrub running off.\\nThis simulates Hero Mode from other games in the series.\tEnhancements / Difficulty\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tNoRandomDrops\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tNo Random Drops\tDisables Random Drops, except from the Goron Pot, Dampe, and Bosses.\tEnhancements / Difficulty\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tEnableBombchuDrops\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tEnable Bombchu Drops\tBombchus will sometimes drop in place of Bombs.\tEnhancements / Difficulty\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tTreesDropSticks\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tTrees Drop Sticks\tBonking into Trees will have a chance to drop up to 3 Sticks. Must have obtained sticks previously.\tEnhancements / Difficulty\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tDampeDropRate\tENUM\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ENone\u001F1\u001EVanilla\u001F2\u001EJalapeño\u001F3\u001ESerrano\u001F4\u001EHabanero\u001F5\u001EGhost Pepper\u001F6\u001EDampe's Inferno\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tDampe Drop Rate\tAdjusts rate Dampe drops flames during race.\tEnhancements / Difficulty\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tDeleteFileOnDeath\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tDelete File on Death\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Difficulty\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tSwitchTimerMultiplier\tINT\t0\t-5\t5\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tSwitch Timer Multiplier\t-5 will be half as much time, +5 will be 6x as much time. Affects timed switches, torches, GTG statue eyes, & doors in race with Dampe.\tEnhancements / Difficulty\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tGoronPot\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tAlways Win Goron Pot\tAlways get the Heart Piece/Purple Rupee from the Spinning Goron Pot.\tEnhancements / Difficulty\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tDampeWin\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tAlways Win Dampe Digging Game\tAlways win the Heart Piece/Purple Rupee on the first dig in Dampe's Grave Digging game. In a Randomizer file, this defaults to on if this enhancement has never been changed.\tEnhancements / Difficulty\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tAllDogsRichard\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tAll Dogs are Richard\tAll dogs can be traded in and will count as Richard.\tEnhancements / Difficulty\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tCuccoStayDurationMult\tINT\t1\t1\t5\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tCuccos Stay Put Multiplier\tCuccos will stay in place longer after putting them down, by a multiple of the value of the slider.\tEnhancements / Difficulty\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tCuccosToReturn\tINT\t7\t0\t7\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tCuccos Needed By Anju\tThe amount of cuccos needed to receive the bottle from Anju the Cucco Lady.\tEnhancements / Difficulty\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tHyperBosses\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tHyper Bosses\tAll Major Bosses move and act twice as fast.\tEnhancements / Difficulty\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tHyperEnemies\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tHyper Enemies\tAll Regular Enemies and Mini-Bosses move and act twice as fast.\tEnhancements / Difficulty\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tGuardVision\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tEnable Visual Guard Vision\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Difficulty\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tLeeverSpawnRate\tINT\t0\t0\t10\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tLeever Spawn Rateseconds\tThe time between groups of Leevers spawning.\tEnhancements / Difficulty\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tCustomizeShootingGallery\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tCustomize Behavior\tTurn on/off changes to the shooting gallery behavior.\tEnhancements / Minigames\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tInstantShootingGalleryWin\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tInstant Win\tSkips the Shooting Gallery minigame.\tEnhancements / Minigames\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tConstantAdultGallery\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tNo Rupee Randomization\tForces the rupee order to not be randomized as adult, making it the same as child.\tEnhancements / Minigames\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tShootingGalleryAmmoChild\tINT\t15\t10\t30\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tChild Starting Ammunitionseeds\tThe ammunition at the start of the Shooting Gallery minigame as Child.\tEnhancements / Minigames\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tShootingGalleryAmmoAdult\tINT\t15\t10\t30\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tAdult Starting Ammunitionarrows\tThe ammunition at the start of the Shooting Gallery minigame as Adult.\tEnhancements / Minigames\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tCustomizeBombchuBowling\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tCustomize Behavior\tTurn on/off changes to the Bombchu Bowling behavior.\tEnhancements / Minigames\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tBombchuBowlingNoSmallCucco\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tRemove Small Cucco\tPrevents the small Cucco from appearing in the Bombchu Bowling minigame.\tEnhancements / Minigames\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tBombchuBowlingNoBigCucco\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tRemove Big Cucco\tPrevents the big Cucco from appearing in the Bombchu Bowling minigame.\tEnhancements / Minigames\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tBombchuBowlingAmmo\tINT\t10\t3\t20\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tBombchu Countbombchus\tThe number of Bombchus available at the start of the Bombchu Bowling minigame.\tEnhancements / Minigames\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tBombchuBowlingFirstPrize\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ERandom\u001F1\u001EBomb Bag\u001F2\u001EPurple Rupee\u001F3\u001EBombchus\u001F4\u001EHeart Piece\u001F5\u001EBombs\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFirst Prize\tThe prize the cycle starts on.\tEnhancements / Minigames\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tCustomizeHorsebackArchery\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tCustomize Behavior\tTurn on/off changes to the Horseback Archery minigame behavior.\tEnhancements / Minigames\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tInstantHorsebackArcheryWin\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tInstant Win\tSkips the Horseback Archery minigame, automatically awarding the prize.\tEnhancements / Minigames\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tHorsebackArcheryAlwaysScore\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tAlways Score 100\tEvery arrow that hits a target scores 100 points (inner ring) regardless of where it lands.\tEnhancements / Minigames\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tHorsebackArcheryAmmo\tINT\t20\t15\t40\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tArrow Count\tThe number of arrows available at the start of the Horseback Archery minigame.\tEnhancements / Minigames\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tCustomizeFrogsOcarinaGame\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tCustomize Behavior\tTurn on/off changes to the Frogs' Ocarina Game behavior.\tEnhancements / Minigames\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tInstantFrogsGameWin\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tInstant Win\tSkips the Frogs' Ocarina Game.\tEnhancements / Minigames\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tFrogsUnlimitedFailTime\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tUnlimited Playback Time\tRemoves the timer to play back the song.\tEnhancements / Minigames\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tFrogsModifyFailTime\tINT\t1\t1\t5\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tModify Note Timer\tAdjusts the time allowed for playback before failing.\tEnhancements / Minigames\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tCustomizeOcarinaGame\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tCustomize Behavior\tTurn on/off changes to the Lost Woods Ocarina Game behavior.\tEnhancements / Minigames\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tInstantOcarinaGameWin\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tInstant Win\tSkips the Lost Woods Ocarina Memory Game.\tEnhancements / Minigames\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FOcarinaGame\tNoteSpeed\tINT\t1\t1\t5\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tNote Play Speed\tAdjust the speed that the Skull Kids play the notes.\tEnhancements / Minigames\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tOcarinaUnlimitedFailTime\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tUnlimited Playback Time\tRemoves the timer to play back the song.\tEnhancements / Minigames\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FOcarinaGame\tStartingNotes\tINT\t3\t1\t8\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tNumber of Starting Notesnotes\tAdjust the number of notes the Skull Kids play to start the first round.\tEnhancements / Minigames\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FOcarinaGame\tRoundOneNotes\tINT\t5\t\u0001\t8\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tRound One Notesnotes\tAdjust the number of notes you need to play to end the first round.\tEnhancements / Minigames\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FOcarinaGame\tRoundTwoNotes\tINT\t6\t\u0001\t8\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tRound Two Notesnotes\tAdjust the number of notes you need to play to end the second round.\tEnhancements / Minigames\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FOcarinaGame\tRoundThreeNotes\tINT\t8\t\u0001\t8\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tRound Three Notesnotes\tAdjust the number of notes you need to play to end the third round.\tEnhancements / Minigames\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tSkipAmyPuzzle\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tSolve Amy's Puzzle\tAmy's block-pushing puzzle is instantly solved.\tEnhancements / Minigames\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tIngoRaceOnce\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ETwice\u001F1\u001EOnce\u001F2\u001ENone\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tNumber of Races\tNumber of races Link must win against Ingo to earn Epona. Only works if Link is riding Epona, not the other rideable horse.\tEnhancements / Minigames\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FDivingGame\tTimeLimit\tINT\t50\t30\t120\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tTime Limitseconds\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Minigames\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tCustomizeFishing\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tCustomize Behavior\tTurn on/off changes to the Fishing behavior.\tEnhancements / Minigames\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tInstantFishing\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tInstant Fishing\tAll fish will be caught instantly.\tEnhancements / Minigames\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tGuaranteeFishingBite\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tGuarantee Bite\tWhen a line is stable, guarantee a bite. Otherwise use Default logic.\tEnhancements / Minigames\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tFishNeverEscape\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFish never Escape\tOnce a hook has been set, Fish will never let go while being reeled in.\tEnhancements / Minigames\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tLoachesAlwaysAppear\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tLoaches always Appear\tLoaches will always appear in the fishing pond instead of every four visits.\tEnhancements / Minigames\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tSkipKeepConfirmation\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tSkip Keep Confirmation\tThe Pond Owner will not ask to confirm if you want to keep a smaller Fish.\tEnhancements / Minigames\n",
    "shipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tAllHyruleLoaches\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tAll Fish are Hyrule Loaches\tEvery fish in the Fishing Pond will always be a Hyrule Loach.\\n\\nNOTE: This requires reloading the area.\tEnhancements / Minigames\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tMinimumFishWeightChild\tINT\t10\t3\t10\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tChild Minimum Weightlbs.\tThe minimum weight for the unique Fishing Reward as a child.\tEnhancements / Minigames\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tMinimumFishWeightAdult\tINT\t13\t6\t13\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tAdult Minimum Weightlbs.\tThe minimum weight for the unique fishing reward as an adult.\tEnhancements / Minigames\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tFishingBlankB\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tAllow fishing with blank B\tAllow fishing even when not having any item equipped on the B button, fixing a vanilla bug. Always enabled in randomizer.\tEnhancements / Minigames\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tDampeBothPrizes\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tDampe's Race\tDampe awards both prizes on the first race, not just the Hookshot.\tEnhancements / Minigames\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tHorsebackArcheryBothPrizes\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tHorseback Archery\tLink can win both Horseback Archery prizes in one attempt\tEnhancements / Minigames\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tBounceOffWalls\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tBounce off Walls\tAllows Link to bounce off walls when linear velocity is high enough. This is relevant when frequently being knocked back by traps, CC, or in Anchor.\tEnhancements / Extra Modes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tMirroredWorldMode\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EDisabled\u001F1\u001EAlways\u001F2\u001ERandom\u001F3\u001ERandom (Seeded)\u001F4\u001EDungeons\u001F5\u001EDungeons (Vanilla)\u001F6\u001EDungeons (MQ)\u001F7\u001EDungeons Random\u001F8\u001EDungeons Random (Seeded)\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tMirrored World\tMirrors the world horizontally:\\n\\n - Always: Always mirror the world.\\n - Random: Randomly decide to mirror the world on each scene change.\\n - Random (Seeded): Scenes are mirrored based on the current randomizer seed/file.\\n - Dungeons: Mirror the world in Dungeons.\\n - Dungeons (Vanilla): Mirror the world in Vanilla Dungeons.\\n - Dungeons (MQ): Mirror the world in MQ Dungeons.\\n - Dungeons Random: Randomly decide to mirror the world in Dungeons.\\n - Dungeons Random (Seeded): Dungeons are mirrored based on the current randomizer seed/file.\tEnhancements / Extra Modes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tIvanCoopModeEnabled\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tIvan the Fairy (Coop Mode)\tEnables Ivan the Fairy. Player 2 can control Ivan and press the C-Buttons to use items and mess with Player 1!\tEnhancements / Extra Modes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tDogFollowsEverywhere\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tDogs Follow You Everywhere\tAllows dogs to follow you anywhere you go, even if you leave the Market.\tEnhancements / Extra Modes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tRupeeDash\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tRupee Dash Mode\tRupees reduce over time; Link suffers damage when the count hits 0.\tEnhancements / Extra Modes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tRupeeDashScaling\tBOOL\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tRupee Dash Wallet Scaling\tThe larger Link's wallet, the faster Rupees reduce.\tEnhancements / Extra Modes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tRupeeDashInterval\tINT\t5\t1\t10\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tRupee Dash Intervalseconds\tInterval between Rupee reduction in Rupee Dash Mode.\tEnhancements / Extra Modes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tShadowTag\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tShadow Tag Mode\tA Wallmaster follows Link everywhere, don't get caught!\tEnhancements / Extra Modes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\tHurtContainer\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tHurt Container Mode\tChanges Heart Piece and Heart Container functionality.\\n\\n - Each Heart Container or full Heart Piece reduces Link's Hearts by 1.\\n - Can be enabled retroactively after a File has already started.\tEnhancements / Extra Modes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FExtraTraps\tEnabled\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tAdditional Traps\tEnables additional Trap variants.\tEnhancements / Extra Modes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FExtraTraps\tIce\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFreeze Traps\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Extra Modes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FExtraTraps\tBurn\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tBurn Traps\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Extra Modes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FExtraTraps\tShock\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tShock Traps\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Extra Modes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FExtraTraps\tKnockback\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tKnockback Traps\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Extra Modes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FExtraTraps\tSpeed\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tSpeed Traps\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Extra Modes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FExtraTraps\tBomb\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tBomb Traps\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Extra Modes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FExtraTraps\tVoid\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tVoid Traps\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Extra Modes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FExtraTraps\tAmmo\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tAmmo Traps\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Extra Modes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FExtraTraps\tKill\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tDeath Traps\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Extra Modes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FExtraTraps\tTeleport\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EOff\u001F1\u001ESimple\u001F2\u001EAdvanced\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tTeleport Traps\tWhere a Teleport Trap can send you. Off keeps them out of the trap pool.\\n\\nSimple: Link's House and the six warp song pads.\\nAdvanced: The same pool the randomizer uses when it shuffles spawns and warp songs.\tEnhancements / Extra Modes\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\tInfiniteMoney\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tMoney\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Cheats\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\tInfiniteHealth\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tHealth\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Cheats\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\tInfiniteAmmo\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tAmmo\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Cheats\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\tInfiniteMagic\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tMagic\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Cheats\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\tInfiniteNayru\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tNayru's Love\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Cheats\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\tInfiniteEponaBoost\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tEpona Boost\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Cheats\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\tTimelessEquipment\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tTimeless Equipment\tAllows any item to be equipped, regardless of age.\\nAlso allows child to use adult strength upgrades.\tEnhancements / Cheats\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\tNoRestrictItems\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tUnrestricted Items\tAllows you to use any item at any location\tEnhancements / Cheats\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\tSuperTunic\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tSuper Tunic\tMakes every tunic have the effects of every other tunic.\tEnhancements / Cheats\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\tFireproofDekuShield\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFireproof Deku Shield\tPrevents the Deku Shield from burning on contact with fire.\tEnhancements / Cheats\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\tShieldTwoHanded\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tShield with Two-Handed Weapons\tThis allows you to put up your shield with any two-handed weapon in hand except for Deku Sticks.\tEnhancements / Cheats\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\tDekuStick\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ENormal\u001F1\u001EUnbreakable\u001F2\u001EUnbreakable + Always on Fire\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tDeku Sticks\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Cheats\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\tBombTimerMultiplier\tFLOAT\t1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tBomb Timer Multiplier\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Cheats\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\tHookshotEverything\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tHookshot Everything\tMakes every surface in the game hookshotable.\tEnhancements / Cheats\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\tHookshotReachMultiplier\tFLOAT\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tHookshot Reach Multiplier\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Cheats\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\tNoClip\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tNo Clip\tAllows you to walk through walls.\tEnhancements / Cheats\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\tClimbEverything\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tClimb Everything\tMakes every surface in the game climbable.\tEnhancements / Cheats\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\tMoonJumpOnL\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tMoon Jump on L\tHolding L makes you float into the air.\tEnhancements / Cheats\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\tNoRedeadFreeze\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tNo ReDead/Gibdo Freeze\tPrevents ReDeads and Gibdos from being able to freeze you with their scream.\tEnhancements / Cheats\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\tNoKeeseGuayTarget\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tKeese/Guay don't Target You\tKeese and Guay no longer target you and simply ignore you as if you were wearing the Skull Mask.\tEnhancements / Cheats\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\tDisableSandstorm\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tDisable Haunted Wasteland Sandstorm\tDisables sandstorm effect in Haunted Wasteland.\tEnhancements / Cheats\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\tGSTargetable\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tTargetable Gold Skulltula\tAllows Z-Targeting Gold Skulltulas.\tEnhancements / Cheats\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\tEasyFrameAdvance\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tEasy Frame Advancing with Pause\tContinue holding START button when unpausing to only advance a single frame and then re-pause.\tEnhancements / Cheats\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\tEasyISG\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tEasy ISG\tPassive Infinite Sword Glitch\\nIt makes your sword's swing effect and hitbox stay active indefinitely.\tEnhancements / Cheats\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\tEasyQPA\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tEasy QPA\tGives you the glitched damage value of the quick put away glitch.\tEnhancements / Cheats\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\tDropsDontDie\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tDrops Don't Despawn\tDrops from enemies, grass, etc. don't disappear after a set amount of time.\tEnhancements / Cheats\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\tNoFishDespawn\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFish don't Despawn\tPrevents fish from automatically despawning after a while when dropped.\tEnhancements / Cheats\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\tNoBugsDespawn\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tBugs don't Despawn\tPrevents bugs from automatically despawning after a while when dropped.\tEnhancements / Cheats\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\tFreezeTime\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFreeze Time\tFreezes the time of day.\tEnhancements / Cheats\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\tTimeSync\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tTime Sync\tSyncs the in-game time with the real world time.\tEnhancements / Cheats\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\u001FSpeedModifier\tSpeedToggle\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tToggle modifier instead of holding\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Cheats\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\u001FSpeedModifier\tDoesntChangeJump\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tDon't affect jump distance/velocity\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Cheats\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\u001FSpeedModifier\tValue\tFLOAT\t1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tMultiplier\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Cheats\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\tSaveStatePromise\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tI promise I have read the warning\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Cheats\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\tSaveStatesEnabled\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tI understand, enable save states\tF5 to save, F6 to change slots, F7 to load\tEnhancements / Cheats\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\tEnableBetaQuest\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tEnable Beta Quest\tTurns on OoT Beta Quest. *WARNING*: This will reset your game!\tEnhancements / Cheats\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\tBetaQuestWorld\tINT\t0\t0\t8\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tBeta Quest World\tSet the Beta Quest world to explore. *WARNING*: Changing this will reset your game!\\nCtrl+Click to type in a value.\tEnhancements / Cheats\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgTimeDisplay\tFontScale\tFLOAT\t1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tFont Scale\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Timers\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgTimeDisplay\tShowWindowBG\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tHide Background\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Timers\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgRandoSettings\tManualSeedEntry\tBOOL\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tManual seed entry\t\u0001\tRandomizer / General\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgRandoEnhancements\tRandoRelevantNavi\tBOOL\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tRando-Relevant Navi Hints\tReplace Navi's overworld quest hints with rando-related gameplay hints.\tRandomizer / General\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgRandoEnhancements\tRandomizeRupeeNames\tBOOL\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tRandom Rupee Names\tWhen obtaining Rupees, randomize what the Rupee is called in the textbox.\tRandomizer / General\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgRandoEnhancements\tColoredMapsAndCompasses\tBOOL\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tMap & Compass Colors Match Dungeon\tMatches the color of maps & compasses to the dungeon they belong to. This helps identify maps & compasses from afar and adds a little bit of flair.\\n\\nThis only applies to seeds with maps & compasses shuffled to \"Any Dungeon\", \"Overworld\", or \"Anywhere\".\tRandomizer / General\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgRandoEnhancements\tGenericJabberNutModel\tBOOL\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tJabber Nut Colors Match Kind\tWith Shuffle Speak, the jabber nut model & color will be generic.\tRandomizer / General\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgRandoEnhancements\tQuestItemFanfares\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tQuest Item Fanfares\tPlay unique fanfares when obtaining quest items (medallions/stones/songs). Note that these fanfares can be longer than usual.\tRandomizer / General\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgRandoEnhancements\tMysteriousShuffle\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tMysterious Shuffled Items\tDisplays a \"Mystery Item\" model in place of any freestanding/GS/shop items that were shuffled, and replaces item names for them and scrubs and merchants, regardless of hint settings, so you never know what you're getting.\tRandomizer / General\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgRandoEnhancements\tSimplerBossSoulModels\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tSimpler Boss Soul Models\tWhen shuffling boss souls, they'll appear as a simpler model instead of showing the bosses' models. This might make boss souls more distinguishable from a distance, and can help with performance.\tRandomizer / General\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgRandoEnhancements\u001FTimeSavers\tSkipGetItemAnimation\tENUM\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EDisabled\u001F1\u001EJunk Items\u001F2\u001EAll Items\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tSkip Get Item Animations\t\u0001\tRandomizer / General\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgRandoEnhancements\u001FTimeSavers\tSkipGetItemAnimationScale\tFLOAT\t10.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tItem Scale\tThe size of the item when it is picked up.\tRandomizer / General\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgRandoEnhancements\tEntrancesOnSigns\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tSigns Hint Entrances\tIf enabled, signs near loading zones will tell you where they lead.\tRandomizer / General\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgRemote\u001FCrowdControl\tEnemyNameTags\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tEnemy Name Tags\tWhen viewers spawn enemies, the enemy will have a name tag above them with the viewer's name.\tNetwork / Crowd Control\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgRemote\u001FCrowdControl\tSpawnedEnemiesIgnoredIngame\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tSpawned Enemies Ignored Ingame\tEnemies spawned by CrowdControl won't be considered for \"clear enemy rooms\", so they don't need to be killed to complete these rooms.\tNetwork / Crowd Control\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FAdvancedResolution\tVerticalResolutionToggle\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tSet fixed vertical resolution (disables resolution slider)\tOverride the resolution scale slider and use the settings below, irrespective of window size.\tSettings / Advanced Resolution\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FAdvancedResolution\tPixelPerfectMode\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tPixel Perfect Mode\tDon't scale image to fill window.\tSettings / Advanced Resolution\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FAdvancedResolution\u001FIntegerScale\tFitAutomatically\tBOOL\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tAutomatically scale image to fit viewport\tAutomatically sets scale factor to fit window. Only available in Pixel Perfect Mode.\tSettings / Advanced Resolution / Integer Scale\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FAdvancedResolution\u001FIntegerScale\tExceedBoundsBy\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tAllow integer scale factor to go +1 above maximum screen bounds.\t\u0001\tSettings / Advanced Resolution / Integer Scale\nshipwright\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FAdvancedResolution\tEnabled\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t9.3.1\tEnable advanced settings.\t\u0001\tSettings / Graphics\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FItemTracker\tWindowGroup\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tSplit Window Groups\t\u0001\tSettings / Item Tracker\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FItemTracker\tItemCounts\tBOOL\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tShow Item Counts\t\u0001\tSettings / Item Tracker\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FItemTracker\tWindowType\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EFloating\u001F1\u001EWindow\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tWindow Type\t\u0001\tSettings / Item Tracker\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FItemTracker\tScale\tFLOAT\t1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tScale\t\u0001\tSettings / Item Tracker\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FItemTracker\tOpacity\tFLOAT\t0.5\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tOpacity\t\u0001\tSettings / Item Tracker\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FTimeSplits\tEnable\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tEnable Time Splits\t\u0001\tSettings / Time Splits\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FTimeSplits\tShowHeaders\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tShow Headers\t\u0001\tSettings / Time Splits\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FTimeSplits\tOpacity\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tHide Background\t\u0001\tSettings / Time Splits\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FTimeSplits\tHighlight\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tHighlight Active Split\t\u0001\tSettings / Time Splits\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FTimeSplits\tFollow\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tFollow Active Split\t\u0001\tSettings / Time Splits\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FTimeSplits\tCompare\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tCompare Splits\t\u0001\tSettings / Time Splits\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FGraphics\u001FMotionBlur\tMode\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EDynamic (default)\u001F1\u001EAlways Off\u001F2\u001EAlways On\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tMotion Blur Mode\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Graphics / Motion Blur\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FGraphics\u001FMotionBlur\tInterpolate\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tInterpolate\tChange motion blur capture to also happen on interpolated frames instead of only on game frames.\\nThis notably reduces the overall motion blur strength but smooths out the trails.\tEnhancements / Graphics / Motion Blur\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FGraphics\u001FMotionBlur\tStrength\tINT\t180\t0\t255\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tStrength\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Graphics / Motion Blur\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCollisionViewer\tEnabled\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tEnabled\t\u0001\tCollision Viewer\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCollisionViewer\tApplyShading\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tApply Shading\t\u0001\tCollision Viewer\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCollisionViewer\tSceneCollisionMode\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EDisabled\u001F1\u001ESolid\u001F2\u001ETransparent\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tScene\t\u0001\tCollision Viewer\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCollisionViewer\tBGActorsCollisionMode\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EDisabled\u001F1\u001ESolid\u001F2\u001ETransparent\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tBG Actors\t\u0001\tCollision Viewer\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCollisionViewer\tColCheckCollisionMode\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EDisabled\u001F1\u001ESolid\u001F2\u001ETransparent\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tCol Check\t\u0001\tCollision Viewer\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCollisionViewer\tWaterboxCollisionMode\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EDisabled\u001F1\u001ESolid\u001F2\u001ETransparent\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tWaterbox\t\u0001\tCollision Viewer\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEventLog\tEnabled\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tEnable\t\u0001\tEvent Log\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEventLog\u001FFilter\tFlagSet\tBOOL\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tFlagSet\t\u0001\tEvent Log / Filter\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEventLog\u001FFilter\tFlagUnset\tBOOL\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tFlagUnset\t\u0001\tEvent Log / Filter\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEventLog\u001FFilter\tSceneFlagSet\tBOOL\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tSceneFlagSet\t\u0001\tEvent Log / Filter\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEventLog\u001FFilter\tSceneFlagUnset\tBOOL\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tSceneFlagUnset\t\u0001\tEvent Log / Filter\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEventLog\u001FFilter\tActorInit\tBOOL\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tActorInit\t\u0001\tEvent Log / Filter\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEventLog\u001FFilter\tActorKill\tBOOL\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tActorKill\t\u0001\tEvent Log / Filter\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEventLog\u001FFilter\tSceneInit\tBOOL\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tSceneInit\t\u0001\tEvent Log / Filter\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEventLog\u001FFilter\tRoomInit\tBOOL\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tRoomInit\t\u0001\tEvent Log / Filter\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEventLog\u001FFilter\tOpenText\tBOOL\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tOpenText\t\u0001\tEvent Log / Filter\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEventLog\u001FFilter\tItemGive\tBOOL\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tItemGive\t\u0001\tEvent Log / Filter\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgRando\tEnabled\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tEnable Rando (Randomizes new files upon creation)\t\u0001\tRando\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgRando\tGenerateSpoiler\tBOOL\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tGenerate Spoiler File\t\u0001\tRando\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgRando\tCSMC\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tContainer Style Matches Contents\tThis will make the contents of a container match the container itself. Eg chests, pots, crates, grass, etc.\tRando\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgRando\tJunkItems\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EDefault (Cycle)\u001F1\u001EStatic\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tJunk Items\tNote: For both Options, junk items will be randomly rolled from a pool of obtainable items.\\n\\nDefault (Cycle): Junk items will cycle every few seconds, allowing you to choose which item to pick up\\n\\nStatic: Junk items will be static, only changing when obtainability status changes.\tRando\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgRando\tTrapItems\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EDefault (Dynamic)\u001F1\u001EStatic\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tTrap Behavior\t\u0001\tRando\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgRando\u001FCheckTracker\tOutOfLogicMode\tENUM\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ENormal\u001F1\u001EColored\u001F2\u001EHidden\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tOut of Logic Checks\t\u0001\tRando / Check Tracker\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgRando\u001FCheckTracker\tCollectedMode\tENUM\t2\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ENormal\u001F1\u001EColored\u001F2\u001EHidden\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tCollected Checks\t\u0001\tRando / Check Tracker\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgRando\u001FCheckTracker\tSkippedMode\tENUM\t2\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ENormal\u001F1\u001EColored\u001F2\u001EHidden\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tSkipped Checks\t\u0001\tRando / Check Tracker\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgRando\u001FCheckTracker\tShowCurrentScene\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tOnly Show Current Scene\t\u0001\tRando / Check Tracker\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgRando\u001FCheckTracker\tScrollToCurrentScene\tBOOL\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tAuto Scroll To Current Scene\t\u0001\tRando / Check Tracker\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgRando\u001FCheckTracker\tShowSearch\tBOOL\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tShow Search\t\u0001\tRando / Check Tracker\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgRando\u001FCheckTracker\tShowCheckTypeFilter\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tShow Check Type Filters\t\u0001\tRando / Check Tracker\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgRando\u001FCheckTracker\tOpacity\tFLOAT\t0.5\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tOpacity\t\u0001\tRando / Check Tracker\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgRando\u001FCheckTracker\tScale\tFLOAT\t1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tScale\t\u0001\tRando / Check Tracker\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FMenu\tTheme\tENUM\t5\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ERed\u001F1\u001EDark Red\u001F2\u001EOrange\u001F3\u001EGreen\u001F4\u001EDark Green\u001F5\u001ELight Blue\u001F6\u001EBlue\u001F7\u001EDark Blue\u001F8\u001EIndigo\u001F9\u001EViolet\u001F10\u001EPurple\u001F11\u001EBrown\u001F12\u001EGray\u001F13\u001EDark Gray\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tMenu Theme\tChanges the Theme of the Menu Widgets.\tSettings / General\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FMenu\tBackgroundOpacity\tFLOAT\t0.85\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tMenu Background Opacity\tSets the opacity of the background of the port menu.\tSettings / General\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\tControlNav\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tMenu Controller Navigation\tAllows controller navigation of the 2Ship menu (Settings, Enhancements,...)\\nCAUTION: This will disable game inputs while the menu is visible.\\n\\nD-pad to move between items, A to select, B to move up in scope.\tSettings / General\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\tCursorVisibility\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tCursor Always Visible\tMakes the cursor always visible, even in full screen.\tSettings / General\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FMenu\tSidebarSearch\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tSearch In Sidebar\tDisplays the Search menu as a sidebar entry in Settings instead of in the header.\tSettings / General\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FMenu\tSearchAutofocus\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tSearch Input Autofocus\tSearch input box gets autofocus when visible. Does not affect using other widgets.\tSettings / General\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FMods\tAlternateAssetsHotkey\tBOOL\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tAlt Assets Tab hotkey\tAllows pressing the Tab key to toggle alternate assets.\tSettings / General\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\tImGuiScale\tENUM\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ESmall\u001F1\u001ENormal\u001F2\u001ELarge\u001F3\u001EX-Large\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tImGui Menu Scaling\tChanges the scaling of the ImGui menu elements.\tSettings / General\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FAudio\tMasterVolume\tFLOAT\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tMaster Volume\tAdjust the overall sound volume.\tSettings / Audio\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FAudio\tMainMusicVolume\tFLOAT\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tMain Music Volume\tAdjust the background music volume.\tSettings / Audio\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FAudio\tSubMusicVolume\tFLOAT\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tSub Music Volume\tAdjust the sub music volume.\tSettings / Audio\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FAudio\tSoundEffectsVolume\tFLOAT\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tSound Effects Volume\tAdjust the sound effects volume.\tSettings / Audio\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FAudio\tFanfareVolume\tFLOAT\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tFanfare Volume\tAdjust the fanfare volume.\tSettings / Audio\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FAudio\tAmbienceVolume\tFLOAT\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tAmbience Volume\tAdjust the ambient sound volume.\tSettings / Audio\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\tInternalResolution\tFLOAT\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tInternal Resolution\tMultiplies your output resolution by the value inputted, as a more intensive but effective form of anti-aliasing.\tSettings / Graphics\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\tMSAAValue\tINT\t1\t1\t8\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tAnti-aliasing (MSAA)\tActivates MSAA (multi-sample anti-aliasing) from 2x up to 8x, to smooth the edges of rendered geometry.\\nHigher sample count will result in smoother edges on models, but may reduce performance.\tSettings / Graphics\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\tgInterpolationFPS\tINT\t20\t20\t360\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tCurrent FPS\tUses Matrix Interpolation to create extra frames, resulting in smoother graphics. This is purely visual and does not impact game logic, execution of glitches etc.\\n\\nA higher target FPS than your monitor's refresh rate will waste resources, and might give a worse result.\tSettings / Graphics\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\tgMatchRefreshRate\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tMatch Refresh Rate\tMatches interpolation value to the refresh rate of your display.\tSettings / Graphics\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\tVsyncEnabled\tBOOL\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tEnable Vsync\tRemoves tearing, but clamps your max FPS to your displays refresh rate.\tSettings / Graphics\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\tSdlWindowedFullscreen\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tWindowed Fullscreen\tEnables Windowed Fullscreen Mode.\tSettings / Graphics\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\tEnableMultiViewports\tBOOL\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tAllow multi-windows\tAllows multiple windows to be opened at once. Requires a reload to take effect.\tSettings / Graphics\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgNotifications\tDuration\tFLOAT\t10.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tDurationseconds\tHow long notifications are displayed for.\tSettings / Overlay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgNotifications\tBgOpacity\tFLOAT\t0.5\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tBackground Opacity\tHow opaque the background of notifications is.\tSettings / Overlay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgNotifications\tSize\tFLOAT\t1.8\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tSize\tHow large notifications are.\tSettings / Overlay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgDisplayOverlay\tBackground\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tHide Window Background\tHides the background of the Display Overlay window.\tSettings / Overlay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgDisplayOverlay\tScale\tFLOAT\t1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tScale\tAdjust the Scale for the Display Overlay window.\tSettings / Overlay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCamera\tFixTargettingCameraSnap\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tFix Targeting Camera Snap\tFixes the camera snap that occurs when you are moving and press the targeting button.\tEnhancements / Camera\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCamera\u001FFirstPerson\tDisableFirstPersonAutoCenterView\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tDisable Auto-Centering\tDisables the auto-centering of the camera in first person mode.\tEnhancements / Camera\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCamera\u001FFirstPerson\tInvertX\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tInvert X Axis\tInverts the X Axis of the Camera in First Person Mode.\tEnhancements / Camera\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCamera\u001FFirstPerson\tInvertY\tBOOL\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tInvert Y Axis\tInverts the Y Axis of the Camera in First Person Mode.\tEnhancements / Camera\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCamera\u001FFirstPerson\tSensitivityX\tFLOAT\t1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tX Axis Sensitivity\tAdjusts the Sensitivity of the X Axis in First Person Mode.\tEnhancements / Camera\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCamera\u001FFirstPerson\tSensitivityY\tFLOAT\t1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tY Axis Sensitivity\tAdjusts the Sensitivity of the Y Axis in First Person Mode.\tEnhancements / Camera\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCamera\u001FFirstPerson\tGyroEnabled\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tGyro Aiming\tEnables Gyro Aiming in First Person Mode.\tEnhancements / Camera\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCamera\u001FFirstPerson\tGyroInvertX\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tInvert Gyro X Axis\tInverts the X Axis of the Gyro in First Person Mode.\tEnhancements / Camera\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCamera\u001FFirstPerson\tGyroInvertY\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tInvert Gyro Y Axis\tInverts the Y Axis of the Gyro in First Person Mode.\tEnhancements / Camera\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCamera\u001FFirstPerson\tGyroSensitivityX\tFLOAT\t1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tGyro X Axis Sensitivity\tAdjusts the Sensitivity of the X Axis of the Gyro in First Person Mode.\tEnhancements / Camera\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCamera\u001FFirstPerson\tGyroSensitivityY\tFLOAT\t1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tGyro Y Axis Sensitivity\tAdjusts the Sensitivity of the Y Axis of the Gyro in First Person Mode.\tEnhancements / Camera\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCamera\u001FFirstPerson\tRightStickEnabled\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tRight Stick Aiming\tEnables Right Stick Aiming in First Person Mode.\tEnhancements / Camera\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCamera\u001FFirstPerson\tMoveInFirstPerson\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tMove while aiming\tAllows movement with the left stick while in first person mode.\tEnhancements / Camera\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCamera\u001FFirstPerson\tRightStickInvertX\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tInvert Right Stick X Axis\tInverts the X Axis of the Right Stick in First Person Mode.\tEnhancements / Camera\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCamera\u001FFirstPerson\tRightStickInvertY\tBOOL\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tInvert Right Stick Y Axis\tInverts the Y Axis of the Right Stick in First Person Mode.\tEnhancements / Camera\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCamera\u001FFirstPerson\tRightStickSensitivityX\tFLOAT\t1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tRight Stick X Axis Sensitivity\tAdjusts the Sensitivity of the X Axis of the Right Stick in First Person Mode.\tEnhancements / Camera\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCamera\u001FFirstPerson\tRightStickSensitivityY\tFLOAT\t1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tRight Stick Y Axis Sensitivity\tAdjusts the Sensitivity of the Y Axis of the Right Stick in First Person Mode.\tEnhancements / Camera\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCamera\u001FFreeLook\tEnable\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tFree Look\tEnables free look camera control.\\nNote: You must remap C buttons off of the right stick in the controller config menu, and map the camera stick to the right stick.\tEnhancements / Camera\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCamera\u001FFreeLook\tMaxCameraDistance\tINT\t185\t100\t900\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tCamera Distance\tMaximum Camera Distance for Free Look.\tEnhancements / Camera\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCamera\u001FFreeLook\tTransitionSpeed\tINT\t25\t1\t900\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tCamera Transition Speed\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Camera\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCamera\u001FFreeLook\tMaxPitch\tFLOAT\t72.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tMax Camera Height Angle\\xC2\\xB0\tMaximum Height of the Camera.\tEnhancements / Camera\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCamera\u001FFreeLook\tMinPitch\tFLOAT\t-49.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tMin Camera Height Angle\\xC2\\xB0\tMinimum Height of the Camera.\tEnhancements / Camera\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCamera\u001FDebugCam\tEnable\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tDebug Camera\tEnables debug camera control.\tEnhancements / Camera\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCamera\u001FRightStick\tInvertXAxis\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tInvert Camera X Axis\tInverts the Camera X Axis\tEnhancements / Camera\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCamera\u001FRightStick\tInvertYAxis\tBOOL\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tInvert Camera Y Axis\tInverts the Camera Y Axis\tEnhancements / Camera\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCamera\u001FRightStick\u001FCameraSensitivity\tX\tFLOAT\t1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tThird-Person Camera\\nHorizontal Sensitivity\tAdjust the Sensitivity of the x axis when in Third Person.\tEnhancements / Camera\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCamera\u001FRightStick\u001FCameraSensitivity\tY\tFLOAT\t1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tThird-Person Camera\\nVertical Sensitivity\tAdjust the Sensitivity of the x axis when in Third Person.\tEnhancements / Camera\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCamera\u001FDebugCam\t6DOF\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tEnable Roll (6\\xC2\\xB0 of Freedom)\tThis allows for all six degrees of movement with the camera, NOTE: Yaw will work differently in this system, instead rotating around the focal point, rather than a polar axis.\tEnhancements / Camera\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCamera\u001FDebugCam\tCameraSpeed\tFLOAT\t0.5\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tCamera Speed\tAdjusts the speed of the Camera.\tEnhancements / Camera\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\tInfiniteHealth\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tInfinite Health\tAlways have full Hearts.\tEnhancements / Cheats\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\tInfiniteMagic\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tInfinite Magic\tAlways have full Magic.\tEnhancements / Cheats\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\tInfiniteRupees\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tInfinite Rupees\tAlways have a full Wallet.\tEnhancements / Cheats\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\tInfiniteConsumables\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tInfinite Consumables\tAlways have max Consumables, you must have collected the consumables first.\tEnhancements / Cheats\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\tInfiniteEponaCarrots\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tInfinite Epona Carrots\tAllows Epona to boost without consuming carrots.\tEnhancements / Cheats\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\tEasyFrameAdvance\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tEasy Frame Advance\tContinue holding START button when unpausing to only advance a single frame and then re-pause.\tEnhancements / Cheats\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\tLongerFlowerGlide\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tLonger Deku Flower Glide\tAllows Deku Link to glide longer, no longer dropping after a certain distance.\tEnhancements / Cheats\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\tNoClip\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tNo Clip\tAllows Link to phase through collision.\tEnhancements / Cheats\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\tUnbreakableRazorSword\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tUnbreakable Razor Sword\tAllows to Razor Sword to be used indefinitely without dulling its blade.\tEnhancements / Cheats\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\tUnrestrictedItems\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tUnrestricted Items\tAllows all Forms to use all Items.\tEnhancements / Cheats\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\tHookshotAnywhere\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tHookshot Anywhere\tAllows most surfaces to be hookshot-able.\tEnhancements / Cheats\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\tMoonJumpOnL\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tMoon Jump on L\tHolding L makes you float into the air.\tEnhancements / Cheats\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\tElegyAnywhere\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tElegy of Emptiness Anywhere\tAllows Elegy of Emptiness outside of Ikana.\tEnhancements / Cheats\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\tClimbAnywhere\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tClimb Anywhere\tAllows climbing on most walls regardless of vines.\tEnhancements / Cheats\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgCheats\u001FSpeedModifier\tValue\tFLOAT\t1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tMultiplier\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Cheats\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FPlayer\tFastFlowerLaunch\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tFast Deku Flower Launch\tSpeeds up the time it takes to be able to get maximum height fromlaunching out of a Deku Flower.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FPlayer\tInfiniteDekuHopping\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tInfinite Deku Hopping\tAllows Deku Link to hop indefinitely in water without drowning. This also prevents the velocity loss while in the air.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FPlayer\tInstantPutaway\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tInstant Putaway\tAllows Link to instantly puts away held item without waiting.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FPlayer\tUnsheatheWithoutSlashing\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tUnsheathe Sword Without Slashing\tAllows Link to unsheathe sword without slashing automatically.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FPlayer\tFierceDeityPutaway\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tFierce Deity Putaway\tAllows Fierce Deity Link to put away his sword.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FPlayer\tClimbSpeed\tINT\t1\t1\t5\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tClimb speed\tIncreases the speed at which Link climbs vines and ladders.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FPlayer\tFasterPushAndPull\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tFaster Push/Pull\tSpeeds up the time it takes to push/pull various objects.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FPlayer\tPreventDiveOverWater\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tPrevent Diving Over Water\tPrevents Link from automatically diving over bodies of water.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FPlayer\tUnderwaterOcarina\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tUnderwater Ocarina\tAllows Zora to use the Ocarina of Time when grounded underwater.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FPlayer\tManualJump\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tManual Jump\tZ + A to Jump and B while midair to Jump Attack.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FDpad\tDpadEquips\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tDpad Equips\tAllows you to equip items to your D-pad.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FEquipment\tItemUnequip\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tUnequip Items\tIn the pause menu, press the same C-button or D-pad button an item is equipped to in order to unequip it.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FEquipment\tMagicArrowEquipSpeed\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tFast Magic Arrow Equip Animation\tRemoves the animation for equipping Magic Arrows.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FPlayerActions\tInstantRecall\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tInstant Fin Boomerangs Recall\tPressing B will instantly recall the fin boomerang back to Zora Link after they are thrown.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FEquipment\tTwoHandedSwordSpinAttack\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tTwo-Handed Sword Spin Attack\tEnables magic spin attacks for the Fierce Deity Sword and Great Fairy's Sword.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FEquipment\tBetterPictoMessage\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tBetter Picto Message\tInform the player what target if any is being captured in the pictograph.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FItems\tPictoBoxOnCUp\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tPicto Box on C-Up\tPress C-Up to activate the Pictograph Box once acquired, without needing to equip it to a C-button.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FPlayerActions\tArrowCycle\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tArrow Type Cycling\tWhile aiming the bow, use R to cycle between Normal, Fire, Ice and Light arrows.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FEquipment\tInvertShieldY\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tInvert Shield Y Axis\tInvert the Y axis while holding the shield so that it moves up with the left stick.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FEquipment\tGreatFairySwordBButton\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tGreat Fairy Sword B-Button Attack\tWhen the Great Fairy's Sword is held, pressing B attacks with it instead of drawing your equipped sword. The sword can still be put away with A as normal.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgModes\tPlayAsKafei\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tPlay as Kafei\tRequires scene reload to take effect.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgModes\tHyruleWarriorsStyledLink\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tHyrule Warriors Styled Link\tWhen acquired, places the Keaton and Fierce Deity masks on Link similarly to how he wears them in Hyrule Warriors.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgModes\tTimeMovesWhenYouMove\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tTime Moves when you Move\tTime only moves when Link is not standing still.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgModes\u001FMirroredWorld\tStoneTowerTempleFix\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tFix Inverted Stone Tower Temple\tMirrors (or unmirrors) the inverted Stone Tower Temple to make its layout consistent.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FGameplay\tExtendedProjectileInteractionDistance\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tExtended Projectile Interaction Distance\tAllows projectiles and explosions to hit breakable objects at a distance matching your Increase Actor Draw Distance setting.\\n\\nDoes not affect pickup ranges, talk prompts, or physical body collision.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FShops\tCuriosityShopRefills\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tCuriosity Shop Refills\tAdds refillable bottles to the Curiosity Shop after completing certain prerequisites:\\n- Seahorse: After obtaining a Bottle, Zora Mask, Pictograph Box & (Rando Only) Swim Ability\\n- Gold Dust: After obtaining the Gold Dust bottle\\n- Chateau Romani: After obtaining Chateau Romani\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n",
    "2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FA11y\tNoScreenFlashForEnemyKill\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tDisable Screen Flash for Enemy Kills\tDisables the white screen flash on enemy kill.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FA11y\tNoFinalDayQuakes\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tDisable Final Day Quakes\tEarthquakes will not occur on the final day.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FGraphics\tBowReticle\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tBow Reticle\tGives the bow a reticle when you draw an arrow.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FMinigames\tMarkShootingGalleryOctoroks\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tMark Shooting Gallery Octoroks\tPlaces markers on the Town Shooting Gallery Octoroks, indicating whether they should be hit.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FItems\tExtraPowderKegs\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tExtra Powder Kegs\tAllows carrying up to 3 Powder Kegs at once instead of the vanilla limit of 1.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FEquipment\tBombArrows\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tBomb Arrows\tAllows equipping Bomb Arrows by equipping Bombs onto a bow button in the pause menu.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FPlayerActions\tRemoteBombchu\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tRemote Bombchu Control\tAllows you to control the direction of the Bombchu while it is moving. Press B to detonate. Press A to stop controlling the Bombchu.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FEquipment\tChuDrops\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tBombchu Drops\tWhen a bomb drop is spawned, it has a 50% chance to be a Bombchu instead.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FItems\tRemoveExplosiveLimit\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tRemove Explosive Limit\tRemoves the cap of 3 active explosives being deployed at once.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FSaving\tFileSlot3\tBOOL\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\t3rd Save File Slot\tAdds a 3rd file slot that can be used for saves\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FSaving\tNewFileSetup\tBOOL\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tNew File Setup Steps\tAfter picking an empty file, asks whether it should be a randomizer file and lets you apply one of your loaded presets before entering a name.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FSaving\tPersistentOwlSaves\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tPersistent Owl Saves\tContinuing a save will not remove the owl save. Playing Song of Time, allowing the moon to crash or finishing the game will remove the owl save and become the new last save.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FSaving\tPauseSave\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tPause Menu Save\tRe-introduce the pause menu save system. Pressing B in the pause menu will give you the option to create a persistent Owl Save from your current location.\\n\\nWhen loading back into the game, you will be placed either at the entrance of the dungeon you saved in, or in South Clock Town, unless Remember Save Location is enabled.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FSaving\tRememberSaveLocation\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tRemember Save Location\tWhen loading a save, places Link at the last entrance he went through.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FSaving\tAutosave\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tAutosave\tAutomatically create a persistent Owl Save on the chosen interval.\\n\\nWhen loading back into the game, you will be placed either at the entrance of the dungeon you saved in, or in South Clock Town, unless Remember Save Location is enabled.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FSaving\tAutosaveInterval\tINT\t5\t1\t60\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tAutosave Intervalminutes\tSets the interval between Autosaves.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCycle\tSaveOnMoonCrash\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tSave Game on Moon Crash\tMoon Crashes will save game data similar to the Song of Time,\\ninstead of wiping owl save data. Automatically enabled in glitchless \\nrando seeds.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCycle\tDoNotResetBottleContent\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tDo not reset Bottle content\tPlaying the Song of Time will not reset the bottles' content.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCycle\tDoNotResetConsumables\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tDo not reset Consumables\tPlaying the Song of Time will not reset the consumables.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCycle\tDoNotResetRazorSword\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tDo not reset Razor Sword\tPlaying the Song of Time will not reset the Sword back to Kokiri Sword.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCycle\tDoNotResetRupees\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tDo not reset Rupees\tPlaying the Song of Time will not reset the your rupees.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCycle\tDoNotResetTimeSpeed\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tDo not reset Time Speed\tPlaying the Song of Time will not reset the current time speed set by Inverted Song of Time.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCycle\tDoNotResetChateau\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tDo not reset Chateau status\tPlaying the Song of Time will not reset the infinite magic status granted by Chateau Romani.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCycle\tDoNotResetScarecrowSong\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tDo not reset Scarecrow's Song\tPlaying the Song of Time will not reset the Scarecrow's Song.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCycle\tKeepExpressMail\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tKeep Express Mail\tAllows the player to keep the Express Mail in their inventory after delivering it the first time, so that both deliveries can be done within one cycle.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCycle\tStopOceansideSpiderHouseSquatter\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tStop Oceanside Spider House squatter\tThe Oceanside Spider House squatter will not move in until the player interacts with him. Forced on for randomizers.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCycle\tOceansideWalletAnyDay\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tOceanside wallet any day\tAllows the wallet reward to be collected on any day.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCycle\tTingleAlwaysInClockTown\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tTingle Always in Clock Town\tTingle will always appear in North Clock Town, not just during the day.\tEnhancements / Gameplay\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FGraphics\t24HoursClock\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\t24 Hours Clock\tChanges from a 12 Hour to a 24 Hour Clock.\tEnhancements / Graphics\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FMods\tAlternateAssets\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tUse Alternate Assets\tToggle between standard assets and alternate assets. Usually mods will indicate if this setting has to be used or not.\tEnhancements / Graphics\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FMods\tDisableBombBillboarding\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tDisable Bomb Billboarding\tDisables bombs always rotating to face the camera. To be used in conjunction with mods that want to replace bombs with 3D objects.\tEnhancements / Graphics\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FMods\tDisableGrottoRotation\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tDisable Grotto Fixed Rotation\tDisables Grottos rotating with the Camera. To be used in conjuction with mods that want to replace grottos with 3D objects.\tEnhancements / Graphics\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FGraphics\t3DItemDrops\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\t3D Item Drops\tMakes item drops 3D\tEnhancements / Graphics\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FGraphics\tAuthenticLogo\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tAuthentic Logo\tHide the game version and build details and display the authentic model and texture on the boot logo start screen.\tEnhancements / Graphics\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FGraphics\tDisableBlackBars\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tDisable Black Bar Letterboxes\tDisables Black Bar Letterboxes during cutscenes and Z-targeting.\\nNote: There may be minor visual glitches that were covered up by the black bars.\\nPlease disable this setting before reporting a bug.\tEnhancements / Graphics\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FGraphics\tEnemyHealthBars\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tEnemy Health Bars\tRenders a health bar for enemies and bosses when Z-targeted.\tEnhancements / Graphics\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FGraphics\tFixSceneGeometrySeams\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tFix Scene Geometry Seams\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Graphics\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FGraphics\tDisableSceneGeometryDistanceCheck\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tDisable Scene Geometry Distance Check\tDisables the distance check for scene geometry, allowing it to be drawn no matter how far away it is from the player. This may have unintended side effects.\tEnhancements / Graphics\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FGraphics\tActorCullingAccountsForWidescreen\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tWidescreen Actor Culling\tAdjusts the culling planes to account for widescreen resolutions. This may have unintended side effects.\tEnhancements / Graphics\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FGraphics\tIncreaseActorDrawDistance\tINT\t1\t1\t5\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tIncrease Actor Draw Distance\tIncrease the range in which Actors are drawn. This may have unintended side effects.\tEnhancements / Graphics\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\tLowResMode\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tN64 Mode\tSets the aspect ratio to 4:3 and lowers resolution to 240p, the N64's native resolution.\tEnhancements / Graphics\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FMasks\tEquipWhileSwimming\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tEquippable While Swimming\tHuman Link can equip any non-transformation mask while swimming.\tEnhancements / Items/Songs\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FMasks\tBlastMaskKeg\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tBlast Mask has Powder Keg Force\tBlast Mask can also destroy objects only the Powder Keg can.\tEnhancements / Items/Songs\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FMasks\tFastTransformation\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tFast Transformation\tRemoves the delay when using transformation masks.\tEnhancements / Items/Songs\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FMasks\t3DSMaskEquip\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\t3DS Style Mask Equipping\tAllows equipping masks while in other forms, returning you to human form with the mask immediately equipped, like in MM3D.\tEnhancements / Items/Songs\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FMasks\tEasyMaskEquip\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tEasy Mask Equip\tIn the pause menu, press A on any owned mask to put it on or take it off without assigning it to a button. Mask-specific restrictions still apply.\tEnhancements / Items/Songs\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FMasks\tFierceDeitysAnywhere\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tFierce Deity's Mask Anywhere\tAllow using Fierce Deity's mask outside of boss rooms.\tEnhancements / Items/Songs\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FMasks\u001FPersistentBunnyHood\tEnabled\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tPersistent Bunny Hood\tPermanently toggle a speed boost from the bunny hood by pressing 'A' on it in the mask menu.\tEnhancements / Items/Songs\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FMasks\tBlastMaskCooldown\tFLOAT\t15.5\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tBlast Mask Cooldown\tCustomize the Cooldown between Blast Mask usage. Default is 15.5 seconds.\tEnhancements / Items/Songs\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FMasks\tGoronRollingIgnoresMagic\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tGoron Rolling Ignores Magic\tGoron rolling will use spikes even when Link doesn't have magic, and doesn't consume any.\tEnhancements / Items/Songs\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FMasks\tGoronRollingFastSpikes\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tGoron Rolling Fast Spikes\tSpeeds up the wind-up towards spiky rolling to be near instant.\tEnhancements / Items/Songs\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FMasks\tGoronRollingSpikesRequireShield\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tGoron Rolling Spikes Require Shield Button Press\tGoron rolling will only use spikes if the Shield button is pressed, similar to Zora Link's swimming magic shield.\tEnhancements / Items/Songs\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FSongs\tBetterSongOfDoubleTime\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tBetter Song of Double Time\tWhen playing the Song of Double Time, you can now choose the exact time you want to go to, similar to the 3DS version.\\n\\nHolding Z allows decreasing the time adjustment factor, while holding R will increase the factor.\tEnhancements / Items/Songs\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FSongs\tEnableSunsSong\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tEnable Sun's Song\tEnables the partially implemented Sun's Song. RIGHT-DOWN-UP-RIGHT-DOWN-UP to play it. This song will make time move very fast until either Link moves to a different scene, or when the time switches to a new time period.\tEnhancements / Items/Songs\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FPlayback\tDpadOcarina\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tD-pad Ocarina\tEnables using the D-pad for Ocarina playback.\tEnhancements / Items/Songs\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FPlayback\tRightStickOcarina\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tRight Stick Ocarina\tEnables using the Right Stick for Ocarina playback.\tEnhancements / Items/Songs\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FSongs\tSongItems\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tSong Items\tEquip songs to C/D-Pad buttons from the Quest Status page. Songs auto-play when used, skipping manual note input.\tEnhancements / Items/Songs\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FSongs\tPauseOwlWarp\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tPause Owl Warp\tAllows warping to registered Owl Statues from the pause menu map screen. Requires that you can play Song of Soaring normally.\\n\\nAccounts for Index-Warp being active, by presenting all valid warps for the registered map points. Great Bay Coast warp is always given for index 0 warp as a convenience.\tEnhancements / Items/Songs\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FSongs\tBetterOwlWarpMenu\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tBetter Owl Warp Menu\tMakes cursor movement conform more to Control Stick direction when choosing an Owl Statue to warp to.\tEnhancements / Items/Songs\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FSongs\tZoraEggCount\tINT\t7\t1\t7\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tZora Eggs For Bossa Nova\tThe number of eggs required to unlock New Wave Bossa Nova.\tEnhancements / Items/Songs\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FPlayback\tNoDropOcarinaInput\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tPrevent Dropped Ocarina Inputs\tPrevent dropping inputs when playing the Ocarina quickly.\tEnhancements / Items/Songs\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FPlayback\tSkipScarecrowSong\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tSkip Scarecrow Song\tPierre appears when the Ocarina is pulled out.\tEnhancements / Items/Songs\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FSongs\tFasterSongPlayback\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tFaster Song Playback\tSpeeds up the playback of songs.\tEnhancements / Items/Songs\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FSongs\tSkipSoTCutscenes\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tSkip Song of Time cutscenes\tSkips the cutscenes when playing any of the Song of Time songs.\tEnhancements / Items/Songs\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FSongs\tSkipSoaringCutscene\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tSkip Soaring cutscene\tSkips the cutscene when using the Song of Soaring to warp.\tEnhancements / Items/Songs\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FItems\tColorPictograph\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tColor Pictograph\tWill take and display pictographs in color.\tEnhancements / Items/Songs\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCutscenes\tHideTitleCards\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tHide Title Cards\tHides Title Cards when entering areas.\tEnhancements / Time Savers\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCutscenes\tSkipOnePointCutscenes\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tSkip One Point Cutscenes\tSkips freezing Link to focus on various events like chest spawning, door unlocking, switch pressed, etc\tEnhancements / Time Savers\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCutscenes\tSkipEntranceCutscenes\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tSkip Entrance Cutscenes\tSkip cutscenes that occur when first entering a new area.\tEnhancements / Time Savers\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCutscenes\tSkipToFileSelect\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tSkip to File Select\tSkip the opening title sequence and go straight to the file select menu after boot.\\n\\nNote: Takes priority over debug warp points with [Boot] enabled.\tEnhancements / Time Savers\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCutscenes\tSkipIntroSequence\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tSkip Intro Sequence\tWhen starting a game you will be taken straight to South Clock Town as Deku Link.\tEnhancements / Time Savers\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCutscenes\tSkipFirstCycle\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tSkip First Cycle\tWhen starting a game you will be taken straight to South Clock Town as Human Link with Deku Mask, Ocarina, Song of Time, and Song of Healing.\tEnhancements / Time Savers\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCutscenes\tSkipStoryCutscenes\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tSkip Story Cutscenes\tThis skips many of the cutscenes associated with the main story.\tEnhancements / Time Savers\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCutscenes\tSkipMiscInteractions\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tSkip Misc Interactions\tThis skips many minor cutscenes and interactions.\tEnhancements / Time Savers\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCutscenes\tSkipEnemyCutscenes\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tSkip Enemy Cutscenes\tSkips cutscenes specific to enemies and boss battles.\tEnhancements / Time Savers\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FDialogue\tFastBankSelection\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tFast Bank Selection\tPressing the Z or R buttons while the Deposit/Withdrawal Rupees dialogue is open will set the Rupees to Links current Rupees or 0 respectively.\tEnhancements / Time Savers\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FDialogue\tFastText\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tFast Text\tSpeeds up text rendering, and enables holding of B progress to next message.\tEnhancements / Time Savers\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FDialogue\tAutoBombersCode\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tAuto Bombers' Code\tAutomatically fill in the Bombers' code once you've got the notebook.\tEnhancements / Time Savers\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FDialogue\tSkipBottlePickupMessages\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tSkip Bottle Pickup Messages\tSkip pickup messages for bottle swipes.\tEnhancements / Time Savers\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FCutscenes\tAutoAdvanceEndingText\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tAuto Advance Ending Text\tAfter completing the game, textboxes shown on the way to the credits advance on their own once they've been up long enough to read, so the ending plays out without controller input.\tEnhancements / Time Savers\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FTimesavers\tSwampBoatSpeed\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tSwamp Boat Timesaver\tHold Z to speed up the boat ride in through the Swamp.\tEnhancements / Time Savers\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FTimesavers\tGalleryTwofer\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tShooting Gallery Both Rewards\tWhen getting a perfect score at the Shooting Gallery, receive both rewards back to back instead of having to play twice.\tEnhancements / Time Savers\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FTimesavers\tMarineLabHP\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tFast Marine Lab Fish\tOnly requires a single fish to be fed for the Piece of Heart to spawn. Requires a Scene Reload to take effect.\tEnhancements / Time Savers\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FTimesavers\tDampeDiggingSkip\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tFast Dampe Flame Digging\tOnly requires digging up one flame to spawn the big poe.\tEnhancements / Time Savers\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FTimesavers\tAlwaysShowShrineFeathers\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tAlways Show Shrine of Truth Feathers\tAlways reveals the feather-marked path to the Shrine of Truth.\tEnhancements / Time Savers\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FTimesavers\tFastChests\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tFast Chests\tUses the quick kick animation for all chests in vanilla gameplay.\tEnhancements / Time Savers\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FTimesavers\tFasterSceneTransitions\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tFaster Scene Transitions\tFade in and out more quickly when moving between areas.\tEnhancements / Time Savers\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FTimesavers\tPowderKegCertification\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tSkip Powder Keg Certification\tSkips requiring to take the Powder Keg Test before being given the Certification.\tEnhancements / Time Savers\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FTimesavers\tSkipBalladOfWindfish\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tSkip Ballad of Windfish\tPlay the complete Ballad after playing in one form if you have all three transformation masks.\tEnhancements / Time Savers\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FTimesavers\tAutoBankDeposit\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tAuto Bank Deposit\tAutomatically deposits excess Rupees into your bank account when your wallet is full. Deposits stop when the bank reaches maximum capacity. Bank rewards are granted automatically. Notifications display deposit amount and new balance.\tEnhancements / Time Savers\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FTimesavers\tFasterRupeeAccumulator\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tFaster Rupee Accumulator\tCauses your Wallet to fill and empty faster when you gain or lose money.\tEnhancements / Time Savers\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FTimesavers\tFasterBottles\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tFaster Bottles\tSpeeds up animation when using a bottle item.\tEnhancements / Time Savers\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FFixes\tConsoleCrashes\tBOOL\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tFix Console Crashes\tFixes crashes that would typically happen on Console. Disabling this option will simply soft reset 2Ship when encountering these crashes instead of actually crashing the program.\\n\\nIncludes the following:\\n- HESS/Weirdshot crashes\\n- Action Swap crash without arrow ammo\\n- Owl Warp menu crash when moving the cursor with Index-Warp active\\n- Remote Hookshot Hookslide crashes when over voids in Great Bay Temple\tEnhancements / Fixes\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgFixes\tFixButtonEnvColor\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tFix Button Env Color\tFixes a missing gDPSetEnvColor, which causes ammo counts and B button action labels to be the wrong color prior to obtaining magic or other conditions.\tEnhancements / Fixes\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgFixes\tFixEponaStealingSword\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tFix Epona stealing Sword\tThis fixes a bug where Epona can steal your sword when you mount her without a bow in your inventory.\tEnhancements / Fixes\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FFixes\tFierceDeityZTargetMovement\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tFix Fierce Deity Z-Target movement\tFixes Fierce Deity movement being choppy when Z-targeting.\tEnhancements / Fixes\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FFixes\tControlCharacters\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tFix Text Control Characters\tFixes certain control characters not functioning properly depending on their position within the text.\tEnhancements / Fixes\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgFixes\tFixIkanaGreatFairyFountainColor\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tFix Ikana Great Fairy Fountain Color\tFixes a bug that results in the Ikana Great Fairy fountain looking green instead of yellow, this was fixed in the EU version.\tEnhancements / Fixes\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FFixes\tFixTexturesOOB\tBOOL\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tFix Texture overflow OOB\tFixes textures that normally overflow to be patched with the correct size or format.\tEnhancements / Fixes\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FFixes\tCompletedHeartContainerAudio\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tFix Completed Heart Container Audio\tFixes a bug that results in the wrong audio playing upon receiving a 4th piece of heart to fill a new heart container.\tEnhancements / Fixes\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FFixes\tDekuButlerFixShockLoopAnimation\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tFix Deku Butler Shock Animation\tFixes a bug where the Deku Butler loops the incorrect animation in the cutscene that plays after freeing the Deku Princess.\tEnhancements / Fixes\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FRestorations\tConstantFlipsHops\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tConstant Distance Backflips and Sidehops\tBackflips and Sidehops travel a constant distance as they did in OoT.\tEnhancements / Restorations\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FRestorations\tSideRoll\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tSide Rolls\tRestores side rolling from OoT.\tEnhancements / Restorations\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FRestorations\tOoTFasterSwim\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tFaster Swim\tRestores the ability to swim faster by spamming the B button, as in OoT.\tEnhancements / Restorations\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FRestorations\tTatlISG\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tTatl ISG\tRestores Navi ISG from OoT, but now with Tatl.\tEnhancements / Restorations\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FRestorations\tWoodfallMountainAppearance\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tWoodfall Mountain Appearance\tRestores the appearance of Woodfall mountain to not look poisoned when viewed from Termina Field after clearing Woodfall Temple\\n\\nRequires a scene reload to take effect.\tEnhancements / Restorations\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FRestorations\tJPGrottos\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tJP Deku Palace Grottos\tRestores the Deku Palace Grottos to their original Japanese layout.\tEnhancements / Restorations\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FRestorations\tDayTelopDuration\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tDay Transition Duration\tRestores the day transition title card duration, which was longer on original hardware due to disguising load times.\tEnhancements / Restorations\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FRestorations\tBonkCollision\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tBonk Collision\tCorrects rolls to allow bonking trees near the end of the roll, as in OoT.\tEnhancements / Restorations\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FRestorations\tSoilPatch\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tSoil Patch Burrowed Bugs\tRemoves the cutscene lock when bugs burrow into a Skulltula soil patch, allowing the player to re-bottle them, as in OoT.\tEnhancements / Restorations\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\tSimulatedInputLag\tINT\t0\t0\t6\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tSimulated Input Lag\tBuffers your inputs to be executed a specified amount of frames later.\tEnhancements / Restorations\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FRestorations\tPauseBufferWindow\tINT\t0\t0\t40\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tPause Buffer Input Window\tAmount of time in frames you have to buffer an input while unpausing the game. Original hardware is around 20.\tEnhancements / Restorations\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FDifficultyOptions\tHyperEnemies\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tHyper Enemies\tDouble the rate at which enemies are updated, making them more difficult\tEnhancements / Difficulty Options\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FDifficultyOptions\tBossHealthMultiplier\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001E1x (Default)\u001F1\u001E1.25x\u001F2\u001E1.50x\u001F3\u001E1.75x\u001F4\u001E2x\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tBoss Health Multiplier\tMultiply the health of all bosses. Requires a Scene Reload to take effect.\tEnhancements / Difficulty Options\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FDifficultyOptions\tDamageMultiplier\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001E1x\u001F1\u001E2x\u001F2\u001E4x\u001F3\u001E8x\u001F4\u001E16x\u001F10\u001E1 Hit KO\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tDamage Multiplier\tAdjusts the amount of damage Link takes from all sources.\tEnhancements / Difficulty Options\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FDifficultyOptions\tPermanentHeartLoss\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tPermanent Heart Loss\tWhen you lose 4 quarters of a heart you will permanently lose that heart container.\\n\\nDisabling this after the fact will not restore any received heart containers.\tEnhancements / Difficulty Options\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FDifficultyOptions\tDeleteFileOnDeath\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tDelete File on Death\t\u0001\tEnhancements / Difficulty Options\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FDifficultyOptions\tJinxedTimer\tINT\t60\t0\t60\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tJinxed Timerseconds\tSet the duration of the Jinxed effect. Setting it to 0 will prevent the effect entirely.\tEnhancements / Difficulty Options\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FMinigames\tBombersHideAndSeek\tINT\t5\t1\t5\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tBombers Hide-and-Seek Count\tSets the number of Bomber Kids you have to find to complete the hide-and-seek game.\tEnhancements / Difficulty Options\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FMinigames\tSwordsmanSchoolScore\tINT\t30\t1\t30\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tSwordsman School Winning Score\tSets the score required to win the Swordsman School.\tEnhancements / Difficulty Options\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FMinigames\tHoneyAndDarlingDay1\tINT\t8\t1\t8\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tHoney & Darling Day 1 (Bombchus)\tSets the score required to win the Honey & Darling minigame on Day 1.\tEnhancements / Difficulty Options\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FMinigames\tHoneyAndDarlingDay2\tINT\t8\t1\t8\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tHoney & Darling Day 2 (Bombs)\tSets the score required to win the Honey & Darling minigame on Day 2.\tEnhancements / Difficulty Options\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FMinigames\tHoneyAndDarlingDay3\tINT\t16\t1\t16\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tHoney & Darling Day 3 (Bow)\tSets the score required to win the Honey & Darling minigame on Day 3.\tEnhancements / Difficulty Options\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FMinigames\tTownArcheryScore\tINT\t50\t1\t50\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tTown Archery Perfect Score\tSets the score required to win the Town Archery minigame. Reaching this score will end the minigame.\tEnhancements / Difficulty Options\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FMinigames\tRandomizeShootingGalleryOctoroks\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tRandomize Shooting Gallery Octoroks\tRandomizes the positions of Octoroks in the Town Shooting Gallery minigame each time they appear.\tEnhancements / Difficulty Options\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FMinigames\tSwampArcheryScore\tINT\t2180\t1000\t2180\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tSwamp Archery Perfect Score\tSets the score required to win the Swamp Archery minigame, if this is changed it also speeds up the final score counting.\tEnhancements / Difficulty Options\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FMinigames\tRomaniTargetPractice\tINT\t10\t1\t10\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tRomani Target Practice Winning Score\tSets the score required to win Romani's Target Practice.\tEnhancements / Difficulty Options\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FMinigames\tCuccoShackCuccoCount\tINT\t10\t1\t10\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tCucco Shack Cucco Count\tChoose how many cuccos you need to raise to make Grog happy.\tEnhancements / Difficulty Options\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FMinigames\tSkipHorseRace\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tSkip Gorman Horse Race\tInstantly win the Gorman Horse Race\tEnhancements / Difficulty Options\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FMinigames\tBeaverRaceRingsCollected\tINT\t20\t1\t20\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tBeaver Race Rings Collected\tSets the number of rings required for both Beavers. If the slider is set to 20, the first Beaver will require 20 rings, and the second Beaver will require 25 rings, which are their vanilla values.\tEnhancements / Difficulty Options\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FMinigames\tSkipLittleBeaver\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tSkip Little Beaver Brother Races\tOnly Race the Older Beaver.\tEnhancements / Difficulty Options\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FMinigames\tBoatArcheryScore\tINT\t20\t1\t50\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tSwamp Boat Archery Target Score\tSets the initial target score of the Swamp Boat Archery minigame. The target score gets set the first time you play the minigame in each cycle.\tEnhancements / Difficulty Options\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FMinigames\tBoatArcheryHealth\tINT\t10\t1\t30\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tKoume's Health\tSets Koume's health in the Swamp Boat Archery minigame. If Koume is hit this many times, the minigame will end.\tEnhancements / Difficulty Options\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FMinigames\tBoatArcheryInvincible\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tInvincible\tKoume's health does not decrease when hit.\tEnhancements / Difficulty Options\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FDifficultyOptions\tLowerBankRewardThresholds\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tLower Bank Reward Thresholds\tReduces the amount of rupees required to receive the rewards from the bank.\\nFrom: 200 -> 1000 -> 5000\\nTo:   100 ->  500 -> 1000\tEnhancements / Difficulty Options\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FDifficultyOptions\tDisableTakkuriSteal\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tDisable Takkuri Steal\tPrevents the Takkuri from stealing key items like bottles and swords. It may still steal other items.\tEnhancements / Difficulty Options\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FDifficultyOptions\tNoHeartDrops\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tNo Heart Drops\tPrevents spawning of any hearts or fairies.\tEnhancements / Difficulty Options\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FDifficultyOptions\tNoRandomDrops\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tNo Random Drops\tPrevents spawning of any collectibles.\tEnhancements / Difficulty Options\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgEnhancements\u001FDifficultyOptions\tFrogChoirCount\tINT\t5\t1\t5\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tFrog Choir Count\tChoose how many frogs you need to save for the choir performance.\tEnhancements / Difficulty Options\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FAdvancedResolution\tVerticalResolutionToggle\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tSet fixed vertical resolution (disables Resolution slider)\tOverride the resolution scale slider and use the settings below, irrespective of window size.\tSettings / Advanced Resolution\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FAdvancedResolution\tPixelPerfectMode\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tPixel Perfect Mode\tDon't scale image to fill window.\tSettings / Advanced Resolution\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FAdvancedResolution\u001FIntegerScale\tFitAutomatically\tBOOL\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tAutomatically scale image to fit viewport\tAutomatically sets scale factor to fit window. Only available in Pixel Perfect Mode.\tSettings / Advanced Resolution / Integer Scale\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FAdvancedResolution\u001FIntegerScale\tExceedBoundsBy\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tAllow integer scale factor to go +1 above maximum screen bounds.\t\u0001\tSettings / Advanced Resolution / Integer Scale\n2ship2harkinian\t\u0001\tCVars\u001FgSettings\u001FAdvancedResolution\tEnabled\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t5.0.1\tEnable advanced settings.\t\u0001\tSettings / Graphics\nstarship\t\u0001\tCVars\tgGameMasterVolume\tFLOAT\t1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv2.0.0\tMaster Volume\t\u0001\tAudio\nstarshi