rer\nopenq4\t\u0001\t\tr_shadowMapTexelBiasScale\tFLOAT\t0.45\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.13.2\t\u0001\ttexel-aware receiver bias scale for projected and point shadow maps\tRenderer\nopenq4\t\u0001\t\tr_shadowMapNormalOffsetScale\tFLOAT\t1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.13.2\t\u0001\tnormal-offset shadow bias in shadow texels; reduces slope acne but excessive values can move contact edges (point-light use is bounded by r_shadowMapPointMaxWorldBias)\tRenderer\nopenq4\t\u0001\t\tr_shadowMapCasterCulling\tINT\t2\t0\t2\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.13.2\t\u0001\tshadow caster face culling: 0 = always two-sided, 1 = force material-oriented near faces, 2 = automatic (near faces for sealed hulls outside the light, two-sided for open/uncertain/enclosing geometry)\tRenderer\nopenq4\t\u0001\t\tr_shadowMapReceiverPlaneBias\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.13.2\t\u0001\tenable the experimental derivative receiver-plane depth-bias approximation for projected shadow filters\tRenderer\nopenq4\t\u0001\t\tr_shadowMapFilterTaps\tINT\t9\t1\t13\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.13.2\t\u0001\tprojected-light PCF tap budget: 1, 5, 9, or 13\tRenderer\nopenq4\t\u0001\t\tr_shadowMapPointFilterTaps\tINT\t9\t1\t13\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.13.2\t\u0001\tpoint-light PCF tap budget: 1, 5, 9, or 13\tRenderer\nopenq4\t\u0001\t\tr_shadowMapFilterMode\tINT\t0\t0\t2\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.13.2\t\u0001\tprojected-light shadow filter mode: 0 = fixed PCF, 1 = stable rotated Poisson, 2 = PCSS-lite when raw depth is available\tRenderer\nopenq4\t\u0001\t\tr_shadowMapPointFilterMode\tINT\t0\t0\t1\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.13.2\t\u0001\tpoint-light shadow filter mode: 0 = fixed PCF, 1 = stable rotated Poisson\tRenderer\nopenq4\t\u0001\t\tr_shadowMapDistantFilterScale\tFLOAT\t0.35\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.13.2\t\u0001\tscale projected PCF and PCSS radii for parallel/global sky lights whose shadow texels cover more world space\tRenderer\nopenq4\t\u0001\t\tr_shadowMapPCSSLightRadius\tFLOAT\t4.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.13.2\t\u0001\tprojected PCSS-lite blocker search radius in shadow texels\tRenderer\nopenq4\t\u0001\t\tr_shadowMapPCSSMaxRadius\tFLOAT\t8.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.13.2\t\u0001\tprojected PCSS-lite maximum filter radius in shadow texels\tRenderer\nopenq4\t\u0001\t\tr_shadowMapPointHighPrecision\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.13.2\t\u0001\tstore point-light shadow depth in an fp16 color cubemap instead of packed RGBA8 depth. The packed path quantizes finer (1.5e-5 vs 4.9e-4 near the far envelope) at half the memory, and the default hardware-compare path samples the depth cubemap directly, so this only affects the manual fallback. OpenGL only: the Vulkan backend always stores native depth, which quantizes finer than either colour format\tRenderer\nopenq4\t\u0001\t\tr_shadowMapPointLights\tBOOL\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.13.2\t\u0001\tshadow-map point lights when r_useShadowMap is enabled; disabled falls back to stencil shadows for point lights. Point lights are the dominant light class in Quake 4 content, so disabling this makes r_useShadowMap nearly a no-op\tRenderer\nopenq4\t\u0001\t\tr_shadowMapPointSize\tINT\t512\t128\t2048\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.13.2\t\u0001\tpoint-light cube face resolution; separate from r_shadowMapSize because a cube costs six faces of color+depth storage per cached light\tRenderer\nopenq4\t\u0001\t\tr_shadowMapAtlasSize\tINT\t4096\t2048\t8192\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.13.2\t\u0001\tedge size of the shared projected-light shadow atlas; cached lights occupy r_shadowMapSize-sized cells inside it (CSM lights use a 2x2 cell block)\tRenderer\nopenq4\t\u0001\t\tr_shadowMapPointDepthCompare\tBOOL\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.13.2\t\u0001\tuse hardware comparison sampling for point-light depth cubemaps when GLSL 1.30 support is available\tRenderer\nopenq4\t\u0001\t\tr_shadowMapStableAlphaHash\tBOOL\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.13.2\t\u0001\tseed shadow-map hashed alpha from stable world coordinates instead of screen-space fragments\tRenderer\nopenq4\t\u0001\t\tr_shadowMapMaxUpdatesPerView\tINT\t0\t0\t1024\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.13.2\t\u0001\tmaximum shadow-map passes rendered per backend view, 0 = unlimited\tRenderer\nopenq4\t\u0001\t\tr_shadowMapStaticCache\tBOOL\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.13.2\t\u0001\treuse resident shadow maps for static-only lights instead of rerendering every backend view\tRenderer\nopenq4\t\u0001\t\tr_shadowMapStaticHysteresisFrames\tINT\t2\t0\t120\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.13.2\t\u0001\tframes to wait after dynamic casters disappear before static shadow-map reuse\tRenderer\nopenq4\t\u0001\t\tr_shadowMapResidentFrames\tINT\t120\t1\t3600\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.13.2\t\u0001\tframes a resident static shadow map may remain unused before its cache slot can be expired\tRenderer\nopenq4\t\u0001\t\tr_shadowMapProjectedCacheSize\tINT\t8\t0\t16\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.13.2\t\u0001\tstatic projected-light shadow-map cache slots\tRenderer\nopenq4\t\u0001\t\tr_shadowMapPointCacheSize\tINT\t12\t0\t16\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.13.2\t\u0001\tstatic point-light cubemap cache slots\tRenderer\nopenq4\t\u0001\t\tr_shadowMapCacheCSM\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.13.2\t\u0001\tallow static-cache reuse for view-fitted CSM/global shadow-map passes\tRenderer\nopenq4\t\u0001\t\tr_shadowMapTranslucentFilterRadius\tFLOAT\t-1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.13.2\t\u0001\ttranslucent shadow moment filter radius in texels, -1 = inherit opaque shadow radius\tRenderer\nopenq4\t\u0001\t\tr_shadowMapTranslucentMinVariance\tFLOAT\t0.00001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.13.2\t\u0001\tminimum variance used when resolving translucent shadow moments\tRenderer\nopenq4\t\u0001\t\tr_shadowMapTranslucentBleedReduction\tFLOAT\t0.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.13.2\t\u0001\tlight-bleed reduction applied to translucent shadow moment resolve\tRenderer\nopenq4\t\u0001\t\tr_softParticles\tBOOL\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.13.2\t\u0001\tdepth-fade eligible BSE particles against opaque scene depth when GLSL is available\tR