\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.13.2\t\u0001\tmaximum MVD file size in MiB; 0 disables the limit\tSystem\nopenq4\t\u0001\t\tmvd_maxDurationMinutes\tINT\t360\t0\t1440\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.13.2\t\u0001\tmaximum MVD recording duration in minutes; 0 disables the limit\tSystem\nopenq4\t\u0001\t\tmvd_enforceContent\tBOOL\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.13.2\t\u0001\trefuse MVD playback when the declaration checksum differs\tSystem\nopenq4\t\u0001\t\tgui_filter_password\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.13.2\t\u0001\tPassword filter\tInterface\nopenq4\t\u0001\t\tgui_filter_players\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.13.2\t\u0001\tPlayers filter\tInterface\nopenq4\t\u0001\t\tgui_filter_gameType\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.13.2\t\u0001\tGametype filter\tInterface\nopenq4\t\u0001\t\tgui_filter_idle\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.13.2\t\u0001\tIdle servers filter\tInterface\nopenq4\t\u0001\t\tgui_filter_game\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.13.2\t\u0001\tGame filter\tInterface\nopenq4\t\u0001\t\tgui_filter_mod\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.13.2\t\u0001\tServer browser mod filter; empty shows every mod\tInterface\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tsv_hostname\tSTRING\tnoname\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tSets the name of the server.\tServer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tsv_maxclientsPerIP\tINT\t3\t1\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tLimits number of simultaneous connections from the same IP address.\tServer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tsv_clientTLD\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tClient country detection code.\tServer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tsv_minRate\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tMinimum server bandwidth (in bit per second) a client can use.\tServer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tsv_maxRate\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tMaximum server bandwidth (in bit per second) a client can use.\tServer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tsv_dlRate\tINT\t100\t0\t500\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tBandwidth allotted to PK3 file downloads via UDP, in kbyte/s.\tServer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tsv_floodProtect\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tToggle server flood protection to keep players from bringing the server down.\tServer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tsv_dlURL\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tServer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tsv_lanForceRate\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tForces LAN clients to the maximum rate instead of accepting client setting.\tServer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tsv_banFile\tSTRING\tserverbans.dat\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tName of the file that is used for storing the server bans.\tServer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tsv_levelTimeReset\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tWhether or not to reset leveltime after new map loads.\tServer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tsv_filter\tSTRING\tfilter.txt\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tCvar that point on filter file, if it is then filtering will be disabled.\tServer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_overBrightBits\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tSets the intensity of overall brightness of texture pixels.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_mapOverBrightBits\tINT\t2\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tSets the number of overbright bits baked into all lightmaps and map data.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_intensity\tFLOAT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tGlobal texture lighting scale.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_defaultImage\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tReplace default (missing) image texture by either exact file or solid #rgb|#rrggbb background color.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_simpleMipMaps\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tWhether or not to use a simple mipmapping algorithm or a more correct one: 0: off (proper linear filter) 1: on (for slower machines)\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_vertexLight\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tSet to 1 to use vertex light instead of lightmaps, collapse all multi-stage shaders into single-stage ones, might cause rendering artifacts.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_picmip\tINT\t0\t0\t16\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tSet texture quality, lower is better.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_nomip\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tApply picmip only on worldspawn textures.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_neatsky\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tDisables texture mipping for skies.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_roundImagesDown\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tWhen images are scaled, round images down instead of up.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_detailtextures\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tEnables usage of shader stages flagged as detail.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_texturebits\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tNumber of texture bits per texture.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_mergeLightmaps\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tMerge built-in small lightmaps into bigger lightmaps (atlases).\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_vbo\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tUse Vertex Buffer Objects to cache static map geometry, may improve FPS on modern GPUs, increases hunk memory usage by 15-30MB (map-dependent).\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_mapGreyScale\tFLOAT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tDesaturate world map textures only, works independently from \\\\r_greyscale, negative values only desaturate lightmaps.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_subdivisions\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tDistance to subdivide bezier curved surfaces. Higher values mean less subdivision and less geometric complexity.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_lodCurveError\tFLOAT\t250\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tLevel of detail error on curved surface grids. Higher values result in better quality at a distance.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_lodbias\tINT\t-2\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tSets the level of detail of in-game models: -2: Ultra (further delays LOD transition in the distance) -1: Very High (delays LOD transition in the distance) 0: High 1: Medium 2: Low\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_zproj\tINT\t64\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tProjected viewport frustum.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_stereoSeparation\tINT\t64\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tControl eye separation. Resulting separation is \\\\r_zproj divided by this value in standard units.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_ignoreGLErrors\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tIgnore OpenGL errors.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_teleporterFlash\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tShow a white screen instead of a black screen when being teleported in hyperspace.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_fastsky\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tDraw flat colored skies.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_drawSun\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tDraw sun shader in skies.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_dynamiclight\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tEnables dynamic lighting.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_dlightMode\tINT\t0\t0\t2\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tDynamic light mode: 0: VQ3 'fake' dynamic lights 1: High-quality per-pixel dynamic lights, slightly faster than VQ3's on modern hardware 2: Same as 1 but applies to all MD3 models too\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_dlightScale\tFLOAT\t0.5\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tScales dynamic light radius.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_dlightSpecPower\tFLOAT\t8\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tFactors specularity effect from dynamic lights on surfaces.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_dlightSpecColor\tFLOAT\t-0.25\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tColor base for specular component: <= 0: use current texture and modulate by abs(r_dlightSpecColor) > 0: use constant color with RGB components set to \\\\r_dlightSpecColor\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_dlightIntensity\tFLOAT\t1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tAdjusts dynamic light intensity but not radius.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_dlightSaturation\tFLOAT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_ext_multisample\tINT\t0\t0\t8\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tFor anti-aliasing geometry edges, valid values: 0|2|4|6|8. Requires \\\\r_fbo 1.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_hdr\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tEnables high dynamic range frame buffer texture format. Requires \\\\r_fbo 1. -1: 4-bit, for testing purposes, heavy color banding, might not work on all systems 0: 8 bit, default, moderate color banding with multi-stage shaders 1: 16 bit, enhanced blending precision, no color banding, might decrease performance on AMD / Intel GPUs\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_bloom\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tEnables bloom post-processing effect. Requires \\\\r_fbo 1.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_bloom_threshold\tFLOAT\t0.6\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tColor level to extract to bloom texture, default is 0.6.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_bloom_threshold_mode\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tColor extraction mode: 0: (r|g|b) >= threshold 1: (r + g + b ) / 3 >= threshold 2: luma(r, g, b) >= threshold\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_bloom_intensity\tFLOAT\t0.5\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tFinal bloom blend factor, default is 0.5.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_bloom_passes\tINT\t5\t3\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tCount of downsampled passes (framebuffers) to blend on final bloom image, default is 5.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_bloom_blend_base\tINT\t1\t0\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t0-based, topmost downsampled framebuffer to use for final image, high values can be used for stronger haze effect, results in overall weaker intensity.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_bloom_modulate\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tModulate extracted color: 0: off (color = color, i.e. no changes) 1: by itself (color = color * color) 2: by intensity (color = color * luma(color))\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_bloom_filter_size\tINT\t6\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tFilter size of Gaussian Blur effect for each pass, bigger filter size means stronger and wider blur, lower values are faster, default is 6.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_bloom_reflection\tFLOAT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tBloom lens reflection effect, value is an intensity factor of the effect, negative value means blend only reflection and skip main bloom texture.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_dlightBacks\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tWhether or not dynamic lights should light up back-face culled geometry, affects only VQ3 dynamic lights.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_finish\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tForce a glFinish call after rendering a scene.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_textureMode\tSTRING\tGL_LINEAR_MIPMAP_NEAREST\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tTexture interpolation mode: GL_NEAREST: Nearest neighbor interpolation and will therefore appear similar to Quake II except with the added colored lighting GL_LINEAR: Linear interpolation and will appear to blend in objects that are closer than the resolution that the textures are set as GL_NEAREST_MIPMAP_NEAREST: Nearest neighbor interpolation with mipmapping for bilinear hardware, mipmapping will blend objects that are farther away than the resolution that they are set as GL_LINEAR_MIPMAP_NEAREST: Linear interpolation with mipmapping for bilinear hardware GL_NEAREST_MIPMAP_LINEAR: Nearest neighbor interpolation with mipmapping for trilinear hardware GL_LINEAR_MIPMAP_LINEAR: Linear interpolation with mipmapping for trilinear hardware\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_gamma\tFLOAT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tGamma correction factor.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_facePlaneCull\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tEnables culling of planar surfaces with back side test.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_railWidth\tINT\t16\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tRadius of railgun trails.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_railCoreWidth\tINT\t6\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tSize of railgun trail rings when enabled in game code (normally \\\\cg_oldRail 0).\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_railSegmentLength\tINT\t32\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tLength of segments in railgun trails.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_anaglyphMode\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tEnable rendering of anaglyph images. Valid options for 3D glasses types: 0: Disabled 1: Red-cyan 2: Red-blue 3: Red-green 4: Green-magenta\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_greyscale\tFLOAT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tDesaturate rendered frame, requires \\\\r_fbo 1.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_flareSize\tFLOAT\t40\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tRadius of light flares. Requires \\\\r_flares 1.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_marksOnTriangleMeshes\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tEnables impact marks on triangle mesh surfaces (ie: MD3 models.) Requires impact marks to be enabled in the game code.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_aviMotionJpegQuality\tINT\t90\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tControls quality of Jpeg video capture when \\\\cl_aviMotionJpeg 1.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_screenshotJpegQuality\tINT\t90\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tControls quality of Jpeg screenshots when using screenshotJpeg.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_allowExtensions\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tUse all of the OpenGL extensions your card is capable of.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_ext_compressed_textures\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tEnables texture compression.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_ext_multitexture\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tEnables hardware multi-texturing (0: off, 1: on).\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_ext_compiled_vertex_array\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tEnables hardware-compiled vertex array rendering method.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_ext_texture_env_add\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tEnables additive blending in multitexturing. Requires \\\\r_ext_multitexture 1.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_ext_texture_filter_anisotropic\tBOOL\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tAllow anisotropic filtering.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_ext_max_anisotropy\tINT\t8\t1\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tSets maximum anisotropic level for your graphics driver. Requires \\\\r_ext_texture_filter_anisotropic.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_ignorehwgamma\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tOverrides hardware gamma capabilities.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_flares\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tEnables corona effects on light sources.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_fbo\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tUse framebuffer objects, enables gamma correction in windowed mode and allows arbitrary video size and screenshot/video capture. Required for bloom, HDR rendering, anti-aliasing and greyscale effects. OpenGL 3.0+ required.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_ext_supersample\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tSuper-sample anti-aliasing, requires \\\\r_fbo 1.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_renderWidth\tINT\t800\t96\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tVideo width to render to when \\\\r_renderScale > 0.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_renderHeight\tINT\t600\t72\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tVideo height to render to when \\\\r_renderScale > 0.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_renderScale\tINT\t0\t0\t4\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tScaling mode to be used with custom render resolution: 0 - disabled 1 - nearest filtering, stretch to full size 2 - nearest filtering, preserve aspect ratio (black bars on sides) 3 - linear filtering, stretch to full size 4 - linear filtering, preserve aspect ratio (black bars on sides)\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tvm_ui\tINT\t2\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tOther\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tvm_cgame\tINT\t2\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tOther\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tvm_game\tINT\t2\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tOther\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tnet_enabled\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tNetwork\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tnet_mcast6iface\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tOutgoing interface to use for scan.\tNetwork\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tnet_socksEnabled\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tToggle the use of network socks 5 protocol enabling firewall access (can only be set at initialization time from the OS command line).\tNetwork\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tnet_socksServer\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tSet the address (name or IP number) of the SOCKS server (firewall machine), NOT a Q3ATEST server (can only be set at initialization time from the OS command line).\tNetwork\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tnet_socksPort\tINT\t1080\t0\t65535\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tSet proxy and/or firewall port, default is 1080 (can only be set at initialization time from the OS command line).\tNetwork\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tnet_socksUsername\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tVariable holds username for socks firewall. Supports no authentication and username/password authentication method (RFC-1929). It does NOT support GSS-API method (RFC-1961) authentication (can only be set at initialization time from the OS command line).\tNetwork\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tfs_excludeReference\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tExclude specified pak files from download list on client side. Format is <moddir>/<pakname> (without .pk3 suffix), you may list multiple entries separated by space.\tOther\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tcom_maxfpsUnfocused\tINT\t60\t0\t1000\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tSets maximum frames per second in unfocused game window.\tSystem\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tcom_yieldCPU\tINT\t1\t0\t16\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tAttempt to sleep specified amount of time between rendered frames when game is active, this will greatly reduce CPU load. Use 0 only if you're experiencing some lag.\tSystem\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tcom_affinityMask\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tBind game process to bitmask-specified CPU core(s), special characters: A or a - all default cores P or p - performance cores E or e - efficiency cores 0x<value> - use hexadecimal notation + or - can be used to add or exclude particular cores\tSystem\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tcom_introplayed\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tSkips the introduction cinematic.\tSystem\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tcom_skipIdLogo\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tSkip playing Id Software logo cinematic at startup.\tSystem\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_dither\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_presentBits\tINT\t24\t16\t30\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_device\tINT\t-1\t-2\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_ext_alpha_to_coverage\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tEnables alpha-to-coverage multisampling, requires \\\\r_fbo 1.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tin_joystickNo\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tSelect which joystick to use.\tInput\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tin_joystickUseAnalog\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tDo not translate joystick axis events to keyboard commands.\tInput\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tin_keyboardDebug\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tPrint keyboard debug info.\tInput\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tin_forceCharset\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tTry to translate non-ASCII chars in keyboard input or force EN/US keyboard layout.\tInput\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tin_mouse\tINT\t1\t-1\t1\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tInput\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tin_joystick\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tWhether or not joystick support is on.\tInput\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tjoy_threshold\tFLOAT\t0.15\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tThreshold of joystick moving distance.\tOther\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tj_pitch\tFLOAT\t0.022\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tJoystick pitch rotation speed/direction.\tInput\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tj_yaw\tFLOAT\t-0.022\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tJoystick yaw rotation speed/direction.\tInput\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tj_forward\tFLOAT\t-0.25\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tJoystick forward movement speed/direction.\tInput\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tj_side\tFLOAT\t0.25\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tJoystick side movement speed/direction.\tInput\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tj_up\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tJoystick up movement speed/direction.\tInput\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tj_pitch_axis\tINT\t3\t0\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tSelects which joystick axis controls pitch.\tInput\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tj_yaw_axis\tINT\t2\t0\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tSelects which joystick axis controls yaw.\tInput\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tj_forward_axis\tINT\t1\t0\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tSelects which joystick axis controls forward/back.\tInput\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tj_side_axis\tINT\t0\t0\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tSelects which joystick axis controls left/right.\tInput\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tj_up_axis\tINT\t4\t0\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tSelects which joystick axis controls up/down.\tInput\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tcl_consoleKeys\tSTRING\t~ ` 0x7e 0x60\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tSpace delimited list of key names or characters that toggle the console.\tClient\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_swapInterval\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tV-blanks to wait before swapping buffers. 0: No V-Sync 1: Synced to the monitor's refresh rate.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_stereoEnabled\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tEnable stereo rendering for techniques like shutter glasses.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tin_nograb\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tDo not capture mouse in game, may be useful during online streaming.\tInput\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\ts_sdlBits\tINT\t16\t8\t16\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tBits per-sample to request for SDL audio output (possible options: 8 or 16). When set to 0 it uses 16.\tSound\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\ts_sdlChannels\tINT\t2\t1\t2\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tNumber of audio channels to request for SDL audio output. The Quake 3 audio mixer only supports mono and stereo. Additional channels are silent.\tSound\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\ts_sdlDevSamps\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tNumber of audio samples to provide to the SDL audio output device. When set to 0 it picks a value based on s_sdlSpeed.\tSound\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\ts_sdlMixSamps\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tNumber of audio samples for Quake 3's audio mixer when using SDL audio output.\tSound\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\ts_sdlCapture\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tSet to 1 to enable SDL audio capture.\tSound\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tcl_yawspeed\tINT\t140\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tSide-to-side turning speed using keys (+left and +right).\tClient\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tcl_pitchspeed\tINT\t140\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tUp and down pitching speed using keys (+lookup and +lookdown).\tClient\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tcl_maxpackets\tINT\t125\t15\t125\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tSet how many client packets are sent to the server per second, can't exceed \\\\com_maxFPS.\tClient\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tcl_packetdup\tINT\t1\t0\t5\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tLimits the number of previous client commands added in packet, helps in packet loss mitigation, increases client command packets size a bit.\tClient\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tcl_run\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tPersistent player running movement.\tClient\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tsensitivity\tINT\t5\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tSets base mouse sensitivity (mouse speed).\tOther\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tcl_mouseAccel\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tToggle the use of mouse acceleration the mouse speeds up or becomes more sensitive as it continues in one direction.\tClient\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tcl_freelook\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tAllow pitching or up/down look with mouse.\tClient\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tcl_mouseAccelStyle\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tChoose between two different mouse acceleration styles.\tClient\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tcl_mouseAccelOffset\tFLOAT\t5\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tSets how much base mouse delta will be doubled by acceleration. Requires 'cl_mouseAccelStyle 1'.\tClient\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tm_pitch\tFLOAT\t0.022\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tSet the up and down movement distance of the player in relation to how much the mouse moves.\tInput\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tm_yaw\tFLOAT\t0.022\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tSet the speed at which the player's screen moves left and right while using the mouse.\tInput\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tm_forward\tFLOAT\t0.25\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tSet the back and forth movement distance of the player in relation to how much the mouse moves.\tInput\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tm_side\tFLOAT\t0.25\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tSet the strafe movement distance of the player in relation to how much the mouse moves.\tInput\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tm_filter\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tToggle use of mouse 'smoothing'.\tInput\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tvid_xpos\tINT\t3\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tSaves/sets window X-coordinate when windowed, requires \\\\vid_restart.\tOther\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tvid_ypos\tINT\t22\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tSaves/sets window Y-coordinate when windowed, requires \\\\vid_restart.\tOther\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_noborder\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tSetting to 1 will remove window borders and title bar in windowed mode, hold ALT to drag & drop it with opened console.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_mode\tINT\t-2\t-2\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tSet video mode: -2 - use current desktop resolution -1 - use \\\\r_customWidth and \\\\r_customHeight 0..N - enter \\\\modelist for details\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_modeFullscreen\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tDedicated fullscreen mode, set to \"\" to use \\\\r_mode in all cases.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_fullscreen\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tFullscreen mode. Set to 0 for windowed mode.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_customPixelAspect\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tEnables custom aspect of the screen, with \\\\r_mode -1.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_customWidth\tINT\t1600\t4\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tCustom width to use with \\\\r_mode -1.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_customHeight\tINT\t1024\t4\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tCustom height to use with \\\\r_mode -1.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_colorbits\tINT\t0\t0\t32\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tSets color bit depth, set to 0 to use desktop settings.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_stencilbits\tINT\t8\t0\t8\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tStencil buffer size, required to be 8 for stencil shadows.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_depthbits\tINT\t0\t0\t32\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tSets precision of Z-buffer.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tcl_renderer\tSTRING\topengl\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tSets your desired renderer, requires \\\\vid_restart.\tClient\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tcl_autoRecordDemo\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tAuto-record demos when starting or joining a game.\tClient\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tcl_drawRecording\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tHide (0) or shorten (1) \"RECORDING\" HUD message when recording demo.\tClient\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tcl_aviFrameRate\tINT\t25\t1\t1000\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tThe framerate used for capturing video.\tClient\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tcl_aviMotionJpeg\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tEnable/disable the MJPEG codec for avi output.\tClient\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tcl_allowDownload\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tEnables downloading of content needed in server. Valid bitmask flags: 1: Downloading enabled 2: Do not use HTTP/FTP downloads 4: Do not use UDP downloads\tClient\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tcl_mapAutoDownload\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tAutomatic map download for play and demo playback (via automatic \\\\dlmap call).\tClient\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_inGameVideo\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tControls whether in-game video should be drawn.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tcg_autoswitch\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tGame\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tcl_maxPing\tINT\t800\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tClient\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tcl_lanForcePackets\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tBypass \\\\cl_maxpackets for LAN games, send packets every frame.\tClient\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tcl_guidServerUniq\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tMakes cl_guid unique for each server.\tClient\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tcl_dlURL\tSTRING\thttp://ws.q3df.org/maps/download/%1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tCvar must point to download location.\tClient\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tcl_dlDirectory\tBOOL\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tClient\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tcl_reconnectArgs\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tClient\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tname\tSTRING\tUnnamedPlayer\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tOther\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\trate\tINT\t25000\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tOther\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tsnaps\tINT\t40\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tOther\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tmodel\tSTRING\tsarge\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tOther\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\theadmodel\tSTRING\tsarge\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tOther\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tteam_model\tSTRING\tsarge\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tOther\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tteam_headmodel\tSTRING\tsarge\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tOther\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tcolor1\tINT\t4\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tOther\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tcolor2\tINT\t5\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tOther\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\thandicap\tINT\t100\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tOther\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tsex\tSTRING\tmale\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tOther\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tcl_anonymous\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tClient\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tcg_predictItems\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tGame\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tcg_viewsize\tINT\t100\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tGame\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\ts_khz\tINT\t22\t0\t48\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tSpecifies the sound sampling rate, (8, 11, 22, 44, 48) in kHz. Default value is 22.\tSound\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\ts_mixAhead\tFLOAT\t0.2\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tAmount of time to pre-mix sound data to avoid potential skips/stuttering in case of unstable framerate. Higher values add more CPU usage.\tSound\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\ts_mixOffset\tFLOAT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tSound\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\ts_device\tSTRING\tdefault\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tSound\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\ts_volume\tFLOAT\t0.8\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tSets master volume for all game audio.\tSound\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\ts_musicVolume\tFLOAT\t0.25\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tSets volume for in-game music only.\tSound\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\ts_doppler\tBOOL\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tEnables doppler effect on moving projectiles.\tSound\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\ts_muteWhenUnfocused\tBOOL\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tMutes all audio while game window is unfocused.\tSound\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\ts_muteWhenMinimized\tBOOL\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tMutes all audio while game is minimized.\tSound\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tcon_autoclear\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tEnable/disable clearing console input text when console is closed.\tConsole\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tcon_scale\tFLOAT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tConsole font size scale.\tConsole\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_ext_framebuffer_object\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_ext_texture_float\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_ext_framebuffer_multisample\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tFor anti-aliasing geometry edges (FBO).\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_arb_seamless_cube_map\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_arb_vertex_array_object\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_ext_direct_state_access\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_floatLightmap\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_postProcess\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tEnable post-processing.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_toneMap\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tEnable tone mapping. Requires r_hdr and r_postProcess.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_autoExposure\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tDo automatic exposure based on scene brightness. Hardcoded to -2 to 2 on maps that don't specify otherwise. Requires r_hdr, r_postProcess, and r_toneMap.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_depthPrepass\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tDo a depth-only pass before rendering. Speeds up rendering in cases where advanced features are used. Required for r_sunShadows.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_ssao\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tEnable screen-space ambient occlusion.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_normalMapping\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tEnable normal maps for materials that support it.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_specularMapping\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tEnable specular maps for materials that support it.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_deluxeMapping\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tEnable deluxe mapping (map is compiled with light directions). Even if the map doesn't have deluxe mapping compiled in, an approximation based on the lightgrid will be used.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_parallaxMapping\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tEnable parallax mapping for materials that support it. 0: No 1: Use parallax occlusion mapping 2: Use relief mapping\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_parallaxMapOffset\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tSet the parallax height offset.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_parallaxMapShadows\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tEnable self-shadowing on parallax map supported materials.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_cubeMapping\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_cubemapSize\tINT\t128\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_deluxeSpecular\tFLOAT\t0.3\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_pbr\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\tEnable physically based rendering.\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_baseNormalX\tFLOAT\t1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_baseNormalY\tFLOAT\t1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_baseParallax\tFLOAT\t0.05\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_baseSpecular\tFLOAT\t0.04\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_baseGloss\tFLOAT\t0.3\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_glossType\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_pshadowDist\tINT\t128\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_imageUpsample\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_imageUpsampleMaxSize\tINT\t1024\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_imageUpsampleType\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_genNormalMaps\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlatest\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer\nquake3e\t\u0001\t\tr_drawSunRays\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tlat