ait\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tDebug: log how long the render thread waits for command ring space\tDebug\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tpdr_log_glare_queries\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tDebug: log the light glares' occlusion query results and waits\tDebug\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tpdr_sample_threads_after_s\tINT\t0\t0\t3600\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tDebug: after this many seconds, sample the busiest threads once and log their hottest functions, 0 = off\tDebug\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tpdr_sample_threads_duration_s\tINT\t10\t1\t120\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tDebug: how long the thread sampler samples for\tDebug\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tpdr_gpu_wait_mode\tINT\t1\t0\t2\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tPause between polls while the game waits for free command-buffer space: 0 = busy spin (original), 1 = yield the core, 2 = sleep 200us\tPerformance\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tpdr_vulkan_float24_depth\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tOn Vulkan, convert float24 depth in the pixel shader (depth_float24_convert_in_pixel_shader, depth_float24_round, depth_bias_shader_offset), which light glares need. Not applied on D3D12, where it breaks the depth of the gun and hands\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tpdr_glare_query_wait_ms\tINT\t30\t0\t100\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tLight glares read their occlusion queries three frames later. With occlusion_query = async or strict, wait up to this long for a result that is not ready yet instead of hiding the glare, 0 = don't wait\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tpdr_tp_enable\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tThird-person camera (solo only): camera behind Joanna, body shown, first-person gun hidden\tGameplay\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tpdr_tp_offset_x\tFLOAT\t35.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tThird-person camera offset, camera-local X (right)\tGameplay\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tpdr_tp_offset_y\tFLOAT\t15.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tThird-person camera offset, camera-local Y (up)\tGameplay\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tpdr_tp_offset_z\tFLOAT\t-170.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tThird-person camera offset, camera-local Z (forward, < 0 = behind)\tGameplay\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tpdr_mouse_look\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tNative mouse look: on foot the mouse turns the camera directly (1:1, no dead zone or response curve) instead of emulating the right stick. Elsewhere (menus, hoverbike, CamSpy) the stick emulation stays in charge. Needs mnk_mode and mnk_mouse\tMouse\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tpdr_mouse_sensitivity\tFLOAT\t2.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tMouse look sensitivity: camera turn per mouse count = 0.022 deg x this (as in Source games)\tMouse\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tpdr_mouse_invert_x\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tInvert the horizontal mouse look axis\tMouse\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tpdr_mouse_invert_y\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tInvert the vertical mouse look axis\tMouse\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tpdr_mouse_zoom_scaling\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tScale mouse look with the camera's field of view, so zoomed aiming turns the picture by the same amount per mouse count\tMouse\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tpdr_mouse_zoom_sensitivity\tFLOAT\t1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tExtra mouse look factor while zoomed in; the turn is already scaled to the FOV\tMouse\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tpdr_skip_live_prompt\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tAnswer the startup \"Gamer Profile not online\" prompt with \"Continue playing offline\" (headless would pick \"Connect\" and hang)\tGameplay\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tdev_debug_runtime\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tEnable runtime debug tools (stub sweep, missing function scan)\tDebug\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\td3d12_debug\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tEnable Direct3D 12 and DXGI debug layer\tUI/D3D12\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\td3d12_break_on_error\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tBreak on Direct3D 12 validation errors\tUI/D3D12\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\td3d12_break_on_warning\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tBreak on Direct3D 12 validation warnings\tUI/D3D12\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\td3d12_adapter\tINT\t-1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tIndex of the DXGI adapter to use (-1 for the gpu_vendor one, else the one with the most dedicated video memory, -2 for WARP)\tUI/D3D12\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\td3d12_queue_priority\tINT\t1\t0\t2\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tGraphics command queue priority (0=normal, 1=high, 2=realtime)\tUI/D3D12\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\td3d12_allow_variable_refresh_rate_and_tearing\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tAllow variable refresh rate and tearing\tUI/D3D12\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvulkan_validation_enabled\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tEnable Vulkan validation layers\tUI/Vulkan\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvulkan_device\tINT\t-1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tVulkan device index (-1 for auto selection)\tUI/Vulkan\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvulkan_prefer_geometry_shader\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tPrefer physical devices supporting geometryShader when auto-selecting\tUI/Vulkan\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvulkan_prefer_fragment_stores_and_atomics\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tPrefer physical devices supporting