UM\tinfo\t\u0001\t\u0001\ttrace\u001Fdebug\u001Finfo\u001Fwarn\u001Ferror\u001Fcritical\u001Foff\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tGlobal log level: trace, debug, info, warn, error, critical, off\tLog\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tlog_file\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tLog file path (empty = auto sequential naming)\tLog\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tlog_noisy\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tEnable noisy/high-frequency log macros\tLog\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tlog_flush_interval\tINT\t0\t0\t60\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tPeriodic flush interval in seconds (0 = off)\tLog\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tclock_no_scaling\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tDisable clock scaling (inverted: false = scaling enabled)\tClock\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tclock_source_raw\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tUse raw clock source without scaling\tClock\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tperf_log_csv\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tPath to write per-frame CSV log (empty = disabled)\tPerf\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tgpu_allow_invalid_fetch_constants\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tAllow invalid fetch constants\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tgpu_allow_invalid_upload_range\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tAllows games to read data from pages that are marked as no access.\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tnative_2x_msaa\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tEnable native 2x MSAA\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tdraw_resolution_scaled_texture_offsets\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tScale texture offsets with draw resolution\tGPU/Shader\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tprecise_interpolation\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tInterpolate pixel shader inputs manually from the per-vertex values (Vulkan with VK_KHR_fragment_shader_barycentric) to avoid host interpolation imprecision, which causes noise in games that compare interpolated values for equality, such as Perfect Dark Zero and Tenchu Z on Nvidia.\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tdepth_float24_round\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tRound float24 depth values\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tdepth_float24_convert_in_pixel_shader\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tConvert float24 depth in pixel shader\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tdepth_transfer_not_equal_test\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tUse not-equal test for depth transfer\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tgamma_render_target_as_unorm16\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tUse R16G16B16A16_UNORM for gamma render targets (more accurate than sRGB)\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tdump_shaders\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tPath to dump shaders to\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tmulsc_round_toward_zero\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tRound mulsc products toward zero instead of to nearest even. This fixes bad geometry in several Volition Engine titles and possibly others. This rounding behavior hasn't been confirmed on real hardware, so it's disabled by default.\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tuse_fuzzy_alpha_epsilon\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tUse approximate compare for alpha test values to prevent flickering on NVIDIA graphics cards\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tgpu_debug_markers\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tInsert debug markers into GPU command streams for tools like PIX and RenderDoc. Automatically enabled when RenderDoc is detected.\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tforce_depth_clamp\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tUse host depth clamping instead of near and far plane clipping when guest clipping is enabled. X/Y/W clipping is unaffected. On Vulkan, this requires depthClamp support.\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tocclusion_query_fake_lower_threshold\tINT\t80\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tLower end of the fake sample count value written on EVENT_WRITE_ZPD when real occlusion queries are disabled. -1 writes nothing, resulting in some games that sit and hang. 0 means the fake result stays fully occluded.\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tocclusion_query_fake_upper_threshold\tINT\t100\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tUpper end of the fake sample count value written on EVENT_WRITE_ZPD when real occlusion queries are disabled. Keep this higher than occlusion_query_fake_lower_threshold. Ignored if occlusion_query_fake_lower_threshold is -1.\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\txenos_sample_positions\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tRasterize 2x and 4x MSAA render targets at the Xenos sample positions, like real hardware, if the GPU and driver support it. Only applies to RTV/FBO - ROV/FSI render targets always use Xenos positions since they safely map coverage and calculate depth in-shader.\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\ttexture_point_snap\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tSnap normalized point sampled 2D texture coordinates to texel centers. Fixes texture seams in titles that use virtual textures, e.g. idTech 5, but may cause rendering issues in other titles.\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\thalf_pixel_offset\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tEnable half pixel offset\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tresolve_resolution_scale_fill_half_pixel_offset\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tFill half pixel offset during resolution scale resolve\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tdepth_bias_shader_offset\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tRoute decal host render target draws with polygon offset through shader depth. This avoids Z-fighting in games that rely on tiny depth bias values that host fixed function depth bias cannot reproduce reliably. This likely causes some minor performance penalty, but the cost should be minimal if only a small portion of the scene is affected.\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\twindow_offset_in_edram\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tRenders every tile of a predicated tiling frame at the same position as the depth prepass by applying the window offset in EDRAM rather than the viewport. Fixes depth artifacts in the bottom tile of the screen. Disable this if tiles start shifting or banding. Works on every render target path. ROV and FSI apply it to every tile since their pixel shaders directly address EDRAM and can offset sideways or past the end of EDRAM, RTV and FBO keep sideways offsets, and tiles that would run past the target, in the viewport.\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\texecute_unclipped_draw_vs_on_cpu\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tExecute unclipped draw vertex shader on CPU\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\texecute_unclipped_draw_vs_on_cpu_with_scissor\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tExecute unclipped draw VS on CPU with scissor\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tforce_convert_line_loops_to_strips\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tForce convert line loops to strips\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tforce_convert_quad_lists_to_triangle_lists\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tForce convert quad lists to triangle lists\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tforce_convert_triangle_fans_to_lists\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tForce convert triangle fans to lists\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tprimitive_processor_cache_min_indices\tINT\t0\t0\t1000000\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tMinimum indices for primitive processor cache\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tnative_stencil_value_output_d3d12_intel\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tNative stencil value output for Intel D3D12\tGPU/D3D12\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\trender_target_path_d3d12\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tD3D12 render target implementation path\tGPU/D3D12\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tnative_stencil_value_output\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tEnable native stencil value output\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\td3d12_bindless\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tUse bindless resources where available\tGPU/D3D12\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\td3d12_readback_memexport\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tRead data written by memory export in shaders on the CPU\tGPU/D3D12\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\td3d12_readback_resolve\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tRead render-to-texture results on the CPU\tGPU/D3D12\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\td3d12_submit_on_primary_buffer_end\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tSubmit command list when PM4 primary buffer ends\tGPU/D3D12\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\td3d12_dxbc_disasm\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tDump DXBC disassembly\tGPU/D3D12\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\td3d12_dxbc_disasm_dxilconv\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tDump DXIL conversion disassembly\tGPU/D3D12\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\td3d12_pipeline_creation_threads\tINT\t-1\t-1\t32\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tNumber of pipeline creation threads (-1 for auto)\tGPU/D3D12\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\td3d12_tessellation_wireframe\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tRender tessellation as wireframe\tGPU/D3D12\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvulkan_sparse_shared_memory\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tUse sparse shared memory on Vulkan\tGPU/Vulkan\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvulkan_force_expand_point_sprites_in_vs\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tForce Vulkan point sprite expansion in the vertex shader, even when geometry shaders are available\tGPU/Vulkan\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvulkan_force_expand_rectangle_lists_in_vs\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tForce Vulkan rectangle list expansion in the vertex shader, even when geometry shaders are available\tGPU/Vulkan\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvulkan_force_convert_quad_lists_to_triangle_lists\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tForce Vulkan quad list conversion to triangle lists in primitive processing, even when geometry shaders are available\tGPU/Vulkan\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tnon_seamless_cube_map\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tUse non-seamless cube map sampling\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\trender_target_path_vulkan\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tVulkan render target implementation path\tGPU/Vulkan\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvulkan_readback_resolve\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tRead render-to-texture results on the CPU\tGPU/Vulkan\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvulkan_readback_memexport\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tRead data written by memory export in shaders on the CPU\tGPU/Vulkan\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvulkan_async_skip_incomplete_frames\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tWhen async shader compilation is enabled, skip presenting frames with draws skipped while their pipelines are being created, to avoid visible flashing\tGPU/Vulkan\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvulkan_submit_on_primary_buffer_end\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tSubmit command buffer when PM4 primary buffer ends\tGPU/Vulkan\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvulkan_dynamic_rendering\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tUse VK_KHR_dynamic_rendering for Vulkan GPU emulation when supported by the device (falls back to render passes otherwise)\tGPU/Vulkan\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvulkan_depth_bias_force_unorm\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tApply the depth bias in constant units on float depth buffers where VK_EXT_depth_bias_control supports it, so the bias keeps its absolute size at every depth. Otherwise, the bias unit of a float depth buffer shrinks with the depth, and decals may Z-fight, especially with reversed depth.\tGPU/Vulkan\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvulkan_pipeline_creation_threads\tINT\t-1\t-1\t32\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tNumber of pipeline creation threads for Vulkan async pipeline creation (-1 for auto)\tGPU/Vulkan\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvulkan_tessellation_wireframe\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tRender tessellation as wireframe\tGPU/Vulkan\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tmrt_edram_used_range_clamp_to_min\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tClamp MRT EDRAM used range to minimum\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\texecute_unclipped_draw_vs_on_cpu_for_psi_render_backend\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tExecute unclipped draw VS on CPU for PSI render backend\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tsnorm16_render_target_full_range\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tUse full range for SNORM16 render targets\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tdirect_host_resolve\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tResolve from host render targets directly to shared memory when possible\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tno_discard_stencil_in_transfer_pipelines\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tSkip stencil bit discard in render target transfer pipelines. May improve performance on some GPUs.\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\taliased_depth_read_only\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tMatches interlock behavior by handling disjoint color and depth aliases for host render targets, keeping read-only depth bound when color writes only the unused stencil bits. May slightly increase overhead from keeping both host targets live and bound.\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tdraw_resolution_scale_threshold\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tSurface pitch in pixels at or below render targets skip being upscaled by draw_resolution_scale_x/y. 0 disables it. Small offscreen surfaces like bloom or depth of field buffers often break when upscaled and keeping them native avoids that. The pitch is compared after alignment to 80 pixel EDRAM tiles, so prefer conservative values, only as high as the broken effects need. Host render targets only.\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tdxbc_switch\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tUse switch statements in DXBC\tGPU/Shader\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tdxbc_source_map\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tGenerate source maps for DXBC\tGPU/Shader\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tspirv_disable_rounding_mode_rte\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tDisable RoundingModeRTE capability in SPIR-V shaders. Enable this to allow shader debugging in RenderDoc, which doesn't support this capability.\tGPU/Vulkan\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\ttexture_cache_memory_limit_render_to_texture\tINT\t24\t1\t256\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tTexture cache memory limit for render-to-texture (MB)\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\ttexture_cache_memory_limit_soft\tINT\t384\t64\t4096\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tSoft texture cache memory limit (MB)\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\ttexture_cache_memory_limit_hard\tINT\t768\t128\t8192\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tHard texture cache memory limit (MB)\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\ttexture_cache_memory_limit_soft_lifetime\tINT\t30\t1\t3600\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tSoft texture cache memory limit lifetime (seconds)\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tgpu_3d_to_2d_texture\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tSample problematic 3D textures through 2D-compatible wrappers\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tanisotropic_override\tINT\t3\t-1\t5\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tForces anisotropic filtering for eligible textures. Higher values keep textures sharper at oblique angles, but increase texture sampling cost. -1 = No override 0 = Disable anisotropic filtering 1 = Force 1x anisotropic filtering 2 = Force 2x anisotropic filtering 3 = Force 4x anisotropic filtering 4 = Force 8x anisotropic filtering 5 = Force 16x anisotropic filtering\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tdraw_resolution_scale_x\tINT\t1\t1\t8\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tDraw resolution scale X (1 = no scaling)\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tdraw_resolution_scale_y\tINT\t1\t1\t8\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tDraw resolution scale Y (1 = no scaling)\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tresolution_scale\tINT\t1\t1\t8\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tDraw resolution scale for both X and Y axes (same as setting draw_resolution_scale_x and draw_resolution_scale_y)\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\ttiled_shared_memory\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tEnable tiled/sparse resources for efficient large address space support. Disable for graphics debugger compatibility.\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tpre_mask_resolve_l2_block\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tPre-mask scaled resolve L2 blocks to the write range before iterating\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvsync\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tEnable vertical sync\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tclear_memory_page_state\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tRefresh page-valid state from GPU-written memory at frame end. Disable for minor CPU overhead reduction, but may break memory coherency.\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tocclusion_query\tENUM\tfast\t\u0001\t\u0001\tfake\u001Ffast\u001Ffast-alt\u001Fstrict\u001Fasync\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tControls hardware occlusion query behavior for EVENT_WRITE_ZPD. Used for effects like lens flares, object culling, and auto-exposure. fake: Write a fake result without asking the GPU. Safe for most games, though some effects may look slightly wrong. fast: Ask the GPU but don't wait for the answer. Writes a cached result immediately and updates it when the GPU catches up. Cached results bias toward visible when guessing. (default) fast-alt: Variant of fast mode that keeps cached zero results for unresolved reports. May improve effects relying on precise visibility, but may be less stable for occlusion culling. strict: Ask the GPU and wait for the real result before continuing. Most accurate, but may be somewhat less performant. async: Ask the GPU and write the real result once it arrives, without waiting. Until then the query reads as not ready. As accurate as strict for titles that poll results frames later (lens flares), but titles that spin on a result wait longer.\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tocclusion_query_full_counters\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tControls in-shader emulation of the ZFail, StencilFail and Total ZPD counters to supplement both native and counter-based ZPass testing. Most titles only use the ZPass counter, so this is off by default since it's typically slow and rife with readback sync. RTV/FBO approximates Total and ZFail, whereas ROV/FSI uses depth/stencil tests in-shader to count everything like Xenos does.\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tocclusion_query_viz\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tEnables VIZ_QUERY (VIZ) visibility tests for draws with a VIZ token. VIZ is the 360's version of conditional rendering / predication queries. Titles mostly use it to combat overdraw, but it can also be used for post-process effects like lens flares. When enabled, coarse occlusion queries feed predicates which, when available, can skip draws that aren't visible. Since VIZ is primarily a GPU mechanism, most readback sync is avoided. With that said, VIZ and standard occlusion queries can both cause a noticeable penalty with ROV and FSI, especially when combined.\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\treadback_resolve\tENUM\tnone\t\u0001\t\u0001\tnone\u001Ffast\u001Fsome\u001Ffull\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tControls CPU readback of render-to-texture resolve results. none: Disable readback (default) fast: Read previous frame (delayed, copy every frame) some: Read previous frame (delayed, copy on cache miss) full: Immediate sync readback (accurate but stalls)\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\treadback_resolve_half_pixel_offset\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tWhen resolution scaling and readback resolve are enabled, resolve downscaling keeps one supersample out of each scaled pixel block. This selects the center of the block instead of the top-left corner, which can be closer to where the GPU would have sampled the original pixel, and can help with thin features and edge coverage. Both choices give a real rendered value, but they can disagree where geometry edges fall inside a pixel block. This matters when the CPU reads the resolve as data instead of an image, such as for gamma correction readbacks, occlusion checks, and GPU buffers reused later in the frame.\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\treadback_memexport\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tEnable CPU readback of shader memexport writes for guest memory coherency (can reduce correctness issues, but may add GPU/CPU sync cost)\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\treadback_memexport_fast\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tUse fast double-buffered memexport readback when possible, with automatic fallback to full synchronous readback\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tasync_shader_compilation\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tCompile shaders and create pipelines asynchronously in background threads. This reduces stutter but may cause brief visual artifacts while pipelines are being prepared.\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tswap_post_effect\tENUM\tnone\t\u0001\t\u0001\tnone\u001Ffxaa\u001Ffxaa_extreme\u001Fsmaa\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tSwap post effect: none, fxaa, fxaa_extreme, smaa\tGPU\nperfect-dark-remaster-recomp\t\u0001\t\tstore_shaders\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1,4\t\u0001\tStore shaders persistently and load them when loading games to avoid runtime spikes and freezes when playing the game not for the first time.\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\twet_mouse_look\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tNative mouse look: mouse motion turns the third-person camera directly (1:1, no stick response curve or turn speed) instead of emulating the right stick. Where the camera hook does not run (menus, turrets) the stick emulation stays in charge. Needs mnk_mode and mnk_mouse\tMouse\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\twet_mouse_sensitivity\tFLOAT\t2.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tMouse look sensitivity: camera turn per mouse count = 0.022 deg x this (as in Source games)\tMouse\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\twet_mouse_invert_x\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tInvert the horizontal mouse look axis (on top of the in-game option)\tMouse\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\twet_mouse_invert_y\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tInvert the vertical mouse look axis (on top of the in-game option)\tMouse\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tgraphics_backend\tENUM\tany\t\u0001\t\u0001\tany\u001Fd3d12\u001Fvulkan\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tGraphics API backend: any, d3d12, vulkan\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tdev_debug_runtime\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tEnable runtime debug tools (stub sweep, missing function scan)\tDebug\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\twet_fps60_unlock\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tUnlock 60 FPS\tGameplay\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\twet_disable_motion_blur\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tDisable motion blur\tGraphics\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\twet_disable_depth_of_field\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tDisable depth of field\tGraphics\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\twet_disable_shaky_camera\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tDisable shaky camera and film effect\tGraphics\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\twet_gpu_wait_mode\tINT\t1\t0\t2\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tPause between polls while the game waits for free command-buffer space: 0 = busy spin (original), 1 = yield the core, 2 = sleep 200us\tPerformance\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\twet_match_display_refresh\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tUse the primary monitor's refresh rate as the guest video mode rate instead of video_mode_refresh_rate (Windows only, needs vsync)\tGraphics\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\td3d12_debug\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tEnable Direct3D 12 and DXGI debug layer\tUI/D3D12\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\td3d12_break_on_error\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tBreak on Direct3D 12 validation errors\tUI/D3D12\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\td3d12_break_on_warning\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tBreak on Direct3D 12 validation warnings\tUI/D3D12\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\td3d12_adapter\tINT\t-1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tIndex of the DXGI adapter to use (-1 for the gpu_vendor one, else the one with the most dedicated video memory, -2 for WARP)\tUI/D3D12\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\td3d12_queue_priority\tINT\t1\t0\t2\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tGraphics command queue priority (0=normal, 1=high, 2=realtime)\tUI/D3D12\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\td3d12_allow_variable_refresh_rate_and_tearing\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tAllow variable refresh rate and tearing\tUI/D3D12\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvulkan_validation_enabled\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tEnable Vulkan validation layers\tUI/Vulkan\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvulkan_device\tINT\t-1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tVulkan device index (-1 for auto selection)\tUI/Vulkan\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvulkan_prefer_geometry_shader\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tPrefer physical devices supporting geometryShader when auto-selecting\tUI/Vulkan\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvulkan_prefer_fragment_stores_and_atomics\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tPrefer physical devices supporting fragmentStoresAndAtomics when auto-selecting\tUI/Vulkan\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvulkan_prefer_vertex_pipeline_stores_and_atomics\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tPrefer physical devices supporting vertexPipelineStoresAndAtomics when auto-selecting\tUI/Vulkan\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvulkan_prefer_fill_mode_non_solid\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tPrefer physical devices supporting fillModeNonSolid when auto-selecting\tUI/Vulkan\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvulkan_log_debug_messages\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tLog Vulkan debug messages\tUI/Vulkan\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tpresent_render_pass_clear\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tClear render pass during presentation\tUI/Presenter\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvulkan_allow_present_mode_immediate\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tAllow immediate present mode (no vsync)\tUI/Vulkan\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvulkan_allow_present_mode_mailbox\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tAllow mailbox present mode (triple buffering)\tUI/Vulkan\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvulkan_allow_present_mode_fifo_relaxed\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tAllow FIFO relaxed present mode\tUI/Vulkan\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvulkan_semaphore_reuse_workaround\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tWait for presentation queue idle before each frame to prevent semaphore reuse. May fix rendering issues but causes significant performance loss.\tUI/Vulkan\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvulkan_require_fragment_stores_and_atomics\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tDeprecated and ignored for parity; fragmentStoresAndAtomics is always required for Vulkan GPU emulation\tUI/Vulkan\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvulkan_require_vertex_pipeline_stores_and_atomics\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tDeprecated and ignored for parity; vertexPipelineStoresAndAtomics is always required for Vulkan GPU emulation\tUI/Vulkan\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvulkan_require_geometry_shader\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tRequire geometryShader support for Vulkan GPU emulation (disable to allow fallback primitive emulation paths)\tUI/Vulkan\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvulkan_require_fill_mode_non_solid\tBOOL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tRequire fillModeNonSolid support for Vulkan GPU emulation (disable to allow fallback to solid fill for line/point polygon modes)\tUI/Vulkan\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\thost_present_from_non_ui_thread\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tAllow presentation from non-UI thread\tUI/Presenter\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tgpu_vendor\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tGraphics card to use: nvidia, amd, intel or a PCI vendor id such as 0x10de (Vulkan and Direct3D 12). Empty prefers a discrete GPU over an integrated one. vulkan_device / d3d12_adapter name an index and win over this.\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tpresent_letterbox\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tEnable letterboxing for non-native aspect ratios\tUI/Presenter\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tpresent_safe_area_x\tINT\t90\t0\t100\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tHorizontal safe area percentage (0-100)\tUI/Presenter\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tpresent_safe_area_y\tINT\t90\t0\t100\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tVertical safe area percentage (0-100)\tUI/Presenter\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tpresent_effect\tENUM\tbilinear\t\u0001\t\u0001\tbilinear\u001Fcas\u001Ffsr\u001Ffsr2\u001Ffsr3\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tGuest output effect: bilinear, cas, fsr, fsr2 or fsr3 (experimental, single-frame until temporal inputs exist)\tUI/Presenter\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tpresent_cas_additional_sharpness\tFLOAT\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tAdditional CAS sharpness in [0, 1]\tUI/Presenter\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tpresent_fsr_max_upsampling_passes\tINT\t\u0001\t1\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tMaximum chained FSR EASU passes\tUI/Presenter\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tpresent_fsr_sharpness_reduction\tFLOAT\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tFSR RCAS sharpness reduction in stops\tUI/Presenter\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tpresent_fsr_quality_mode\tENUM\tauto\t\u0001\t\u0001\tauto\u001Fnativeaa\u001Fquality\u001Fbalanced\u001Fperformance\u001Fultra_performance\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tTemporal FSR quality mode: auto, nativeaa, quality, balanced, performance, ultra_performance\tUI/Presenter\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tpresent_dither\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tEnable output dithering in the final present pass\tUI/Presenter\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tpresent_allow_overscan_cutoff\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tAllow overscan cutoff based on safe area settings\tUI/Presenter\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\twindow_width\tINT\t0\t0\t8192\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tWindow width in logical pixels (0 = use app default)\tUI/Window\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\twindow_height\tINT\t0\t0\t8192\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tWindow height in logical pixels (0 = use app default)\tUI/Window\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tfullscreen\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tStart the window in fullscreen mode\tUI/Window\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tfullscreen_exclusive\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tSwitch the display mode in fullscreen instead of going borderless at the desktop mode\tUI/Window\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tmonitor\tINT\t0\t0\t16\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tMonitor index to display on (0 = default, 1 = primary, 2 = second monitor, etc.)\tUI/Window\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvideo_driver\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tSDL video driver to use, such as \"wayland\" or \"x11\". Empty picks SDL's default for the session\tUI/Window\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvideo_mode_width\tINT\t1280\t640\t4095\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tGuest video mode width in pixels\tDisplay\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvideo_mode_height\tINT\t720\t480\t4095\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tGuest video mode height in pixels\tDisplay\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tresolution\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tCommon resolution preset for both guest video mode and window (for example: 720p, 1080p, 1440p, 4k, 1280x720)\tDisplay\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvideo_mode_refresh_rate\tFLOAT\t60.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tGuest video mode refresh rate in Hz\tDisplay\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tgpu_plugin\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tGPU emulation plugin to load at startup (e.g. 'xenos'); empty disables GPU emulation\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\taudio_maxqframes\tINT\t8\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tMax buffered audio frames (range 4-64). Lower reduces latency but may cause stuttering.\tAudio\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tffmpeg_verbose\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tVerbose FFmpeg output (debug and above)\tAudio\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\taudio_mute\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tMute audio output\tAudio\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\trexcrt_heap_enable\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tEnable o1heap-backed CRT heap for RtlAllocateHeap/Free/Size/ReAlloc\tcrt\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\trexcrt_heap_size_mb\tINT\t256\t1\t2048\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tHeap size in megabytes\tcrt\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tkernel_pix\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tEnable PIX debugging support\tKernel\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tavpack\tINT\t8\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tVideo modes (A/V pack): 0 = PAL-60 Component (SD), 1 = Unused, 2 = PAL-60 SCART, 3 = 480p Component (HD), 4 = HDMI+A, 5 = PAL-60 Composite/S-Video, 6 = VGA, 7 = TV PAL-60, 8 = HDMI\tVideo\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tlog_high_frequency_kernel_calls\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tLog kernel calls with the kHighFrequency tag\tKernel\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tcl\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tSpecify additional command-line provided to guest\tKernel\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tkernel_debug_monitor\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tEnable debug monitor\tKernel\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tkernel_cert_monitor\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tEnable cert monitor\tKernel\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\theadless\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tDon't display any UI, using defaults for prompts as needed\tKernel\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tlicense_mask\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tSet license mask for activated content\tKernel\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tuser_country\tINT\t103\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tUser's country ID\tKernel\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tuser_language\tINT\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tUser's language ID\tKernel\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tallow_game_relative_writes\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tNot useful to non-developers. Allows code to write to paths relative to game://. Used for generating test data to compare with original hardware.\tFilesystem\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tdump_source\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tSpecifies the file to dump from\tFilesystem\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tdump_path\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tSpecifies the directory to dump files to\tFilesystem\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tinput_backend\tENUM\tsdl\t\u0001\t\u0001\tsdl\u001Fxinput\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tInput backend: sdl, xinput\tInput\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tguide_button\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tEnable guide button pass-through\tInput\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvibration\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tEnable controller vibration\tInput\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tleft_stick_deadzone_percentage\tFLOAT\t0.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tDeadzone applied to the left stick, as a fraction of its range\tInput\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tright_stick_deadzone_percentage\tFLOAT\t0.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tDeadzone applied to the right stick, as a fraction of its range\tInput\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tmnk_mode\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tEnable keyboard/mouse controller emulation\tInput\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tmnk_mouse\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tUse the mouse for the right stick. Off means the right stick comes from the keybind_rstick_* keys only\tInput\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tmnk_sensitivity\tFLOAT\t1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tMouse sensitivity for right stick\tInput\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tkeybind_a\tSTRING\tSemicolon,Space\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tA button\tInput/Keybinds/Controller\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tkeybind_b\tSTRING\tQuote,Backspace\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tB button\tInput/Keybinds/Controller\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tkeybind_x\tSTRING\tL\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tX button\tInput/Keybinds/Controller\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tkeybind_y\tSTRING\tP\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tY button\tInput/Keybinds/Controller\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tkeybind_left_trigger\tSTRING\tQ,I\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tLeft trigger\tInput/Keybinds/Controller\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tkeybind_right_trigger\tSTRING\tE,O\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tRight trigger\tInput/Keybinds/Controller\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tkeybind_left_shoulder\tSTRING\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tLeft shoulder\tInput/Keybinds/Controller\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tkeybind_right_shoulder\tSTRING\t3\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tRight shoulder\tInput/Keybinds/Controller\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tkeybind_lstick_up\tSTRING\tW\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tLeft stick up\tInput/Keybinds/Controller\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tkeybind_lstick_down\tSTRING\tS\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tLeft stick down\tInput/Keybinds/Controller\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tkeybind_lstick_left\tSTRING\tA\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tLeft stick left\tInput/Keybinds/Controller\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tkeybind_lstick_right\tSTRING\tD\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tLeft stick right\tInput/Keybinds/Controller\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tkeybind_lstick_press\tSTRING\tF\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tLeft stick press\tInput/Keybinds/Controller\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tkeybind_rstick_up\tSTRING\tUp\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tRight stick up\tInput/Keybinds/Controller\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tkeybind_rstick_down\tSTRING\tDown\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tRight stick down\tInput/Keybinds/Controller\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tkeybind_rstick_left\tSTRING\tLeft\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tRight stick left\tInput/Keybinds/Controller\n",
    "wet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tkeybind_rstick_right\tSTRING\tRight\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tRight stick right\tInput/Keybinds/Controller\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tkeybind_rstick_press\tSTRING\tK\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tRight stick press\tInput/Keybinds/Controller\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tkeybind_dpad_up\tSTRING\tShift+Up\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tD-pad up\tInput/Keybinds/Controller\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tkeybind_dpad_down\tSTRING\tShift+Down\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tD-pad down\tInput/Keybinds/Controller\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tkeybind_dpad_left\tSTRING\tShift+Left\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tD-pad left\tInput/Keybinds/Controller\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tkeybind_dpad_right\tSTRING\tShift+Right\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tD-pad right\tInput/Keybinds/Controller\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tkeybind_back\tSTRING\tZ,Tab\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tBack button\tInput/Keybinds/Controller\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tkeybind_start\tSTRING\tX,Return\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tStart button\tInput/Keybinds/Controller\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tkeybind_guide\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tGuide button\tInput/Keybinds/Controller\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tmnk_passthrough\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tSurface raw keystrokes to the title instead of emulating a pad, for titles that read a USB keyboard. Enables the device on its own\tInput\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\thid_mappings_file\tSTRING\tgamecontrollerdb.txt\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tPath to SDL gamecontroller mappings file\tInput\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tmax_file_size_bytes\tINT\t1048576\t65536\t67108864\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tTarget source file size in bytes; sets how many recomp files a project is split into, chosen once and then persisted\tCodegen\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tprogress_log_frequency\tINT\t100\t1\t100000\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tLog progress every N functions\tCodegen\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tanalysis_report\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tWrite every analyzed function (address, size, source) to this file, so two SDK versions or configs can be compared; empty disables\tCodegen\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tmax_discovery_iterations\tINT\t1000\t1\t100000\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tMax iterations for function discovery convergence\tCodegen\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tmax_vtable_iterations\tINT\t100\t1\t100000\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tMax iterations for vtable discovery\tCodegen\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tmax_resolve_iterations\tINT\t100\t1\t100000\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tMax iterations for call target resolution\tCodegen\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tmax_eh_states\tINT\t100\t1\t100000\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tMax C++ EH states before rejecting handler\tCodegen\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tmax_eh_try_blocks\tINT\t50\t1\t100000\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tMax try blocks before rejecting handler\tCodegen\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tmax_eh_ip_map_entries\tINT\t200\t1\t100000\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tMax IP-to-state map entries\tCodegen\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tmax_seh_scope_entries\tINT\t100\t1\t100000\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tMax SEH scope table entries\tCodegen\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tbackward_scan_limit\tINT\t64\t1\t10000\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tMax instructions to scan backward for jump table patterns\tCodegen\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tmax_jump_table_entries\tINT\t512\t1\t100000\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tMax entries per detected jump table\tCodegen\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tmax_blocks_per_function\tINT\t10000\t1\t1000000\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tSafety limit on blocks per function\tCodegen\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tgame_data_root\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tOverride game data path\tRuntime\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tuser_data_root\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tOverride user data path\tRuntime\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tupdate_data_root\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tOverride update data path\tRuntime\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tcache_root\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tOverride shader cache path\tRuntime\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tmetadata_root\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tOverride metadata path\tRuntime\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tignore_thread_priorities\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tIgnores game-specified thread priorities\tKernel\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tignore_thread_affinities\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tIgnores game-specified thread affinities\tKernel\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tprotect_zero\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tProtect the zero page from reads and writes\tMemory\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tprotect_on_release\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tProtect released memory to prevent accesses\tMemory\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tscribble_heap\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tScribble 0xCD into all allocated heap memory\tMemory\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tunregistered_function_log\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tAppend each guest address called without a recompiled function to this file, as a [functions] entry for the project config\tRuntime\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\twritable_code_segments\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tEnables a program to write to its own code segments in memory\tMemory\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tlog_level\tENUM\tinfo\t\u0001\t\u0001\ttrace\u001Fdebug\u001Finfo\u001Fwarn\u001Ferror\u001Fcritical\u001Foff\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tGlobal log level: trace, debug, info, warn, error, critical, off\tLog\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tlog_file\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tLog file path (empty = auto sequential naming)\tLog\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tlog_noisy\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tEnable noisy/high-frequency log macros\tLog\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tlog_flush_interval\tINT\t0\t0\t60\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tPeriodic flush interval in seconds (0 = off)\tLog\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tclock_no_scaling\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tDisable clock scaling (inverted: false = scaling enabled)\tClock\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tclock_source_raw\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tUse raw clock source without scaling\tClock\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tperf_log_csv\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tPath to write per-frame CSV log (empty = disabled)\tPerf\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tgpu_allow_invalid_fetch_constants\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tAllow invalid fetch constants\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tgpu_allow_invalid_upload_range\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tAllows games to read data from pages that are marked as no access.\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tnative_2x_msaa\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tEnable native 2x MSAA\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tdraw_resolution_scaled_texture_offsets\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tScale texture offsets with draw resolution\tGPU/Shader\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tprecise_interpolation\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tInterpolate pixel shader inputs manually from the per-vertex values (Vulkan with VK_KHR_fragment_shader_barycentric) to avoid host interpolation imprecision, which causes noise in games that compare interpolated values for equality, such as Perfect Dark Zero and Tenchu Z on Nvidia.\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tdepth_float24_round\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tRound float24 depth values\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tdepth_float24_convert_in_pixel_shader\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tConvert float24 depth in pixel shader\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tdepth_transfer_not_equal_test\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tUse not-equal test for depth transfer\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tgamma_render_target_as_unorm16\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tUse R16G16B16A16_UNORM for gamma render targets (more accurate than sRGB)\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tdump_shaders\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tPath to dump shaders to\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tmulsc_round_toward_zero\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tRound mulsc products toward zero instead of to nearest even. This fixes bad geometry in several Volition Engine titles and possibly others. This rounding behavior hasn't been confirmed on real hardware, so it's disabled by default.\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tuse_fuzzy_alpha_epsilon\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tUse approximate compare for alpha test values to prevent flickering on NVIDIA graphics cards\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tgpu_debug_markers\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tInsert debug markers into GPU command streams for tools like PIX and RenderDoc. Automatically enabled when RenderDoc is detected.\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tforce_depth_clamp\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tUse host depth clamping instead of near and far plane clipping when guest clipping is enabled. X/Y/W clipping is unaffected. On Vulkan, this requires depthClamp support.\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tocclusion_query_fake_lower_threshold\tINT\t80\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tLower end of the fake sample count value written on EVENT_WRITE_ZPD when real occlusion queries are disabled. -1 writes nothing, resulting in some games that sit and hang. 0 means the fake result stays fully occluded.\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tocclusion_query_fake_upper_threshold\tINT\t100\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tUpper end of the fake sample count value written on EVENT_WRITE_ZPD when real occlusion queries are disabled. Keep this higher than occlusion_query_fake_lower_threshold. Ignored if occlusion_query_fake_lower_threshold is -1.\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\txenos_sample_positions\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tRasterize 2x and 4x MSAA render targets at the Xenos sample positions, like real hardware, if the GPU and driver support it. Only applies to RTV/FBO - ROV/FSI render targets always use Xenos positions since they safely map coverage and calculate depth in-shader.\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\ttexture_point_snap\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tSnap normalized point sampled 2D texture coordinates to texel centers. Fixes texture seams in titles that use virtual textures, e.g. idTech 5, but may cause rendering issues in other titles.\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\thalf_pixel_offset\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tEnable half pixel offset\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tresolve_resolution_scale_fill_half_pixel_offset\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tFill half pixel offset during resolution scale resolve\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tdepth_bias_shader_offset\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tRoute decal host render target draws with polygon offset through shader depth. This avoids Z-fighting in games that rely on tiny depth bias values that host fixed function depth bias cannot reproduce reliably. This likely causes some minor performance penalty, but the cost should be minimal if only a small portion of the scene is affected.\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\twindow_offset_in_edram\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tRenders every tile of a predicated tiling frame at the same position as the depth prepass by applying the window offset in EDRAM rather than the viewport. Fixes depth artifacts in the bottom tile of the screen. Disable this if tiles start shifting or banding. Works on every render target path. ROV and FSI apply it to every tile since their pixel shaders directly address EDRAM and can offset sideways or past the end of EDRAM, RTV and FBO keep sideways offsets, and tiles that would run past the target, in the viewport.\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\texecute_unclipped_draw_vs_on_cpu\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tExecute unclipped draw vertex shader on CPU\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\texecute_unclipped_draw_vs_on_cpu_with_scissor\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tExecute unclipped draw VS on CPU with scissor\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tforce_convert_line_loops_to_strips\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tForce convert line loops to strips\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tforce_convert_quad_lists_to_triangle_lists\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tForce convert quad lists to triangle lists\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tforce_convert_triangle_fans_to_lists\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tForce convert triangle fans to lists\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tprimitive_processor_cache_min_indices\tINT\t0\t0\t1000000\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tMinimum indices for primitive processor cache\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tnative_stencil_value_output_d3d12_intel\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tNative stencil value output for Intel D3D12\tGPU/D3D12\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\trender_target_path_d3d12\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tD3D12 render target implementation path\tGPU/D3D12\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tnative_stencil_value_output\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tEnable native stencil value output\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\td3d12_bindless\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tUse bindless resources where available\tGPU/D3D12\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\td3d12_readback_memexport\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tRead data written by memory export in shaders on the CPU\tGPU/D3D12\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\td3d12_readback_resolve\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tRead render-to-texture results on the CPU\tGPU/D3D12\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\td3d12_submit_on_primary_buffer_end\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tSubmit command list when PM4 primary buffer ends\tGPU/D3D12\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\td3d12_dxbc_disasm\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tDump DXBC disassembly\tGPU/D3D12\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\td3d12_dxbc_disasm_dxilconv\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tDump DXIL conversion disassembly\tGPU/D3D12\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\td3d12_pipeline_creation_threads\tINT\t-1\t-1\t32\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tNumber of pipeline creation threads (-1 for auto)\tGPU/D3D12\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\td3d12_tessellation_wireframe\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tRender tessellation as wireframe\tGPU/D3D12\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvulkan_sparse_shared_memory\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tUse sparse shared memory on Vulkan\tGPU/Vulkan\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvulkan_force_expand_point_sprites_in_vs\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tForce Vulkan point sprite expansion in the vertex shader, even when geometry shaders are available\tGPU/Vulkan\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvulkan_force_expand_rectangle_lists_in_vs\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tForce Vulkan rectangle list expansion in the vertex shader, even when geometry shaders are available\tGPU/Vulkan\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvulkan_force_convert_quad_lists_to_triangle_lists\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tForce Vulkan quad list conversion to triangle lists in primitive processing, even when geometry shaders are available\tGPU/Vulkan\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tnon_seamless_cube_map\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tUse non-seamless cube map sampling\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\trender_target_path_vulkan\tSTRING\t\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tVulkan render target implementation path\tGPU/Vulkan\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvulkan_readback_resolve\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tRead render-to-texture results on the CPU\tGPU/Vulkan\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvulkan_readback_memexport\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tRead data written by memory export in shaders on the CPU\tGPU/Vulkan\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvulkan_async_skip_incomplete_frames\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tWhen async shader compilation is enabled, skip presenting frames with draws skipped while their pipelines are being created, to avoid visible flashing\tGPU/Vulkan\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvulkan_submit_on_primary_buffer_end\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tSubmit command buffer when PM4 primary buffer ends\tGPU/Vulkan\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvulkan_dynamic_rendering\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tUse VK_KHR_dynamic_rendering for Vulkan GPU emulation when supported by the device (falls back to render passes otherwise)\tGPU/Vulkan\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvulkan_depth_bias_force_unorm\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tApply the depth bias in constant units on float depth buffers where VK_EXT_depth_bias_control supports it, so the bias keeps its absolute size at every depth. Otherwise, the bias unit of a float depth buffer shrinks with the depth, and decals may Z-fight, especially with reversed depth.\tGPU/Vulkan\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvulkan_pipeline_creation_threads\tINT\t-1\t-1\t32\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tNumber of pipeline creation threads for Vulkan async pipeline creation (-1 for auto)\tGPU/Vulkan\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvulkan_tessellation_wireframe\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tRender tessellation as wireframe\tGPU/Vulkan\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tmrt_edram_used_range_clamp_to_min\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tClamp MRT EDRAM used range to minimum\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\texecute_unclipped_draw_vs_on_cpu_for_psi_render_backend\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tExecute unclipped draw VS on CPU for PSI render backend\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tsnorm16_render_target_full_range\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tUse full range for SNORM16 render targets\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tdirect_host_resolve\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tResolve from host render targets directly to shared memory when possible\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tno_discard_stencil_in_transfer_pipelines\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tSkip stencil bit discard in render target transfer pipelines. May improve performance on some GPUs.\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\taliased_depth_read_only\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tMatches interlock behavior by handling disjoint color and depth aliases for host render targets, keeping read-only depth bound when color writes only the unused stencil bits. May slightly increase overhead from keeping both host targets live and bound.\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tdraw_resolution_scale_threshold\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tSurface pitch in pixels at or below render targets skip being upscaled by draw_resolution_scale_x/y. 0 disables it. Small offscreen surfaces like bloom or depth of field buffers often break when upscaled and keeping them native avoids that. The pitch is compared after alignment to 80 pixel EDRAM tiles, so prefer conservative values, only as high as the broken effects need. Host render targets only.\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tdxbc_switch\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tUse switch statements in DXBC\tGPU/Shader\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tdxbc_source_map\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tGenerate source maps for DXBC\tGPU/Shader\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tspirv_disable_rounding_mode_rte\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tDisable RoundingModeRTE capability in SPIR-V shaders. Enable this to allow shader debugging in RenderDoc, which doesn't support this capability.\tGPU/Vulkan\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\ttexture_cache_memory_limit_render_to_texture\tINT\t24\t1\t256\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tTexture cache memory limit for render-to-texture (MB)\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\ttexture_cache_memory_limit_soft\tINT\t384\t64\t4096\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tSoft texture cache memory limit (MB)\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\ttexture_cache_memory_limit_hard\tINT\t768\t128\t8192\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tHard texture cache memory limit (MB)\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\ttexture_cache_memory_limit_soft_lifetime\tINT\t30\t1\t3600\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tSoft texture cache memory limit lifetime (seconds)\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tgpu_3d_to_2d_texture\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tSample problematic 3D textures through 2D-compatible wrappers\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tanisotropic_override\tINT\t3\t-1\t5\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tForces anisotropic filtering for eligible textures. Higher values keep textures sharper at oblique angles, but increase texture sampling cost. -1 = No override 0 = Disable anisotropic filtering 1 = Force 1x anisotropic filtering 2 = Force 2x anisotropic filtering 3 = Force 4x anisotropic filtering 4 = Force 8x anisotropic filtering 5 = Force 16x anisotropic filtering\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tdraw_resolution_scale_x\tINT\t1\t1\t8\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tDraw resolution scale X (1 = no scaling)\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tdraw_resolution_scale_y\tINT\t1\t1\t8\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tDraw resolution scale Y (1 = no scaling)\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tresolution_scale\tINT\t1\t1\t8\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tDraw resolution scale for both X and Y axes (same as setting draw_resolution_scale_x and draw_resolution_scale_y)\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\ttiled_shared_memory\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tEnable tiled/sparse resources for efficient large address space support. Disable for graphics debugger compatibility.\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tpre_mask_resolve_l2_block\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tPre-mask scaled resolve L2 blocks to the write range before iterating\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tvsync\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tEnable vertical sync\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tclear_memory_page_state\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tRefresh page-valid state from GPU-written memory at frame end. Disable for minor CPU overhead reduction, but may break memory coherency.\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tocclusion_query\tENUM\tfast\t\u0001\t\u0001\tfake\u001Ffast\u001Ffast-alt\u001Fstrict\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tControls hardware occlusion query behavior for EVENT_WRITE_ZPD. Used for effects like lens flares, object culling, and auto-exposure. fake: Write a fake result without asking the GPU. Safe for most games, though some effects may look slightly wrong. fast: Ask the GPU but don't wait for the answer. Writes a cached result immediately and updates it when the GPU catches up. Cached results bias toward visible when guessing. (default) fast-alt: Variant of fast mode that keeps cached zero results for unresolved reports. May improve effects relying on precise visibility, but may be less stable for occlusion culling. strict: Ask the GPU and wait for the real result before continuing. Most accurate, but may be somewhat less performant.\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tocclusion_query_full_counters\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tControls in-shader emulation of the ZFail, StencilFail and Total ZPD counters to supplement both native and counter-based ZPass testing. Most titles only use the ZPass counter, so this is off by default since it's typically slow and rife with readback sync. RTV/FBO approximates Total and ZFail, whereas ROV/FSI uses depth/stencil tests in-shader to count everything like Xenos does.\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tocclusion_query_viz\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tEnables VIZ_QUERY (VIZ) visibility tests for draws with a VIZ token. VIZ is the 360's version of conditional rendering / predication queries. Titles mostly use it to combat overdraw, but it can also be used for post-process effects like lens flares. When enabled, coarse occlusion queries feed predicates which, when available, can skip draws that aren't visible. Since VIZ is primarily a GPU mechanism, most readback sync is avoided. With that said, VIZ and standard occlusion queries can both cause a noticeable penalty with ROV and FSI, especially when combined.\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\treadback_resolve\tENUM\tnone\t\u0001\t\u0001\tnone\u001Ffast\u001Fsome\u001Ffull\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tControls CPU readback of render-to-texture resolve results. none: Disable readback (default) fast: Read previous frame (delayed, copy every frame) some: Read previous frame (delayed, copy on cache miss) full: Immediate sync readback (accurate but stalls)\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\treadback_resolve_half_pixel_offset\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tWhen resolution scaling and readback resolve are enabled, resolve downscaling keeps one supersample out of each scaled pixel block. This selects the center of the block instead of the top-left corner, which can be closer to where the GPU would have sampled the original pixel, and can help with thin features and edge coverage. Both choices give a real rendered value, but they can disagree where geometry edges fall inside a pixel block. This matters when the CPU reads the resolve as data instead of an image, such as for gamma correction readbacks, occlusion checks, and GPU buffers reused later in the frame.\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\treadback_memexport\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tEnable CPU readback of shader memexport writes for guest memory coherency (can reduce correctness issues, but may add GPU/CPU sync cost)\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\treadback_memexport_fast\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tUse fast double-buffered memexport readback when possible, with automatic fallback to full synchronous readback\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tasync_shader_compilation\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tCompile shaders and create pipelines asynchronously in background threads. This reduces stutter but may cause brief visual artifacts while pipelines are being prepared.\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tswap_post_effect\tENUM\tnone\t\u0001\t\u0001\tnone\u001Ffxaa\u001Ffxaa_extreme\u001Fsmaa\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tSwap post effect: none, fxaa, fxaa_extreme, smaa\tGPU\nwet-recomp\t\u0001\t\tstore_shaders\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.4\t\u0001\tStore shaders persistently and load them when loading games to avoid runtime spikes and freezes when playing the game not for the first time.\tGPU\nrsdkv3\t\u0001\tDev\tDevMenu\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.3.3\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nrsdkv3\t\u0001\tDev\tEngineDebugMode\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.3.3\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nrsdkv3\t\u0001\tDev\tTxtScripts\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.3.3\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nrsdkv3\t\u0001\tDev\tStartingCategory\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.3.3\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nrsdkv3\t\u0001\tDev\tStartingScene\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.3.3\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nrsdkv3\t\u0001\tDev\tFastForwardSpeed\tINT\t8\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.3.3\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nrsdkv3\t\u0001\tDev\tUseSteamDir\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.3.3\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nrsdkv3\t\u0001\tDev\tUseHQModes\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.3.3\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nrsdkv3\t\u0001\tDev\tDataFile\tSTRING\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.3.3\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nrsdkv3\t\u0001\tGame\tLanguage\tINT\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.3.3\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nrsdkv3\t\u0001\tGame\tGameType\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\t1.3.3\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\nrsdkv3\t\u0001\tGame\tOriginalC